Created by the variables \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:blob/\:main/\:build/\:lib/\:pylint/\:checkers/\:variables\:.py> checker.
.SS invalid\-all\-object / E0604
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBInvalid object %r in __all__, must contain only strings\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIUsed when an invalid (non\-string) object occurs in __all__.\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
__all__ = (
    None,  # [invalid\-all\-object]
    Fruit,
    Worm,
)


class Fruit:
    pass


class Worm:
    pass

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCorrect code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
__all__ = [\(dqFruit\(dq, \(dqWorm\(dq]


class Fruit:
    pass


class Worm:
    pass

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBAdditional details:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B From The Python Language Reference – The import statement \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:reference/\:simple_stmts\:.html#\:the-import-statement>:
\(dqThe \fIpublic names\fP defined by a module are determined by checking the module\(aqs namespace for a variable named \fB__all__\fP; if defined, it must be a sequence of strings which are names defined or imported by that module.\(dq
.UNINDENT
.sp
