.SS return\-arg\-in\-generator / E0106
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBReturn with argument inside generator\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIUsed when a \(dqreturn\(dq statement with an argument is found in a generator function or method (e.g. with some \(dqyield\(dq statements).\fP
.sp
\fBCorrect code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def yield_numbers():
    for number in range(10):
        yield number
        return \(dqI am now allowed!\(dq  # This was not allowed in Python 3.3 and earlier.

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBAdditional details:\fP
.sp
This is a message that isn\(aqt going to be raised for python > 3.3. It was raised
for code like:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def interrogate_until_you_find_jack(pirates):
    for pirate in pirates:
        if pirate == \(dqCaptain Jack Sparrow\(dq:
            return \(dqArrr! We\(aqve found our captain!\(dq
        yield pirate
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Which is now valid and equivalent to the previously expected:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def interrogate_until_you_find_jack(pirates):
    for pirate in pirates:
        if pirate == \(dqCaptain Jack Sparrow\(dq:
            raise StopIteration(\(dqArrr! We\(aqve found our captain!\(dq)
        yield pirate
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
