.SS bad\-builtin / W0141
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBUsed builtin function %s\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIUsed when a disallowed builtin function is used (see the bad\-function option). Usual disallowed functions are the ones like map, or filter , where Python offers now some cleaner alternative like list comprehension.\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
numbers = list(map(lambda x: 2 * x, [1, 2, 3]))  # [bad\-builtin]
print(numbers)

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCorrect code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
numbers = [2 * x for x in [1, 2, 3]]
print(numbers)

.EE
