.SS broad\-exception\-caught / W0718
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBCatching too general exception %s\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIIf you use a naked \(ga\(gaexcept Exception:\(ga\(ga clause, you might end up catching exceptions other than the ones you expect to catch. This can hide bugs or make it harder to debug programs when unrelated errors are hidden.\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
try:
    import platform_specific_module
except Exception:  # [broad\-exception\-caught]
    platform_specific_module = None

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCorrect code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
try:
    import platform_specific_module
except ImportError:
    platform_specific_module = None

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBAdditional details:\fP
.sp
For example, you\(aqre trying to import a library with required system dependencies and you catch
everything instead of only import errors, you will miss the error message telling you, that
your code could work if you had installed the system dependencies.
.sp
