.SS broad\-exception\-raised / W0719
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBRaising too general exception: %s\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIRaising exceptions that are too generic force you to catch exceptions generically too. It will force you to use a naked \(ga\(gaexcept Exception:\(ga\(ga clause. You might then end up catching exceptions other than the ones you expect to catch. This can hide bugs or make it harder to debug programs when unrelated errors are hidden.\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def small_apple(apple, length):
    if len(apple) < length:
        raise Exception(\(dqApple is too small!\(dq)  # [broad\-exception\-raised]
    print(f\(dq{apple} is proper size.\(dq)

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
