.SS dangerous\-default\-value / W0102
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBDangerous default value %s as argument\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIUsed when a mutable value as list or dictionary is detected in a default value for an argument.\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def whats_on_the_telly(penguin=[]):  # [dangerous\-default\-value]
    penguin.append(\(dqproperty of the zoo\(dq)
    return penguin

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCorrect code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def whats_on_the_telly(penguin=None):
    if penguin is None:
        penguin = []
    penguin.append(\(dqproperty of the zoo\(dq)
    return penguin

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBAdditional details:\fP
.sp
With a mutable default value, with each call the default value is modified, i.e.:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
whats_on_the_telly() # [\(dqproperty of the zoo\(dq]
whats_on_the_telly() # [\(dqproperty of the zoo\(dq, \(dqproperty of the zoo\(dq]
whats_on_the_telly() # [\(dqproperty of the zoo\(dq, \(dqproperty of the zoo\(dq, \(dqproperty of the zoo\(dq]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
