        print(i)

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBAdditional details:\fP
.sp
A common issue is that this message is triggered when using \fIpytest\fP fixtures \%<https://\:docs\:.pytest\:.org/\:en/\:7\:.1\:.x/\:how-to/\:fixtures\:.html>:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import pytest

@pytest.fixture
def setup():
    ...


def test_something(setup):  # [redefined\-outer\-name]
    ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
One solution to this problem is to explicitly name the fixture:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
@pytest.fixture(name=\(dqsetup\(dq)
def setup_fixture():
    ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Alternatively \fIpylint\fP plugins like pylint\-pytest \%<https://\:pypi\:.org/\:project/\:pylint-pytest> can be used.
.sp
Created by the variables \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:blob/\:main/\:build/\:lib/\:pylint/\:checkers/\:variables\:.py> checker.
