.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBAdditional details:\fP
.sp
Directly asserting a string literal will always pass. The solution is to
test something that could fail, or not assert at all.
.sp
For assertions using \fBassert\fP there are similar messages: assert\-on\-string\-literal / W0129 \%<#\:assert-on-string-literal> and assert\-on\-tuple / W0199 \%<#\:assert-on-tuple>\&.
.sp
