.SS return\-in\-finally / W0134
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fB\(aqreturn\(aq shadowed by the \(aqfinally\(aq clause.\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIEmitted when a \(aqreturn\(aq statement is found in a \(aqfinally\(aq block. This will overwrite the return value of a function and should be avoided.\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def second_favorite():
    fruits = [\(dqkiwi\(dq, \(dqpineapple\(dq]
    try:
        return fruits[1]
    finally:
        # because of this \(gareturn\(ga statement, this function will always return \(dqkiwi\(dq
        return fruits[0]  # [return\-in\-finally]

.EE
