.SS unidiomatic\-typecheck / C0123
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBUse isinstance() rather than type() for a typecheck.\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIThe idiomatic way to perform an explicit typecheck in Python is to use isinstance(x, Y) rather than type(x) == Y, type(x) is Y. Though there are unusual situations where these give different results.\fP
.sp
