.SS typevar\-name\-incorrect\-variance / C0105
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBType variable name does not reflect variance%s\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIEmitted when a TypeVar name doesn\(aqt reflect its type variance. According to PEP8, it is recommended to add suffixes \(aq_co\(aq and \(aq_contra\(aq to the variables used to declare covariant or contravariant behaviour respectively. Invariant (default) variables do not require a suffix. The message is also emitted when invariant variables do have a suffix.\fP
.sp
