.SS use\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-comparison\-to\-string / C1804
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fB\(dq%s\(dq can be simplified to \(dq%s\(dq, if it is strictly a string, as an empty string is falsey\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIEmpty string are considered false in a boolean context. Following this check blindly in weakly typed code base can create hard to debug issues. If the value can be something else that is falsey but not a string (for example \(ga\(gaNone\(ga\(ga, an empty sequence, or \(ga\(ga0\(ga\(ga) the code will not be equivalent.\fP
.sp
\fBCaution:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This message is disabled by default. To enable it, add \fBuse\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-comparison\-to\-string\fP to the \fBenable\fP option.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
