.SS comparison\-of\-constants / R0133
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBComparison between constants: \(dq%s %s %s\(dq has a constant value\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIWhen two literals are compared with each other the result is a constant. Using the constant directly is both easier to read and more performant. Initializing \(aqTrue\(aq and \(aqFalse\(aq this way is not required since Python 2.3.\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
