.SS consider\-using\-dict\-comprehension / R1717
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBConsider using a dictionary comprehension\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIEmitted when we detect the creation of a dictionary using the dict() callable and a transient list. Although there is nothing syntactically wrong with this code, it is hard to read and can be simplified to a dict comprehension. Also it is faster since you don\(aqt need to create another transient list\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
NUMBERS = [1, 2, 3]

# +1: [consider\-using\-dict\-comprehension]
DOUBLED_NUMBERS = dict([(number, number * 2) for number in NUMBERS])

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCorrect code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
NUMBERS = [1, 2, 3]

DOUBLED_NUMBERS = {number: number * 2 for number in NUMBERS}

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBAdditional details:\fP
.sp
pyupgrade \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:asottile/\:pyupgrade> or ruff \%<https://\:docs\:.astral\:.sh/\:ruff> can fix this issue automatically.
.sp
