.SS match\-class\-positional\-attributes / R1906
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBUse keyword attributes instead of positional ones (%s)\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIKeyword attributes are more explicit and slightly faster since CPython can skip the \(ga__match_args__\(ga lookup.\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Book:
    __match_args__ = (\(dqtitle\(dq, \(dqyear\(dq)

    def __init__(self, title, year):
        self.title = title
        self.year = year


def func(item: Book):
    match item:
        case Book(\(dqabc\(dq, 2000):  # [match\-class\-positional\-attributes]
            ...

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCorrect code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
