.SS no\-else\-break / R1723
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBUnnecessary \(dq%s\(dq after \(dqbreak\(dq, %s\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIUsed in order to highlight an unnecessary block of code following an if containing a break statement. As such, it will warn when it encounters an else following a chain of ifs, all of them containing a break statement.\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def next_seven_elements(iterator):
    for i, item in enumerate(iterator):
        if i == 7:  # [no\-else\-break]
            break
        else:
            yield item

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCorrect code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def next_seven_elements(iterator):
    for i, item in enumerate(iterator):
        if i == 7:
            break
        yield item

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Created by the refactoring \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:blob/\:main/\:build/\:lib/\:pylint/\:checkers/\:refactoring/\:refactoring_checker\:.py> checker.
.SS no\-else\-continue / R1724
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBUnnecessary \(dq%s\(dq after \(dqcontinue\(dq, %s\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIUsed in order to highlight an unnecessary block of code following an if containing a continue statement. As such, it will warn when it encounters an else following a chain of ifs, all of them containing a continue statement.\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def even_number_under(n: int):
    for i in range(n):
        if i % 2 == 1:  # [no\-else\-continue]
            continue
        else:
            yield i

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
