.SS stop\-iteration\-return / R1708
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBDo not raise StopIteration in generator, use return statement instead\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIAccording to PEP479, the raise of StopIteration to end the loop of a generator may lead to hard to find bugs. This PEP specify that raise StopIteration has to be replaced by a simple return statement\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.sp
\fBfruit_generator.py\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def fruit_generator():
    for fruit in [\(dqapple\(dq, \(dqbanana\(dq]:
        yield fruit
    raise StopIteration  # [stop\-iteration\-return]

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBtwo_fruit_generator.py\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def two_fruits_generator(fruits):
    for fruit in fruits:
        yield fruit, next(fruits)  # [stop\-iteration\-return]

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBtwo_good_fruit_generator.py\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def two_good_fruits_generator(fruits):
    for fruit in fruits:
        if not fruit.is_tasty():
            continue
        while True:
            next_fruit = next(fruits)  # [stop\-iteration\-return]
            if next_fruit.is_tasty():
                yield fruit, next_fruit
                break

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCorrect code:\fP
.sp
\fBfruit_generator.py\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def fruit_generator():
    \(dq\(dq\(dqThe example is simple enough you don\(aqt need an explicit return.\(dq\(dq\(dq
    for fruit in [\(dqapple\(dq, \(dqbanana\(dq]:
        yield fruit

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBtwo_fruit_generator.py\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def two_fruits_generator(fruits):
    \(dq\(dq\(dqCatching the StopIteration.\(dq\(dq\(dq
    for fruit in fruits:
        try:
            yield fruit, next(fruits)
        except StopIteration:
            print(\(dqSorry there is only one fruit left.\(dq)
            yield fruit, None

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBtwo_good_fruit_generator.py\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def two_good_fruits_generator(fruits):
    \(dq\(dq\(dqA return can be used to end the iterator early, but not a StopIteration.\(dq\(dq\(dq
    for fruit in fruits:
        if not fruit.is_tasty():
            continue
        while True:
            next_fruit = next(fruits, None)
            if next_fruit is None:
                print(\(dqSorry there is only one fruit left.\(dq)
                yield fruit, None
                # We reached the end of the \(aqfruits\(aq generator but raising a
                # StopIteration instead of returning would create a RuntimeError
                return
            if next_fruit.is_tasty():
                yield fruit, next_fruit
                break

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBAdditional details:\fP
.sp
It\(aqs possible to give a default value to \fBnext\fP or catch the \fBStopIteration\fP,
or return directly. A \fBStopIteration\fP cannot be propagated from a generator.
.sp
