.SS trailing\-comma\-tuple / R1707
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBDisallow trailing comma tuple\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIIn Python, a tuple is actually created by the comma symbol, not by the parentheses. Unfortunately, one can actually create a tuple by misplacing a trailing comma, which can lead to potential weird bugs in your code. You should always use parentheses explicitly for creating a tuple.\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
COMPASS = \(dqnorth\(dq, \(dqsouth\(dq, \(dqeast\(dq, \(dqwest\(dq,  # [trailing\-comma\-tuple]

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCorrect code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
COMPASS = (\(dqnorth\(dq, \(dqsouth\(dq, \(dqeast\(dq, \(dqwest\(dq)

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
