.SS useless\-return / R1711
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fBUseless return at end of function or method\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIEmitted when a single \(dqreturn\(dq or \(dqreturn None\(dq statement is found at the end of function or method definition. This statement can safely be removed because Python will implicitly return None\fP
.sp
\fBProblematic code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import sys


def print_python_version():  # [useless\-return]
    print(sys.version)
    return None

.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBCorrect code:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
