Created by the main \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:blob/\:main/\:build/\:lib/\:pylint/\:lint/\:pylinter\:.py> checker.
.SS c\-extension\-no\-member / I1101
.sp
\fBMessage emitted:\fP
.sp
\fB%s %r has no %r member%s, but source is unavailable. Consider adding this module to extension\-pkg\-allow\-list if you want to perform analysis based on run\-time introspection of living objects.\fP
.sp
\fBDescription:\fP
.sp
\fIUsed when a variable is accessed for non\-existent member of C extension. Due to unavailability of source static analysis is impossible, but it may be performed by introspecting living objects in run\-time.\fP
.sp
\fBCaution:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
By default, this message will not fail the execution (pylint will return 0).
To make pylint fail for this message use the \fB\-\-fail\-on=I1101\fP option
or \fB\-\-fail\-on=I\fP to fail on all enabled informational messages.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBAdditional details:\fP
.sp
\fBc\-extension\-no\-member\fP is an informational variant of \fBno\-member\fP to encourage
allowing introspection of C extensions as described in the
page \%<https://\:pylint\:.readthedocs\:.io/\:en/\:latest/\:user_guide/\:messages/\:error/\:no-member\:.html>
for \fBno\-member\fP\&.
.sp
Created by the typecheck \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:blob/\:main/\:build/\:lib/\:pylint/\:checkers/\:typecheck\:.py> checker.
.SS deprecated\-pragma / I0022
.sp
