.SS Lambda\-Expressions checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBlambda\-expressions\fP\&.
.SS Lambda\-Expressions checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B unnecessary\-lambda\-assignment (C3001)
\fILambda expression assigned to a variable. Define a function using the \(dqdef\(dq keyword instead.\fP
Used when a lambda expression is assigned to variable rather than defining a
standard function with the \(dqdef\(dq keyword.
.TP
.B unnecessary\-direct\-lambda\-call (C3002)
\fILambda expression called directly. Execute the expression inline instead.\fP
Used when a lambda expression is directly called rather than executing its
contents inline.
.UNINDENT
.SS Logging checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBlogging\fP\&.
.sp
See also logging checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:logging-options>
.SS Logging checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B logging\-unsupported\-format (E1200)
\fIUnsupported logging format character %r (%#02x) at index %d\fP
Used when an unsupported format character is used in a logging statement
format string.
.TP
.B logging\-format\-truncated (E1201)
\fILogging format string ends in middle of conversion specifier\fP
Used when a logging statement format string terminates before the end of a
conversion specifier.
.TP
.B logging\-too\-many\-args (E1205)
\fIToo many arguments for logging format string\fP
Used when a logging format string is given too many arguments.
.TP
.B logging\-too\-few\-args (E1206)
\fINot enough arguments for logging format string\fP
Used when a logging format string is given too few arguments.
.TP
.B logging\-not\-lazy (W1201)
\fIUse %s formatting in logging functions\fP
Used when a logging statement has a call form of \(dqlogging.<logging
method>(format_string % (format_args...))\(dq. Use another type of string
formatting instead. You can use % formatting but leave interpolation to the
logging function by passing the parameters as arguments. If logging\-fstring\-
interpolation is disabled then you can use fstring formatting. If logging\-
format\-interpolation is disabled then you can use str.format.
.TP
.B logging\-format\-interpolation (W1202)
\fIUse %s formatting in logging functions\fP
Used when a logging statement has a call form of \(dqlogging.<logging
method>(format_string.format(format_args...))\(dq. Use another type of string
formatting instead. You can use % formatting but leave interpolation to the
logging function by passing the parameters as arguments. If logging\-fstring\-
interpolation is disabled then you can use fstring formatting. If logging\-
not\-lazy is disabled then you can use % formatting as normal.
.TP
.B logging\-fstring\-interpolation (W1203)
\fIUse %s formatting in logging functions\fP
Used when a logging statement has a call form of \(dqlogging.<logging
method>(f\(dq...\(dq)\(dq.Use another type of string formatting instead. You can use %
formatting but leave interpolation to the logging function by passing the
parameters as arguments. If logging\-format\-interpolation is disabled then you
can use str.format. If logging\-not\-lazy is disabled then you can use %
formatting as normal.
.UNINDENT
.SS Match Statements checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBmatch_statements\fP\&.
.SS Match Statements checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B bare\-name\-capture\-pattern (E1901)
\fIThe name capture \(gacase %s\(ga makes the remaining patterns unreachable. Use a dotted name (for example an enum) to fix this.\fP
Emitted when a name capture pattern is used in a match statement and there
are case statements below it.
.TP
.B invalid\-match\-args\-definition (E1902)
\fI\(ga__match_args__\(ga must be a tuple of strings.\fP
Emitted if \fI__match_args__\fP isn\(aqt a tuple of strings required for match.
.TP
.B too\-many\-positional\-sub\-patterns (E1903)
\fI%s expects %d positional sub\-patterns (given %d)\fP
Emitted when the number of allowed positional sub\-patterns exceeds the number
of allowed sub\-patterns specified in \fI__match_args__\fP\&.
.TP
.B multiple\-class\-sub\-patterns (E1904)
\fIMultiple sub\-patterns for attribute %s\fP
Emitted when there is more than one sub\-pattern for a specific attribute in a
class pattern.
.TP
.B match\-class\-bind\-self (R1905)
\fIUse \(aq%s() as %s\(aq instead\fP
Match class patterns are faster if the name binding happens for the whole
pattern and any lookup for \fI__match_args__\fP can be avoided.
.TP
.B match\-class\-positional\-attributes (R1906)
\fIUse keyword attributes instead of positional ones (%s)\fP
Keyword attributes are more explicit and slightly faster since CPython can
skip the \fI__match_args__\fP lookup.
.UNINDENT
.SS Method Args checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBmethod_args\fP\&.
.sp
See also method_args checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:method-args-options>
.SS Method Args checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B positional\-only\-arguments\-expected (E3102)
\fI\(ga%s()\(ga got some positional\-only arguments passed as keyword arguments: %s\fP
Emitted when positional\-only arguments have been passed as keyword arguments.
Remove the keywords for the affected arguments in the function call.
.TP
.B missing\-timeout (W3101)
\fIMissing timeout argument for method \(aq%s\(aq can cause your program to hang indefinitely\fP
Used when a method needs a \(aqtimeout\(aq parameter in order to avoid waiting for
a long time. If no timeout is specified explicitly the default value is used.
For example for \(aqrequests\(aq the program will never time out (i.e. hang
indefinitely).
.UNINDENT
