.SS Miscellaneous checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B fixme (W0511)
Used when a warning note as FIXME or XXX is detected.
.TP
.B use\-symbolic\-message\-instead (I0023)
Used when a message is enabled or disabled by id.
.UNINDENT
.SS Modified Iteration checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBmodified_iteration\fP\&.
.SS Modified Iteration checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B modified\-iterating\-dict (E4702)
\fIIterated dict \(aq%s\(aq is being modified inside for loop body, iterate through a copy of it instead.\fP
Emitted when items are added or removed to a dict being iterated through.
Doing so raises a RuntimeError.
.TP
.B modified\-iterating\-set (E4703)
\fIIterated set \(aq%s\(aq is being modified inside for loop body, iterate through a copy of it instead.\fP
Emitted when items are added or removed to a set being iterated through.
Doing so raises a RuntimeError.
.TP
.B modified\-iterating\-list (W4701)
\fIIterated list \(aq%s\(aq is being modified inside for loop body, consider iterating through a copy of it instead.\fP
Emitted when items are added or removed to a list being iterated through.
Doing so can result in unexpected behaviour, that is why it is preferred to
use a copy of the list.
.UNINDENT
.SS Nested Min Max checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBnested_min_max\fP\&.
.SS Nested Min Max checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B nested\-min\-max (W3301)
\fIDo not use nested call of \(aq%s\(aq; it\(aqs possible to do \(aq%s\(aq instead\fP
Nested calls \fBmin(1, min(2, 3))\fP can be rewritten as \fBmin(1, 2, 3)\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.SS Newstyle checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBnewstyle\fP\&.
.SS Newstyle checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B bad\-super\-call (E1003)
\fIBad first argument %r given to super()\fP
Used when another argument than the current class is given as first argument
of the super builtin.
.UNINDENT
.SS Nonascii\-Checker checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBnonascii\-checker\fP\&.
.SS Nonascii\-Checker checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B non\-ascii\-file\-name (W2402)
\fI%s name \(dq%s\(dq contains a non\-ASCII character.\fP
Under python 3.5, PEP 3131 allows non\-ascii identifiers, but not non\-ascii
file names.Since Python 3.5, even though Python supports UTF\-8 files, some
editors or tools don\(aqt.
.TP
.B non\-ascii\-name (C2401)
\fI%s name \(dq%s\(dq contains a non\-ASCII character, consider renaming it.\fP
Used when the name contains at least one non\-ASCII unicode character. See
\%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0672/#\:confusing-features> for a background why
this could be bad. If your programming guideline defines that you are
programming in English, then there should be no need for non ASCII characters
in Python Names. If not you can simply disable this check.
.TP
.B non\-ascii\-module\-import (C2403)
\fI%s name \(dq%s\(dq contains a non\-ASCII character, use an ASCII\-only alias for import.\fP
Used when the name contains at least one non\-ASCII unicode character. See
\%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0672/#\:confusing-features> for a background why
this could be bad. If your programming guideline defines that you are
programming in English, then there should be no need for non ASCII characters
in Python Names. If not you can simply disable this check.
.UNINDENT
.SS Refactoring checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBrefactoring\fP\&.
.sp
See also refactoring checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:refactoring-options>
.SS Refactoring checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B consider\-merging\-isinstance (R1701)
\fIConsider merging these isinstance calls to isinstance(%s, (%s))\fP
Used when multiple consecutive isinstance calls can be merged into one.
.TP
.B too\-many\-nested\-blocks (R1702)
\fIToo many nested blocks (%s/%s)\fP
Used when a function or a method has too many nested blocks. This makes the
code less understandable and maintainable.
.TP
.B simplifiable\-if\-statement (R1703)
\fIThe if statement can be replaced with %s\fP
Used when an if statement can be replaced with \(aqbool(test)\(aq.
.TP
.B redefined\-argument\-from\-local (R1704)
\fIRedefining argument with the local name %r\fP
Used when a local name is redefining an argument, which might suggest a
potential error. This is taken in account only for a handful of name binding
operations, such as for iteration, with statement assignment and exception
handler assignment.
.TP
.B no\-else\-return (R1705)
\fIUnnecessary \(dq%s\(dq after \(dqreturn\(dq, %s\fP
Used in order to highlight an unnecessary block of code following an if, or a
try/except containing a return statement. As such, it will warn when it
encounters an else following a chain of ifs, all of them containing a return
statement.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-ternary (R1706)
\fIConsider using ternary (%s)\fP
Used when one of known pre\-python 2.5 ternary syntax is used.
.TP
.B trailing\-comma\-tuple (R1707)
\fIDisallow trailing comma tuple\fP
In Python, a tuple is actually created by the comma symbol, not by the
parentheses. Unfortunately, one can actually create a tuple by misplacing a
trailing comma, which can lead to potential weird bugs in your code. You
should always use parentheses explicitly for creating a tuple.
.TP
.B stop\-iteration\-return (R1708)
\fIDo not raise StopIteration in generator, use return statement instead\fP
According to PEP479, the raise of StopIteration to end the loop of a
generator may lead to hard to find bugs. This PEP specify that raise
StopIteration has to be replaced by a simple return statement
.TP
.B simplify\-boolean\-expression (R1709)
\fIBoolean expression may be simplified to %s\fP
Emitted when redundant pre\-python 2.5 ternary syntax is used.
.TP
.B inconsistent\-return\-statements (R1710)
\fIEither all return statements in a function should return an expression, or none of them should.\fP
According to PEP8, if any return statement returns an expression, any return
statements where no value is returned should explicitly state this as return
None, and an explicit return statement should be present at the end of the
function (if reachable)
.TP
.B useless\-return (R1711)
\fIUseless return at end of function or method\fP
Emitted when a single \(dqreturn\(dq or \(dqreturn None\(dq statement is found at the end
of function or method definition. This statement can safely be removed
because Python will implicitly return None
.TP
.B consider\-swap\-variables (R1712)
\fIConsider using tuple unpacking for swapping variables\fP
You do not have to use a temporary variable in order to swap variables. Using
\(dqtuple unpacking\(dq to directly swap variables makes the intention more clear.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-join (R1713)
\fIConsider using str.join(sequence) for concatenating strings from an iterable\fP
Using str.join(sequence) is faster, uses less memory and increases
readability compared to for\-loop iteration.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-in (R1714)
\fIConsider merging these comparisons with \(aqin\(aq by using \(aq%s %sin (%s)\(aq. Use a set instead if elements are hashable.\fP
To check if a variable is equal to one of many values, combine the values
into a set or tuple and check if the variable is contained \(dqin\(dq it instead of
checking for equality against each of the values. This is faster and less
verbose.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-get (R1715)
\fIConsider using dict.get for getting values from a dict if a key is present or a default if not\fP
Using the builtin dict.get for getting a value from a dictionary if a key is
present or a default if not, is simpler and considered more idiomatic,
although sometimes a bit slower
.TP
.B chained\-comparison (R1716)
\fISimplify chained comparison between the operands\fP
This message is emitted when pylint encounters boolean operation like \(dqa < b
and b < c\(dq, suggesting instead to refactor it to \(dqa < b < c\(dq
.TP
.B consider\-using\-dict\-comprehension (R1717)
\fIConsider using a dictionary comprehension\fP
Emitted when we detect the creation of a dictionary using the dict() callable
and a transient list. Although there is nothing syntactically wrong with this
code, it is hard to read and can be simplified to a dict comprehension. Also
it is faster since you don\(aqt need to create another transient list
.TP
.B consider\-using\-set\-comprehension (R1718)
\fIConsider using a set comprehension\fP
Although there is nothing syntactically wrong with this code, it is hard to
read and can be simplified to a set comprehension. Also it is faster since
you don\(aqt need to create another transient list
.TP
.B simplifiable\-if\-expression (R1719)
\fIThe if expression can be replaced with %s\fP
Used when an if expression can be replaced with \(aqbool(test)\(aq or simply \(aqtest\(aq
if the boolean cast is implicit.
.TP
.B no\-else\-raise (R1720)
\fIUnnecessary \(dq%s\(dq after \(dqraise\(dq, %s\fP
Used in order to highlight an unnecessary block of code following an if, or a
try/except containing a raise statement. As such, it will warn when it
encounters an else following a chain of ifs, all of them containing a raise
statement.
.TP
.B unnecessary\-comprehension (R1721)
\fIUnnecessary use of a comprehension, use %s instead.\fP
Instead of using an identity comprehension, consider using the list, dict or
set constructor. It is faster and simpler.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-sys\-exit (R1722)
\fIConsider using \(aqsys.exit\(aq instead\fP
Contrary to \(aqexit()\(aq or \(aqquit()\(aq, \(aqsys.exit\(aq does not rely on the site module
being available (as the \(aqsys\(aq module is always available).
.TP
.B no\-else\-break (R1723)
\fIUnnecessary \(dq%s\(dq after \(dqbreak\(dq, %s\fP
Used in order to highlight an unnecessary block of code following an if
containing a break statement. As such, it will warn when it encounters an
else following a chain of ifs, all of them containing a break statement.
.TP
.B no\-else\-continue (R1724)
\fIUnnecessary \(dq%s\(dq after \(dqcontinue\(dq, %s\fP
Used in order to highlight an unnecessary block of code following an if
containing a continue statement. As such, it will warn when it encounters an
else following a chain of ifs, all of them containing a continue statement.
.TP
.B super\-with\-arguments (R1725)
\fIConsider using Python 3 style super() without arguments\fP
Emitted when calling the super() builtin with the current class and instance.
On Python 3 these arguments are the default and they can be omitted.
.TP
.B simplifiable\-condition (R1726)
\fIBoolean condition \(dq%s\(dq may be simplified to \(dq%s\(dq\fP
Emitted when a boolean condition is able to be simplified.
.TP
.B condition\-evals\-to\-constant (R1727)
\fIBoolean condition \(aq%s\(aq will always evaluate to \(aq%s\(aq\fP
Emitted when a boolean condition can be simplified to a constant value.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-generator (R1728)
\fIConsider using a generator instead \(aq%s(%s)\(aq\fP
If your container can be large using a generator will bring better
performance.
.TP
.B use\-a\-generator (R1729)
\fIUse a generator instead \(aq%s(%s)\(aq\fP
Comprehension inside of \(aqany\(aq, \(aqall\(aq, \(aqmax\(aq, \(aqmin\(aq or \(aqsum\(aq is unnecessary. A
generator would be sufficient and faster.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-min\-builtin (R1730)
\fIConsider using \(aq%s\(aq instead of unnecessary if block\fP
Using the min builtin instead of a conditional improves readability and
conciseness.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-max\-builtin (R1731)
\fIConsider using \(aq%s\(aq instead of unnecessary if block\fP
Using the max builtin instead of a conditional improves readability and
conciseness.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-with (R1732)
\fIConsider using \(aqwith\(aq for resource\-allocating operations\fP
Emitted if a resource\-allocating assignment or call may be replaced by a
\(aqwith\(aq block. By using \(aqwith\(aq the release of the allocated resources is
ensured even in the case of an exception.
.TP
.B unnecessary\-dict\-index\-lookup (R1733)
\fIUnnecessary dictionary index lookup, use \(aq%s\(aq instead\fP
Emitted when iterating over the dictionary items (key\-item pairs) and
accessing the value by index lookup. The value can be accessed directly
instead.
.TP
.B use\-list\-literal (R1734)
\fIConsider using [] instead of list()\fP
Emitted when using list() to create an empty list instead of the literal [].
The literal is faster as it avoids an additional function call.
.TP
.B use\-dict\-literal (R1735)
\fIConsider using \(aq%s\(aq instead of a call to \(aqdict\(aq.\fP
Emitted when using dict() to create a dictionary instead of a literal \(aq{ ...
}\(aq. The literal is faster as it avoids an additional function call.
.TP
.B unnecessary\-list\-index\-lookup (R1736)
\fIUnnecessary list index lookup, use \(aq%s\(aq instead\fP
Emitted when iterating over an enumeration and accessing the value by index
lookup. The value can be accessed directly instead.
.TP
.B use\-yield\-from (R1737)
\fIUse \(aqyield from\(aq directly instead of yielding each element one by one\fP
Yielding directly from the iterator is faster and arguably cleaner code than
yielding each element one by one in the loop.
.TP
.B unnecessary\-negation (C0117)
\fIConsider changing \(dq%s\(dq to \(dq%s\(dq\fP
Used when a boolean expression contains an unneeded negation, e.g. when two
negation operators cancel each other out.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-enumerate (C0200)
\fIConsider using enumerate instead of iterating with range and len\fP
Emitted when code that iterates with range and len is encountered. Such code
can be simplified by using the enumerate builtin.
.TP
.B consider\-iterating\-dictionary (C0201)
\fIConsider iterating the dictionary directly instead of calling .keys()\fP
Emitted when the keys of a dictionary are iterated through the \fB\&.keys()\fP
method or when \fB\&.keys()\fP is used for a membership check. It is enough to
iterate through the dictionary itself, \fBfor key in dictionary\fP\&. For
membership checks, \fBif key in dictionary\fP is faster.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-dict\-items (C0206)
\fIConsider iterating with .items()\fP
Emitted when iterating over the keys of a dictionary and accessing the value
by index lookup. Both the key and value can be accessed by iterating using
the .items() method of the dictionary instead.
.TP
.B use\-maxsplit\-arg (C0207)
\fIUse %s instead\fP
Emitted when accessing only the first or last element of str.split(). The
first and last element can be accessed by using str.split(sep, maxsplit=1)[0]
or str.rsplit(sep, maxsplit=1)[\-1] instead.
.TP
.B use\-sequence\-for\-iteration (C0208)
\fIUse a sequence type when iterating over values\fP
When iterating over values, sequence types (e.g., \fBlists\fP, \fBtuples\fP,
\fBranges\fP) are more efficient than \fBsets\fP\&.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-f\-string (C0209)
\fIFormatting a regular string which could be an f\-string\fP
Used when we detect a string that is being formatted with format() or % which
could potentially be an f\-string. The use of f\-strings is preferred. Requires
Python 3.6 and \fBpy\-version >= 3.6\fP\&.
.TP
.B use\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-len (C1802)
\fIDo not use \(galen(SEQUENCE)\(ga without comparison to determine if a sequence is empty\fP
Empty sequences are considered false in a boolean context. You can either
remove the call to \(aqlen\(aq (\fBif not x\fP) or compare the length against a
scalar (\fBif len(x) > 1\fP).
.TP
.B use\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-comparison (C1803)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq can be simplified to \(dq%s\(dq, if it is strictly a sequence, as an empty %s is falsey\fP
Empty sequences are considered false in a boolean context. Following this
check blindly in weakly typed code base can create hard to debug issues. If
the value can be something else that is falsey but not a sequence (for
example \fBNone\fP, an empty string, or \fB0\fP) the code will not be equivalent.
.TP
.B use\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-comparison\-to\-string (C1804)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq can be simplified to \(dq%s\(dq, if it is strictly a string, as an empty string is falsey\fP
Empty string are considered false in a boolean context. Following this check
blindly in weakly typed code base can create hard to debug issues. If the
value can be something else that is falsey but not a string (for example
\fBNone\fP, an empty sequence, or \fB0\fP) the code will not be equivalent.
.TP
.B use\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-comparison\-to\-zero (C1805)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq can be simplified to \(dq%s\(dq, if it is strictly an int, as 0 is falsey\fP
0 is considered false in a boolean context. Following this check blindly in
weakly typed code base can create hard to debug issues. If the value can be
something else that is falsey but not an int (for example \fBNone\fP, an empty
string, or an empty sequence) the code will not be equivalent.
.UNINDENT
.SS Similarities checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBsimilarities\fP\&.
.sp
See also similarities checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:similarities-options>
.SS Similarities checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B duplicate\-code (R0801)
\fISimilar lines in %s files\fP
Indicates that a set of similar lines has been detected among multiple file.
This usually means that the code should be refactored to avoid this
duplication.
.UNINDENT
.SS Similarities checker Reports
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B RP0801
Duplication
.UNINDENT
.SS Spelling checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBspelling\fP\&.
.sp
See also spelling checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:spelling-options>
.SS Spelling checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B wrong\-spelling\-in\-comment (C0401)
\fIWrong spelling of a word \(aq%s\(aq in a comment:\fP
Used when a word in comment is not spelled correctly.
.TP
.B wrong\-spelling\-in\-docstring (C0402)
\fIWrong spelling of a word \(aq%s\(aq in a docstring:\fP
Used when a word in docstring is not spelled correctly.
.TP
.B invalid\-characters\-in\-docstring (C0403)
\fIInvalid characters %r in a docstring\fP
Used when a word in docstring cannot be checked by enchant.
.UNINDENT
.SS Stdlib checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBstdlib\fP\&.
.SS Stdlib checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B invalid\-envvar\-value (E1507)
\fI%s does not support %s type argument\fP
Env manipulation functions support only string type arguments. See
\%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:os\:.html#\:os\:.getenv>\&.
.TP
.B singledispatch\-method (E1519)
\fIsingledispatch decorator should not be used with methods, use singledispatchmethod instead.\fP
singledispatch should decorate functions and not class/instance methods. Use
singledispatchmethod for those cases.
.TP
.B singledispatchmethod\-function (E1520)
\fIsingledispatchmethod decorator should not be used with functions, use singledispatch instead.\fP
singledispatchmethod should decorate class/instance methods and not
functions. Use singledispatch for those cases.
.TP
.B bad\-open\-mode (W1501)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq is not a valid mode for open.\fP
Python supports: r, w, a[, x] modes with b, +, and U (only with r) options.
See \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:functions\:.html#\:open>
.TP
.B boolean\-datetime (W1502)
\fIUsing datetime.time in a boolean context.\fP
Using datetime.time in a boolean context can hide subtle bugs when the time
they represent matches midnight UTC. This behaviour was fixed in Python 3.5.
See \%<https://\:bugs\:.python\:.org/\:issue13936> for reference. This message can\(aqt be
emitted when using Python >= 3.5.
.TP
.B redundant\-unittest\-assert (W1503)
\fIRedundant use of %s with constant value %r\fP
The first argument of assertTrue and assertFalse is a condition. If a
constant is passed as parameter, that condition will be always true. In this
case a warning should be emitted.
.TP
.B bad\-thread\-instantiation (W1506)
\fIthreading.Thread needs the target function\fP
The warning is emitted when a threading.Thread class is instantiated without
the target function being passed as a kwarg or as a second argument. By
default, the first parameter is the group param, not the target param.
.TP
.B shallow\-copy\-environ (W1507)
\fIUsing copy.copy(os.environ). Use os.environ.copy() instead.\fP
os.environ is not a dict object but proxy object, so shallow copy has still
effects on original object. See \%<https://\:bugs\:.python\:.org/\:issue15373> for
reference.
.TP
.B invalid\-envvar\-default (W1508)
\fI%s default type is %s. Expected str or None.\fP
Env manipulation functions return None or str values. Supplying anything
different as a default may cause bugs. See
\%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:os\:.html#\:os\:.getenv>\&.
.TP
.B subprocess\-popen\-preexec\-fn (W1509)
\fIUsing preexec_fn keyword which may be unsafe in the presence of threads\fP
The preexec_fn parameter is not safe to use in the presence of threads in
your application. The child process could deadlock before exec is called. If
you must use it, keep it trivial! Minimize the number of libraries you call
into. See \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:subprocess\:.html#\:popen-constructor>
.TP
.B subprocess\-run\-check (W1510)
\fI\(aqsubprocess.run\(aq used without explicitly defining the value for \(aqcheck\(aq.\fP
The \fBcheck\fP keyword is set to False by default. It means the process
launched by \fBsubprocess.run\fP can exit with a non\-zero exit code and fail
silently. It\(aqs better to set it explicitly to make clear what the error\-
handling behavior is.
.TP
.B unspecified\-encoding (W1514)
\fIUsing open without explicitly specifying an encoding\fP
It is better to specify an encoding when opening documents. Using the system
default implicitly can create problems on other operating systems. See
\%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0597> This message can\(aqt be emitted when using
Python >= 3.15.
.TP
.B forgotten\-debug\-statement (W1515)
\fILeaving functions creating breakpoints in production code is not recommended\fP
Calls to breakpoint(), sys.breakpointhook() and pdb.set_trace() should be
removed from code that is not actively being debugged.
.TP
.B method\-cache\-max\-size\-none (W1518)
\fI\(aqlru_cache(maxsize=None)\(aq or \(aqcache\(aq will keep all method args alive indefinitely, including \(aqself\(aq\fP
By decorating a method with lru_cache or cache the \(aqself\(aq argument will be
linked to the function and therefore never garbage collected. Unless your
instance will never need to be garbage collected (singleton) it is
recommended to refactor code to avoid this pattern or add a maxsize to the
cache. The default value for maxsize is 128.
.TP
.B deprecated\-method (W4902)
\fIUsing deprecated method %s()\fP
The method is marked as deprecated and will be removed in the future.
.TP
.B deprecated\-argument (W4903)
\fIUsing deprecated argument %s of method %s()\fP
The argument is marked as deprecated and will be removed in the future.
.TP
.B deprecated\-class (W4904)
\fIUsing deprecated class %s of module %s\fP
The class is marked as deprecated and will be removed in the future.
.TP
.B deprecated\-decorator (W4905)
\fIUsing deprecated decorator %s()\fP
The decorator is marked as deprecated and will be removed in the future.
.TP
.B deprecated\-attribute (W4906)
\fIUsing deprecated attribute %r\fP
The attribute is marked as deprecated and will be removed in the future.
.UNINDENT
.SS String checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBstring\fP\&.
.sp
See also string checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:string-options>
.SS String checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B bad\-format\-character (E1300)
\fIUnsupported format character %r (%#02x) at index %d\fP
Used when an unsupported format character is used in a format string.
.TP
.B truncated\-format\-string (E1301)
\fIFormat string ends in middle of conversion specifier\fP
Used when a format string terminates before the end of a conversion
specifier.
.TP
.B mixed\-format\-string (E1302)
\fIMixing named and unnamed conversion specifiers in format string\fP
Used when a format string contains both named (e.g. \(aq%(foo)d\(aq) and unnamed
(e.g. \(aq%d\(aq) conversion specifiers. This is also used when a named conversion
specifier contains * for the minimum field width and/or precision.
.TP
.B format\-needs\-mapping (E1303)
\fIExpected mapping for format string, not %s\fP
Used when a format string that uses named conversion specifiers is used with
an argument that is not a mapping.
.TP
.B missing\-format\-string\-key (E1304)
\fIMissing key %r in format string dictionary\fP
Used when a format string that uses named conversion specifiers is used with
a dictionary that doesn\(aqt contain all the keys required by the format string.
.TP
.B too\-many\-format\-args (E1305)
\fIToo many arguments for format string\fP
Used when a format string that uses unnamed conversion specifiers is given
too many arguments.
.TP
.B too\-few\-format\-args (E1306)
\fINot enough arguments for format string\fP
Used when a format string that uses unnamed conversion specifiers is given
too few arguments
.TP
.B bad\-string\-format\-type (E1307)
\fIArgument %r does not match format type %r\fP
Used when a type required by format string is not suitable for actual
argument type
.TP
.B bad\-str\-strip\-call (E1310)
\fISuspicious argument in %s.%s call\fP
The argument to a str.{l,r,}strip call contains a duplicate character,
.TP
.B bad\-format\-string\-key (W1300)
\fIFormat string dictionary key should be a string, not %s\fP
Used when a format string that uses named conversion specifiers is used with
a dictionary whose keys are not all strings.
.TP
.B unused\-format\-string\-key (W1301)
\fIUnused key %r in format string dictionary\fP
Used when a format string that uses named conversion specifiers is used with
a dictionary that contains keys not required by the format string.
.TP
.B bad\-format\-string (W1302)
\fIInvalid format string\fP
Used when a PEP 3101 format string is invalid.
.TP
.B missing\-format\-argument\-key (W1303)
\fIMissing keyword argument %r for format string\fP
Used when a PEP 3101 format string that uses named fields doesn\(aqt receive one
or more required keywords.
.TP
.B unused\-format\-string\-argument (W1304)
\fIUnused format argument %r\fP
Used when a PEP 3101 format string that uses named fields is used with an
argument that is not required by the format string.
.TP
.B format\-combined\-specification (W1305)
\fIFormat string contains both automatic field numbering and manual field specification\fP
Used when a PEP 3101 format string contains both automatic field numbering
(e.g. \(aq{}\(aq) and manual field specification (e.g. \(aq{0}\(aq).
.TP
.B missing\-format\-attribute (W1306)
\fIMissing format attribute %r in format specifier %r\fP
Used when a PEP 3101 format string uses an attribute specifier ({0.length}),
but the argument passed for formatting doesn\(aqt have that attribute.
.TP
.B invalid\-format\-index (W1307)
\fIUsing invalid lookup key %r in format specifier %r\fP
Used when a PEP 3101 format string uses a lookup specifier ({a[1]}), but the
argument passed for formatting doesn\(aqt contain or doesn\(aqt have that key as an
attribute.
.TP
.B duplicate\-string\-formatting\-argument (W1308)
\fIDuplicate string formatting argument %r, consider passing as named argument\fP
Used when we detect that a string formatting is repeating an argument instead
of using named string arguments
.TP
.B f\-string\-without\-interpolation (W1309)
\fIUsing an f\-string that does not have any interpolated variables\fP
Used when we detect an f\-string that does not use any interpolation
variables, in which case it can be either a normal string or a bug in the
code.
.TP
.B format\-string\-without\-interpolation (W1310)
\fIUsing formatting for a string that does not have any interpolated variables\fP
Used when we detect a string that does not have any interpolation variables,
in which case it can be either a normal string without formatting or a bug in
the code.
.TP
.B anomalous\-backslash\-in\-string (W1401)
\fIAnomalous backslash in string: \(aq%s\(aq. String constant might be missing an r prefix.\fP
Used when a backslash is in a literal string but not as an escape.
.TP
.B anomalous\-unicode\-escape\-in\-string (W1402)
\fIAnomalous Unicode escape in byte string: \(aq%s\(aq. String constant might be missing an r or u prefix.\fP
Used when an escape like u is encountered in a byte string where it has no
effect.
.TP
.B implicit\-str\-concat (W1404)
\fIImplicit string concatenation found in %s\fP
String literals are implicitly concatenated in a literal iterable definition
: maybe a comma is missing ?
.TP
.B inconsistent\-quotes (W1405)
\fIQuote delimiter %s is inconsistent with the rest of the file\fP
Quote delimiters are not used consistently throughout a module (with
allowances made for avoiding unnecessary escaping).
.TP
.B redundant\-u\-string\-prefix (W1406)
\fIThe u prefix for strings is no longer necessary in Python >=3.0\fP
Used when we detect a string with a u prefix. These prefixes were necessary
in Python 2 to indicate a string was Unicode, but since Python 3.0 strings
are Unicode by default.
.UNINDENT
.SS Threading checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBthreading\fP\&.
.SS Threading checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B useless\-with\-lock (W2101)
\fI\(aq%s()\(aq directly created in \(aqwith\(aq has no effect\fP
Used when a new lock instance is created by using with statement which has no
effect. Instead, an existing instance should be used to acquire lock.
.UNINDENT
.SS Typecheck checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBtypecheck\fP\&.
.sp
See also typecheck checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:typecheck-options>
.SS Typecheck checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B no\-member (E1101)
\fI%s %r has no %r member%s\fP
Used when a variable is accessed for a nonexistent member.
.TP
.B not\-callable (E1102)
\fI%s is not callable\fP
Used when an object being called has been inferred to a non callable object.
.TP
.B assignment\-from\-no\-return (E1111)
\fIAssigning result of a function call, where the function has no return\fP
Used when an assignment is done on a function call but the inferred function
doesn\(aqt return anything.
.TP
.B no\-value\-for\-parameter (E1120)
\fINo value for argument %s in %s call\fP
Used when a function call passes too few arguments.
.TP
.B too\-many\-function\-args (E1121)
\fIToo many positional arguments for %s call\fP
Used when a function call passes too many positional arguments.
.TP
.B unexpected\-keyword\-arg (E1123)
\fIUnexpected keyword argument %r in %s call\fP
Used when a function call passes a keyword argument that doesn\(aqt correspond
to one of the function\(aqs parameter names.
.TP
.B redundant\-keyword\-arg (E1124)
\fIArgument %r passed by position and keyword in %s call\fP
Used when a function call would result in assigning multiple values to a
function parameter, one value from a positional argument and one from a
keyword argument.
.TP
.B missing\-kwoa (E1125)
\fIMissing mandatory keyword argument %r in %s call\fP
Used when a function call does not pass a mandatory keyword\-only argument.
.TP
.B invalid\-sequence\-index (E1126)
\fISequence index is not an int, slice, or instance with __index__\fP
Used when a sequence type is indexed with an invalid type. Valid types are
ints, slices, and objects with an __index__ method.
.TP
.B invalid\-slice\-index (E1127)
\fISlice index is not an int, None, or instance with __index__\fP
Used when a slice index is not an integer, None, or an object with an
__index__ method.
.TP
.B assignment\-from\-none (E1128)
\fIAssigning result of a function call, where the function returns None\fP
Used when an assignment is done on a function call but the inferred function
returns nothing but None.
.TP
.B not\-context\-manager (E1129)
\fIContext manager \(aq%s\(aq doesn\(aqt implement __enter__ and __exit__.\fP
Used when an instance in a with statement doesn\(aqt implement the context
manager protocol(__enter__/__exit__).
.TP
.B invalid\-unary\-operand\-type (E1130)
Emitted when a unary operand is used on an object which does not support this
type of operation.
.TP
.B unsupported\-binary\-operation (E1131)
Emitted when a binary arithmetic operation between two operands is not
supported.
.TP
.B repeated\-keyword (E1132)
\fIGot multiple values for keyword argument %r in function call\fP
Emitted when a function call got multiple values for a keyword.
.TP
.B not\-an\-iterable (E1133)
\fINon\-iterable value %s is used in an iterating context\fP
Used when a non\-iterable value is used in place where iterable is expected
.TP
.B not\-a\-mapping (E1134)
\fINon\-mapping value %s is used in a mapping context\fP
Used when a non\-mapping value is used in place where mapping is expected
.TP
.B unsupported\-membership\-test (E1135)
\fIValue \(aq%s\(aq doesn\(aqt support membership test\fP
Emitted when an instance in membership test expression doesn\(aqt implement
membership protocol (__contains__/__iter__/__getitem__).
.TP
.B unsubscriptable\-object (E1136)
\fIValue \(aq%s\(aq is unsubscriptable\fP
Emitted when a subscripted value doesn\(aqt support subscription (i.e. doesn\(aqt
define __getitem__ method or __class_getitem__ for a class).
.TP
.B unsupported\-assignment\-operation (E1137)
\fI%r does not support item assignment\fP
Emitted when an object does not support item assignment (i.e. doesn\(aqt define
__setitem__ method).
.TP
.B unsupported\-delete\-operation (E1138)
\fI%r does not support item deletion\fP
Emitted when an object does not support item deletion (i.e. doesn\(aqt define
__delitem__ method).
.TP
.B invalid\-metaclass (E1139)
\fIInvalid metaclass %r used\fP
Emitted whenever we can detect that a class is using, as a metaclass,
something which might be invalid for using as a metaclass.
.TP
.B dict\-iter\-missing\-items (E1141)
\fIUnpacking a dictionary in iteration without calling .items()\fP
Emitted when trying to iterate through a dict without calling .items()
.TP
.B await\-outside\-async (E1142)
\fI\(aqawait\(aq should be used within an async function\fP
Emitted when await is used outside an async function.
.TP
.B unhashable\-member (E1143)
\fI\(aq%s\(aq is unhashable and can\(aqt be used as a %s in a %s\fP
Emitted when a dict key or set member is not hashable (i.e. doesn\(aqt define
__hash__ method).
.TP
.B invalid\-slice\-step (E1144)
\fISlice step cannot be 0\fP
Used when a slice step is 0 and the object doesn\(aqt implement a custom
__getitem__ method.
.TP
.B async\-context\-manager\-with\-regular\-with (E1145)
\fIContext manager \(aq%s\(aq is async and should be used with \(aqasync with\(aq.\fP
Used when an async context manager is used with a regular \(aqwith\(aq statement
instead of \(aqasync with\(aq.
.TP
.B keyword\-arg\-before\-vararg (W1113)
\fIKeyword argument before variable positional arguments list in the definition of %s function\fP
When defining a keyword argument before variable positional arguments, one
can end up in having multiple values passed for the aforementioned parameter
in case the method is called with keyword arguments.
.TP
.B arguments\-out\-of\-order (W1114)
\fIPositional arguments appear to be out of order\fP
Emitted when the caller\(aqs argument names fully match the parameter names in
the function signature but do not have the same order.
.TP
.B non\-str\-assignment\-to\-dunder\-name (W1115)
\fINon\-string value assigned to __name__\fP
Emitted when a non\-string value is assigned to __name__
.TP
.B isinstance\-second\-argument\-not\-valid\-type (W1116)
\fISecond argument of isinstance is not a type\fP
Emitted when the second argument of an isinstance call is not a type.
.TP
.B kwarg\-superseded\-by\-positional\-arg (W1117)
\fI%r will be included in %r since a positional\-only parameter with this name already exists\fP
Emitted when a function is called with a keyword argument that has the same
name as a positional\-only parameter and the function contains a keyword
variadic parameter dict.
.TP
.B c\-extension\-no\-member (I1101)
\fI%s %r has no %r member%s, but source is unavailable. Consider adding this module to extension\-pkg\-allow\-list if you want to perform analysis based on run\-time introspection of living objects.\fP
Used when a variable is accessed for non\-existent member of C extension. Due
to unavailability of source static analysis is impossible, but it may be
performed by introspecting living objects in run\-time.
.UNINDENT
.SS Unicode Checker checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBunicode_checker\fP\&.
.SS Unicode Checker checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B invalid\-unicode\-codec (E2501)
\fIUTF\-16 and UTF\-32 aren\(aqt backward compatible. Use UTF\-8 instead\fP
For compatibility use UTF\-8 instead of UTF\-16/UTF\-32. See also
\%<https://\:bugs\:.python\:.org/\:issue1503789> for a history of this issue. And
\%<https://\:softwareengineering\:.stackexchange\:.com/\:questions/\:102205> for some
possible problems when using UTF\-16 for instance.
.TP
.B bidirectional\-unicode (E2502)
\fIContains control characters that can permit obfuscated code executed differently than displayed\fP
bidirectional unicode are typically not displayed characters required to
display right\-to\-left (RTL) script (i.e. Chinese, Japanese, Arabic, Hebrew,
\&...) correctly. So can you trust this code? Are you sure it displayed
correctly in all editors? If you did not write it or your language is not
RTL, remove the special characters, as they could be used to trick you into
executing code, that does something else than what it looks like. More
Information: \%<https://\:en\:.wikipedia\:.org/\:wiki/\:Bidirectional_text>
\%<https://\:trojansource\:.codes>
.TP
.B invalid\-character\-backspace (E2510)
\fIInvalid unescaped character backspace, use \(dqb\(dq instead.\fP
Moves the cursor back, so the character after it will overwrite the character
before.
.TP
.B invalid\-character\-carriage\-return (E2511)
\fIInvalid unescaped character carriage\-return, use \(dqr\(dq instead.\fP
Moves the cursor to the start of line, subsequent characters overwrite the
start of the line.
.TP
.B invalid\-character\-sub (E2512)
\fIInvalid unescaped character sub, use \(dqx1A\(dq instead.\fP
Ctrl+Z \(dqEnd of text\(dq on Windows. Some programs (such as type) ignore the rest
of the file after it.
.TP
.B invalid\-character\-esc (E2513)
\fIInvalid unescaped character esc, use \(dqx1B\(dq instead.\fP
Commonly initiates escape codes which allow arbitrary control of the
terminal.
.TP
.B invalid\-character\-nul (E2514)
\fIInvalid unescaped character nul, use \(dq0\(dq instead.\fP
Mostly end of input for python.
.TP
.B invalid\-character\-zero\-width\-space (E2515)
\fIInvalid unescaped character zero\-width\-space, use \(dqu200B\(dq instead.\fP
Invisible space character could hide real code execution.
.TP
.B bad\-file\-encoding (C2503)
\fIPEP8 recommends UTF\-8 as encoding for Python files\fP
PEP8 recommends UTF\-8 default encoding for Python files. See
\%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0008/#\:source-file-encoding>
.UNINDENT
.SS Unnecessary\-Dunder\-Call checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBunnecessary\-dunder\-call\fP\&.
.SS Unnecessary\-Dunder\-Call checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B unnecessary\-dunder\-call (C2801)
\fIUnnecessarily calls dunder method %s. %s.\fP
Used when a dunder method is manually called instead of using the
corresponding function/method/operator.
.UNINDENT
.SS Unnecessary Ellipsis checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBunnecessary_ellipsis\fP\&.
.SS Unnecessary Ellipsis checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B unnecessary\-ellipsis (W2301)
\fIUnnecessary ellipsis constant\fP
Used when the ellipsis constant is encountered and can be avoided. A line of
code consisting of an ellipsis is unnecessary if there is a docstring on the
preceding line or if there is a statement in the same scope.
.UNINDENT
.SS Unsupported Version checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBunsupported_version\fP\&.
.SS Unsupported Version checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B using\-f\-string\-in\-unsupported\-version (W2601)
\fIF\-strings are not supported by all versions included in the py\-version setting\fP
Used when the py\-version set by the user is lower than 3.6 and pylint
encounters an f\-string.
.TP
.B using\-final\-decorator\-in\-unsupported\-version (W2602)
\fItyping.final is not supported by all versions included in the py\-version setting\fP
Used when the py\-version set by the user is lower than 3.8 and pylint
encounters a \fBtyping.final\fP decorator.
.TP
.B using\-exception\-groups\-in\-unsupported\-version (W2603)
\fIException groups are not supported by all versions included in the py\-version setting\fP
Used when the py\-version set by the user is lower than 3.11 and pylint
encounters \fBexcept*\fP or \fIExceptionGroup\(ga\fP\&.
.TP
.B using\-generic\-type\-syntax\-in\-unsupported\-version (W2604)
\fIGeneric type syntax (PEP 695) is not supported by all versions included in the py\-version setting\fP
Used when the py\-version set by the user is lower than 3.12 and pylint
encounters generic type syntax.
.TP
.B using\-assignment\-expression\-in\-unsupported\-version (W2605)
\fIAssignment expression is not supported by all versions included in the py\-version setting\fP
Used when the py\-version set by the user is lower than 3.8 and pylint
encounters an assignment expression (walrus) operator.
.TP
.B using\-positional\-only\-args\-in\-unsupported\-version (W2606)
\fIPositional\-only arguments are not supported by all versions included in the py\-version setting\fP
Used when the py\-version set by the user is lower than 3.8 and pylint
encounters positional\-only arguments.
.UNINDENT
.SS Variables checker
.sp
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBvariables\fP\&.
.sp
See also variables checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:variables-options>
.SS Variables checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B used\-before\-assignment (E0601)
\fIUsing variable %r before assignment\fP
Emitted when a local variable is accessed before its assignment took place.
Assignments in try blocks are assumed not to have occurred when evaluating
associated except/finally blocks. Assignments in except blocks are assumed
not to have occurred when evaluating statements outside the block, except
when the associated try block contains a return statement.
.TP
.B undefined\-variable (E0602)
\fIUndefined variable %r\fP
Used when an undefined variable is accessed.
.TP
.B undefined\-all\-variable (E0603)
\fIUndefined variable name %r in __all__\fP
Used when an undefined variable name is referenced in __all__.
.TP
.B invalid\-all\-object (E0604)
\fIInvalid object %r in __all__, must contain only strings\fP
Used when an invalid (non\-string) object occurs in __all__.
.TP
.B invalid\-all\-format (E0605)
\fIInvalid format for __all__, must be tuple or list\fP
Used when __all__ has an invalid format.
.TP
.B possibly\-used\-before\-assignment (E0606)
\fIPossibly using variable %r before assignment\fP
Emitted when a local variable is accessed before its assignment took place in
both branches of an if/else switch.
.TP
.B no\-name\-in\-module (E0611)
\fINo name %r in module %r\fP
Used when a name cannot be found in a module.
.TP
.B unpacking\-non\-sequence (E0633)
\fIAttempting to unpack a non\-sequence%s\fP
Used when something which is not a sequence is used in an unpack assignment
.TP
.B potential\-index\-error (E0643)
\fIInvalid index for iterable length\fP
Emitted when an index used on an iterable goes beyond the length of that
iterable.
.TP
.B global\-variable\-undefined (W0601)
\fIGlobal variable %r undefined at the module level\fP
Used when a variable is defined through the \(dqglobal\(dq statement but the
variable is not defined in the module scope.
.TP
.B global\-variable\-not\-assigned (W0602)
\fIUsing global for %r but no assignment is done\fP
When a variable defined in the global scope is modified in an inner scope,
the \(aqglobal\(aq keyword is required in the inner scope only if there is an
assignment operation done in the inner scope.
.TP
.B global\-statement (W0603)
\fIUsing the global statement\fP
Used when you use the \(dqglobal\(dq statement to update a global variable. Pylint
discourages its usage. That doesn\(aqt mean you cannot use it!
.TP
.B global\-at\-module\-level (W0604)
\fIUsing the global statement at the module level\fP
Used when you use the \(dqglobal\(dq statement at the module level since it has no
effect.
.TP
.B unused\-import (W0611)
\fIUnused %s\fP
Used when an imported module or variable is not used.
.TP
.B unused\-variable (W0612)
\fIUnused variable %r\fP
Used when a variable is defined but not used.
.TP
.B unused\-argument (W0613)
\fIUnused argument %r\fP
Used when a function or method argument is not used.
.TP
.B unused\-wildcard\-import (W0614)
\fIUnused import(s) %s from wildcard import of %s\fP
Used when an imported module or variable is not used from a \fI\(aqfrom X import
*\(aq\fP style import.
.TP
.B redefined\-outer\-name (W0621)
\fIRedefining name %r from outer scope (line %s)\fP
Used when a variable\(aqs name hides a name defined in an outer scope or except
handler.
.TP
.B redefined\-builtin (W0622)
\fIRedefining built\-in %r\fP
Used when a variable or function override a built\-in.
.TP
.B undefined\-loop\-variable (W0631)
\fIUsing possibly undefined loop variable %r\fP
Used when a loop variable (i.e. defined by a for loop or a list comprehension
or a generator expression) is used outside the loop.
.TP
.B unbalanced\-tuple\-unpacking (W0632)
\fIPossible unbalanced tuple unpacking with sequence %s: left side has %d label%s, right side has %d value%s\fP
Used when there is an unbalanced tuple unpacking in assignment
.TP
.B cell\-var\-from\-loop (W0640)
\fICell variable %s defined in loop\fP
A variable used in a closure is defined in a loop. This will result in all
closures using the same value for the closed\-over variable.
.TP
.B possibly\-unused\-variable (W0641)
\fIPossibly unused variable %r\fP
Used when a variable is defined but might not be used. The possibility comes
from the fact that locals() might be used, which could consume or not the
said variable
.TP
.B self\-cls\-assignment (W0642)
\fIInvalid assignment to %s in method\fP
Invalid assignment to self or cls in instance or class method respectively.
.TP
.B unbalanced\-dict\-unpacking (W0644)
\fIPossible unbalanced dict unpacking with %s: left side has %d label%s, right side has %d value%s\fP
Used when there is an unbalanced dict unpacking in assignment or for loop
.UNINDENT
.SS Optional checkers
.sp
Pylint provides the following optional plugins:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Deprecated Builtins checker
.IP \(bu 2
Broad Try Clause checker
.IP \(bu 2
Else If Used checker
.IP \(bu 2
Code Style checker
.IP \(bu 2
Comparison\-Placement checker
.IP \(bu 2
Confusing Elif checker
.IP \(bu 2
Consider Refactoring Into While checker
.IP \(bu 2
Consider Ternary Expression checker
.IP \(bu 2
Dict\-Init\-Mutate checker
.IP \(bu 2
Parameter Documentation checker
.IP \(bu 2
Docstyle checker
.IP \(bu 2
Dunder checker
.IP \(bu 2
Empty\-Comment checker
.IP \(bu 2
Eq\-Without\-Hash checker
.IP \(bu 2
Consider\-Using\-Any\-Or\-All checker
.IP \(bu 2
Magic\-Value checker
.IP \(bu 2
Design checker
.IP \(bu 2
No Self Use checker
.IP \(bu 2
Overlap\-Except checker
.IP \(bu 2
Import\-Private\-Name checker
.IP \(bu 2
Redefined\-Loop\-Name checker
.IP \(bu 2
Multiple Types checker
.IP \(bu 2
Set Membership checker
.IP \(bu 2
Typing checker
.IP \(bu 2
While Used checker
.UNINDENT
.sp
You can activate any or all of these extensions by adding a \fBload\-plugins\fP line to the \fBMAIN\fP section of your \fB\&.pylintrc\fP, for example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.docparams,pylint.extensions.docstyle
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Broad Try Clause checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.broad_try_clause\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBbroad_try_clause\fP\&.
.sp
See also broad_try_clause checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:broad-try-clause-options>
.SS Broad Try Clause checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B too\-many\-try\-statements (W0717)
Try clause contains too many statements.
.UNINDENT
.SS Code Style checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.code_style\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBcode_style\fP\&.
.SS Code Style checker Documentation
.sp
Checkers that can improve code consistency.
As such they don\(aqt necessarily provide a performance benefit and
are often times opinionated.
.sp
See also code_style checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:code-style-options>
.SS Code Style checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B consider\-using\-namedtuple\-or\-dataclass (R6101)
\fIConsider using namedtuple or dataclass for dictionary values\fP
Emitted when dictionary values can be replaced by namedtuples or dataclass
instances.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-tuple (R6102)
\fIConsider using an in\-place tuple instead of list\fP
Only for style consistency! Emitted where an in\-place defined \fBlist\fP can be
replaced by a \fBtuple\fP\&. Due to optimizations by CPython, there is no
performance benefit from it.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-assignment\-expr (R6103)
\fIUse \(aq%s\(aq instead\fP
Emitted when an if assignment is directly followed by an if statement and
both can be combined by using an assignment expression \fB:=\fP\&. Requires
Python 3.8 and \fBpy\-version >= 3.8\fP\&.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-augmented\-assign (R6104)
\fIUse \(aq%s\(aq to do an augmented assign directly\fP
Emitted when an assignment is referring to the object that it is assigning
to. This can be changed to be an augmented assign. Disabled by default!
.TP
.B prefer\-typing\-namedtuple (R6105)
\fIPrefer \(aqtyping.NamedTuple\(aq over \(aqcollections.namedtuple\(aq\fP
\(aqtyping.NamedTuple\(aq uses the well\-known \(aqclass\(aq keyword with type\-hints for
readability (it\(aqs also faster as it avoids an internal exec call). Disabled
by default!
.TP
.B consider\-math\-not\-float (R6106)
\fIConsider %smath.%s instead of %s\fP
Using math.inf or math.nan permits to benefit from typing and it is up to 4
times faster than a float call (after the initial import of math). This check
also catches typos in float calls as a side effect.
.UNINDENT
.SS Comparison\-Placement checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.comparison_placement\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBcomparison\-placement\fP\&.
.SS Comparison\-Placement checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B misplaced\-comparison\-constant (C2201)
\fIComparison should be %s\fP
Used when the constant is placed on the left side of a comparison. It is
usually clearer in intent to place it in the right hand side of the
comparison.
.UNINDENT
.SS Confusing Elif checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.confusing_elif\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBconfusing_elif\fP\&.
.SS Confusing Elif checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B confusing\-consecutive\-elif (R5601)
\fIConsecutive elif with differing indentation level, consider creating a function to separate the inner elif\fP
Used when an elif statement follows right after an indented block which
itself ends with if or elif. It may not be obvious if the elif statement was
willingly or mistakenly unindented. Extracting the indented if statement into
a separate function might avoid confusion and prevent errors.
.UNINDENT
.SS Consider\-Using\-Any\-Or\-All checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.for_any_all\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBconsider\-using\-any\-or\-all\fP\&.
.SS Consider\-Using\-Any\-Or\-All checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B consider\-using\-any\-or\-all (C0501)
\fI\(gafor\(ga loop could be \(ga%s\(ga\fP
A for loop that checks for a condition and return a bool can be replaced with
any or all.
.UNINDENT
.SS Consider Refactoring Into While checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.consider_refactoring_into_while_condition\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBconsider_refactoring_into_while\fP\&.
.SS Consider Refactoring Into While checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B consider\-refactoring\-into\-while\-condition (R3501)
\fIConsider using \(aqwhile %s\(aq instead of \(aqwhile %s:\(aq an \(aqif\(aq, and a \(aqbreak\(aq\fP
Emitted when \fIwhile True:\fP loop is used and the first statement is a break
condition. The \fBif / break\fP construct can be removed if the check is
inverted and moved to the \fBwhile\fP statement.
.UNINDENT
.SS Consider Ternary Expression checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.consider_ternary_expression\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBconsider_ternary_expression\fP\&.
.SS Consider Ternary Expression checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B consider\-ternary\-expression (W0160)
\fIConsider rewriting as a ternary expression\fP
Multiple assign statements spread across if/else blocks can be rewritten with
a single assignment and ternary expression
.UNINDENT
.SS Deprecated Builtins checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.bad_builtin\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBdeprecated_builtins\fP\&.
.SS Deprecated Builtins checker Documentation
.sp
This used to be the \fBbad\-builtin\fP core checker, but it was moved to
an extension instead. It can be used for finding prohibited used builtins,
such as \fBmap\fP or \fBfilter\fP, for which other alternatives exists.
.sp
If you want to control for what builtins the checker should warn about,
you can use the \fBbad\-functions\fP option:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ pylint a.py \-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.bad_builtin \-\-bad\-functions=apply,reduce
\&...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
See also deprecated_builtins checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:deprecated-builtins-options>
.SS Deprecated Builtins checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B bad\-builtin (W0141)
\fIUsed builtin function %s\fP
Used when a disallowed builtin function is used (see the bad\-function
option). Usual disallowed functions are the ones like map, or filter , where
Python offers now some cleaner alternative like list comprehension.
.UNINDENT
.SS Design checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.mccabe\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBdesign\fP\&.
.SS Design checker Documentation
.sp
You can now use this plugin for finding complexity issues in your code base.
.sp
Activate it through \fBpylint \-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.mccabe\fP\&. It introduces
a new warning, \fBtoo\-complex\fP, which is emitted when a code block has a complexity
higher than a preestablished value, which can be controlled through the
\fBmax\-complexity\fP option, such as in this example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ cat a.py
def f10():
    \(dq\(dq\(dqMcCabe rating: 11\(dq\(dq\(dq
    myint = 2
    if myint == 5:
        return myint
    elif myint == 6:
        return myint
    elif myint == 7:
        return myint
    elif myint == 8:
        return myint
    elif myint == 9:
        return myint
    elif myint == 10:
        if myint == 8:
            while True:
                return True
        elif myint == 8:
            with myint:
                return 8
    else:
        if myint == 2:
            return myint
        return myint
    return myint
$ pylint a.py \-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.mccabe
R:1: \(aqf10\(aq is too complex. The McCabe rating is 11 (too\-complex)
$ pylint a.py \-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.mccabe \-\-max\-complexity=50
$
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
See also design checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:design-options>
.SS Design checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B too\-complex (R1260)
\fI%s is too complex. The McCabe rating is %d\fP
Used when a method or function is too complex based on McCabe Complexity
Cyclomatic
.UNINDENT
.SS Dict\-Init\-Mutate checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.dict_init_mutate\fP\&.
