.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B else\-if\-used (R5501)
\fIConsider using \(dqelif\(dq instead of \(dqelse\(dq then \(dqif\(dq to remove one indentation level\fP
Used when an else statement is immediately followed by an if statement and
does not contain statements that would be unrelated to it.
.UNINDENT
.SS Empty\-Comment checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.empty_comment\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBempty\-comment\fP\&.
.SS Empty\-Comment checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B empty\-comment (R2044)
\fILine with empty comment\fP
Used when a # symbol appears on a line not followed by an actual comment
.UNINDENT
.SS Eq\-Without\-Hash checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.eq_without_hash\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBeq\-without\-hash\fP\&.
.SS Eq\-Without\-Hash checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B eq\-without\-hash (W1641)
\fIImplementing __eq__ without also implementing __hash__\fP
Used when a class implements __eq__ but not __hash__. Objects get None as
their default __hash__ implementation if they also implement __eq__.
.UNINDENT
.SS Import\-Private\-Name checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.private_import\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBimport\-private\-name\fP\&.
.SS Import\-Private\-Name checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B import\-private\-name (C2701)
\fIImported private %s (%s)\fP
Used when a private module or object prefixed with _ is imported. PEP8
guidance on Naming Conventions states that public attributes with leading
underscores should be considered private.
.UNINDENT
.SS Magic\-Value checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.magic_value\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBmagic\-value\fP\&.
.sp
See also magic\-value checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:magic-value-options>
.SS Magic\-Value checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B magic\-value\-comparison (R2004)
\fIConsider using a named constant or an enum instead of \(aq%s\(aq.\fP
Using named constants instead of magic values helps improve readability and
maintainability of your code, try to avoid them in comparisons.
.UNINDENT
.SS Multiple Types checker
