.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.no_self_use\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBno_self_use\fP\&.
.SS No Self Use checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B no\-self\-use (R6301)
\fIMethod could be a function\fP
Used when a method doesn\(aqt use its bound instance, and so could be written as
a function.
.UNINDENT
.SS Overlap\-Except checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.overlapping_exceptions\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBoverlap\-except\fP\&.
.SS Overlap\-Except checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B overlapping\-except (W0714)
\fIOverlapping exceptions (%s)\fP
Used when exceptions in handler overlap or are identical
.UNINDENT
.SS Parameter Documentation checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.docparams\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBparameter_documentation\fP\&.
.SS Parameter Documentation checker Documentation
.sp
If you document the parameters of your functions, methods and constructors and
their types systematically in your code this optional component might
be useful for you. Sphinx style, Google style, and Numpy style are supported.
(For some examples, see \%<https://\:pypi\:.org/\:project/\:sphinxcontrib-napoleon> .)
.sp
You can activate this checker by adding the line:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.docparams
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
to the \fBMAIN\fP section of your \fB\&.pylintrc\fP\&.
.sp
This checker verifies that all function, method, and constructor docstrings
include documentation of the
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
parameters and their types
.IP \(bu 2
return value and its type
.IP \(bu 2
exceptions raised
.UNINDENT
.sp
and can handle docstrings in
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Sphinx style (\fBparam\fP, \fBtype\fP, \fBreturn\fP, \fBrtype\fP,
\fBraise\fP / \fBexcept\fP):
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def function_foo(x, y, z):
    \(aq\(aq\(aqfunction foo ...

    :param x: bla x
    :type x: int

    :param y: bla y
    :type y: float

    :param int z: bla z

    :return: sum
    :rtype: float

    :raises OSError: bla
    \(aq\(aq\(aq
    return x + y + z
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
or the Google style (\fBArgs:\fP, \fBReturns:\fP, \fBRaises:\fP):
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def function_foo(x, y, z):
    \(aq\(aq\(aqfunction foo ...

    Args:
        x (int): bla x
        y (float): bla y

        z (int): bla z

    Returns:
        float: sum

    Raises:
        OSError: bla
    \(aq\(aq\(aq
    return x + y + z
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
or the Numpy style (\fBParameters\fP, \fBReturns\fP, \fBRaises\fP):
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def function_foo(x, y, z):
    \(aq\(aq\(aqfunction foo ...

    Parameters
    \-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-\-
    x: int
        bla x
    y: float
        bla y

    z: int
        bla z

    Returns
    \-\-\-\-\-\-\-
    float
        sum

    Raises
    \-\-\-\-\-\-
    OSError
        bla
    \(aq\(aq\(aq
    return x + y + z
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
You\(aqll be notified of \fBmissing parameter documentation\fP but also of
\fBnaming inconsistencies\fP between the signature and the documentation which
often arise when parameters are renamed automatically in the code, but not in
the documentation.
\fBNote:\fP by default docstrings of private and magic methods are not checked.
To change this behaviour (for example, to also check \fB__init__\fP) add
\fBno\-docstring\-rgx=^(?!__init__$)_\fP to the \fBBASIC\fP section of your \fB\&.pylintrc\fP\&.
.sp
Constructor parameters can be documented in either the class docstring or
the \fB__init__\fP docstring, but not both:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class ClassFoo(object):
    \(aq\(aq\(aqSphinx style docstring foo

    :param float x: bla x

    :param y: bla y
    :type y: int
    \(aq\(aq\(aq
    def __init__(self, x, y):
        pass

class ClassBar(object):
    def __init__(self, x, y):
        \(aq\(aq\(aqGoogle style docstring bar

        Args:
            x (float): bla x
            y (int): bla y
        \(aq\(aq\(aq
        pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
In some cases, having to document all parameters is a nuisance, for instance if
many of your functions or methods just follow a \fBcommon interface\fP\&. To remove
this burden, the checker accepts missing parameter documentation if one of the
following phrases is found in the docstring:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
For the other parameters, see
.IP \(bu 2
For the parameters, see
.UNINDENT
.sp
(with arbitrary whitespace between the words). Please add a link to the
docstring defining the interface, e.g. a superclass method, after \(dqsee\(dq:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def callback(x, y, z):
    \(aq\(aq\(aqSphinx style docstring for callback ...

    :param x: bla x
    :type x: int

    For the other parameters, see
    :class:\(gaMyFrameworkUsingAndDefiningCallback\(ga
    \(aq\(aq\(aq
    return x + y + z

def callback(x, y, z):
    \(aq\(aq\(aqGoogle style docstring for callback ...

    Args:
        x (int): bla x

    For the other parameters, see
    :class:\(gaMyFrameworkUsingAndDefiningCallback\(ga
    \(aq\(aq\(aq
    return x + y + z
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Naming inconsistencies in existing parameter and their type documentations are
still detected.
.sp
See also parameter_documentation checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:parameter-documentation-options>
.SS Parameter Documentation checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B multiple\-constructor\-doc (W9005)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq has constructor parameters documented in class and __init__\fP
Please remove parameter declarations in the class or constructor.
.TP
.B missing\-raises\-doc (W9006)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq not documented as being raised\fP
Please document exceptions for all raised exception types.
.TP
.B redundant\-returns\-doc (W9008)
\fIRedundant returns documentation\fP
Please remove the return/rtype documentation from this method.
.TP
.B redundant\-yields\-doc (W9010)
\fIRedundant yields documentation\fP
Please remove the yields documentation from this method.
.TP
.B missing\-return\-doc (W9011)
\fIMissing return documentation\fP
Please add documentation about what this method returns.
.TP
.B missing\-return\-type\-doc (W9012)
\fIMissing return type documentation\fP
Please document the type returned by this method.
.TP
.B missing\-yield\-doc (W9013)
\fIMissing yield documentation\fP
Please add documentation about what this generator yields.
.TP
.B missing\-yield\-type\-doc (W9014)
\fIMissing yield type documentation\fP
Please document the type yielded by this method.
.TP
.B missing\-param\-doc (W9015)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq missing in parameter documentation\fP
Please add parameter declarations for all parameters.
.TP
.B missing\-type\-doc (W9016)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq missing in parameter type documentation\fP
Please add parameter type declarations for all parameters.
.TP
.B differing\-param\-doc (W9017)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq differing in parameter documentation\fP
Please check parameter names in declarations.
.TP
.B differing\-type\-doc (W9018)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq differing in parameter type documentation\fP
Please check parameter names in type declarations.
.TP
.B useless\-param\-doc (W9019)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq useless ignored parameter documentation\fP
Please remove the ignored parameter documentation.
.TP
.B useless\-type\-doc (W9020)
\fI\(dq%s\(dq useless ignored parameter type documentation\fP
Please remove the ignored parameter type documentation.
.TP
.B missing\-any\-param\-doc (W9021)
\fIMissing any documentation in \(dq%s\(dq\fP
Please add parameter and/or type documentation.
.UNINDENT
.SS Redefined\-Loop\-Name checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.redefined_loop_name\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBredefined\-loop\-name\fP\&.
.SS Redefined\-Loop\-Name checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B redefined\-loop\-name (W2901)
\fIRedefining %r from loop (line %s)\fP
Used when a loop variable is overwritten in the loop body.
.UNINDENT
.SS Set Membership checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.set_membership\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBset_membership\fP\&.
.SS Set Membership checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B use\-set\-for\-membership (R6201)
\fIConsider using set for membership test\fP
Membership tests are more efficient when performed on a lookup optimized
datatype like \fBsets\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.SS Typing checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.typing\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBtyping\fP\&.
.SS Typing checker Documentation
.sp
Find issue specifically related to type annotations.
.sp
See also typing checker\(aqs options\(aq documentation \%<#\:typing-options>
.SS Typing checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B broken\-noreturn (E6004)
\fI\(aqNoReturn\(aq inside compound types is broken in 3.7.0 / 3.7.1\fP
\fBtyping.NoReturn\fP inside compound types is broken in Python 3.7.0 and
3.7.1. If not dependent on runtime introspection, use string annotation
instead. E.g. \fBCallable[..., \(aqNoReturn\(aq]\fP\&.
\%<https://\:bugs\:.python\:.org/\:issue34921>
.TP
.B broken\-collections\-callable (E6005)
\fI\(aqcollections.abc.Callable\(aq inside Optional and Union is broken in 3.9.0 / 3.9.1 (use \(aqtyping.Callable\(aq instead)\fP
\fBcollections.abc.Callable\fP inside Optional and Union is broken in Python
3.9.0 and 3.9.1. Use \fBtyping.Callable\fP for these cases instead.
\%<https://\:bugs\:.python\:.org/\:issue42965>
.TP
.B deprecated\-typing\-alias (W6001)
\fI\(aq%s\(aq is deprecated, use \(aq%s\(aq instead\fP
Emitted when a deprecated typing alias is used.
.TP
.B consider\-using\-alias (R6002)
\fI\(aq%s\(aq will be deprecated with PY39, consider using \(aq%s\(aq instead%s\fP
Only emitted if \(aqruntime\-typing=no\(aq and a deprecated typing alias is used in
a type annotation context in Python 3.7 or 3.8.
.TP
.B consider\-alternative\-union\-syntax (R6003)
\fIConsider using alternative union syntax instead of \(aq%s\(aq%s\fP
Emitted when \fBtyping.Union\fP or \fBtyping.Optional\fP is used instead of the
shorthand union syntax. For example, \fBUnion[int, float]\fP instead of \fBint |
float\fP\&. Using the shorthand for unions aligns with Python typing
recommendations, removes the need for imports, and avoids confusion in
function signatures.
.TP
.B redundant\-typehint\-argument (R6006)
\fIType \(ga%s\(ga is used more than once in union type annotation. Remove redundant typehints.\fP
Duplicated type arguments will be skipped by \fImypy\fP tool, therefore should be
removed to avoid confusion.
.TP
.B unnecessary\-default\-type\-args (R6007)
\fIType \(ga%s\(ga has unnecessary default type args. Change it to \(ga%s\(ga.\fP
Emitted when types have default type args which can be omitted. Mainly used
for \fItyping.Generator\fP and \fItyping.AsyncGenerator\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.SS While Used checker
.sp
This checker is provided by \fBpylint.extensions.while_used\fP\&.
Verbatim name of the checker is \fBwhile_used\fP\&.
.SS While Used checker Messages
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B while\-used (W0149)
\fIUsed \(gawhile\(ga loop\fP
Unbounded \fIwhile\fP loops can often be rewritten as bounded \fIfor\fP loops.
Exceptions can be made for cases such as event loops, listeners, etc.
.UNINDENT
.SS API
.sp
You can call \fBPylint\fP, \fBsymilar\fP and \fBpyreverse\fP from another
Python program thanks to their APIs:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from pylint import run_pylint, run_pyreverse, run_symilar

run_pylint(\(dq\-\-disable=C\(dq, \(dqmyfile.py\(dq)
run_pyreverse(...)
run_symilar(...)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Pylint
.SS As you would launch the command line
.sp
You can use the \fBrun_pylint\fP function, which is the same function
called by the command line (using \fBsys.argv\fP). You can supply
arguments yourself:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from pylint import run_pylint

run_pylint(argv=[\(dq\-\-disable=line\-too\-long\(dq, \(dqmyfile.py\(dq])
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Recover the result in a stream
.sp
You can also use \fBpylint.lint.Run\fP directly if you want to do something that
can\(aqt be done using only pylint\(aqs command line options. Here\(aqs the basic example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from pylint.lint import Run

Run(argv=[\(dq\-\-disable=line\-too\-long\(dq, \(dqmyfile.py\(dq])
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
With \fBRun\fP it is possible to invoke pylint programmatically with a
reporter initialized with a custom stream:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from io import StringIO

from pylint.lint import Run
from pylint.reporters.text import TextReporter

pylint_output = StringIO()  # Custom open stream
reporter = TextReporter(pylint_output)
Run([\(dqtest_file.py\(dq], reporter=reporter, exit=False)
print(pylint_output.getvalue())  # Retrieve and print the text report
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The reporter can accept any stream object as as parameter. In this example,
the stream outputs to a file:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from pylint.lint import Run
from pylint.reporters.text import TextReporter

with open(\(dqreport.out\(dq, \(dqw\(dq) as f:
    reporter = TextReporter(f)
    Run([\(dqtest_file.py\(dq], reporter=reporter, exit=False)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This would be useful to capture pylint output in an open stream which
can be passed onto another program.
.sp
If your program expects that the files being linted might be edited
between runs, you will need to clear pylint\(aqs inference cache:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from pylint.lint import pylinter
pylinter.MANAGER.clear_cache()
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS How To Guides
.SS How to Write a Checker
.sp
You can find some simple examples in the distribution
(custom.py \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:blob/\:main/\:examples/\:custom\:.py>
,
custom_raw.py \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:blob/\:main/\:examples/\:custom_raw\:.py>
and
deprecation_checker.py \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:blob/\:main/\:examples/\:deprecation_checker\:.py>).
.sp
There are three kinds of checkers:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Raw checkers, which analyse each module as a raw file stream.
.IP \(bu 2
Token checkers, which analyse a file using the list of tokens that
represent the source code in the file.
.IP \(bu 2
AST checkers, which work on an AST representation of the module.
.UNINDENT
.sp
The AST representation is provided by the \fBastroid\fP library.
\fBastroid\fP adds additional information and methods
over \fBast\fP in the standard library,
to make tree navigation and code introspection easier.
.SS Writing an AST Checker
.sp
Let\(aqs implement a checker to make sure that all \fBreturn\fP nodes in a function
return a unique constant.
Firstly we will need to fill in some required boilerplate:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import astroid
from astroid import nodes
from typing import TYPE_CHECKING, Optional

from pylint.checkers import BaseChecker

if TYPE_CHECKING:
    from pylint.lint import PyLinter


class UniqueReturnChecker(BaseChecker):

    name = \(dqunique\-returns\(dq
    msgs = {
        \(dqW0001\(dq: (
            \(dqReturns a non\-unique constant.\(dq,
            \(dqnon\-unique\-returns\(dq,
            \(dqAll constants returned in a function should be unique.\(dq,
        ),
    }
    options = (
        (
            \(dqignore\-ints\(dq,
            {
                \(dqdefault\(dq: False,
                \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqyn\(dq,
                \(dqmetavar\(dq: \(dq<y or n>\(dq,
                \(dqhelp\(dq: \(dqAllow returning non\-unique integers\(dq,
            },
        ),
    )
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
So far we have defined the following required components of our checker:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
.INDENT 2.0
.TP
.B A name. The name is used to generate a special configuration
section for the checker, when options have been provided.
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
.INDENT 2.0
.TP
.B A message dictionary. Each checker is being used for finding problems
in your code, the problems being displayed to the user through \fBmessages\fP\&.
The message dictionary should specify what messages the checker is
going to emit. See Defining a Message for the details about defining a new message.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
We have also defined an optional component of the checker.
The options list defines any user configurable options.
It has the following format:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
options = (
    (\(dqoption\-symbol\(dq, {\(dqargparse\-like\-kwarg\(dq: \(dqvalue\(dq}),
)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBoption\-symbol\fP is a unique name for the option.
This is used on the command line and in config files.
The hyphen is replaced by an underscore when used in the checker,
similarly to how you would use  \fBargparse.Namespace\fP:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if not self.linter.config.ignore_ints:
    ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Next we\(aqll track when we enter and leave a function.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def __init__(self, linter: Optional[\(dqPyLinter\(dq] = None) \-> None:
    super().__init__(linter)
    self._function_stack = []

def visit_functiondef(self, node: nodes.FunctionDef) \-> None:
    self._function_stack.append([])

def leave_functiondef(self, node: nodes.FunctionDef) \-> None:
    self._function_stack.pop()
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
In the constructor we initialise a stack to keep a list of return nodes
for each function.
An AST checker is a visitor, and should implement
\fBvisit_<lowered class name>\fP or \fBleave_<lowered class name>\fP
methods for the nodes it\(aqs interested in.
In this case we have implemented \fBvisit_functiondef\fP and \fBleave_functiondef\fP
to add a new list of return nodes for this function,
and to remove the list of return nodes when we leave the function.
.sp
Finally we\(aqll implement the check.
We will define a \fBvisit_return\fP function,
which is called with an \fB\&.astroid.nodes.Return\fP node.
.sp
We\(aqll need to be able to figure out what attributes an
\fB\&.astroid.nodes.Return\fP node has available.
We can use \fBastroid.extract_node\fP for this:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
>>> node = astroid.extract_node(\(dqreturn 5\(dq)
>>> node
<Return l.1 at 0x7efe62196390>
>>> help(node)
>>> node.value
<Const.int l.1 at 0x7efe62196ef0>
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
We could also construct a more complete example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
>>> node_a, node_b = astroid.extract_node(\(dq\(dq\(dq
\&... def test():
\&...     if True:
\&...         return 5 #@
\&...     return 5 #@
\&... \(dq\(dq\(dq)
>>> node_a.value
<Const.int l.4 at 0x7efe621a74e0>
>>> node_a.value.value
5
>>> node_a.value.value == node_b.value.value
True
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
For \fBastroid.extract_node\fP, you can use \fB#@\fP at the end of a line to choose which statements will be extracted into nodes.
.sp
For more information on \fBastroid.extract_node\fP,
see the astroid documentation \%<https://\:pylint\:.readthedocs\:.io/\:projects/\:astroid/\:en/\:latest>\&.
.sp
Now we know how to use the astroid node, we can implement our check.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def visit_return(self, node: nodes.Return) \-> None:
    if not isinstance(node.value, nodes.Const):
        return
    for other_return in self._function_stack[\-1]:
        if node.value.value == other_return.value.value and not (
            self.linter.config.ignore_ints and node.value.pytype() == int
        ):
            self.add_message(\(dqnon\-unique\-returns\(dq, node=node)

    self._function_stack[\-1].append(node)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Once we have established that the source code has failed our check,
we use \fB~.BaseChecker.add_message\fP to emit our failure message.
.sp
Finally, we need to register the checker with pylint.
Add the \fBregister\fP function to the top level of the file.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def register(linter: \(dqPyLinter\(dq) \-> None:
    \(dq\(dq\(dqThis required method auto registers the checker during initialization.
    :param linter: The linter to register the checker to.
    \(dq\(dq\(dq
    linter.register_checker(UniqueReturnChecker(linter))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
We are now ready to debug and test our checker!
.SS Debugging a Checker
.sp
It is very simple to get to a point where we can use \fBpdb\fP\&.
We\(aqll need a small test case.
Put the following into a Python file:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def test():
    if True:
        return 5
    return 5

def test2():
    if True:
        return 1
    return 5
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
After inserting pdb into our checker and installing it,
we can run pylint with only our checker:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ pylint \-\-load\-plugins=my_plugin \-\-disable=all \-\-enable=non\-unique\-returns test.py
(Pdb)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Now we can debug our checker!
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
\fBmy_plugin\fP refers to a module called \fBmy_plugin.py\fP\&.
The preferred way of making this plugin available to pylint is
by installing it as a package. This can be done either from a packaging index like
\fBPyPI\fP or by installing it from a local source such as with \fBpip install\fP\&.
.sp
Alternatively, the plugin module can be made available to pylint by
putting this module\(aqs parent directory in your \fBPYTHONPATH\fP
environment variable.
.sp
If your pylint config has an \fBinit\-hook\fP that modifies
\fBsys.path\fP to include the module\(aqs parent directory, this
will also work, but only if either:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
the \fBinit\-hook\fP and the \fBload\-plugins\fP list are both
defined in a configuration file, or...
.IP \(bu 2
the \fBinit\-hook\fP is passed as a command\-line argument and
the \fBload\-plugins\fP list is in the configuration file
.UNINDENT
.sp
So, you cannot load a custom plugin by modifying \fBsys.path\fP if you
supply the \fBinit\-hook\fP in a configuration file, but pass the module name
in via \fB\-\-load\-plugins\fP on the command line.
This is because pylint loads plugins specified on command
line before loading any configuration from other sources.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Defining a Message
.sp
Pylint message is defined using the following format:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
msgs = {
    \(dqE0401\(dq: ( # message id
     \(dqUnable to import %s\(dq, # template of displayed message
     \(dqimport\-error\(dq, # message symbol
     \(dqUsed when pylint has been unable to import a module.\(dq,  # Message description
     { # Additional parameters:
          # message control support for the old names of the messages:
         \(dqold_names\(dq: [(\(dqF0401\(dq, \(dqold\-import\-error\(dq)]
         \(dqminversion\(dq: (3, 5), # No check under this version
         \(dqmaxversion\(dq: (3, 7), # No check above this version
     },
 ),
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The message is then formatted using the \fBargs\fP parameter from \fBadd_message\fP i.e. in
\fBself.add_message(\(dqimport\-error\(dq, args=module_we_cant_import, node=importnode)\fP, the value in \fBmodule_we_cant_import\fP say \fBpatglib\fP will be interpolled and the final result will be:
\fBUnable to import patglib\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBmessage\-id\fP should be a 4\-digit number,
prefixed with a \fBmessage category\fP\&.
There are multiple message categories,
these being \fBC\fP, \fBW\fP, \fBE\fP, \fBF\fP, \fBR\fP,
standing for \fBConvention\fP, \fBWarning\fP, \fBError\fP, \fBFatal\fP and \fBRefactoring\fP\&.
The 4 digits should not conflict with existing checkers
and the first 2 digits should consistent across the checker (except shared messages).
It is safe to use 51\-99 as the first 2 digits for custom checkers because this range is reserved for them.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBdisplayed\-message\fP is used for displaying the message to the user,
once it is emitted.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBmessage\-symbol\fP is an alias of the message id
and it can be used wherever the message id can be used.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBmessage\-help\fP is used when calling \fBpylint \-\-help\-msg\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Optionally message can contain optional extra options:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBold_names\fP option permits to change the message id or symbol of a message without breaking the message control used on the old messages by users. The option is specified as a list
of tuples (\fBmessage\-id\fP, \fBold\-message\-symbol\fP) e.g. \fB{\(dqold_names\(dq: [(\(dqF0401\(dq, \(dqold\-import\-error\(dq)]}\fP\&.
The symbol / msgid association must be unique so if you\(aqre changing the message id the symbol also need to change and you can generally use the \fBold\-\fP prefix for that.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBminversion\fP or \fBmaxversion\fP options specify minimum or maximum version of python
relevant for this message. The option value is specified as tuple with major version number
as first number and minor version number as second number e.g. \fB{\(dqminversion\(dq: (3, 5)}\fP
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBshared\fP option enables sharing message between multiple checkers. As mentioned
previously, normally the message cannot be shared between multiple checkers.
To allow having message shared between multiple checkers, the \fBshared\fP option must
be set to \fBTrue\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.SS Parallelize a Checker
.sp
\fBBaseChecker\fP has two methods \fBget_map_data\fP and \fBreduce_map_data\fP that
permit to parallelize the checks when used with the \fB\-j\fP option. If a checker
actually needs to reduce data it should define \fBget_map_data\fP as returning
something different than \fBNone\fP and let its \fBreduce_map_data\fP handle a list
of the types returned by \fBget_map_data\fP\&.
.sp
An example can be seen by looking at \fBpylint/checkers/similar.py\fP\&.
.SS Testing a Checker
.sp
Pylint is very well suited to test driven development.
You can implement the template of the checker,
produce all of your test cases and check that they fail,
implement the checker,
then check that all of your test cases work.
.sp
Pylint provides a \fBpylint.testutils.CheckerTestCase\fP
to make test cases very simple.
We can use the example code that we used for debugging as our test cases.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import astroid
import my_plugin
import pylint.testutils


class TestUniqueReturnChecker(pylint.testutils.CheckerTestCase):
    CHECKER_CLASS = my_plugin.UniqueReturnChecker

    def test_finds_non_unique_ints(self):
        func_node, return_node_a, return_node_b = astroid.extract_node(\(dq\(dq\(dq
        def test(): #@
            if True:
                return 5 #@
            return 5 #@
        \(dq\(dq\(dq)

        self.checker.visit_functiondef(func_node)
        self.checker.visit_return(return_node_a)
        with self.assertAddsMessages(
            pylint.testutils.MessageTest(
                msg_id=\(dqnon\-unique\-returns\(dq,
                node=return_node_b,
            ),
        ):
            self.checker.visit_return(return_node_b)

    def test_ignores_unique_ints(self):
        func_node, return_node_a, return_node_b = astroid.extract_node(\(dq\(dq\(dq
        def test(): #@
            if True:
                return 1 #@
            return 5 #@
        \(dq\(dq\(dq)

        with self.assertNoMessages():
            self.checker.visit_functiondef(func_node)
            self.checker.visit_return(return_node_a)
            self.checker.visit_return(return_node_b)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Once again we are using \fBastroid.extract_node\fP to
construct our test cases.
\fBpylint.testutils.CheckerTestCase\fP has created the linter and checker for us,
we simply simulate a traversal of the AST tree
using the nodes that we are interested in.
.SS How To Write a Pylint Plugin
.sp
Pylint provides support for writing two types of extensions.
First, there is the concept of \fBcheckers\fP,
which can be used for finding problems in your code.
Secondly, there is also the concept of \fBtransform plugin\fP,
which represents a way through which the inference and
the capabilities of Pylint can be enhanced
and tailored to a particular module, library of framework.
.sp
In general, a plugin is a module which should have a function \fBregister\fP,
which takes an instance of \fBpylint.lint.PyLinter\fP as input.
.sp
A plugin can optionally define a function, \fBload_configuration\fP,
which takes an instance of \fBpylint.lint.PyLinter\fP as input. This
function is called after Pylint loads configuration from configuration
file and command line interface. This function should load additional
plugin specific configuration to Pylint.
.sp
So a basic hello\-world plugin can be implemented as:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# Inside hello_plugin.py
from typing import TYPE_CHECKING

import astroid

if TYPE_CHECKING:
    from pylint.lint import PyLinter


def register(linter: \(dqPyLinter\(dq) \-> None:
  \(dq\(dq\(dqThis required method auto registers the checker during initialization.

  :param linter: The linter to register the checker to.
  \(dq\(dq\(dq
  print(\(aqHello world\(aq)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
We can run this plugin by placing this module in the PYTHONPATH and invoking
\fBpylint\fP as:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ pylint \-E \-\-load\-plugins hello_plugin foo.py
Hello world
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
We can extend hello\-world plugin to ignore some specific names using
\fBload_configuration\fP function:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# Inside hello_plugin.py
from typing import TYPE_CHECKING

import astroid

if TYPE_CHECKING:
    from pylint.lint import PyLinter


def register(linter: \(dqPyLinter\(dq) \-> None:
  \(dq\(dq\(dqThis required method auto registers the checker during initialization.

  :param linter: The linter to register the checker to.
  \(dq\(dq\(dq
  print(\(aqHello world\(aq)

def load_configuration(linter):

  name_checker = get_checker(linter, NameChecker)
  # We consider as good names of variables Hello and World
  name_checker.config.good_names += (\(aqHello\(aq, \(aqWorld\(aq)

  # We ignore bin directory
  linter.config.black_list += (\(aqbin\(aq,)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Depending if we need a \fBtransform plugin\fP or a \fBchecker\fP, this might not
be enough. For the former, this is enough to declare the module as a plugin,
but in the case of the latter, we need to register our checker with the linter
object, by calling the following inside the \fBregister\fP function:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
linter.register_checker(OurChecker(linter))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
For more information on writing a checker see How to Write a Checker \%<#\:write-a-checker>\&.
.SS Transform plugins
.SS Why write a plugin?
.sp
Pylint is a static analysis tool and Python is a dynamically typed language.
So there will be cases where Pylint cannot analyze files properly (this problem
can happen in statically typed languages also if reflection or dynamic
evaluation is used).
.sp
The plugins are a way to tell Pylint how to handle such cases,
since only the user would know what needs to be done. They are usually operating
on the AST level, by modifying or changing it in a way which can ease its
understanding by Pylint.
.SS Example
.sp
Let us run Pylint on a module from the Python source: warnings.py \%<https://\:hg\:.python\:.org/\:cpython/\:file/\:2\:.7/\:Lib/\:warnings\:.py> and see what happens:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
amitdev$ pylint \-E Lib/warnings.py
E:297,36: Instance of \(aqWarningMessage\(aq has no \(aqmessage\(aq member (no\-member)
E:298,36: Instance of \(aqWarningMessage\(aq has no \(aqfilename\(aq member (no\-member)
E:298,51: Instance of \(aqWarningMessage\(aq has no \(aqlineno\(aq member (no\-member)
E:298,64: Instance of \(aqWarningMessage\(aq has no \(aqline\(aq member (no\-member)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Did we catch a genuine error? Let\(aqs open the code and look at \fBWarningMessage\fP class:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class WarningMessage(object):

  \(dq\(dq\(dqHolds the result of a single showwarning() call.\(dq\(dq\(dq

  _WARNING_DETAILS = (\(dqmessage\(dq, \(dqcategory\(dq, \(dqfilename\(dq, \(dqlineno\(dq, \(dqfile\(dq,
                      \(dqline\(dq)

  def __init__(self, message, category, filename, lineno, file=None,
                  line=None):
    local_values = locals()
    for attr in self._WARNING_DETAILS:
      setattr(self, attr, local_values[attr])
    self._category_name = category.__name__ if category else None

  def __str__(self):
    ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Ah, the fields (\fBmessage\fP, \fBcategory\fP etc) are not defined statically on the class.
Instead they are added using \fBsetattr\fP\&. Pylint would have a tough time figuring
this out.
.SS Enter Plugin
.sp
We can write a transform plugin to tell Pylint how to analyze this properly.
.sp
One way to fix our example with a plugin would be to transform the \fBWarningMessage\fP class,
by setting the attributes so that Pylint can see them. This can be done by
registering a transform function. We can transform any node in the parsed AST like
Module, Class, Function etc. In our case we need to transform a class. It can be done so:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from typing import TYPE_CHECKING

import astroid

if TYPE_CHECKING:
    from pylint.lint import PyLinter


def register(linter: \(dqPyLinter\(dq) \-> None:
  \(dq\(dq\(dqThis required method auto registers the checker during initialization.

  :param linter: The linter to register the checker to.
  \(dq\(dq\(dq
  pass

def transform(cls):
  if cls.name == \(aqWarningMessage\(aq:
    import warnings
    for f in warnings.WarningMessage._WARNING_DETAILS:
      cls.locals[f] = [astroid.ClassDef(f, None)]

astroid.MANAGER.register_transform(astroid.ClassDef, transform)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Let\(aqs go through the plugin. First, we need to register a class transform, which
is done via the \fBregister_transform\fP function in \fBMANAGER\fP\&. It takes the node
type and function as parameters. We need to change a class, so we use \fBastroid.ClassDef\fP\&.
We also pass a \fBtransform\fP function which does the actual transformation.
.sp
\fBtransform\fP function is simple as well. If the class is \fBWarningMessage\fP then we
add the attributes to its locals (we are not bothered about type of attributes, so setting
them as class will do. But we could set them to any type we want). That\(aqs it.
.sp
Note: We don\(aqt need to do anything in the \fBregister\fP function of the plugin since we
are not modifying anything in the linter itself.
.sp
Lets run Pylint with this plugin and see:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
amitdev$ pylint \-E \-\-load\-plugins warning_plugin Lib/warnings.py
amitdev$
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
All the false positives associated with \fBWarningMessage\fP are now gone. This is just
an example, any code transformation can be done by plugins.
.sp
See astroid/brain \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:astroid/\:tree/\:main/\:astroid/\:brain> for real life examples of transform plugins.
.SS Technical Reference
.SS Startup and the Linter Class
.sp
The two main classes in \fBpylint.lint\fP are
\fB\&.pylint.lint.Run\fP and \fB\&.pylint.lint.PyLinter\fP\&.
.sp
The \fB\&.pylint.lint.Run\fP object is responsible for starting up pylint.
It does some basic checking of the given command line options to
find the initial hook to run,
find the config file to use,
and find which plugins have been specified.
It can then create the main \fB\&.pylint.lint.PyLinter\fP instance
and initialise it with the config file and plugins that were discovered
when preprocessing the command line options.
Finally the \fB\&.pylint.lint.Run\fP object launches any child linters
for parallel jobs, and starts the linting process.
.sp
The \fB\&.pylint.lint.PyLinter\fP is responsible for coordinating the
linting process.
It parses the configuration and provides it for the checkers and other plugins,
it handles the messages emitted by the checkers,
it handles the output reporting,
and it launches the checkers.
.SS Checkers
.sp
All of the default pylint checkers exist in \fBpylint.checkers\fP\&.
This is where most of pylint\(aqs brains exist.
Most checkers are AST based and so use \fBastroid\fP\&.
\fBpylint.checkers.utils\fP provides a large number of utility methods for
dealing with \fBastroid\fP\&.
.SS Contributing to pylint
.sp
The contributor guide will help you if you want to contribute to pylint itself.
.SS Contributing
.SS Finding something to do
.sp
Want to contribute to pylint? There\(aqs a lot of things you can do.
Here\(aqs a list of links you can check depending on what you want to do:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Asking a question on discord \%<https://\:discord\:.com/\:invite/\:qYxpadCgkx>, or on github \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:new/\:choose>
.IP \(bu 2
Opening an issue \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:new?\:assignees=&\:labels=Needs+triage+%3Ainbox_tray%3A&\:template=BUG-REPORT\:.yml>
.IP \(bu 2
Making the documentation better \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Documentation+%3Agreen_book%3A%22>
.IP \(bu 2
Making the error message better \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen%20is%3Aissue%20project%3Apylint-dev%2Fpylint%2F4>
.IP \(bu 2
Reproducing bugs and confirming that issues are valid \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Needs+reproduction+%3Amag%3A%22%2C%22Cannot+reproduce+%F0%9F%A4%B7%22>
.IP \(bu 2
Investigating or debugging complicated issues \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Needs+investigation+%F0%9F%94%AC%22>
.IP \(bu 2
Designing or specifying a solution \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Needs+design+proposal+%3Alock%3A%22%2C%22Needs+specification+%3Aclosed_lock_with_key%3A%22>
.IP \(bu 2
Giving your opinion on ongoing discussion \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Needs+decision+%3Alock%3A%22>
.IP \(bu 2
Fixing bugs and crashes \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Bug+%3Abeetle%3A%22%2C%22Crash+%F0%9F%92%A5%22>
.IP \(bu 2
Fixing false positives \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22False+Positive+%F0%9F%A6%9F%22>
.IP \(bu 2
Creating new features or fixing false negatives \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22False+Negative+%F0%9F%A6%8B%22%2C%22Enhancement+%E2%9C%A8%22>
.IP \(bu 2
Reviewing pull requests \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:pulls?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Apr+label%3A%22Needs+review+%F0%9F%94%8D%22>
.UNINDENT
.sp
If you are a pylint maintainer there\(aqs also:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Triaging issues \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Needs+triage+%3Ainbox_tray%3A%22>
.IP \(bu 2
Labeling issues that do not have an actionable label yet \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+-label%3A%22Needs+astroid+Brain+%F0%9F%A7%A0%22+-label%3A%22Needs+astroid+update%22+-label%3A%22Needs+backport%22+-label%3A%22Needs+decision+%3Alock%3A%22+-label%3A%22Needs+investigation+%F0%9F%94%AC%22+-label%3A%22Needs+PR%22+-label%3A%22Needs+reproduction+%3Amag%3A%22+-label%3A%22Needs+review+%F0%9F%94%8D%22+-label%3A%22Needs+triage+%3Ainbox_tray%3A%22+-label%3A%22Waiting+on+author%22+-label%3A%22Work+in+progress%22+-label%3AMaintenance+sort%3Aupdated-desc+-label%3A%22Needs+specification+%3Aclosed_lock_with_key%3A%22+-label%3A%22Needs+design+proposal+%3Alock%3A%22>
.IP \(bu 2
Preparing the next patch release \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Aissue+label%3A%22Needs+backport%22>
.IP \(bu 2
Checking stale pull requests status \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:pulls?\:q=is%3Aopen+is%3Apr+label%3A%22Work+in+progress%22%2C%22Needs+astroid+update%22%2C%22Waiting+on+author%22>
.UNINDENT
.SS Creating a pull request
.sp
Got a change for Pylint?  Below are a few steps you should take to make sure
your patch gets accepted:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
You must use at least Python 3.8 for development of Pylint as it gives
you access to the latest \fBast\fP parser and some pre\-commit hooks do not
support python 3.7.
.IP \(bu 2
Install the dev dependencies, see Contributor installation \%<#\:contributor-install>\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Use our test suite and write new tests, see Testing pylint \%<#\:contributor-testing>\&.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Document your change, if it is a non\-trivial one:
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
A maintainer might label the issue \fBskip\-news\fP if the change does not need to be in the changelog.
.IP \(bu 2
Otherwise, create a news fragment with \fBtowncrier create <IssueNumber>.<type>\fP which will be
included in the changelog. \fB<type>\fP can be one of the types defined in \fI\&./towncrier.toml\fP\&.
If necessary you can write details or offer examples on how the new change is supposed to work.
.IP \(bu 2
Generating the doc is done with \fBtox \-e docs\fP
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Send a pull request from GitHub (see About pull requests \%<https://\:support\:.github\:.com/\:features/\:pull-requests> for more insight about this topic).
.IP \(bu 2
Write comprehensive commit messages and/or a good description of what the PR does.
Relate your change to an issue in the tracker if such an issue exists (see
Closing issues via commit messages \%<https://\:github\:.blog/\:2013-01-22-closing-issues-via-commit-messages> of the GitHub documentation for more
information on this)
.IP \(bu 2
Keep the change small, separate the consensual changes from the opinionated one.
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt hesitate to open multiple PRs if the change requires it. If your review is so
big it requires to actually plan and allocate time to review, it\(aqs more likely
that it\(aqs going to go stale.
.IP \(bu 2
Maintainers might have multiple 5 to 10 minutes review windows per day, Say while waiting
for their teapot to boil, or for their partner to recover from their hilarious nerdy joke,
but only one full hour review time per week, if at all.
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
If you used multiple emails or multiple names when contributing, add your mails
and preferred name in the \fBscript/.contributors_aliases.json\fP file.
.UNINDENT
.SS Tips for Getting Started with Pylint Development
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Read the Technical Reference \%<#\:technical-reference>\&. It gives a short walk through of the pylint
codebase and will help you identify where you will need to make changes
for what you are trying to implement.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBastroid.extract_node\fP is your friend. Most checkers are AST based,
so you will likely need to interact with \fBastroid\fP\&.
A short example of how to use \fBastroid.extract_node\fP is given
here \%<#\:astroid-extract-node>\&.
.IP \(bu 2
When fixing a bug for a specific check, search the code for the warning
message to find where the warning is raised,
and therefore where the logic for that code exists.
.IP \(bu 2
When adding a new checker class you can use the \fBget_unused_message_id_category.py\fP
script in \fB\&./script\fP to get a message id that is not used by
any of the other checkers.
.UNINDENT
.SS Building the documentation
.sp
You can use the makefile in the doc directory to build the documentation:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ make \-C doc/ install\-dependencies
$ make \-C doc/ html
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
We\(aqre reusing generated files for speed, use \fBmake clean\fP or \fBtox \-e docs\fP when you want to start from scratch.
.SS How to choose the target version ?
.sp
Choose depending on the kind of change you\(aqre doing:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
In \fBpatch release\fP (\fB1.2.3\fP), we only fix false positives and crashes.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
In \fBminor releases\fP (\fB1.2.0\fP), we add checks, remove checks, drop python interpreters
past end of life, upgrade astroid minor/major versions and fix false negatives.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
In \fBmajor releases\fP (\fB1.0.0\fP) we change everything else (pylint options, json output, dev API...)
while still trying to minimize disruption.
.UNINDENT
.SS Testing pylint
.sp
Pylint is very well tested and has a high code coverage. New contributions are not accepted
unless they include tests.
.SS Contributor installation
.SS Basic installation
.sp
Pylint is developed using the git \%<https://\:git-scm\:.com> distributed version control system.
.sp
You can clone Pylint using
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
git clone https://github.com/pylint\-dev/pylint
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Before you start testing your code, you need to install your source\-code package locally.
Suppose you just cloned pylint with the previous \fBgit clone\fP command. To set up your
environment for testing, open a terminal and run:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
cd pylint
python3 \-m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install \-r requirements_test_min.txt
pip install \-e .
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This ensures your testing environment is similar to Pylint\(aqs testing environment on GitHub.
.sp
\fBOptionally\fP (Because there\(aqs an auto\-fix if you open a merge request): We have
pre\-commit hooks which should take care of the autoformatting for you before each
commit. To enable it, run \fBpre\-commit install\fP in the \fBpylint\fP root directory.
.SS Astroid installation
.sp
If you\(aqre testing new changes in astroid you need to also clone astroid \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:astroid> and install
with an editable installation alongside pylint as follows:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# Suppose you\(aqre in the pylint directory
git clone https://github.com/pylint\-dev/astroid.git
python3 \-m pip install \-e astroid/
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
You\(aqre now using the local astroid in pylint and can control the version with git for example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
cd astroid/
git switch my\-astroid\-dev\-branch
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Launching tests
.SS pytest
.sp
Since we use pytest to run the tests, you can also use it on its own.
We do recommend using the tox command though:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
pytest tests/ \-k test_functional
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
You can use pytest directly. If you want to run tests on a specific portion of the
code with pytest and your local python version:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
python3 \-m pytest
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Everything in tests/message with coverage for the relevant code (require pytest\-cov \%<https://\:pypi\:.org/\:project/\:pytest-cov>):
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
python3 \-m pytest tests/message/ \-\-cov=pylint.message
coverage html
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Only the functional test \(dqmissing_kwoa_py3\(dq:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
python3 \-m pytest \(dqtests/test_functional.py::test_functional[missing_kwoa_py3]\(dq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS tox
.sp
You can also \fIoptionally\fP install tox and run our tests using the tox package, as in:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
python \-m tox
python \-m tox \-epy313 # for Python 3.13 suite only
python \-m tox \-epylint # for running Pylint over Pylint\(aqs codebase
python \-m tox \-eformatting # for running formatting checks over Pylint\(aqs codebase
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
It\(aqs usually a good idea to run tox with \fB\-\-recreate\fP\&. This flag tells tox to re\-download
all dependencies before running the tests. This can be important when a new version of
astroid \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:astroid> or any of the other dependencies has been published:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
python \-m tox \-\-recreate # The entire tox environment will be recreated
python \-m tox \-\-recreate \-e py310 # The python 3.10 tox environment will be recreated
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
To run only a specific test suite, use a pattern for the test filename
(\fBwithout\fP the \fB\&.py\fP extension), as in:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
python \-m tox \-e py310 \-\- \-k test_functional
python \-m tox \-e py310 \-\- \-k  \e*func\e*
python \-m tox \-\-recreate \-e py310 \-\- \-k test_functional # With recreation of the environment
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Primer tests
.sp
Pylint also uses what we refer to as \fBprimer\fP tests. These are tests that are run automatically
in our Continuous Integration and check whether any changes in Pylint lead to crashes or fatal errors
on the \fBstdlib\fP, and also assess a pull request\(aqs impact on the linting of a selection of external
repositories by posting the diff against \fBpylint\fP\(aqs current output as a comment.
.sp
To run the primer test for the \fBstdlib\fP, which only checks for crashes and fatal errors, you can add
\fB\-\-primer\-stdlib\fP to the pytest command. For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
pytest \-m primer_stdlib \-\-primer\-stdlib
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
To produce the output generated on Continuous Integration for the linting of external repositories,
run these commands:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
python tests/primer/__main__.py prepare \-\-clone
python tests/primer/__main__.py run \-\-type=pr
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
To fully simulate the process on Continuous Integration, you should then checkout \fBmain\fP, and
then run these commands:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
python tests/primer/__main__.py run \-\-type=main
python tests/primer/__main__.py compare
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The list of repositories is created on the basis of three criteria: 1) projects need to use a diverse
range of language features, 2) projects need to be well maintained and 3) projects should not have a codebase
that is too repetitive. This guarantees a good balance between speed of our CI and finding potential bugs.
.sp
You can find the latest list of repositories and any relevant code for these tests in the \fBtests/primer\fP
directory.
.SS Writing tests
.sp
Pylint uses three types of tests: unittests, functional tests and primer tests.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
unittests can be found in \fBpylint/tests\fP\&. Unless you\(aqre working on pylint\(aqs
internal you\(aqre probably not going to have to write any.
.IP \(bu 2
Global functional tests  can be found in the \fBpylint/tests/functional\fP\&. They are
mainly used to test whether Pylint emits the correct messages.
.IP \(bu 2
Configuration\(aqs functional tests  can be found in the
\fBpylint/tests/config/functional\fP\&. They are used to test Pylint\(aqs configuration loading.
.IP \(bu 2
Primer tests \%<#\:primer-tests> you can suggest a new external repository to check but there\(aqs nothing to do
most of the time.
.UNINDENT
.SS Unittest tests
.sp
Most other tests reside in the \(aq/pylint/test\(aq directory. These unittests can be used to test
almost all functionality within Pylint. A good step before writing any new unittests is to look
at some tests that test a similar functionality. This can often help write new tests.
.sp
If your new test requires any additional files you can put those in the
\fB/pylint/test/regrtest_data\fP directory. This is the directory we use to store any data needed for
the unittests.
.SS Functional tests
.sp
These are located under \fB/pylint/test/functional\fP and they are formed of multiple
components. First, each Python file is considered to be a test case and it
should be accompanied by a \fB\&.txt\fP file, having the same name. The \fB\&.txt\fP file contains the \fBpylint\fP messages
that are supposed to be emitted by the given test file.
.sp
In your \fB\&.py\fP test file, each line for which Pylint is supposed to emit a message
has to be annotated with a comment following this pattern \fB# [message_symbol]\fP, as in:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
a, b, c = 1 # [unbalanced\-tuple\-unpacking]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If multiple messages are expected on the same line, then this syntax can be used:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
a, b, c = 1.test # [unbalanced\-tuple\-unpacking, no\-member]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
You can also use  \fB# +n: [\fP where \fBn\fP is an integer to deal with special cases, e.g., where the above regular syntax makes the line too long:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
A = 5
# +1: [singleton\-comparison]
B = A == None  # The test will look for the \(gasingleton\-comparison\(ga message in this line
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If you need special control over Pylint\(aqs configuration, you can also create a \fB\&.rc\fP file, which
can set sections of Pylint\(aqs configuration.
The \fB\&.rc\fP file can also contain a section \fB[testoptions]\fP to pass options for the functional
test runner. The following options are currently supported:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqmin_pyver\(dq: Minimal python version required to run the test
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqmax_pyver\(dq: Python version from which the test won\(aqt be run. If the last supported version is 3.9 this setting should be set to 3.10.
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqmin_pyver_end_position\(dq: Minimal python version required to check the end_line and end_column attributes of the message
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqrequires\(dq: Packages required to be installed locally to run the test
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqexcept_implementations\(dq: List of python implementations on which the test should not run
.IP \(bu 2
\(dqexclude_platforms\(dq: List of operating systems on which the test should not run
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBDifferent output for different Python versions\fP
.sp
Sometimes the linting result can change between Python releases. In these cases errors can be marked as conditional.
Supported operators are \fB<\fP, \fB<=\fP, \fB>\fP and \fB>=\fP\&.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def some_func() \-> X:  # <3.14:[undefined\-variable]
  ...

# It can also be combined with offsets
# +1:<3.14:[undefined\-variable]
def some_other_func() \-> X:
  ...

class X: ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Since the output messages are different, it is necessary to add two separate files for it.
First \fB<test\-file\-name>.314.txt\fP, this will include the output messages for \fB>=3.14\fP, i.e. should be empty here.
Second \fB<test\-file\-name>.txt\fP, this will be the default for all other Python versions.
.sp
\fBNote:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This does only work if the code itself is parsable in all tested Python versions.
For new syntax, use \fBmin_pyver\fP / \fBmax_pyver\fP instead.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBFunctional test file locations\fP
.sp
For existing checkers, new test cases should preferably be appended to the existing test file.
For new checkers, a new file \fBnew_checker_message.py\fP should be created (Note the use of
underscores). This file should then be placed in the \fBtest/functional/n\fP sub\-directory.
.sp
Some additional notes:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
If the checker is part of an extension the test should go in \fBtest/functional/ext/extension_name\fP
.IP \(bu 2
If the test is a regression test it should go in \fBtest/r/regression\fP or \fBtest/r/regression_02\fP\&.
The file name should start with \fBregression_\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
For some sub\-directories, such as \fBtest/functional/u\fP, there are additional sub\-directories (\fBtest/functional/u/use\fP).
Please check if your test file should be placed in any of these directories. It should be placed there
if the sub\-directory name matches the word before the first underscore of your test file name.
.UNINDENT
.sp
The folder structure is enforced when running the test suite, so you might be directed to put the file
in a different sub\-directory.
.sp
\fBRunning and updating functional tests\fP
.sp
During development, it\(aqs sometimes helpful to run all functional tests in your
current environment in order to have faster feedback. Run from Pylint root directory with:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
python tests/test_functional.py
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
You can use all the options you would use for pytest \%<https://\:docs\:.pytest\:.org/\:en/\:latest>, for example \fB\-k \(dqtest_functional[len_checks]\(dq\fP\&.
Furthermore, if required the .txt file with expected messages can be regenerated based
on the current output by appending \fB\-\-update\-functional\-output\fP to the command line:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
python tests/test_functional.py \-\-update\-functional\-output \-k \(dqtest_functional[len_checks]\(dq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Functional tests for configurations
.sp
To test the different ways to configure Pylint there is also a small functional test framework
for configuration files. These tests can be found in the \(aq/pylint/test/config\(aq directory.
.sp
To create a new test create a new file with an unused name in the directory of that type
of configuration file. Subsequently add a \fBfilename.result.json\fP file with \(aqfilename\(aq
being the same name as your configuration file. This file should record
what the configuration should be \fBcompared to the standard configuration\fP\&.
.sp
For example, if the configuration should add a warning to the list of disabled messages
and you changed the configuration for \fBjob\fP to 10 instead of the default 1 the
\fB\&.json\fP file should include:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
\(dqfunctional_append\(dq: {
    \(dqdisable\(dq: [[\(dqa\-message\-to\-be\-added\(dq],]
}
\(dqjobs\(dq: 10,
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Similarly if a message should be removed you can add the following to the \fB\&.json\fP file:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
\(dqfunctional_remove\(dq: {
    \(dqdisable\(dq: [[\(dqa\-message\-to\-be\-removed\(dq],]
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If a configuration is incorrect and should lead to a crash or warning being emitted you can
specify this by adding a \fB\&.out\fP file. This file should have the following name
\fBname_of_configuration_testfile.error_code.out\fP\&. So, if your test is called \fBbad_configuration.toml\fP
and should exit with exit code 2 the \fB\&.out\fP file should be named \fBbad_configuration.2.out\fP\&.
The content of the \fB\&.out\fP file should have a similar pattern as a normal Pylint output. Note that the
module name should be \fB{abspath}\fP and the file name \fB{relpath}\fP\&.
.SS Profiling and performance analysis
.SS Performance analysis for Pylint
.sp
To analyse the performance of Pylint we recommend to use the \fBcProfile\fP module
from \fBstdlib\fP\&. Together with the \fBpstats\fP module this should give you all the tools
you need to profile a Pylint run and see which functions take how long to run.
.sp
The documentation for both modules can be found at cProfile \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:profile\:.html>\&.
.sp
To profile a run of Pylint over itself you can use the following code and run it from the base directory.
Note that \fBcProfile\fP will create a document called \fBstats\fP that is then read by \fBpstats\fP\&. The
human\-readable output will be stored by \fBpstats\fP in \fB\&./profiler_stats\fP\&. It will be sorted by
\fBcumulative time\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import cProfile
import pstats
import sys

sys.argv = [\(dqpylint\(dq, \(dqpylint\(dq]
cProfile.run(\(dqfrom pylint import __main__\(dq, \(dqstats\(dq)

with open(\(dqprofiler_stats\(dq, \(dqw\(dq, encoding=\(dqutf\-8\(dq) as file:
    stats = pstats.Stats(\(dqstats\(dq, stream=file)
    stats.sort_stats(\(dqcumtime\(dq)
    stats.print_stats()
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
You can also interact with the stats object by sorting or restricting the output.
For example, to only print functions from the \fBpylint\fP module and sort by cumulative time you could
use:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import cProfile
import pstats
import sys

sys.argv = [\(dqpylint\(dq, \(dqpylint\(dq]
cProfile.run(\(dqfrom pylint import __main__\(dq, \(dqstats\(dq)

with open(\(dqprofiler_stats\(dq, \(dqw\(dq, encoding=\(dqutf\-8\(dq) as file:
    stats = pstats.Stats(\(dqstats\(dq, stream=file)
    stats.sort_stats(\(dqcumtime\(dq)
    stats.print_stats(\(dqpylint/pylint\(dq)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Lastly, to profile a run over your own module or code you can use:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import cProfile
import pstats
import sys

sys.argv = [\(dqpylint\(dq, \(dqyour_dir/your_file\(dq]
cProfile.run(\(dqfrom pylint import __main__\(dq, \(dqstats\(dq)

with open(\(dqprofiler_stats\(dq, \(dqw\(dq, encoding=\(dqutf\-8\(dq) as file:
    stats = pstats.Stats(\(dqstats\(dq, stream=file)
    stats.sort_stats(\(dqcumtime\(dq)
    stats.print_stats()
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The documentation of the \fBpstats\fP module discusses other possibilities to interact with
the profiling output.
.SS Performance analysis of a specific checker
.sp
To analyse the performance of specific checker within Pylint we can use the human\-readable output
created by \fBpstats\fP\&.
.sp
If you search in the \fBprofiler_stats\fP file for the file name of the checker you will find all functional
calls from functions within the checker. Let\(aqs say we want to check the \fBvisit_importfrom\fP method of the
\fBvariables\fP checker:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
ncalls  tottime  percall  cumtime  percall filename:lineno(function)
622    0.006    0.000    8.039    0.013 /MY_PROGRAMMING_DIR/pylint/pylint/checkers/variables.py:1445(visit_importfrom)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The previous line tells us that this method was called 622 times during the profile and we were inside the
function itself for 6 ms in total. The time per call is less than a millisecond (0.006 / 622)
and thus is displayed as being 0.
.sp
Often you are more interested in the cumulative time (per call). This refers to the time spent within the function
and any of the functions it called or the functions they called (etc.). In our example, the \fBvisit_importfrom\fP
method and all of its child\-functions took a little over 8 seconds to execute, with an execution time of
0.013 ms per call.
.sp
You can also search the \fBprofiler_stats\fP for an individual function you want to check. For example
\fB_analyse_fallback_blocks\fP, a function called by \fBvisit_importfrom\fP in the \fBvariables\fP checker. This
allows more detailed analysis of specific functions:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
ncalls  tottime  percall  cumtime  percall filename:lineno(function)
1    0.000    0.000    0.000    0.000 /MY_PROGRAMMING_DIR/pylint/pylint/checkers/variables.py:1511(_analyse_fallback_blocks)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Parsing the profiler stats with other tools
.sp
Often you might want to create a visual representation of your profiling stats. A good tool
to do this is gprof2dot \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:jrfonseca/\:gprof2dot>\&. This tool can create a \fB\&.dot\fP file from the profiling stats
created by \fBcProfile\fP and \fBpstats\fP\&. You can then convert the \fB\&.dot\fP file to a \fB\&.png\fP
file with one of the many converters found online.
.sp
You can read the gprof2dot \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:jrfonseca/\:gprof2dot> documentation for installation instructions for your specific environment.
.sp
Another option would be snakeviz \%<https://\:jiffyclub\:.github\:.io/\:snakeviz>\&.
.SS OSS\-Fuzz integration
.SS Platform overview
.sp
OSS\-Fuzz \%<https://\:google\:.github\:.io/\:oss-fuzz> is Google\(aqs free fuzzing platform for open source
software. It runs astroid\(aqs fuzz targets to help detect reliability issues that could affect astroid
and Pylint.
.sp
Google provides public build logs \%<https://\:oss-fuzz-build-logs\:.storage\:.googleapis\:.com/\:index\:.html#\:astroid>
and fuzzing stats \%<https://\:introspector\:.oss-fuzz\:.com/\:project-profile?\:project=astroid>, but most
of the details about bug reports and fuzzed testcases require approved access.
.SS Gaining access
.sp
The configuration files for the OSS\-Fuzz integration can be found in the
OSS\-Fuzz repository \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:google/\:oss-fuzz/\:tree/\:master/\:projects/\:astroid>\&.
The \fBproject.yaml\fP file controls who has access to bug reports and testcases. Ping the
maintainers if you\(aqd like to be added to the list (note: a Google account is required for
access).
.SS Fuzzing progress
.sp
Once you have access to OSS\-Fuzz, you can log in to \%<https://\:oss-fuzz\:.com> with your Google account
to see a dashboard of astroid\(aqs fuzzing progress.
.SS Testcases
.sp
The dashboard contains a link to a testcases page \%<https://\:oss-fuzz\:.com/\:testcases?\:project=astroid&\:open=yes>
that lists all testcases that currently trigger a bug in astroid.
.sp
Every testcase has a dedicated page with links to view and download a minimized testcase for
reproducing the failure. Each testcase page also contains a stacktrace for the failure and stats
about how often the failure is encountered while fuzzing.
.SS Reproducing a failure
.sp
You can download a minimized testcase and run it locally to debug a failure on your machine.
For example, to reproduce a failure with the \fBfuzz_parse\fP fuzz target, you can run the following
commands:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
mkdir fuzzing\-repro
cd fuzzing\-repro

# Note: Atheris doesn\(aqt support Python 3.12+ yet:
# https://github.com/google/atheris/issues/82
uv venv \-\-python 3.11
source .venv/bin/activate

git clone https://github.com/pylint\-dev/astroid.git
cd astroid

uv pip install atheris==2.3.0
uv pip install \-\-editable .

# Save the minimized testcase as \(gaminimized.py\(ga in the astroid directory

cat << EOF > ./run_fuzz_parse.py

import astroid
import atheris

with open(\(aqminimized.py\(aq, \(aqrb\(aq) as f:
    fdp = atheris.FuzzedDataProvider(f.read())

code = fdp.ConsumeUnicodeNoSurrogates(fdp.ConsumeIntInRange(0, 4096))
astroid.builder.parse(code)
EOF

python ./run_fuzz_parse.py
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If the failure does not reproduce locally, you can try reproducing the issue in an OSS\-Fuzz
container:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
git clone https://github.com/google/oss\-fuzz.git
cd oss\-fuzz

python infra/helper.py build_image astroid
python infra/helper.py build_fuzzers astroid
python infra/helper.py reproduce astroid fuzz_parse minimized.py
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Some failures may only be reproducible in an OSS\-Fuzz container because of differences in Python
versions between the OSS\-Fuzz platform and your local environment.
.SS Code coverage
.sp
The dashboard also links to code coverage data for individual fuzz targets and combined code
coverage data for all targets (click on the \(dqTOTAL COVERAGE\(dq link for the combined data).
.sp
The combined coverage data is helpful for identifying coverage gaps, insufficient corpus data, and
potential candidates for future fuzz targets.
.SS Bug reports
.sp
Bug reports for new failures are automatically filed in the OSS\-Fuzz bug tracker with an
astroid label \%<https://\:issues\:.oss-fuzz\:.com/\:issues?\:q=project:astroid%20status:open>\&.
Make sure you are logged in to view all existing issues.
.SS Build maintenance
.sp
Google runs compiled fuzz targets on Google Compute Engine VMs. This architecture requires each
project to provide a \fBDockerfile\fP and \fBbuild.sh\fP script to download code, configure
dependencies, compile fuzz targets, and package any corpus files.
.sp
astroid\(aqs build files and fuzz\-target code can be found in the
OSS\-Fuzz repo \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:google/\:oss-fuzz/\:blob/\:master/\:projects/\:astroid>\&.
.sp
If dependencies change or if new fuzz targets are added, then you may need to modify the build files
and build a new Docker image for OSS\-Fuzz.
.SS Building an image
.sp
Run the following commands to build astroid\(aqs OSS\-Fuzz image and fuzz targets:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
git clone https://github.com/google/oss\-fuzz.git
cd oss\-fuzz

python infra/helper.py build_image astroid
python infra/helper.py build_fuzzers astroid
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Any changes you make to the build files must be submitted as pull requests to the OSS\-Fuzz repo.
.SS Debugging build failures
.sp
You can debug build failures during the \fBbuild_fuzzers\fP stage by creating a container and manually
running the \fBcompile\fP command:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# Create a container for building fuzz targets
python infra/helper.py shell astroid

# Run this command inside the container to build the fuzz targets
compile
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The \fBbuild.sh\fP script will be located at \fB/src/build.sh\fP inside the container.
.SS Quick links
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
OSS\-Fuzz dashboard \%<https://\:oss-fuzz\:.com>
.IP \(bu 2
OSS\-Fuzz configuration files, build scripts, and fuzz targets for astroid \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:google/\:oss-fuzz/\:tree/\:master/\:projects/\:astroid>
.IP \(bu 2
All open OSS\-Fuzz bugs for astroid \%<https://\:issues\:.oss-fuzz\:.com/\:issues?\:q=project:astroid%20status:open>
.IP \(bu 2
Google\(aqs OSS\-Fuzz documentation \%<https://\:google\:.github\:.io/\:oss-fuzz>
.UNINDENT
.SS Releasing a pylint version
.sp
So, you want to release the \fBX.Y.Z\fP version of pylint ?
.SS Releasing a major or minor version
.sp
\fBBefore releasing a major or minor version check if there are any
unreleased commits on the maintenance branch. If so, release a last
patch release first. See \(ga\(gaReleasing a patch version\(ga\(ga.\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Write the \fBSummary \-\- Release highlights\fP in \fBdoc/whatsnew\fP and
upgrade the release date.
.IP \(bu 2
Install the release dependencies:
\fBpip3 install \-r requirements_test.txt\fP\&. This pins the exact
\fBastroid\fP version used by the CI (see \fBrequirements_test_min.txt\fP).
Make sure this pinned version is the one installed before running
\fBtbump\fP: a different \fBastroid\fP produces different functional test
output, which then gets committed into the release and breaks the CI.
.IP \(bu 2
Bump the version and release by using
\fBtbump X.Y.0 \-\-no\-push \-\-no\-tag\fP\&. (For example:
\fBtbump 2.4.0 \-\-no\-push \-\-no\-tag\fP)
.IP \(bu 2
Check the commit created with \fBgit show\fP amend the commit if
required.
.IP \(bu 2
Move the \fBmain\fP branch up to a dev version with \fBtbump\fP:
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
tbump X.Y+1.0\-dev0 \-\-no\-tag \-\-no\-push  # You can interrupt after the first step
git commit \-am \(dqUpgrade the version to x.y+1.0\-dev0 following x.y.0 release\(dq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
For example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
tbump 2.5.0\-dev0 \-\-no\-tag \-\-no\-push
git commit \-am \(dqUpgrade the version to 2.5.0\-dev0 following 2.4.0 release\(dq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
tbump will have created a new \fBWhat\(aqs new in Pylint X.Y+1\fP document.
Add it to \fBdoc/whatsnew/3/index.rst\fP\&. Take a look at the examples from \fBdoc/whatsnew\fP\&.
Commit that with \fBgit commit \-a \-\-amend\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Push to a release branch
.IP \(bu 2
Open a merge request with the two commits (no one can push directly
on \fBmain\fP)
.IP \(bu 2
After the merge, recover the merged commits on \fBmain\fP and tag the
first one (the version should be \fBX.Y.Z\fP) as \fBvX.Y.Z\fP (For
example: \fBv2.4.0\fP)
.IP \(bu 2
Push the tag.
.IP \(bu 2
Release the version on GitHub with the same name as the tag and copy
and paste the appropriate changelog in the description. This triggers
the PyPI release.
.IP \(bu 2
Create a \fBmaintenance/X.Y.x\fP (For example: \fBmaintenance/2.4.x\fP
from the \fBv2.4.0\fP tag.)
.IP \(bu 2
Upgrade the pattern for the protected branches in the settings under
\fBBranches\fP / \fBBranch protection rules\fP\&. (For example:
\fBmaintenance/2.4*\fP instead of \fBmaintenance/2.3*\fP\&.). There’s a lot
of configuration done in these settings, do NOT recreate it from
scratch.
.IP \(bu 2
Delete the \fBmaintenance/X.Y\-1.x\fP branch. (For example:
\fBmaintenance/2.3.x\fP)
.IP \(bu 2
Select all the \fIclosed\fP issues labelled \fBbackport maintenance/X.Y\-1.x\fP and
label them \fBbackported\fP, then rename the
\fBbackport maintenance/X.Y\-1.x\fP label to
\fBbackport maintenance/X.Y.x\fP (for example rename
\fBbackport maintenance/2.3.x\fP to \fBbackport maintenance/2.4.x\fP)
.IP \(bu 2
Close the current milestone and create the new ones (For example:
close \fB2.4.0\fP, create \fB2.4.1\fP and \fB2.6.0\fP)
.IP \(bu 2
Hide and deactivate all the patch releases for the previous minor
release on
readthedocs \%<https://\:readthedocs\:.org/\:projects/\:pylint/\:versions>,
except the last one. (For example: hide \fBv2.4.0\fP, \fBv2.4.1\fP,
\fBv2.4.2\fP and keep only \fBv2.4.3\fP)
.UNINDENT
.SS Back\-porting a fix from \fBmain\fP to the maintenance branch
.sp
Whenever a PR on \fBmain\fP should be released in a patch release on the
current maintenance branch:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Label the PR with \fBbackport maintenance/X.Y\-1.x\fP\&. (For example
\fBbackport maintenance/2.3.x\fP)
.IP \(bu 2
Squash the PR before merging (alternatively rebase if there’s a
single commit)
.IP \(bu 2
(If the automated cherry\-pick has conflicts)
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add a \fBNeeds backport\fP label and do it manually.
.IP \(bu 2
You might alternatively also:
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
Cherry\-pick the changes that create the conflict if it’s not a
new feature before doing the original PR cherry\-pick manually.
.IP \(bu 2
Decide to wait for the next minor to release the PR
.IP \(bu 2
In any case upgrade the milestones in the original PR and newly
cherry\-picked PR to match reality.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Release a patch version
.UNINDENT
.SS Releasing a patch version
.sp
We release patch versions when a crash or a bug is fixed on the main
branch and has been cherry\-picked on the maintenance branch.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Install the release dependencies:
\fBpip3 install \-r requirements_test.txt\fP\&. This pins the exact
\fBastroid\fP version used by the CI (see \fBrequirements_test_min.txt\fP).
Make sure this pinned version is the one installed before running
\fBtbump\fP: a different \fBastroid\fP produces different functional test
output, which then gets committed into the release and breaks the CI.
.IP \(bu 2
Bump the version and release by using \fBtbump X.Y\-1.Z \-\-no\-push\fP\&.
(For example: \fBtbump 2.3.5 \-\-no\-push\fP)
.IP \(bu 2
Check the result visually with \fBgit show\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Open a merge request of \fBrelease\-X.Y\-1.Z\(aq\fP in \fBmaintenance/X.Y.x\fP
(For example: \fBrelease\-2.3.5\-branch\fP in \fBmaintenance/2.3.x\fP) to
run the CI tests for this branch.
.IP \(bu 2
Create and push the tag.
.IP \(bu 2
Release the version on GitHub with the same name as the tag and copy
and paste the changelog from the ReadtheDoc generated documentation
from the pull request pipeline in the description. This triggers the
PyPI release.
.IP \(bu 2
Merge the \fBmaintenance/X.Y.x\fP branch on the main branch. The main
branch should have the changelog for \fBX.Y\-1.Z+1\fP (For example
\fBv2.3.6\fP). This merge is required so \fBpre\-commit autoupdate\fP
works for pylint.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix version conflicts properly, or bump the version to \fBX.Y.0\-devZ\fP
(For example: \fB2.4.0\-dev6\fP) before pushing on the main branch
.IP \(bu 2
Close the current milestone and create the new one (For example:
close \fB2.3.5\fP, create \fB2.3.6\fP)
.UNINDENT
.SS Milestone handling
.sp
We move issues that were not done to the next milestone and block
releases only if there are any open issues labelled as \fBblocker\fP\&.
.SS Governance
.SS How to become part of the project ?
.SS How to become a contributor ?
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Follow the code of conduct
.IP \(bu 2
Search by yourself before asking for help
.IP \(bu 2
Open an issue
.IP \(bu 2
Investigate an issue and report your finding
.IP \(bu 2
Open a merge request directly if you feel it\(aqs a consensual change
.UNINDENT
.sp
Reporting a bug is being a contributor already.
.SS How to become a triager ?
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Create a pylint plugin, then migrate it to the \(aqpylint\-dev\(aq github organization.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Or:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Contribute for more than 3 releases consistently.
.IP \(bu 2
Do not be too opinionated, follow the code of conduct without requiring emotional
works from the maintainers. It does not mean that disagreements are impossible,
only that arguments should stay technical and reasonable so the conversation
is civil and productive.
.IP \(bu 2
Have a maintainer suggest that you become triager, without you asking
.IP \(bu 2
Get unanimous approval or neutral agreement from current maintainers.
.UNINDENT
.SS How to become a maintainer ?
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Take ownership of a part of the code that is not maintained well at the moment
or that you contributed personally (if we feel we can\(aqt merge something without
your review, you\(aqre going to be able to merge those yourself soon).
.UNINDENT
.sp
Or:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Contribute two big code merge requests over multiple releases (for example
one checker in 2.13 and the following bug after release and one complicated
bug fixes in 2.14). Otherwise contributing for more than 3 releases consistently
with great technical and interpersonal skills.
.IP \(bu 2
Triage for multiple months (close duplicate, clean up issues, answer questions...)
.IP \(bu 2
Have an admin suggest that you become maintainer, without you asking
.IP \(bu 2
Get unanimous approval or neutral agreement from current maintainers.
.UNINDENT
.SS How to become an admin ?
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Contribute for several hundreds of commits over a long period of time
with excellent interpersonal skills and code quality.
.IP \(bu 2
Maintain pylint for multiple years (code review, triaging and maintenance tasks).
.IP \(bu 2
At this point probably have another admin leave the project or
become inactive for years.
.IP \(bu 2
Have an admin suggest that you become an admin, without you asking.
.IP \(bu 2
Get unanimous approval or neutral agreement from current admins.
.UNINDENT
.SS How are decisions made ?
.sp
Everyone is expected to follow the code of conduct. pylint is a do\-ocracy / democracy.
You\(aqre not allowed to behave poorly because you contributed a lot. But if
you\(aqre not going to do the future maintenance work, your valid opinions might not be
taken into account by those that will be affected by it.
.SS What are the fundamental tenets of pylint development?
.sp
General:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
We favor correctness over performance, because pylint is not used primarily
for its performance. Performance is still important and needs to be taken into
account from the get go.
.IP \(bu 2
We then favor false negatives over false positives if correctness is
impossible to achieve.
.IP \(bu 2
We try to keep the configuration sane, but if there\(aqs a hard decision to take we
add an option so that pylint is multiple sizes fit all (after configuration)
.UNINDENT
.sp
Where to add a new checker or message:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Error messages (things that will result in an error if run) should be builtin
checks, activated by default
.IP \(bu 2
Messages that are opinionated, even slightly, should be opt\-in (added as an extension \%<#\:plugins>)
.IP \(bu 2
We don\(aqt shy away from opinionated checks (like the while checker), but there\(aqs such a
thing as too opinionated, if something is too opinionated it should be an external
pylint plugin \%<#\:plugins>\&.
.UNINDENT
.SS How are disagreements handled ?
.sp
When something is not consensual users, maintainers, and admins discuss until an
agreement is reached.
.sp
Depending on the difficulty of the discussion and the importance of a fast resolution,
a decision can be taken:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Unanimously between discussion participants, contributors and maintainers (preferably)
.IP \(bu 2
By asking discussion participants for their opinions with an emoji survey in the
issue and then using the majority if no maintainers feel strongly about the issue.
.IP \(bu 2
By majority of admins if no admins feel strongly about the issue.
.IP \(bu 2
By asking all users for their opinions in a new issue that will be pinned for
multiple months before taking the decision if two admins feel strongly on an
opposite side of the issue. Once the result is obvious the majority decision
is not up for discussion anymore.
.UNINDENT
.SS Pyreverse
.sp
\fBpyreverse\fP is a powerful tool that creates UML diagrams from your Python code. It helps you visualize:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Package dependencies and structure
.IP \(bu 2
Class hierarchies and relationships
.IP \(bu 2
Method and attribute organization
.UNINDENT
.SS Output Formats
.sp
\fBpyreverse\fP supports multiple output formats:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
.INDENT 2.0
.TP
.B Native formats:
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\&.dot\fP/\fB\&.gv\fP (Graphviz)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\&.puml\fP/\fB\&.plantuml\fP (PlantUML)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\&.mmd\fP/\fB\&.html\fP (MermaidJS)
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
.INDENT 2.0
.TP
.B Additional formats (requires Graphviz installation):
.INDENT 7.0
.IP \(bu 2
All Graphviz output formats \%<https://\:graphviz\:.org/\:docs/\:outputs> (PNG, SVG, PDF, etc.)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpyreverse\fP first generates a temporary \fB\&.gv\fP file, which is then fed to Graphviz to generate the final image
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Getting Started
.sp
Check out the Usage \%<> guide to learn about available options, or see Example Output \%<>
for sample diagrams and common use cases.
.SS Usage
.sp
\fBpyreverse\fP is run from the command line using the following syntax:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
pyreverse [options] <packages>
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
where \fB<packages>\fP is one or more Python packages or modules to analyze.
.sp
The available options are organized into the following categories:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Filtering and Scope \- Control which classes and relationships appear in your diagrams
.IP \(bu 2
Display Options \- Customize the visual appearance including colors and labels
.IP \(bu 2
Output Control \- Select output formats and set the destination directory
.IP \(bu 2
Project Configuration \- Define project settings like source roots and ignored files
.UNINDENT
.SS Filtering and Scope
.SS \-\-all\-ancestors
.sp
\fIShow all ancestors of all classes in <projects>.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBNone\fP
.SS \-\-all\-associated
.sp
\fIShow all classes associated with the target classes, including indirect associations.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBNone\fP
.SS \-\-class
.sp
\fICreate a class diagram with all classes related to <class>; this uses by default the options \-ASmy\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBNone\fP
.SS \-\-filter\-mode
.sp
\fIFilter attributes and functions according to <mode>. Correct modes are:
\(aqPUB_ONLY\(aq filter all non public attributes [DEFAULT], equivalent to PRIVATE+SPECIAL
\(aqALL\(aq no filter
\(aqSPECIAL\(aq filter Python special functions except constructor
\(aqOTHER\(aq filter protected and private attributes\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBPUB_ONLY\fP
.SS \-\-max\-depth
.sp
\fIMaximum depth of packages/modules to include in the diagram, relative to the deepest specified package. A depth of 0 shows only the specified packages/modules, while 1 includes their immediate children, etc. When specifying nested packages,  depth is calculated from the deepest package level. If not specified, all packages/modules in the hierarchy are shown.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBNone\fP
.SS \-\-show\-ancestors
.sp
\fIShow <ancestor> generations of ancestor classes not in <projects>.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBNone\fP
.SS \-\-show\-associated
.sp
\fIShow <association_level> levels of associated classes not in <projects>.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBNone\fP
.SS \-\-show\-builtin
.sp
\fIInclude builtin objects in representation of classes.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBFalse\fP
.SS \-\-show\-stdlib
.sp
\fIInclude standard library objects in representation of classes.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBFalse\fP
.SS Display Options
.SS \-\-color\-palette
.sp
\fIComma separated list of colors to use for the package depth coloring.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fB(\(aq#77AADD\(aq, \(aq#99DDFF\(aq, \(aq#44BB99\(aq, \(aq#BBCC33\(aq, \(aq#AAAA00\(aq, \(aq#EEDD88\(aq, \(aq#EE8866\(aq, \(aq#FFAABB\(aq, \(aq#DDDDDD\(aq)\fP
.SS \-\-colorized
.sp
\fIUse colored output. Classes/modules of the same package get the same color.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBFalse\fP
.SS \-\-max\-color\-depth
.sp
\fIUse separate colors up to package depth of <depth>. Higher depths will reuse colors.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fB2\fP
.SS \-\-module\-names
.sp
\fIInclude module name in the representation of classes.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBNone\fP
.SS \-\-no\-standalone
.sp
\fIOnly show nodes with connections.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBFalse\fP
.SS \-\-only\-classnames
.sp
\fIDon\(aqt show attributes and methods in the class boxes; this disables \-f values.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBFalse\fP
.SS Output Control
.SS \-\-output
.sp
\fICreate a *.<format> output file if format is available. Available formats are: .dot, .puml, .plantuml, .mmd, .html. Any other format will be tried to be created by using the \(aqdot\(aq command line tool, which requires a graphviz installation. In this case, these additional formats are available (see \(gaGraphviz output formats <https://graphviz.org/docs/outputs>\(ga_).\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBdot\fP
.SS \-\-output\-directory
.sp
\fISet the output directory path.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP \fB\(dq\(dq\fP
.SS Project Configuration
.SS \-\-ignore
.sp
\fIFiles or directories to be skipped. They should be base names, not paths.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fB(\(aqCVS\(aq,)\fP
.SS \-\-project
.sp
\fISet the project name. This will later be appended to the output file names.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP \fB\(dq\(dq\fP
.SS \-\-source\-roots
.sp
\fIAdd paths to the list of the source roots. Supports globbing patterns. The source root is an absolute path or a path relative to the current working directory used to determine a package namespace for modules located under the source root.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fB()\fP
.SS \-\-verbose
.sp
\fIMakes pyreverse more verbose/talkative. Mostly useful for debugging.\fP
.sp
\fBDefault:\fP  \fBFalse\fP
.SS Example Output
.sp
Example diagrams generated with the \fB\&.puml\fP output format are shown below.
.SS Package Diagram
[image: Package diagram generated by pyreverse]
[image]
.SS Class Diagram
[image: Class diagram generated by pyreverse]
[image]
.SS Creating Class Diagrams for Specific Classes
.sp
In many cases creating a single diagram depicting all classes in the project yields a rather unwieldy, giant diagram.
While limiting the input path to a single package or module can already help greatly to narrow down the scope, the \fB\-c\fP option
provides another way to create a class diagram focusing on a single class and its collaborators.
For example, running:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
pyreverse \-ASmy \-c pylint.checkers.classes.ClassChecker pylint
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
will generate the full class and package diagrams for \fBpylint\fP, but will additionally generate a file \fBpylint.checkers.classes.ClassChecker.dot\fP:
[image: Package diagram generated by pyreverse]
[image]
.SS Symilar
.sp
The console script \fBsymilar\fP finds copy pasted block of text in a set of files. It provides a command line interface to check only the \fBduplicate\-code\fP message.
.sp
It can be invoked with:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
symilar [\-d|\-\-duplicates min_duplicated_lines] [\-i|\-\-ignore\-comments] [\-\-ignore\-docstrings] [\-\-ignore\-imports] [\-\-ignore\-signatures] file1...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
All files that shall be checked have to be passed in explicitly, e.g.:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
symilar foo.py, bar.py, subpackage/spam.py, subpackage/eggs.py
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBsymilar\fP produces output like the following:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
17 similar lines in 2 files
==tests/data/clientmodule_test.py:3
==tests/data/suppliermodule_test.py:12
  class Ancestor:
      \(dq\(dq\(dq Ancestor method \(dq\(dq\(dq
      cls_member = DoNothing()

      def __init__(self, value):
          local_variable = 0
          self.attr = \(aqthis method shouldn\e\(aqt have a docstring\(aq
          self.__value = value

      def get_value(self):
          \(dq\(dq\(dq nice docstring ;\-) \(dq\(dq\(dq
          return self.__value

      def set_value(self, value):
          self.__value = value
          return \(aqthis method shouldn\e\(aqt have a docstring\(aq
TOTAL lines=58 duplicates=17 percent=29.31
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS 4.x
.sp
This is the full list of change in pylint 4.x minors, by categories.
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 4.0
.sp
:Release:4.0
:Date: 2025\-10\-12
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint now supports Python 3.14.
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint\(aqs inference engine (\fBastroid\fP) is now much more precise,
understanding implicit booleanness and ternary expressions. (Thanks @zenlyj!)
.UNINDENT
.sp
Consider this example:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Result:
    errors: dict | None = None

result = Result()
if result.errors:
    result.errors[field_key]
    # inference engine understands result.errors cannot be None
    # pylint no longer raises unsubscriptable\-object
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The required \fBastroid\fP version is now 4.0.0. See the
astroid changelog \%<https://\:pylint\:.readthedocs\:.io/\:projects/\:astroid/\:en/\:latest/\:changelog\:.html#\:what-s-new-in-astroid-4-0-0>
for additional fixes, features, and performance improvements applicable to pylint.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Handling of \fBinvalid\-name\fP at the module level was patchy. Now,
module\-level constants that are reassigned are treated as variables and checked
against \fB\-\-variable\-rgx\fP rather than \fB\-\-const\-rgx\fP\&. Module\-level lists,
sets, and objects can pass against either regex.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Here, \fBLIMIT\fP is reassigned, so pylint only uses \fB\-\-variable\-rgx\fP:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
LIMIT = 500  # [invalid\-name]
if sometimes:
    LIMIT = 1  # [invalid\-name]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If this is undesired, refactor using \fIexclusive\fP assignment so that it is
evident that this assignment happens only once:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if sometimes:
    LIMIT = 1
else:
    LIMIT = 500  # exclusive assignment: uses const regex, no warning
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Lists, sets, and objects still pass against either \fBconst\-rgx\fP or \fBvariable\-rgx\fP
even if reassigned, but are no longer completely skipped:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
MY_LIST = []
my_list = []
My_List = []  # [invalid\-name]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Remember to adjust the
regexes \%<https://\:pylint\:.readthedocs\:.io/\:en/\:latest/\:user_guide/\:messages/\:convention/\:invalid-name\:.html>
and
allow lists \%<https://\:pylint\:.readthedocs\:.io/\:en/\:latest/\:user_guide/\:configuration/\:all-options\:.html#\:good-names>
to your liking.
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 4.0.7?
.sp
Release date: 2026\-08\-09
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBinvalid\-name\fP when a module\-level variable is assigned
an instance of a \fBTypedDict\fP subclass. Such a name is a value, not a type
definition, so it is now checked against the constant or variable regex instead
of \fBclass\-rgx\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #11231 (#11231 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11231>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the \fBbad\-open\-mode\fP check when the \fBmode\fP argument of
\fBopen\fP is the \fBNotImplemented\fP constant (Python >= 3.14).
.sp
Closes #11099 (#11099 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11099>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the \fBnot\-context\-manager\fP and \fBnot\-async\-context\-manager\fP
checks when the context manager infers to a value without a name, such as the
\fBslice\fP returned by \fBwith slice(...)\fP / \fBasync with slice(...)\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #11102 (#11102 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11102>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBnested\-min\-max\fP (\fBW3301\fP) when the inner \fBmin\fP/\fBmax\fP call carries a keyword argument such as \fBkey=\fP\&. Flattening the call dropped the keyword and changed the result, so nested calls whose inner call has keyword arguments are no longer flagged.
.sp
Closes #11130 (#11130 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11130>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false suggestion from \fBnested\-min\-max\fP (\fBW3301\fP): when rewriting a nested \fBmin\fP/\fBmax\fP into a splat call, arguments positioned after the splatted call were silently dropped, so the suggested code changed the result.
.sp
Closes #11134 (#11134 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11134>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBtoo\-many\-locals\fP (\fBR0914\fP): PEP 695 type parameters, i.e. the \fBT1\fP and \fBT2\fP in a generic \fBdef f[T1, T2]\fP signature, were counted as local variables. They are type\-system constructs, not runtime locals, and are now excluded from the local\-variable count.
.sp
Closes #11136 (#11136 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11136>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fIliteral\-comparison\fP (\fIR0123\fP) emitting a corrupted suggestion for identifiers
that contain \fBis\fP (e.g. \fBaxis is 5\fP was rendered \fBax== == 5\fP). The suggestion
is now rebuilt from the operands and operator.
.sp
Closes #11146 (#11146 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11146>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positives in \fIbad\-string\-format\-type\fP (\fIE1307\fP) for valid \fB%\fP formatting:
\fB%i\fP/\fB%u\fP applied to a float (both truncate like \fB%d\fP) and \fB%a\fP applied to any
non\-int type (\fB%a\fP is type\-agnostic like \fB%s\fP/\fB%r\fP).
.sp
Closes #11147 (#11147 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11147>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for useless\-parent\-delegation / W0246 \%<#\:useless-parent-delegation> when an override changes
the default value of a positional\-only parameter.
.sp
Closes #11148 (#11148 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11148>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash in \fBcomparison\-with\-callable\fP when comparing a lambda assigned as a class attribute.
.sp
Closes #11175 (#11175 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11175>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtoo\-many\-lines\fP could be reported at the line of a \fB# pylint: disable=too\-many\-lines\fP
pragma found in a previously linted module. Pragma positions are now reset between
modules, so the message is reported at line 1 (or at the current module\(aqs own pragma)
regardless of which files were linted before.
.sp
Refs #11191 (#11191 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11191>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash when a call unpacks a dictionary whose keys are not string
constants, e.g. \fBcopy.copy(**{\-1: 1})\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #11222 (#11222 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11222>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 4.0.6?
.sp
Release date: 2026\-06\-14
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBimplicit\-str\-concat\fP is no longer emitted for an implicit concatenation of
a raw string with a non\-raw one (e.g. \fBr\(dq\ed\(dq \(dq\en\(dq\fP). Such literals cannot be
merged into a single string, so the concatenation is intentional rather than a
forgotten comma.
.sp
Closes #6663 (#6663 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6663>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBinvalid\-name\fP (C0103) where the default
\fBtypevar\-rgx\fP rejected \fBTypeVar\fP names containing digits, such as
\fBEc2T\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8499 (#8499 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8499>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBtoo\-many\-arguments\fP in (non\-static) methods and classmethods.
.sp
Closes #8675 (#8675 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8675>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBno\-member\fP when a value is inferred to several
possible types and at least one of them defines a dynamic \fB__getattr__\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9833 (#9833 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9833>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBfunction\-redefined\fP (E0102) when reusing names that
match \fBdummy\-variables\-rgx\fP (such as \fB_\fP), which is common for
\fBpytest\-bdd\fP step definitions. This restores the behavior from before pylint
4.0.0; as a consequence the false negative fixed in #9894 is reintroduced for
functions whose name matches \fBdummy\-variables\-rgx\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #10665 (#10665 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10665>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBundefined\-variable\fP false positive when a name used as a \fBmetaclass\fP
argument in a nested class is referenced again later in the module.
.sp
Closes #10823 (#10823 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10823>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBunused\-variable\fP where global variables matching
\fBdummy\-variables\-rgx\fP were still reported as unused when
\fBallow\-global\-unused\-variables\fP was disabled.
.sp
Closes #10890 (#10890 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10890>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBbad\-dunder\-name\fP when there is a user\-defined \fB__suppress_context__\fP attribute on exception subclasses.
.sp
Closes #10960 (#10960 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10960>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP false positive for names bound by \fBfrom X import *\fP in every branch of an \fBif\fP/\fBelif\fP/\fBelse\fP chain.
.sp
Refs #10980 (#10980 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10980>)
.IP \(bu 2
Check for metaclass __call__ signature when evaluating arguments of a class call.
.sp
Closes #11032 (#11032 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11032>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBmethod\-hidden\fP when \fBcached_property\fP is imported directly with \fBfrom functools import cached_property\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #11037 (#11037 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11037>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix the suggestion of \fBunnecessary\-comprehension\fP for a dict comprehension
that iterates a dict directly, e.g. \fB{a: b for a, b in d}\fP\&. Iterating a dict
yields its keys, so the suggestion is now \fBdict(d.keys())\fP instead of the
incorrect \fBdict(d)\fP, which would simply copy \fBd\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8256 (#8256 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8256>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in \fBconsider\-using\-enumerate\fP when the \fBfor\fP loop target is an attribute (e.g. \fBfor self.idx in range(len(x))\fP) rather than a simple variable name.
.sp
Closes #10099 (#10099 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10099>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash when checking \fBattribute\-defined\-outside\-init\fP on classes that inherit from a base class pylint cannot fully analyze.
.sp
Closes #10892 (#10892 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10892>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBadd_message\fP silently overwriting an explicit \fBcol_offset=0\fP (or any other zero\-valued \fBline\fP/\fBend_lineno\fP/\fBend_col_offset\fP) with the AST node\(aqs value. The internal \fB_add_one_message\fP helper used a falsey check (\fBif not col_offset:\fP) to detect an omitted argument, which incorrectly treated a legitimate \fB0\fP the same as \fBNone\fP\&. It now uses an identity check against \fBNone\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #11020 (#11020 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11020>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the name checker when a non\-constant value is passed as the \fBcovariant\fP or \fBcontravariant\fP argument of a \fBTypeVar\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #11022 (#11022 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11022>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the variable checker when a name resolves to a dataclass\-synthesized \fB__init__\fP, which has no line number.
.sp
Closes #11023 (#11023 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11023>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the variables checker when \fBNotImplemented\fP is used as the test of an \fBif\fP statement, which raised a \fBTypeError\fP in a boolean context on Python 3.14.
.sp
Closes #11025 (#11025 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11025>)
.IP \(bu 2
Avoided a crash from the implicit booleaness checker for \fBlen()\fP calls without arguments.
.sp
Closes #11028 (#11028 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11028>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the variables checker when a class declares a metaclass whose
attribute\-access chain does not bottom out at a name (e.g.
\fBclass C(metaclass=None._)\fP).
Originally reported as \fBpylint\-dev/astroid#3066\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #11031 (#11031 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11031>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the name checker when a chained assignment of a \fBTypeAlias\fP
value has a non\-name target such as a \fBSubscript\fP (for example
\fBa[0] = b = TypeAlias\fP).
.sp
Closes #11056 (#11056 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11056>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the deprecated checker when \fB__import__\fP is called with a
non\-string constant argument (for example \fB__import__(1)\fP).
.sp
Closes #11059 (#11059 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11059>)
.IP \(bu 2
Avoid crashing when enum member inference fails while checking enum subclasses.
.sp
Closes #11069 (#11069 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11069>)
.IP \(bu 2
Prevent a crash in \fBunexpected\-keyword\-arg\fP analysis when
\fBinfer_call_result()\fP raises \fBInferenceError\fP while inspecting
decorator return signatures.
.sp
Closes #11070 (#11070 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11070>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the typecheck checker when a class uses a non\-class object
(for example a function) as its \fBmetaclass=\fP argument.
.sp
Closes #11071 (#11071 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11071>)
.IP \(bu 2
Allow digits in ParamSpec and TypeVarTuple names for \fIinvalid\-name\fP check.
.sp
The default \fIparamspec\-rgx\fP and \fItypevartuple\-rgx\fP patterns rejected names
containing digits (e.g. \fBEc2P\fP, \fBS3Ts\fP), emitting a false \fBinvalid\-name\fP
(C0103). Allow digits in the lowercase segments, consistent with the
\fBtypevar\fP and \fBtypealias\fP patterns.
.sp
Closes #11090 (#11090 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:11090>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Performance Improvements
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The duplicate\-code checker no longer runs when its message (R0801) is disabled, even if \fBreports=yes\fP is set. Previously, the checker\(aqs report (RP0801) would cause the expensive similarity computation to run regardless.
.sp
Closes #3443 (#3443 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3443>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 4.0.5?
.sp
Release date: 2026\-02\-20
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix possibly\-used\-before\-assignment false positive when using self.fail() in tests.
.sp
Closes #10743 (#10743 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10743>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positive for \fBlogging\-unsupported\-format\fP when no arguments are provided to logging functions.
.sp
According to Python\(aqs logging documentation, no formatting is performed when no arguments are supplied, so strings like \fBlogging.error(\(dq%test\(dq)\fP are valid.
.sp
Closes #10752 (#10752 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10752>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBinvalid\-name\fP where a dataclass field typed with \fBFinal\fP
was evaluated against the \fBclass_const\fP regex instead of the \fBclass_attribute\fP regex.
.sp
Closes #10790 (#10790 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10790>)
.IP \(bu 2
Avoid emitting \fIunspecified\-encoding\fP (W1514) when \fIpy\-version\fP is 3.15+.
.sp
Refs #10791 (#10791 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10791>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fI\-\-known_third_party\fP config being ignored.
.sp
Closes #10801 (#10801 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10801>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed dynamic color mapping for \(dqfail\-on\(dq messages when using multiple reporter/output formats.
.sp
Closes #10825 (#10825 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10825>)
.IP \(bu 2
dependency on isort is now set to <9, permitting to use isort 8.
.sp
Closes #10857 (#10857 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10857>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 4.0.4?
.sp
Release date: 2025\-11\-30
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positive for \fBinvalid\-name\fP where module\-level constants were incorrectly classified as variables when a class\-level attribute with the same name exists.
.sp
Closes #10719 (#10719 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10719>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBinvalid\-name\fP on an UPPER_CASED name inside an \fBif\fP branch that assigns an object.
.sp
Closes #10745 (#10745 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10745>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 4.0.3?
.sp
Release date: 2025\-11\-13
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add Enum dunder methods \fB_generate_next_value_\fP, \fB_missing_\fP, \fB_numeric_repr_\fP, \fB_add_alias_\fP, and \fB_add_value_alias_\fP to the list passed to \fB\-\-good\-dunder\-names\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #10435 (#10435 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10435>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positive for \fBinvalid\-name\fP with \fBtyping.Annotated\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #10696 (#10696 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10696>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBf\-string\-without\-interpolation\fP with template strings
when using format spec.
.sp
Closes #10702 (#10702 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10702>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive when an UPPER_CASED class attribute was raising an
\fBinvalid\-name\fP when typed with \fBFinal\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #10711 (#10711 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10711>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBunbalanced\-tuple\-unpacking\fP when a tuple is assigned to a function call and the structure of the function\(aqs return value is ambiguous.
.sp
Closes #10721 (#10721 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10721>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Make \(aqignore\(aq option work as expected again.
.sp
Closes #10669 (#10669 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10669>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash for \fBconsider\-using\-assignment\-expr\fP when a variable annotation without assignment
is used as the \fBif\fP test expression.
.sp
Closes #10707 (#10707 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10707>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash for \fBprefer\-typing\-namedtuple\fP and \fBconsider\-math\-not\-float\fP when
a \fBslice\fP object is called.
.sp
Closes #10708 (#10708 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10708>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 4.0.2?
.sp
Release date: 2025\-10\-20
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for invalid\-name / C0103 \%<#\:invalid-name> on a partially uninferable module\-level constant.
.sp
Closes #10652 (#10652 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10652>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for invalid\-name / C0103 \%<#\:invalid-name> on exclusive module\-level assignments
composed of three or more branches. We won\(aqt raise disallowed\-name / C0104 \%<#\:disallowed-name> on module\-level names that can\(aqt be inferred
until a further refactor to remove this false negative is done.
.sp
Closes #10664 (#10664 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10664>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for invalid\-name / C0103 \%<#\:invalid-name> for \fBTypedDict\fP instances.
.sp
Closes #10672 (#10672 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10672>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 4.0.1?
.sp
Release date: 2025\-10\-14
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Exclude \fB__all__\fP and \fB__future__.annotations\fP from \fBunused\-variable\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #10019 (#10019 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10019>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive for \fBbare\-name\-capture\-pattern\fP if a case guard is used.
.sp
Closes #10647 (#10647 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10647>)
.IP \(bu 2
Check enums created with the \fBEnum()\fP functional syntax to pass against the
\fB\-\-class\-rgx\fP for the invalid\-name / C0103 \%<#\:invalid-name> check, like other enums.
.sp
Closes #10660 (#10660 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10660>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 4.0.0?
.sp
Release date: 2025\-10\-12
.SS Breaking Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-name\fP now distinguishes module\-level constants that are assigned only once
from those that are reassigned and now applies \fB\-\-variable\-rgx\fP to the latter. Values
other than literals (lists, sets, objects) can pass against either the constant or
variable regexes (e.g. \(dqLOGGER\(dq or \(dqlogger\(dq but not \(dqLoGgEr\(dq).
.sp
Remember that \fB\-\-good\-names\fP or \fB\-\-good\-names\-rgxs\fP can be provided to explicitly
allow good names.
.sp
Closes #3585 (#3585 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3585>)
.IP \(bu 2
The unused \fBpylintrc\fP argument to \fBPyLinter.__init__()\fP is deprecated
and will be removed.
.sp
Refs #6052 (#6052 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6052>)
.IP \(bu 2
Commented out code blocks such as \fB#    bar() # TODO: remove dead code\fP will no longer emit \fBfixme\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #9255 (#9255 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9255>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpyreverse\fP \fBRun\fP was changed to no longer call \fBsys.exit()\fP in its \fB__init__\fP\&.
You should now call \fBRun(args).run()\fP which will return the exit code instead.
Having a class that always raised a \fBSystemExit\fP exception was considered a bug.
.sp
Normal usage of pyreverse through the CLI will not be affected by this change.
.sp
Refs #9689 (#9689 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9689>)
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBsuggestion\-mode\fP option was removed, as pylint now always emits user\-friendly hints instead
of false\-positive error messages. You should remove it from your conf if it\(aqs defined.
.sp
Refs #9962 (#9962 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9962>)
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBasync.py\fP checker module has been renamed to \fBasync_checker.py\fP since \fBasync\fP is a Python keyword
and cannot be imported directly. This allows for better testing and extensibility of the async checker functionality.
.sp
Refs #10071 (#10071 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10071>)
.IP \(bu 2
The message\-id of \fBcontinue\-in\-finally\fP was changed from \fBE0116\fP to \fBW0136\fP\&. The warning is
now emitted for every Python version since it will raise a syntax warning in Python 3.14.
See PEP 765 \- Disallow return/break/continue that exit a finally block \%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0765>\&.
.sp
Refs #10480 (#10480 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10480>)
.IP \(bu 2
Removed support for \fBnmp.NaN\fP alias for \fBnumpy.NaN\fP being recognized in \(aqnan\-comparison / W0177 \%<#\:nan-comparison>\(aq. Use \fBnp\fP or \fBnumpy\fP instead.
.sp
Refs #10583 (#10583 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10583>)
.IP \(bu 2
Version requirement for \fBisort\fP has been bumped to >=5.0.0.
The internal compatibility for older \fBisort\fP versions exposed via \fBpylint.utils.IsortDriver\fP has
been removed.
.sp
Refs #10637 (#10637 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10637>)
.UNINDENT
.SS New Features
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
.INDENT 2.0
.TP
.B \fBcomparison\-of\-constants\fP now uses the unicode from the ast instead of reformatting from
the node\(aqs values preventing some bad formatting due to \fButf\-8\fP limitation. The message now uses
\fB\(dq\fP instead of \fB\(aq\fP to better work with what the python ast returns.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Refs #8736 (#8736 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8736>)
.IP \(bu 2
Enhanced pyreverse to properly distinguish between UML relationship types (association, aggregation, composition) based on object ownership semantics. Type annotations without assignment are now treated as associations, parameter assignments as aggregations, and object instantiation as compositions.
.sp
Closes #9045
Closes #9267 (#9045 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9045>)
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBfixme\fP check can now search through docstrings as well as comments, by using
\fBcheck\-fixme\-in\-docstring = true\fP in the \fB[tool.pylint.miscellaneous]\fP section.
.sp
Closes #9255 (#9255 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9255>)
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBuse\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-x\fP checks now distinguish between comparisons
used in boolean contexts and those that are not, enabling them to provide more accurate refactoring suggestions.
.sp
Closes #9353 (#9353 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9353>)
.IP \(bu 2
The verbose option now outputs the filenames of the files that have been checked.
Previously, it only included the number of checked and skipped files.
.sp
Closes #9357 (#9357 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9357>)
.IP \(bu 2
colorized reporter now colorizes messages/categories that have been configured as \fBfail\-on\fP in red inverse.
This makes it easier to quickly find the errors that are causing pylint CI job failures.
.sp
Closes #9898 (#9898 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9898>)
.IP \(bu 2
Enhanced support for @property decorator in pyreverse to correctly display return types of annotated properties when generating class diagrams.
.sp
Closes #10057 (#10057 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10057>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \-\-max\-depth option to pyreverse to control diagram complexity. A depth of 0 shows only top\-level packages, 1 shows one level of subpackages, etc.
This helps manage visualization of large codebases by limiting the depth of displayed packages and classes.
.sp
Refs #10077 (#10077 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10077>)
.IP \(bu 2
Handle deferred evaluation of annotations in Python 3.14.
.sp
Closes #10149 (#10149 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10149>)
.IP \(bu 2
Enhanced pyreverse to properly detect aggregations for comprehensions (list, dict, set, generator).
.sp
Closes #10236 (#10236 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10236>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpyreverse\fP: add support for colorized output when using output format \fBmmd\fP (MermaidJS) and \fBhtml\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #10242 (#10242 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10242>)
.IP \(bu 2
pypy 3.11 is now officially supported.
.sp
Refs #10287 (#10287 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10287>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add support for Python 3.14.
.sp
Refs #10467 (#10467 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10467>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add naming styles for \fBParamSpec\fP and \fBTypeVarTuple\fP that align with the \fBTypeVar\fP style.
.sp
Refs #10541 (#10541 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10541>)
.UNINDENT
.SS New Checks
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBmatch\-statements\fP checker and the following message:
\fBbare\-name\-capture\-pattern\fP\&.
This will emit an error message when a name capture pattern is used in a match statement which would make the remaining patterns unreachable.
This code is a SyntaxError at runtime.
.sp
Closes #7128 (#7128 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7128>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add new check \fBasync\-context\-manager\-with\-regular\-with\fP to detect async context managers used with regular \fBwith\fP statements instead of \fBasync with\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #10408 (#10408 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10408>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBbreak\-in\-finally\fP warning. Using \fBbreak\fP inside the \fBfinally\fP clause
will raise a syntax warning in Python 3.14.
See PEP 765 \- Disallow return/break/continue that exit a finally block \%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0765>\&.
.sp
Refs #10480 (#10480 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10480>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add new checks for invalid uses of class patterns in \fBmatch\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:reference/\:compound_stmts\:.html#\:match>\&.
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
invalid\-match\-args\-definition / E1902 \%<#\:invalid-match-args-definition> is emitted if \fBobject.__match_args__\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:reference/\:datamodel\:.html#\:object\:.__match_args__> isn\(aqt a tuple of strings.
.IP \(bu 2
too\-many\-positional\-sub\-patterns / E1903 \%<#\:too-many-positional-sub-patterns> if there are more positional sub\-patterns than specified in \fBobject.__match_args__\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:reference/\:datamodel\:.html#\:object\:.__match_args__>\&.
.IP \(bu 2
multiple\-class\-sub\-patterns / E1904 \%<#\:multiple-class-sub-patterns> if there are multiple sub\-patterns for the same attribute.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Refs #10559 (#10559 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10559>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add additional checks for suboptimal uses of class patterns in \fBmatch\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:reference/\:compound_stmts\:.html#\:match>\&.
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
match\-class\-bind\-self / R1905 \%<#\:match-class-bind-self> is emitted if a name is bound to \fBself\fP instead of
using an \fBas\fP pattern.
.IP \(bu 2
match\-class\-positional\-attributes / R1906 \%<#\:match-class-positional-attributes> is emitted if a class pattern has positional
attributes when keywords could be used.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Refs #10587 (#10587 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10587>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add a \fBconsider\-math\-not\-float\fP message. \fBfloat(\(dqnan\(dq)\fP and \fBfloat(\(dqinf\(dq)\fP are slower
than their counterpart \fBmath.inf\fP and \fBmath.nan\fP by a factor of 4 (notwithstanding
the initial import of math) and they are also not well typed when using mypy.
This check also catches typos in float calls as a side effect.
.sp
The Code Style checker \%<#\:pylint-extensions-code-style> need to be activated for this check to work.
.sp
Refs #10621 (#10621 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10621>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when a variable defined under
an \fBif\fP and via a named expression (walrus operator) is used later when guarded
under the same \fBif\fP test.
.sp
Closes #10061 (#10061 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10061>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix no\-name\-in\-module / E0611 \%<#\:no-name-in-module> for members of \fBconcurrent.futures\fP with Python 3.14.
.sp
Closes #10632 (#10632 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10632>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Negatives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negative for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when a \fBTYPE_CHECKING\fP import is used as a type annotation prior to erroneous usage.
.sp
Refs #8893 (#8893 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8893>)
.IP \(bu 2
Match cases are now counted as edges in the McCabe graph and will increase the complexity accordingly.
.sp
Refs #9667 (#9667 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9667>)
.IP \(bu 2
Check module\-level constants with type annotations for \fBinvalid\-name\fP\&.
Remember to adjust \fBconst\-naming\-style\fP or \fBconst\-rgx\fP to your liking.
.sp
Closes #9770 (#9770 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9770>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negative where function\-redefined (E0102) was not reported for functions with a leading underscore.
.sp
Closes #9894 (#9894 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9894>)
.IP \(bu 2
We now raise a \fBlogging\-too\-few\-args\fP for format string with no
interpolation arguments at all (i.e. for something like \fBlogging.debug(\(dqAwaiting process %s\(dq)\fP
or \fBlogging.debug(\(dqAwaiting process {pid}\(dq)\fP). Previously we did not raise for such case.
.sp
Closes #9999 (#9999 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9999>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negative for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when a function is defined inside a \fBTYPE_CHECKING\fP guard block and used later.
.sp
Closes #10028 (#10028 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10028>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false negative for \fBpossibly\-used\-before\-assignment\fP when a variable is conditionally defined
and later assigned to a type\-annotated variable.
.sp
Closes #10421 (#10421 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10421>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negative for \fBdeprecated\-module\fP when a \fB__import__\fP method is used instead of \fBimport\fP sentence.
.sp
Refs #10453 (#10453 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10453>)
.IP \(bu 2
Count match cases for \fBtoo\-many\-branches\fP check.
.sp
Refs #10542 (#10542 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10542>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-negative where unused\-import / W0611 \%<#\:unused-import> was not reported for names referenced in a preceding \fBglobal\fP statement.
.sp
Refs #10633 (#10633 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10633>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
When displaying unicode with surrogates (or other potential \fBUnicodeEncodeError\fP),
pylint will now display a \(aq?\(aq character (using \fBencode(encoding=\(dqutf\-8\(dq, errors=\(dqreplace\(dq)\fP)
instead of crashing. The functional tests classes are also updated to handle this case.
.sp
Closes #8736. (#8736 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8736>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed unidiomatic\-typecheck only checking left\-hand side.
.sp
Closes #10217 (#10217 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10217>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash caused by malformed format strings when using \fB\&.format\fP with keyword arguments.
.sp
Closes #10282 (#10282 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10282>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP when using \fBquit()\fP or \fBexit()\fP functions.
.sp
Closes #10508 (#10508 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10508>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in nested\-min\-max / W3301 \%<#\:nested-min-max> when using \fBbuiltins.min\fP or \fBbuiltins.max\fP
instead of \fBmin\fP or \fBmax\fP directly.
.sp
Closes #10626 (#10626 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10626>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash in unnecessary\-dict\-index\-lookup / R1733 \%<#\:unnecessary-dict-index-lookup> when the index of an enumerated list
was deleted inside a for loop.
.sp
Closes #10627 (#10627 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10627>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Remove support for launching pylint with Python 3.9.
Code that supports Python 3.9 can still be linted with the \fB\-\-py\-version=3.9\fP setting.
.sp
Refs #10405 (#10405 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10405>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Internal Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Modified test framework to allow for different test output for different Python versions.
.sp
Refs #10382 (#10382 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10382>)
.UNINDENT
.SS 3.x
.sp
This is the full list of change in pylint 3.x minors, by categories.
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 3.3
.sp
:Release:3.3
:Date: 2024\-09\-20
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.3.9?
.sp
Release date: 2025\-10\-05
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix used\-before\-assignment / E0601 \%<#\:used-before-assignment> for PEP 695 type aliases and parameters.
.sp
Closes #9815 (#9815 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9815>)
.IP \(bu 2
No longer flag undeprecated functions in \fBimportlib.resources\fP as deprecated.
.sp
Closes #10593 (#10593 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10593>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP when using \fBquit()\fP or \fBexit()\fP functions.
.sp
Closes #10508 (#10508 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10508>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBundefined\-variable\fP (E0602) for for\-loop variable shadowing patterns like \fBfor item in item:\fP when the variable was previously defined.
.sp
Closes #10562 (#10562 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10562>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed crash in \fBunnecessary\-list\-index\-lookup\fP when starting an enumeration using
minus the length of an iterable inside a dict comprehension when the len call was only
made in this dict comprehension, and not elsewhere. Also changed the approach,
to use inference in all cases but the simple ones, so we don\(aqt have to fix crashes
one by one for arbitrarily complex expressions in enumerate.
.sp
Closes #10510 (#10510 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10510>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.3.8?
.sp
Release date: 2025\-08\-09
.sp
This patch release includes an exceptional fix for a false negative issue.
For details, see: \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:pull/\:10482#\:issuecomment-3164514082>
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positives for possibly\-used\-before\-assignment / E0606 \%<#\:possibly-used-before-assignment> when variables are exhaustively
assigned within a \fBmatch\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:reference/\:compound_stmts\:.html#\:match> block.
.sp
Closes #9668 (#9668 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9668>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for missing\-raises\-doc / W9006 \%<#\:missing-raises-doc> and missing\-yield\-doc / W9013 \%<#\:missing-yield-doc> when the method length is less than docstring\-min\-length.
.sp
Refs #10104 (#10104 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10104>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for unused\-variable / W0612 \%<#\:unused-variable> when multiple except handlers bind the same name under a try block.
.sp
Closes #10426 (#10426 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10426>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Negatives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-negative for used\-before\-assignment / E0601 \%<#\:used-before-assignment> with \fBfrom __future__ import annotations\fP in function definitions.
.sp
Refs #10482 (#10482 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10482>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a bug in Pyreverse where aggregations and associations were included in diagrams regardless of the selected \-\-filter\-mode (such as PUB_ONLY, ALL, etc.).
.sp
Closes #10373 (#10373 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10373>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix double underscores erroneously rendering as bold in pyreverse\(aqs Mermaid output.
.sp
Closes #10402 (#10402 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10402>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.3.7?
.sp
Release date: 2025\-05\-04
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Comparisons between two calls to \fItype()\fP won\(aqt raise an unidiomatic\-typecheck / C0123 \%<#\:unidiomatic-typecheck> warning anymore, consistent with the behavior applied only for \fB==\fP previously.
.sp
Closes #10161 (#10161 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10161>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash when importing a class decorator that did not exist with the same name as a class attribute after the class definition.
.sp
Closes #10105 (#10105 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10105>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash caused by malformed format strings when using \fI\&.format\fP with keyword arguments.
.sp
Closes #10282 (#10282 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10282>)
.IP \(bu 2
Using a slice as a class decorator now raises a not\-callable / E1102 \%<#\:not-callable> message instead of crashing. A lot of checks that dealt with decorators (too many to list) are now shortcut if the decorator can\(aqt immediately be inferred to a function or class definition.
.sp
Closes #10334 (#10334 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10334>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The algorithm used for no\-member / E1101 \%<#\:no-member> suggestions is now more efficient and cuts the
calculation when the distance score is already above the threshold.
.sp
Refs #10277 (#10277 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10277>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.3.6?
.sp
Release date: 2025\-03\-20
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for used\-before\-assignment / E0601 \%<#\:used-before-assignment> when an inner function\(aqs return type
annotation is a class defined at module scope.
.sp
Closes #9391 (#9391 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9391>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.3.5?
.sp
Release date: 2025\-03\-09
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positives for use\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-comparison / C1803 \%<#\:use-implicit-booleaness-not-comparison>, use\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-comparison\-to\-string / C1804 \%<#\:use-implicit-booleaness-not-comparison-to-string>
and use\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-comparison\-to\-zero / C1805 \%<#\:use-implicit-booleaness-not-comparison-to-zero> when chained comparisons are checked.
.sp
Closes #10065 (#10065 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10065>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for invalid\-getnewargs\-ex\-returned / E0313 \%<#\:invalid-getnewargs-ex-returned> when the tuple or dict has been assigned to a name.
.sp
Closes #10208 (#10208 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10208>)
.IP \(bu 2
Remove \fBgetopt\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:getopt\:.html#\:module-getopt> and \fBoptparse\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:optparse\:.html#\:module-optparse> from the list of deprecated modules.
.sp
Closes #10211 (#10211 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10211>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed conditional import x.y causing false positive possibly\-used\-before\-assignment / E0606 \%<#\:possibly-used-before-assignment>\&.
.sp
Closes #10081 (#10081 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10081>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash when something besides a class is found in an except handler.
.sp
Closes #10106 (#10106 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10106>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed raising invalid\-name / C0103 \%<#\:invalid-name> when using camelCase for private methods with two leading underscores.
.sp
Closes #10189 (#10189 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10189>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Upload release assets to PyPI via Trusted Publishing.
.sp
Closes #10256 (#10256 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10256>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.3.4?
.sp
Release date: 2025\-01\-28
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes \(dqskipped files\(dq count calculation; the previous method was displaying an arbitrary number.
.sp
Closes #10073 (#10073 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10073>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes a crash that occurred when pylint was run in a container on a host with cgroupsv2 and restrictions on CPU usage.
.sp
Closes #10103 (#10103 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10103>)
.IP \(bu 2
Relaxed the requirements for isort so pylint can benefit from isort 6.
.sp
Closes #10203 (#10203 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10203>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.3.3?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-12\-23
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positives for undefined\-variable / E0602 \%<#\:undefined-variable> for classes using Python 3.12
generic type syntax.
.sp
Closes #9335 (#9335 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9335>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for use\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-len / C1802 \%<#\:use-implicit-booleaness-not-len>\&. No lint should be emitted for
generators (\fBlen()\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:functions\:.html#\:len> is not defined for generators).
.sp
Refs #10100 (#10100 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10100>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBUnable to import \(aqcollections.abc\(aq (import\-error)\fP on Python 3.13.1.
.sp
Closes #10112 (#10112 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10112>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.3.2?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-12\-01
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for potential\-index\-error / E0643 \%<#\:potential-index-error> when an indexed iterable
contains a starred element that evaluates to more than one item.
.sp
Closes #10076 (#10076 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10076>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes the issue with \-\-source\-root option not working when the source files are in a subdirectory of the source root (e.g. when using a /src layout).
.sp
Closes #10026 (#10026 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:10026>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.3.1?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-09\-24
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix regression causing some f\-strings to not be inferred as strings.
.sp
Closes #9947 (#9947 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9947>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.3.0?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-09\-20
.SS Changes requiring user actions
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
We migrated \fBsymilar\fP to argparse, from getopt, so the error and help output changed
(for the better). We exit with 2 instead of sometime 1, sometime 2. The error output
is not captured by the runner anymore. It\(aqs not possible to use a value for the
boolean options anymore (\fB\-\-ignore\-comments 1\fP should become \fB\-\-ignore\-comments\fP).
.sp
Refs #9731 (#9731 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9731>)
.UNINDENT
.SS New Features
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add new declare\-non\-slot / E0245 \%<#\:declare-non-slot> error which reports when a class has a \fI__slots__\fP member and a type hint on the class is not present in \fI__slots__\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #9499 (#9499 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9499>)
.UNINDENT
.SS New Checks
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Added too\-many\-positional\-arguments / R0917 \%<#\:too-many-positional-arguments> to allow distinguishing the configuration for too many
total arguments (with keyword\-only params specified after \fI*\fP) from the configuration
for too many positional\-or\-keyword or positional\-only arguments.
.sp
As part of evaluating whether this check makes sense for your project, ensure you
adjust the value of \fI\-\-max\-positional\-arguments\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9099 (#9099 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9099>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add using\-exception\-groups\-in\-unsupported\-version / W2603 \%<#\:using-exception-groups-in-unsupported-version> and
using\-generic\-type\-syntax\-in\-unsupported\-version / W2604 \%<#\:using-generic-type-syntax-in-unsupported-version> for uses of Python 3.11+ or
3.12+ features on lower supported versions provided with \fB\-\-py\-version\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9791 (#9791 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9791>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add using\-assignment\-expression\-in\-unsupported\-version / W2605 \%<#\:using-assignment-expression-in-unsupported-version> for uses of \fB:=\fP (walrus operator)
on Python versions below 3.8 provided with \fB\-\-py\-version\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9820 (#9820 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9820>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add using\-positional\-only\-args\-in\-unsupported\-version / W2606 \%<#\:using-positional-only-args-in-unsupported-version> for uses of positional\-only args on
Python versions below 3.8 provided with \fB\-\-py\-version\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9823 (#9823 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9823>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add unnecessary\-default\-type\-args / R6007 \%<#\:unnecessary-default-type-args> to the \fBtyping\fP extension to detect the use
of unnecessary default type args for \fBtyping.Generator\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:typing\:.html#\:typing\:.Generator> and \fBtyping.AsyncGenerator\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:typing\:.html#\:typing\:.AsyncGenerator>\&.
.sp
Refs #9938 (#9938 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9938>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Negatives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix computation of never\-returning function: \fBtyping.Never\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:typing\:.html#\:typing\:.Never> is handled in addition to \fBtyping.NoReturn\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:typing\:.html#\:typing\:.NoReturn>, and priority is given to the explicit \fI\-\-never\-returning\-functions\fP option.
.sp
Closes #7565. (#7565 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7565>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false negative for await\-outside\-async / E1142 \%<#\:await-outside-async> when await is inside Lambda.
.sp
Refs #9653 (#9653 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9653>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false negative for duplicate\-argument\-name / E0108 \%<#\:duplicate-argument-name> by including \fBpositional\-only\fP, \fB*args\fP and \fB**kwargs\fP arguments in the check.
.sp
Closes #9669 (#9669 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9669>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negative for multiple\-statements / C0321 \%<#\:multiple-statements> when multiple statements are present on \fBelse\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:reference/\:compound_stmts\:.html#\:else> and \fBfinally\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:reference/\:compound_stmts\:.html#\:finally> lines of \fBtry\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:reference/\:compound_stmts\:.html#\:try>\&.
.sp
Refs #9759 (#9759 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9759>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negatives when :py:func::\fIisinstance\fP does not have exactly two arguments.
pylint now emits a too\-many\-function\-args / E1121 \%<#\:too-many-function-args> or no\-value\-for\-parameter / E1120 \%<#\:no-value-for-parameter>
appropriately for \fBisinstance()\fP \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:functions\:.html#\:isinstance> calls.
.sp
Closes #9847 (#9847 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9847>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fI\-\-enable\fP with \fI\-\-disable=all\fP now produces an error, when an unknown msg code is used. Internal \fIpylint\fP messages are no longer affected by \fI\-\-disable=all\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9403 (#9403 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9403>)
.IP \(bu 2
Impossible to compile regexes for paths in the configuration or argument given to pylint won\(aqt crash anymore but
raise an argparse error and display the error message from \fBre.compile\fP instead.
.sp
Closes #9680 (#9680 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9680>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a bug where a \fBtox.ini\fP file with pylint configuration was ignored and it exists in the current directory.
.sp
\fB\&.cfg\fP and \fB\&.ini\fP files containing a \fBPylint\fP configuration may now use a section named \fB[pylint]\fP\&. This enhancement impacts the scenario where these file types are used as defaults when they are present and have not been explicitly referred to, using the \fB\-\-rcfile\fP option.
.sp
Closes #9727 (#9727 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9727>)
.IP \(bu 2
Improve file discovery for directories that are not python packages.
.sp
Closes #9764 (#9764 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9764>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Remove support for launching pylint with Python 3.8.
Code that supports Python 3.8 can still be linted with the \fB\-\-py\-version=3.8\fP setting.
.sp
Refs #9774 (#9774 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9774>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add support for Python 3.13.
.sp
Refs #9852 (#9852 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9852>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Internal Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
All variables, classes, functions and file names containing the word \(aqsimilar\(aq, when it was,
in fact, referring to \(aqsymilar\(aq (the standalone program for the duplicate\-code / R0801 \%<#\:duplicate-code> check) were renamed
to \(aqsymilar\(aq.
.sp
Closes #9734 (#9734 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9734>)
.IP \(bu 2
Remove old\-style classes (Python 2) code and remove check for new\-style class since everything is new\-style in Python 3. Updated doc for exception checker to remove reference to new style class.
.sp
Refs #9925 (#9925 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9925>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 3.2
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B Release
3.2
.TP
.B Date
TBA
.UNINDENT
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.2.7?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-08\-31
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a false positive \fIunreachable\fP for \fINoReturn\fP coroutine functions.
.sp
Closes #9840. (#9840 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9840>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash in refactoring checker when calling a lambda bound as a method.
.sp
Closes #9865 (#9865 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9865>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in \fBundefined\-loop\-variable\fP when providing the \fBiterable\fP argument to \fBenumerate()\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9875 (#9875 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9875>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix to address indeterminacy of error message in case a module name is same as another in a separate namespace.
.sp
Refs #9883 (#9883 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9883>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.2.6?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-07\-21
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Quiet false positives for \fIunexpected\-keyword\-arg\fP when pylint cannot
determine which of two or more dynamically defined classes is being instantiated.
.sp
Closes #9672 (#9672 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9672>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBmissing\-param\-doc\fP where a method which is decorated with \fBtyping.overload\fP was expected to have a docstring specifying its parameters.
.sp
Closes #9739 (#9739 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9739>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a regression that raised \fBinvalid\-name\fP on class attributes merely
overriding invalid names from an ancestor.
.sp
Closes #9765 (#9765 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9765>)
.IP \(bu 2
Treat \fIassert_never()\fP the same way when imported from \fItyping_extensions\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9780 (#9780 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9780>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fIconsider\-using\-min\-max\-builtin\fP when the assignment target is an attribute.
.sp
Refs #9800 (#9800 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9800>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix an \fIAssertionError\fP arising from properties that return partial functions.
.sp
Closes #9214 (#9214 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9214>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash when a subclass extends \fB__slots__\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9814 (#9814 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9814>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.2.5?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-06\-28
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a false positive \fBunreachable\-code\fP when using \fBtyping.Any\fP as return type in python
3.8, the \fBtyping.NoReturn\fP are not taken into account anymore for python 3.8 however.
.sp
Closes #9751 (#9751 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9751>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.2.4?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-06\-26
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Prevent emitting \fBpossibly\-used\-before\-assignment\fP when relying on names
only potentially not defined in conditional blocks guarded by functions
annotated with \fBtyping.Never\fP or \fBtyping.NoReturn\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9674 (#9674 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9674>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash when the lineno of a variable used as an annotation wasn\(aqt available for \fBundefined\-variable\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8866 (#8866 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8866>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash when the \fBstart\fP value in an \fBenumerate\fP was non\-constant and impossible to infer
(like in\(ga\(gaenumerate(apples, start=int(random_apple_index)\(ga\(ga) for \fBunnecessary\-list\-index\-lookup\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9078 (#9078 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9078>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash in \fBsymilar\fP when the \fB\-d\fP or \fB\-i\fP short option were not properly recognized.
It\(aqs still impossible to do \fB\-d=1\fP (you must do \fB\-d 1\fP).
.sp
Closes #9343 (#9343 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9343>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.2.3?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-06\-06
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Classes with only an Ellipsis (\fB\&...\fP) in their body do not trigger multiple\-statements / C0321 \%<#\:multiple-statements>\(aq
anymore if they are inlined (in accordance with black\(aqs 2024 style).
.sp
Closes #9398 (#9398 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9398>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBredefined\-outer\-name\fP when there is a name defined in an exception\-handling block which shares the same name as a local variable that has been defined in a function body.
.sp
Closes #9671 (#9671 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9671>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBuse\-yield\-from\fP when using the return value from the \fByield\fP atom.
.sp
Closes #9696 (#9696 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9696>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.2.2?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-05\-20
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix multiple false positives for generic class syntax added in Python 3.12 (PEP 695).
.sp
Closes #9406 (#9406 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9406>)
.IP \(bu 2
Exclude context manager without cleanup from
\fBcontextmanager\-generator\-missing\-cleanup\fP checks.
.sp
Closes #9625 (#9625 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9625>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.2.1?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-05\-18
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Exclude if/else branches containing terminating functions (e.g. \fIsys.exit()\fP)
from \fIpossibly\-used\-before\-assignment\fP checks.
.sp
Closes #9627 (#9627 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9627>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit \fBtypevar\-name\-incorrect\-variance\fP warnings for PEP 695 style TypeVars.
The variance is inferred automatically by the type checker.
Adding \fB_co\fP or \fB_contra\fP suffix can help to reason about TypeVar.
.sp
Refs #9638 (#9638 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9638>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fIpossibly\-used\-before\-assignment\fP when using
\fItyping.assert_never()\fP (3.11+) to indicate exhaustiveness.
.sp
Closes #9643 (#9643 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9643>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false negative for \fB\-\-ignore\-patterns\fP when the directory to be linted is specified using a dot(\fB\&.\fP) and all files are ignored instead of only the files whose name begin with a dot.
.sp
Closes #9273 (#9273 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9273>)
.IP \(bu 2
Restore \(dqerrors / warnings by module\(dq section to report output (with \fI\-ry\fP).
.sp
Closes #9145 (#9145 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9145>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtrailing\-comma\-tuple\fP should now be correctly emitted when it was disabled globally
but enabled via local message control, after removal of an over\-optimisation.
.sp
Refs #9608. (#9608 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9608>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fI\-\-prefer\-stubs=yes\fP option to opt\-in to the astroid 3.2 feature
that prefers \fI\&.pyi\fP stubs over same\-named \fI\&.py\fP files. This has the
potential to reduce \fIno\-member\fP errors but at the cost of more errors
such as \fInot\-an\-iterable\fP from function bodies appearing as \fI\&...\fP\&.
.sp
Defaults to \fIno\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9626
Closes #9623 (#9626 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9626>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Internal Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Update astroid version to 3.2.1. This solves some reports of \fBRecursionError\fP
and also makes the \fIprefer .pyi stubs\fP feature in astroid 3.2.0 \fIopt\-in\fP
with the aforementioned \fB\-\-prefer\-stubs=y\fP option.
.sp
Refs #9139 (#9139 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9139>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.2.0?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-05\-14
.SS New Features
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Understand \fIsix.PY2\fP and \fIsix.PY3\fP for conditional imports.
.sp
Closes #3501 (#3501 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3501>)
.IP \(bu 2
A new \fIgithub\fP reporter has been added. This reporter  returns the output of \fIpylint\fP in a format that
Github can use to automatically annotate code. Use it with \fIpylint \-\-output\-format=github\fP on your Github Workflows.
.sp
Closes #9443. (#9443 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9443>)
.UNINDENT
.SS New Checks
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add check \fBpossibly\-used\-before\-assignment\fP when relying on names after an \fBif/else\fP
switch when one branch failed to define the name, raise, or return.
.sp
Closes #1727 (#1727 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:1727>)
.IP \(bu 2
Checks for generators that use contextmanagers that don\(aqt handle cleanup properly.
Is meant to raise visibility on the case that a generator is not fully exhausted and the contextmanager is not cleaned up properly.
A contextmanager must yield a non\-constant value and not handle cleanup for GeneratorExit.
The using generator must attempt to use the yielded context value \fIwith x() as y\fP and not just \fIwith x()\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #2832 (#2832 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:2832>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Negatives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
If and Try nodes are now checked for useless return statements as well.
.sp
Closes #9449. (#9449 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9449>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negative for \fBproperty\-with\-parameters\fP in the case of parameters which are \fBpositional\-only\fP, \fBkeyword\-only\fP, \fBvariadic positional\fP or \fBvariadic keyword\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9584 (#9584 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9584>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Positives Fixed
.sp
pylint now understands the \fB@overload\fP decorator return values better.
.sp
Closes #4696 (#4696 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4696>)
Refs #9606 (#9606 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9606>)
.SS Performance Improvements
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Ignored modules are now not checked at all, instead of being checked and then
ignored. This should speed up the analysis of large codebases which have
ignored modules.
.sp
Closes #9442 (#9442 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9442>) (#9442 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9442>)
.IP \(bu 2
ImportChecker\(aqs logic has been modified to avoid context files when possible. This makes it possible
to cache module searches on astroid and reduce execution times.
.sp
Refs #9310. (#9310 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9310>)
.IP \(bu 2
An internal check for \fBtrailing\-comma\-tuple\fP being enabled for a file or not is now
done once per file instead of once for each token.
.sp
Refs #9608. (#9608 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9608>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 3.1
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B Release
3.1
.TP
.B Date
2024\-02\-25
.UNINDENT
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.sp
Two new checks \-\- \fBuse\-yield\-from\fP, \fBdeprecated\-attribute\fP \-\-
and a smattering of bug fixes.
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.1.1?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-05\-13
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Treat \fIattrs.define\fP and \fIattrs.frozen\fP as dataclass decorators in
\fItoo\-few\-public\-methods\fP check.
.sp
Closes #9345 (#9345 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9345>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive with \fBsingledispatchmethod\-function\fP when a method is decorated with both \fBfunctools.singledispatchmethod\fP and \fBstaticmethod\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9531 (#9531 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9531>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBconsider\-using\-dict\-items\fP when iterating using \fBkeys()\fP and then deleting an item using the key as a lookup.
.sp
Closes #9554 (#9554 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9554>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.1.0?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-02\-25
.SS New Features
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Skip \fBconsider\-using\-join\fP check for non\-empty separators if an \fBsuggest\-join\-with\-non\-empty\-separator\fP option is set to \fBno\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8701 (#8701 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8701>)
.IP \(bu 2
Discover \fB\&.pyi\fP files when linting.
.sp
These can be ignored with the \fBignore\-patterns\fP setting.
.sp
Closes #9097 (#9097 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9097>)
.IP \(bu 2
Check \fBTypeAlias\fP and \fBTypeVar\fP (PEP 695) nodes for \fBinvalid\-name\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #9196 (#9196 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9196>)
.IP \(bu 2
Support for resolving external toml files named pylintrc.toml and .pylintrc.toml.
.sp
Closes #9228 (#9228 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9228>)
.IP \(bu 2
Check for \fI\&.clear\fP, \fI\&.discard\fP, \fI\&.pop\fP and \fIremove\fP methods being called on a set while it is being iterated over.
.sp
Closes #9334 (#9334 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9334>)
.UNINDENT
.SS New Checks
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
New message \fIuse\-yield\-from\fP added to the refactoring checker. This message is emitted when yielding from a loop can be replaced by \fIyield from\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9229. (#9229 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9229>)
.IP \(bu 2
Added a \fBdeprecated\-attribute\fP message to check deprecated attributes in the stdlib.
.sp
Closes #8855 (#8855 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8855>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positive for \fBinherit\-non\-class\fP for generic Protocols.
.sp
Closes #9106 (#9106 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9106>)
.IP \(bu 2
Exempt \fBTypedDict\fP from \fBtyping_extensions\fP from \fBtoo\-many\-ancestor\fP checks.
.sp
Refs #9167 (#9167 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9167>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Negatives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Extend broad\-exception\-raised / W0719 \%<#\:broad-exception-raised> and broad\-exception\-caught / W0718 \%<#\:broad-exception-caught> to except*.
.sp
Closes #8827 (#8827 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8827>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false\-negative for unnecessary if blocks using a different than expected ordering of arguments.
.sp
Closes #8947. (#8947 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8947>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Improve the message provided for wrong\-import\-order / C0411 \%<#\:wrong-import-order> check.  Instead of the import statement (\(dqimport x\(dq), the message now specifies the import that is out of order and which imports should come after it.  As reported in the issue, this is particularly helpful if there are multiple imports on a single line that do not follow the PEP8 convention.
.sp
The message will report imports as follows:
For \(dqimport X\(dq, it will report \(dq(standard/third party/first party/local) import X\(dq
For \(dqimport X.Y\(dq and \(dqfrom X import Y\(dq, it will report \(dq(standard/third party/first party/local) import X.Y\(dq
The import category is specified to provide explanation as to why pylint has issued the message and guidance to the developer on how to fix the problem.
.sp
Closes #8808 (#8808 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8808>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Print how many files were checked in verbose mode.
.sp
Closes #8935 (#8935 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8935>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash when an enum class which is also decorated with a \fBdataclasses.dataclass\fP decorator is defined.
.sp
Closes #9100 (#9100 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9100>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Internal Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Update astroid version to 3.1.0.
.sp
Refs #9457 (#9457 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9457>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 3.0
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B Release
3.0.0
.TP
.B Date
2023\-10\-02
.UNINDENT
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.sp
Pylint now support python 3.12 officially.
.sp
This long anticipated major version also provides some important usability
and performance improvements, along with enacting necessary breaking changes
and long\-announced deprecations. The documentation of each message with an
example is very close too.
.sp
The required \fBastroid\fP version is now 3.0.0. See the
astroid changelog \%<https://\:pylint\:.readthedocs\:.io/\:projects/\:astroid/\:en/\:latest/\:changelog\:.html#\:what-s-new-in-astroid-3-0-0>
for additional fixes, features, and performance improvements applicable to pylint.
.sp
Our code is now fully typed. The \fBinvalid\-name\fP message no longer checks for a minimum length of 3 characters by default. Dependencies
like wrapt or setuptools were removed.
.sp
A new \fBjson2\fP reporter has been added. It features an enriched output that is
easier to parse and provides more info, here\(aqs a sample output.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
{
    \(dqmessages\(dq: [
        {
            \(dqtype\(dq: \(dqconvention\(dq,
            \(dqsymbol\(dq: \(dqline\-too\-long\(dq,
            \(dqmessage\(dq: \(dqLine too long (1/2)\(dq,
            \(dqmessageId\(dq: \(dqC0301\(dq,
            \(dqconfidence\(dq: \(dqHIGH\(dq,
            \(dqmodule\(dq: \(dq0123\(dq,
            \(dqobj\(dq: \(dq\(dq,
            \(dqline\(dq: 1,
            \(dqcolumn\(dq: 0,
            \(dqendLine\(dq: 1,
            \(dqendColumn\(dq: 4,
            \(dqpath\(dq: \(dq0123\(dq,
            \(dqabsolutePath\(dq: \(dq0123\(dq
        }
    ],
    \(dqstatistics\(dq: {
        \(dqmessageTypeCount\(dq: {
            \(dqfatal\(dq: 0,
            \(dqerror\(dq: 0,
            \(dqwarning\(dq: 0,
            \(dqrefactor\(dq: 0,
            \(dqconvention\(dq: 1,
            \(dqinfo\(dq: 0
        },
        \(dqmodulesLinted\(dq: 1,
        \(dqscore\(dq: 5.0
    }
}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.0.4?
.sp
Release date: 2024\-02\-23
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBused\-before\-assignment\fP is no longer emitted when using a name in a loop and
depending on an earlier name assignment in an \fBexcept\fP block paired with
\fBelse: continue\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #6804 (#6804 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6804>)
.IP \(bu 2
Avoid false positives for \fBno\-member\fP involving function
attributes supplied by decorators.
.sp
Closes #9246 (#9246 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9246>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positive nested\-min\-max / W3301 \%<#\:nested-min-max> for nested lists.
.sp
Closes #9307 (#9307 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9307>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP in a \fBfinally\fP block
when assignments took place in both the \fBtry\fP block and each exception handler.
.sp
Closes #9451 (#9451 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9451>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Catch incorrect ValueError \fB\(dqgenerator already executing\(dq\fP for Python 3.12.0 \- 3.12.2.
This is fixed upstream in Python 3.12.3.
.sp
Closes #9138 (#9138 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9138>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.0.3?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-12\-11
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positive for \fBunnecessary\-lambda\fP when the call has keyword arguments but not the lambda.
.sp
Closes #9148 (#9148 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9148>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed incorrect suggestion for shallow copy in unnecessary\-comprehension / R1721 \%<#\:unnecessary-comprehension>
.sp
Example of the suggestion:
#pylint: disable=:ref:\fImissing\-module\-docstring\fP
a = [1, 2, 3]
b = [x for x in a]
b[0] = 0
print(a) # [1, 2, 3]
.sp
After changing b = [x for x in a] to b = a based on the suggestion, the script now prints [0, 2, 3]. The correct suggestion should be use list(a) to preserve the original behavior.
.sp
Closes #9172 (#9172 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9172>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positives for \fBundefined\-variable\fP and \fBunused\-argument\fP for
classes and functions using Python 3.12 generic type syntax.
.sp
Closes #9193 (#9193 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9193>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed \fBpointless\-string\-statement\fP false positive for docstrings
on Python 3.12 type aliases.
.sp
Closes #9268 (#9268 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9268>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBinvalid\-exception\-operation\fP when concatenating tuples
of exception types.
.sp
Closes #9288 (#9288 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9288>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a bug where pylint was unable to walk recursively through a directory if the
directory has an \fI__init__.py\fP file.
.sp
Closes #9210 (#9210 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9210>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.0.2?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-10\-22
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP false positive for generic type syntax (PEP 695, Python 3.12).
.sp
Closes #9110 (#9110 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9110>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Escape special symbols and newlines in messages.
.sp
Closes #7874 (#7874 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7874>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes suggestion for \fBnested\-min\-max\fP for expressions with additive operators, list and dict comprehensions.
.sp
Closes #8524 (#8524 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8524>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes ignoring conditional imports with \fBignore\-imports=y\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8914 (#8914 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8914>)
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBinconsistent\-quotes\fP for f\-strings with 3.12 interpreter only if targeting pre\-3.12 versions.
.sp
Closes #9113 (#9113 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9113>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.0.1?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-10\-05
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positive for \fBinherit\-non\-class\fP for generic Protocols.
.sp
Closes #9106 (#9106 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9106>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash when an enum class which is also decorated with a \fBdataclasses.dataclass\fP decorator is defined.
.sp
Closes #9100 (#9100 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9100>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 3.0.0?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-10\-02
.SS Breaking Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Enabling or disabling individual messages will now take effect even if an
\fB\-\-enable=all\fP or \fBdisable=all\fP follows in the same configuration file
(or on the command line).
.sp
This means for the following example, \fBfixme\fP messages will now be emitted:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
pylint my_module \-\-enable=fixme \-\-disable=all
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
To regain the prior behavior, remove the superfluous earlier option.
.sp
Closes #3696 (#3696 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3696>)
.IP \(bu 2
Remove support for launching pylint with Python 3.7.
Code that supports Python 3.7 can still be linted with the \fB\-\-py\-version=3.7\fP setting.
.sp
Refs #6306 (#6306 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6306>)
.IP \(bu 2
Disables placed in a \fBtry\fP block now apply to the \fBexcept\fP block.
Previously, they only happened to do so in the presence of an \fBelse\fP clause.
.sp
Refs #7767 (#7767 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7767>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fIpyreverse\fP now uses a new default color palette that is more colorblind friendly.
The color scheme is taken from Paul Tol\(aqs Notes \%<https://\:personal\:.sron\:.nl/\:~pault>\&.
If you prefer other colors, you can use the \fI\-\-color\-palette\fP option to specify custom colors.
.sp
Closes #8251 (#8251 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8251>)
.IP \(bu 2
Everything related to the \fB__implements__\fP construct was removed. It was based on PEP245
that was proposed in 2001 and rejected in 2006.
.sp
The capability from pyreverse to take \fB__implements__\fP into account when generating diagrams
was also removed.
.sp
Refs #8404 (#8404 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8404>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpyreverse\fP: Support for the \fB\&.vcg\fP output format (Visualization of Compiler Graphs) has been dropped.
.sp
Closes #8416 (#8416 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8416>)
.IP \(bu 2
The warning when the now useless old pylint cache directory (pylint.d) was
found was removed. The cache dir is documented in
the FAQ \%<https://\:pylint\:.readthedocs\:.io/\:en/\:latest/\:faq\:.html#\:where-is-the-persistent-data-stored-to-compare-between-successive-runs>\&.
.sp
Refs #8462 (#8462 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8462>)
.IP \(bu 2
Following a deprecation period, \fBpylint.config.PYLINTRC\fP was removed.
Use the \fBpylint.config.find_default_config_files\fP generator instead.
.sp
Closes #8862 (#8862 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8862>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Changes requiring user actions
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBinvalid\-name\fP message no longer checks for a minimum length of 3 characters by default.
(This was an unadvertised commingling of concerns between casing
and name length, and users regularly reported this to be surprising.)
.sp
If checking for a minimum length is still desired, it can be regained in two ways:
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
If you are content with a \fBdisallowed\-name\fP message (instead of
\fBinvalid\-name\fP), then simply add the option \fBbad\-names\-rgxs=\(dq^..?$\(dq\fP,
which will fail 1\-2 character\-long names. (Ensure you enable
\fBdisallowed\-name\fP\&.)
.IP \(bu 2
If you would prefer an \fBinvalid\-name\fP message to be emitted, or would
prefer finer\-grained control over the circumstances in which messages are
emitted (classes vs. methods, etc.), then avail yourself of the regex
options described
here \%<https://\:pylint\:.readthedocs\:.io/\:en/\:stable/\:user_guide/\:configuration/\:all-options\:.html#\:main-checker>\&.
(In particular, take note of the commented out options in the \(dqexample
configuration\(dq given at the bottom of the section.) The prior regexes can
be found in the
pull request \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:pull/\:8813>
that removed the length requirements.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Closes #2018 (#2018 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:2018>)
.IP \(bu 2
The compare to empty string checker (\fBpylint.extensions.emptystring\fP) and the compare to
zero checker (\fBpylint.extensions.compare\-to\-zero\fP) have been removed and their checks are
now part of the implicit booleaness checker:
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcompare\-to\-zero\fP was renamed \fBuse\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-comparison\-to\-zero\fP and
\fBcompare\-to\-empty\-string\fP was renamed \fBuse\-implicit\-booleaness\-not\-comparison\-to\-string\fP
and they now need to be enabled explicitly.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBpylint.extensions.emptystring\fP and \fBpylint.extensions.compare\-to\-zero\fP extensions
no longer exist and need to be removed from the \fBload\-plugins\fP option.
.IP \(bu 2
Messages related to implicit booleaness were made more explicit and actionable.
This permits to make their likeness explicit and will provide better performance as they
share most of their conditions to be raised.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Closes #6871 (#6871 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6871>)
.IP \(bu 2
epylint was removed. It now lives at: \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:emacsorphanage/\:pylint>\&.
.sp
Refs #7737 (#7737 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7737>)
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBovergeneral\-exceptions\fP option now only takes fully qualified names
into account (\fBbuiltins.Exception\fP not \fBException\fP). If you overrode
this option, you need to use the fully qualified name now.
.sp
There\(aqs still a warning, but it will be removed in 3.1.0.
.sp
Refs #8411 (#8411 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8411>)
.IP \(bu 2
Following a deprecation period, it\(aqs no longer possible to use \fBMASTER\fP
or \fBmaster\fP as configuration section in \fBsetup.cfg\fP or \fBtox.ini\fP\&. It\(aqs bad practice
to not start a section title with the tool name. Please use \fBpylint.main\fP instead.
.sp
Refs #8465 (#8465 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8465>)
.IP \(bu 2
Package stats are now printed when running Pyreverse and a \fB\-\-verbose\fP flag was added to get the original output with parsed modules. You might need to activate the verbose option if you want to keep the old output.
.sp
Closes #8973 (#8973 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8973>)
.UNINDENT
.SS New Features
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A new \fBjson2\fP reporter has been added. It features a more enriched output that is
easier to parse and provides more info.
.sp
Compared to \fBjson\fP the only changes are that messages are now under the \fB\(dqmessages\(dq\fP
key and that \fB\(dqmessage\-id\(dq\fP now follows the camelCase convention and is renamed to
\fB\(dqmessageId\(dq\fP\&.
The new reporter also reports the \(dqscore\(dq of the modules you linted as defined by the
\fBevaluation\fP option and provides statistics about the modules you linted.
.sp
We encourage users to use the new reporter as the \fBjson\fP reporter will no longer
be maintained.
.sp
Closes #4741 (#4741 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4741>)
.IP \(bu 2
In Pyreverse package dependency diagrams, show when a module imports another only for type\-checking.
.sp
Closes #8112 (#8112 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8112>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add new option (\fB\-\-show\-stdlib\fP, \fB\-L\fP) to \fBpyreverse\fP\&.
This is similar to the behavior of \fB\-\-show\-builtin\fP in that standard library
modules are now not included by default, and this option will include them.
.sp
Closes #8181 (#8181 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8181>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add Pyreverse option to exclude standalone nodes from diagrams with \fI\-\-no\-standalone\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8476 (#8476 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8476>)
.UNINDENT
.SS New Checks
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBDataclassChecker\fP module and \fBinvalid\-field\-call\fP checker to check for invalid dataclasses.field() usage.
.sp
Refs #5159 (#5159 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5159>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBreturn\-in\-finally\fP to emit a message if a return statement was found in a finally clause.
.sp
Closes #8260 (#8260 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8260>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new message \fBkwarg\-superseded\-by\-positional\-arg\fP to warn when a function is called with a keyword argument which shares a name with a positional\-only parameter and the function contains a keyword variadic parameter dictionary. It may be surprising behaviour when the keyword argument is added to the keyword variadic parameter dictionary.
.sp
Closes #8558 (#8558 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8558>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Extensions
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add new \fBprefer\-typing\-namedtuple\fP message to the \fBCodeStyleChecker\fP to suggest
rewriting calls to \fBcollections.namedtuple\fP as classes inheriting from \fBtyping.NamedTuple\fP
on Python 3.6+.
.sp
Requires \fBload\-plugins=pylint.extensions.code_style\fP and \fBenable=prefer\-typing\-namedtuple\fP to be raised.
.sp
Closes #8660 (#8660 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8660>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Extend concept of \(dqfunction ambiguity\(dq in \fBsafe_infer()\fP from
differing number of function arguments to differing set of argument names.
.sp
Solves false positives in \fBtensorflow\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #3613 (#3613 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3613>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fIunused\-argument\fP false positive when \fI__new__\fP does not use all the arguments of \fI__init__\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #3670 (#3670 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3670>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBinvalid\-name\fP when a type\-annotated class variable in an \fBenum.Enum\fP class has no assigned value.
.sp
Refs #7402 (#7402 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7402>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBunused\-import\fP false positive for usage of \fBsix.with_metaclass\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7506 (#7506 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7506>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negatives and false positives for \fBtoo\-many\-try\-statements\fP,
\fBtoo\-complex\fP, and \fBtoo\-many\-branches\fP by correctly counting statements
under a \fBtry\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #7767 (#7767 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7767>)
.IP \(bu 2
When checking for unbalanced dict unpacking in for\-loops, Pylint will now test whether the length of each value to be
unpacked matches the number of unpacking targets. Previously, Pylint would test the number of values for the loop
iteration, which would produce a false unbalanced\-dict\-unpacking / W0644 \%<#\:unbalanced-dict-unpacking> warning.
.sp
Closes #8156 (#8156 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8156>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when usage and assignment
are guarded by the same test in different statements.
.sp
Closes #8167 (#8167 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8167>)
.IP \(bu 2
Adds \fBasyncSetUp\fP to the default \fBdefining\-attr\-methods\fP list to silence
\fBattribute\-defined\-outside\-init\fP warning when using
\fBunittest.IsolatedAsyncioTestCase\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #8403 (#8403 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8403>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fIlogging\-not\-lazy\fP is not longer emitted for explicitly concatenated string arguments.
.sp
Closes #8410 (#8410 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8410>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for isinstance\-second\-argument\-not\-valid\-type / W1116 \%<#\:isinstance-second-argument-not-valid-type> when union types contains None.
.sp
Closes #8424 (#8424 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8424>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-name\fP now allows for integers in \fBtypealias\fP names:
\- now valid: \fBGood2Name\fP, \fBGoodName2\fP\&.
\- still invalid: \fB_1BadName\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8485 (#8485 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8485>)
.IP \(bu 2
No longer consider \fBUnion\fP as type annotation as type alias for naming checks.
.sp
Closes #8487 (#8487 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8487>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBunnecessary\-lambda\fP no longer warns on lambdas which use its parameters in
their body (other than the final arguments), e.g.
\fBlambda foo: (bar if foo else baz)(foo)\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8496 (#8496 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8496>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed \fIunused\-import\fP so that it observes the \fIdummy\-variables\-rgx\fP option.
.sp
Closes #8500 (#8500 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8500>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fIUnion\fP typed variables without assignment are no longer treated as
\fITypeAlias\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8540 (#8540 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8540>)
.IP \(bu 2
Allow parenthesized implicitly concatenated strings when \fIcheck\-str\-concat\-over\-line\-jumps\fP is enabled.
.sp
Closes #8552. (#8552 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8552>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBpositional\-only\-arguments\-expected\fP when a function contains both a positional\-only parameter that has a default value, and \fB**kwargs\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8555 (#8555 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8555>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBkeyword\-arg\-before\-vararg\fP when a positional\-only parameter with a default value precedes \fB*args\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8570 (#8570 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8570>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBarguments\-differ\fP when overriding \fI__init_subclass__\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8919 (#8919 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8919>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBno\-value\-for\-parameter\fP when a staticmethod is called in a class body.
.sp
Closes #9036 (#9036 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9036>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Negatives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when calling module\-level functions before definition.
.sp
Closes #1144 (#1144 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:1144>)
.IP \(bu 2
Apply \fBinfer_kwarg_from_call()\fP to more checks
.sp
These mostly solve false negatives for various checks,
save for one false positive for \fBuse\-maxsplit\-arg\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7761 (#7761 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7761>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fITypeAlias\fP variables defined in functions are now checked for \fIinvalid\-name\fP errors.
.sp
Closes #8536 (#8536 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8536>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negative for \fBno\-value\-for\-parameter\fP when a function, whose signature contains both a positional\-only parameter \fBname\fP and also \fB*kwargs\fP, is called with a keyword\-argument for \fBname\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8559 (#8559 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8559>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false negative for \fBtoo\-many\-arguments\fP by considering positional\-only and keyword\-only parameters.
.sp
Closes #8667 (#8667 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8667>)
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBassignment\-from\-no\-return\fP for calls to builtin methods like \fBdict.update()\fP\&.
Calls to \fBlist.sort()\fP now raise \fBassignment\-from\-no\-return\fP
rather than \fBassignment\-from\-none\fP for consistency.
.sp
Closes #8714
Closes #8810 (#8714 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8714>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-using\-augmented\-assign\fP is now applied to dicts and lists as well.
.sp
Closes #8959. (#8959 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8959>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Support \fBduplicate\-code\fP message when parallelizing with \fB\-\-jobs\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #374 (#374 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:374>)
.IP \(bu 2
Support \fBcyclic\-import\fP message when parallelizing with \fB\-\-jobs\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #4171 (#4171 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4171>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-jobs\fP can now be used with \fB\-\-load\-plugins\fP\&.
.sp
This had regressed in astroid 2.5.0.
.sp
Closes #4874 (#4874 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4874>)
.IP \(bu 2
docparams extension considers type comments as type documentation.
.sp
Closes #6287 (#6287 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6287>)
.IP \(bu 2
When parsing comma\-separated lists of regular expressions in the config, ignore
commas that are inside braces since those indicate quantifiers, not delineation
between expressions.
.sp
Closes #7229 (#7229 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7229>)
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBignored\-modules\fP option will now be correctly taken into account for \fBno\-name\-in\-module\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7578 (#7578 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7578>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsys.argv\fP is now always correctly considered as impossible to infer (instead of
using the actual values given to pylint).
.sp
Closes #7710 (#7710 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7710>)
.IP \(bu 2
Avoid duplicative warnings for unqualified exception names in the \fBovergeneral\-exceptions\fP
setting when running with \fB\-\-jobs\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7774 (#7774 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7774>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt show class fields more than once in Pyreverse diagrams.
.sp
Closes #8189 (#8189 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8189>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP false negative when TYPE_CHECKING imports
are used in multiple scopes.
.sp
Closes #8198 (#8198 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8198>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-clear\-cache\-post\-run\fP now also clears LRU caches for pylint utilities
holding references to AST nodes.
.sp
Closes #8361 (#8361 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8361>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash when \fBTYPE_CHECKING\fP is used without importing it.
.sp
Closes #8434 (#8434 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8434>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP false positive when imports
are made under the \fBTYPE_CHECKING\fP else if branch.
.sp
Closes #8437 (#8437 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8437>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a regression of \fBpreferred\-modules\fP where a partial match was used instead of the required full match.
.sp
Closes #8453 (#8453 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8453>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in pyreverse when \(dq/\(dq characters are used in the output filename e.g pyreverse \-o png \-p name/ path/to/project.
.sp
Closes #8504 (#8504 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8504>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt show arrows more than once in Pyreverse diagrams.
.sp
Closes #8522 (#8522 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8522>)
.IP \(bu 2
Improve output of \fBconsider\-using\-generator\fP message for \fBmin()\fP calls with \fBdefault\fP keyword.
.sp
Closes #8563 (#8563 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8563>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash when generating a configuration file: \fBtomlkit.exceptions.TOMLKitError: Can\(aqt add a table to a dotted key\fP
caused by tomlkit \fBv0.11.8\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8632 (#8632 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8632>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a line break error in Pyreverse dot output.
.sp
Closes #8671 (#8671 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8671>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBmethod\-hidden\fP when using \fBcached_property\fP decorator.
.sp
Closes #8753 (#8753 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8753>)
.IP \(bu 2
Dunder methods defined in lambda do not trigger \fBunnecessary\-dunder\-call\fP anymore, if they cannot be replaced by the non\-dunder call.
.sp
Closes #8769 (#8769 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8769>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt show duplicate type annotations in Pyreverse diagrams.
.sp
Closes #8888 (#8888 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8888>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixing inconsistent hashing issue in \fIBaseChecker\fP causing some reports not being exported.
.sp
Closes #9001 (#9001 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9001>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt add \fIOptional\fP to \fI|\fP annotations with \fINone\fP in Pyreverse diagrams.
.sp
Closes #9014 (#9014 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9014>)
.IP \(bu 2
Pyreverse doesn\(aqt show multiple class association arrows anymore, but only the strongest one.
.sp
Refs #9045 (#9045 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9045>)
.IP \(bu 2
Prevented data loss in the linter stats for messages relating
to the linter itself (e.g. \fBunknown\-option\-value\fP), fixing
problems with score, fail\-on, etc.
.sp
Closes #9059 (#9059 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9059>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash in refactoring checker when unary operand used with variable in for loop.
.sp
Closes #9074 (#9074 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9074>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint now exposes its type annotations.
.sp
Closes #5488 and #2079 (#5488 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5488>)
.IP \(bu 2
Search for \fBpyproject.toml\fP recursively in parent directories up to a project or file system root.
.sp
Refs #7163, Closes #3289 (#7163 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7163>)
.IP \(bu 2
All code related to the optparse config parsing has been removed.
.sp
Refs #8405 (#8405 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8405>)
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint now supports python 3.12.
.sp
Refs #8718 (#8718 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8718>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add a CITATION.cff file to the root of the repository containing the necessary metadata to cite Pylint.
.sp
Closes #8760 (#8760 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8760>)
.IP \(bu 2
Renamed the \(dqunneeded\-not / C0113 \%<#\:unneeded-not>\(dq error into \(dqunnecessary_negation\(dq to be clearer.
.sp
Closes #8789 (#8789 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8789>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Internal Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBget_message_definition\fP was removed from the base checker API. You can access
message definitions through the \fBMessageStore\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #8401 (#8401 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8401>)
.IP \(bu 2
Everything related to the \fB__implements__\fP construct was removed. It was based on PEP245
that was proposed in 2001 and rejected in 2006.
.sp
All the classes inheriting \fBInterface\fP in \fBpylint.interfaces\fP were removed.
\fBChecker\fP should only inherit \fBBaseChecker\fP or any of the other checker types
from \fBpylint.checkers\fP\&. \fBReporter\fP should only inherit \fBBaseReporter\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #8404 (#8404 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8404>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmodname\fP and \fBmsg_store\fP are now required to be given in \fBFileState\fP\&.
\fBcollect_block_lines\fP has also been removed. \fBPylinter.current_name\fP
cannot be null anymore.
.sp
Refs #8407 (#8407 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8407>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBReporter.set_output\fP was removed in favor of \fBreporter.out = stream\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #8408 (#8408 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8408>)
.IP \(bu 2
A number of old utility functions and classes have been removed:
.sp
\fBMapReduceMixin\fP: To make a checker reduce map data simply implement
\fBget_map_data\fP and \fBreduce_map_data\fP\&.
.sp
\fBis_inside_lambda\fP: Use \fButils.get_node_first_ancestor_of_type(x, nodes.Lambda)\fP
.sp
\fBcheck_messages\fP: Use \fButils.only_required_for_messages\fP
.sp
\fBis_class_subscriptable_pep585_with_postponed_evaluation_enabled\fP: Use
\fBis_postponed_evaluation_enabled(node)\fP and \fBis_node_in_type_annotation_context(node)\fP
.sp
\fBget_python_path\fP: assumption that there\(aqs always an __init__.py is not true since
python 3.3 and is causing problems, particularly with PEP 420. Use \fBdiscover_package_path\fP
and pass source root(s).
.sp
\fBfix_import_path\fP: Use \fBaugmented_sys_path\fP and pass additional \fBsys.path\fP
entries as an argument obtained from \fBdiscover_package_path\fP\&.
.sp
\fBget_global_option\fP: Use \fBchecker.linter.config\fP to get all global options.
.sp
Related private objects have been removed as well.
.sp
Refs #8409 (#8409 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8409>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcolorize_ansi\fP now only accepts a \fBMessageStyle\fP object.
.sp
Refs #8412 (#8412 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8412>)
.IP \(bu 2
Following a deprecation period, \fBPylinter.check\fP now only works with sequences of strings, not strings.
.sp
Refs #8463 (#8463 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8463>)
.IP \(bu 2
Following a deprecation period, \fBColorizedTextReporter\fP only accepts \fBColorMappingDict\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #8464 (#8464 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8464>)
.IP \(bu 2
Following a deprecation period, \fBMessageTest\fP\(aqs \fBend_line\fP and \fBend_col_offset\fP
must be accurate in functional tests (for python 3.8 or above on cpython, and for
python 3.9 or superior on pypy).
.sp
Refs #8466 (#8466 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8466>)
.IP \(bu 2
Following a deprecation period, the \fBdo_exit\fP argument of the \fBRun\fP class (and of the \fB_Run\fP
class in testutils) were removed.
.sp
Refs #8472 (#8472 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8472>)
.IP \(bu 2
Following a deprecation period, the \fBpy_version\fP argument of the
\fBMessageDefinition.may_be_emitted\fP function is now required. The most likely solution
is to use \(aqlinter.config.py_version\(aq if you need to keep using this
function, or to use \(aqMessageDefinition.is_message_enabled\(aq instead.
.sp
Refs #8473 (#8473 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8473>)
.IP \(bu 2
Following a deprecation period, the \fBOutputLine\fP class now requires
the right number of argument all the time. The functional output can be
regenerated automatically to achieve that easily.
.sp
Refs #8474 (#8474 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8474>)
.IP \(bu 2
Following a deprecation period, \fBis_typing_guard\fP, \fBis_node_in_typing_guarded_import_block\fP and
\fBis_node_in_guarded_import_block\fP from \fBpylint.utils\fP were removed: use a combination of
\fBis_sys_guard\fP and \fBin_type_checking_block\fP instead.
.sp
Refs #8475 (#8475 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8475>)
.IP \(bu 2
Following a deprecation period, the \fBlocation\fP argument of the
\fBMessage\fP class must now be a \fBMessageLocationTuple\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #8477 (#8477 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8477>)
.IP \(bu 2
Following a deprecation period, the \fBcheck_single_file\fP function of the
\fBPylinter\fP is replaced by \fBPylinter.check_single_file_item\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #8478 (#8478 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8478>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Performance Improvements
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP runs (at least) ~5% faster after improvements to \fBastroid\fP
that make better use of the inference cache.
.sp
Refs pylint\-dev/astroid#529 (#529 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:529>)
.IP \(bu 2
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
Optimize \fBis_trailing_comma()\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Cache \fBclass_is_abstract()\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Refs #1954 (#1954 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:1954>)
.IP \(bu 2
Exit immediately if all messages are disabled.
.sp
Closes #8715 (#8715 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8715>)
.UNINDENT
.SS 2.x
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.17
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B Release
2.17
.TP
.B Date
2023\-03\-08
.UNINDENT
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.sp
2.17 is a small release that is the first to support python 3.11
officially with the addition of TryStar nodes.
.sp
There\(aqs still two new default checks: \fBbad\-chained\-comparison\fP and
\fBimplicit\-flag\-alias\fP, one of them already fixed a previously
undetected bug in sentry.
.sp
Thanks to the community effort our documentation is almost complete,
and every messages should have a proper documentation now. A big thank
you to everyone who participated !
.sp
The next release is going to be \fB3.0.0\fP, bring breaking changes and enact long
announced deprecations. There\(aqs going to be frequent beta releases,
before the official releases, everyone is welcome to try the betas
so we find problems before the actual release.
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.17.7?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-09\-30
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a regression in pylint 2.17.6 / astroid 2.15.7 causing various
messages for code involving \fBTypeVar\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #9069 (#9069 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9069>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash in refactoring checker when unary operand used with variable in for
loop.
.sp
Closes #9074 (#9074 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9074>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.17.6?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-09\-24
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
When parsing comma\-separated lists of regular expressions in the config,
ignore
commas that are inside braces since those indicate quantifiers, not
delineation
between expressions.
.sp
Closes #7229 (#7229 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7229>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsys.argv\fP is now always correctly considered as impossible to infer
(instead of
using the actual values given to pylint).
.sp
Closes #7710 (#7710 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7710>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt show class fields more than once in Pyreverse diagrams.
.sp
Closes #8189 (#8189 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8189>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt show arrows more than once in Pyreverse diagrams.
.sp
Closes #8522 (#8522 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8522>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt show duplicate type annotations in Pyreverse diagrams.
.sp
Closes #8888 (#8888 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8888>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt add \fIOptional\fP to \fI|\fP annotations with \fINone\fP in Pyreverse diagrams.
.sp
Closes #9014 (#9014 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:9014>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.17.5?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-07\-26
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBunused\-variable\fP when there is an import in a
\fBif TYPE_CHECKING:\fP block and \fBallow\-global\-unused\-variables\fP is set to
\fBno\fP in the configuration.
.sp
Closes #8696 (#8696 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8696>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positives generated when supplying arguments as \fB**kwargs\fP to IO
calls like open().
.sp
Closes #8719 (#8719 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8719>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive where pylint was ignoring method calls annotated as
\fBNoReturn\fP during the \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP check.
.sp
Closes #8747 (#8747 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8747>)
.IP \(bu 2
Exempt parents with only type annotations from the \fBinvalid\-enum\-extension\fP
message.
.sp
Closes #8830 (#8830 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8830>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed crash when a call to \fBsuper()\fP was placed after an operator (e.g.
\fBnot\fP).
.sp
Closes #8554 (#8554 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8554>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash for \fBmodified\-while\-iterating\fP checker when deleting
members of a dict returned from a call.
.sp
Closes #8598 (#8598 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8598>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash in \fBinvalid\-metaclass\fP check when a metaclass had duplicate
bases.
.sp
Closes #8698 (#8698 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8698>)
.IP \(bu 2
Avoid \fBconsider\-using\-f\-string\fP on modulos with brackets in template.
.sp
Closes #8720. (#8720 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8720>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash when \fB__all__\fP exists but cannot be inferred.
.sp
Closes #8740 (#8740 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8740>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash when a variable is assigned to a class attribute of identical name.
.sp
Closes #8754 (#8754 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8754>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash when calling \fBcopy.copy()\fP without arguments.
.sp
Closes #8774 (#8774 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8774>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash when a \fBnonlocal\fP is defined at module\-level.
.sp
Closes #8735 (#8735 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8735>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.17.4?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-05\-06
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBbad\-dunder\-name\fP when there is a user\-defined
\fB__index__\fP method.
.sp
Closes #8613 (#8613 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8613>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpyreverse\fP: added escaping of vertical bar character in annotation labels
produced by DOT printer to ensure it is not treated as field separator of
record\-based nodes.
.sp
Closes #8603 (#8603 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8603>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash when generating a configuration file:
\fBtomlkit.exceptions.TOMLKitError: Can\(aqt add a table to a dotted key\fP
caused by tomlkit \fBv0.11.8\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8632 (#8632 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8632>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.17.3?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-04\-24
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fIunused\-argument\fP false positive when \fI__new__\fP does not use all the
arguments of \fI__init__\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #3670 (#3670 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3670>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBunused\-import\fP false positive for usage of \fBsix.with_metaclass\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7506 (#7506 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7506>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fIlogging\-not\-lazy\fP is not longer emitted for explicitly concatenated string
arguments.
.sp
Closes #8410 (#8410 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8410>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for isinstance\-second\-argument\-not\-valid\-type / W1116 \%<#\:isinstance-second-argument-not-valid-type> when union
types contains None.
.sp
Closes #8424 (#8424 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8424>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed \fIunused\-import\fP so that it observes the \fIdummy\-variables\-rgx\fP option.
.sp
Closes #8500 (#8500 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8500>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fIUnion\fP typed variables without assignment are no longer treated as
\fITypeAlias\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8540 (#8540 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8540>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBpositional\-only\-arguments\-expected\fP when a function
contains both a positional\-only parameter that has a default value, and
\fB**kwargs\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8555 (#8555 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8555>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBkeyword\-arg\-before\-vararg\fP when a positional\-only
parameter with a default value precedes \fB*args\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8570 (#8570 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8570>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Improve output of \fBconsider\-using\-generator\fP message for \fBmin()\fP calls
with \fBdefault\fP keyword.
.sp
Closes #8563 (#8563 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8563>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.17.2?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-04\-03
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-name\fP now allows for integers in \fBtypealias\fP names:
\- now valid: \fBGood2Name\fP, \fBGoodName2\fP\&.
\- still invalid: \fB_1BadName\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8485 (#8485 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8485>)
.IP \(bu 2
No longer consider \fBUnion\fP as type annotation as type alias for naming
checks.
.sp
Closes #8487 (#8487 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8487>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBunnecessary\-lambda\fP no longer warns on lambdas which use its parameters in
their body (other than the final arguments), e.g.
\fBlambda foo: (bar if foo else baz)(foo)\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8496 (#8496 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8496>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in pyreverse when \(dq/\(dq characters are used in the output filename
e.g pyreverse \-o png \-p name/ path/to/project.
.sp
Closes #8504 (#8504 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8504>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.17.1?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-03\-22
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Adds \fBasyncSetUp\fP to the default \fBdefining\-attr\-methods\fP list to silence
\fBattribute\-defined\-outside\-init\fP warning when using
\fBunittest.IsolatedAsyncioTestCase\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #8403 (#8403 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8403>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-clear\-cache\-post\-run\fP now also clears LRU caches for pylint utilities
holding references to AST nodes.
.sp
Closes #8361 (#8361 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8361>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash when \fBTYPE_CHECKING\fP is used without importing it.
.sp
Closes #8434 (#8434 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8434>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a regression of \fBpreferred\-modules\fP where a partial match was used
instead of the required full match.
.sp
Closes #8453 (#8453 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8453>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Internal Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The following utilities are deprecated in favor of the more robust
\fBin_type_checking_block\fP
and will be removed in pylint 3.0:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBis_node_in_guarded_import_block\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBis_node_in_typing_guarded_import_block\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBis_typing_guard\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBis_sys_guard\fP is still available, which was part of
\fBis_node_in_guarded_import_block\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #8433 (#8433 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8433>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.17.0?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-03\-08
.SS New Features
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fIpyreverse\fP now supports custom color palettes with the \fI\-\-color\-palette\fP
option.
.sp
Closes #6738 (#6738 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6738>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBinvalid\-name\fP check for \fBTypeAlias\fP names.
.sp
Closes #7081. (#7081 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7081>)
.IP \(bu 2
Accept values of the form \fB<class name>.<attribute name>\fP for the
\fBexclude\-protected\fP list.
.sp
Closes #7343 (#7343 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7343>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fI\-\-version\fP option to \fIpyreverse\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #7851 (#7851 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7851>)
.IP \(bu 2
Adds new functionality with preferred\-modules configuration to detect
submodules.
.sp
Refs #7957 (#7957 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7957>)
.IP \(bu 2
Support implicit namespace packages (PEP 420).
.sp
Closes #8154 (#8154 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8154>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add globbing pattern support for \fB\-\-source\-roots\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #8290 (#8290 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8290>)
.IP \(bu 2
Support globbing pattern when defining which file/directory/module to lint.
.sp
Closes #8310 (#8310 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8310>)
.IP \(bu 2
pylint now supports \fBTryStar\fP nodes from Python 3.11 and should be fully
compatible with Python 3.11.
.sp
Closes #8387 (#8387 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8387>)
.UNINDENT
.SS New Checks
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add a \fBbad\-chained\-comparison\fP check that emits a warning when
there is a chained comparison where one expression is semantically
incompatible with the other.
.sp
Closes #6559 (#6559 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6559>)
.IP \(bu 2
Adds an \fBimplicit\-flag\-alias\fP check that emits a warning when a class
derived from \fBenum.IntFlag\fP assigns distinct integer values that share
common bit positions.
.sp
Refs #8102 (#8102 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8102>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix various false positives for functions that return directly from
structural pattern matching cases.
.sp
Closes #5288 (#5288 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5288>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when
\fBtyping.TYPE_CHECKING\fP is used with if/elif/else blocks.
.sp
Closes #7574 (#7574 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7574>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for isinstance\-second\-argument\-not\-valid\-type / W1116 \%<#\:isinstance-second-argument-not-valid-type> with union
types.
.sp
Closes #8205 (#8205 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8205>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP for named expressions
appearing after the first element in a list, tuple, or set.
.sp
Closes #8252 (#8252 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8252>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBwrong\-spelling\-in\-comment\fP with class names in a
python 2 type comment.
.sp
Closes #8370 (#8370 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8370>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Negatives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false negative for missing\-parentheses\-for\-call\-in\-test / W0126 \%<#\:missing-parentheses-for-call-in-test>\(aq when
inference
failed for the internal of the call as we did not need that information to
raise
correctly.
.sp
Refs #8185 (#8185 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8185>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negative for inconsistent\-returns with while\-loops.
.sp
Closes #8280 (#8280 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8280>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP false positive when the walrus operator
is used with a ternary operator in dictionary key/value initialization.
.sp
Closes #8125 (#8125 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8125>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBno\-name\-in\-module\fP false positive raised when a package defines a
variable with the
same name as one of its submodules.
.sp
Closes #8148 (#8148 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8148>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash happening for python interpreter < 3.9 following a failed typing
update.
.sp
Closes #8161 (#8161 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8161>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBnested\-min\-max\fP suggestion message to indicate it\(aqs possible to splat
iterable objects.
.sp
Closes #8168 (#8168 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8168>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash happening when a class attribute was negated in the start
argument of an enumerate.
.sp
Closes #8207 (#8207 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8207>)
.IP \(bu 2
Prevent emitting \fBinvalid\-name\fP for the line on which a \fBglobal\fP
statement is declared.
.sp
Closes #8307 (#8307 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8307>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Update explanation for \fBglobal\-variable\-not\-assigned\fP and add confidence.
.sp
Closes #5073 (#5073 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5073>)
.IP \(bu 2
The governance model and the path to become a maintainer have been documented
as
part of our effort to guarantee that the software supply chain in which
pylint is
included is secure.
.sp
Refs #8329 (#8329 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8329>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.16
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B Release
2.16
.TP
.B Date
2023\-02\-01
.UNINDENT
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.sp
In 2.16.0 we added aggregation and composition understanding in \fBpyreverse\fP, and a way to clear
the cache in between run in server mode (originally for the VS Code integration). Apart from the bug
fixes there\(aqs also a lot of new checks, and new extensions that have been asked for for a long time
that were implemented.
.sp
If you want to benefit from all the new checks load the following plugins:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
pylint.extensions.dict_init_mutate,
pylint.extensions.dunder,
pylint.extensions.typing,
pylint.extensions.magic_value,
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
We still welcome any community effort to help review, integrate, and add good/bad examples to the doc for
<\%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5953>>\(ga_. This should be doable without any \fBpylint\fP or \fBastroid\fP
knowledge, so this is the perfect entrypoint if you want to contribute to \fBpylint\fP or open source without
any experience with our code!
.sp
Last but not least @clavedeluna and @nickdrozd became triagers, welcome to the team !
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.16.4?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-03\-06
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for isinstance\-second\-argument\-not\-valid\-type / W1116 \%<#\:isinstance-second-argument-not-valid-type> with union
types.
.sp
Closes #8205 (#8205 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8205>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.16.3?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-03\-03
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBwrong\-spelling\-in\-comment\fP with class names in a
python 2 type comment.
.sp
Closes #8370 (#8370 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8370>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Prevent emitting \fBinvalid\-name\fP for the line on which a \fBglobal\fP
statement is declared.
.sp
Closes #8307 (#8307 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8307>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.16.2?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-02\-13
.SS New Features
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fI\-\-version\fP option to \fIpyreverse\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #7851 (#7851 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7851>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when
\fBtyping.TYPE_CHECKING\fP is used with if/elif/else blocks.
.sp
Closes #7574 (#7574 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7574>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP for named expressions
appearing after the first element in a list, tuple, or set.
.sp
Closes #8252 (#8252 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8252>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP false positive when the walrus operator
is used with a ternary operator in dictionary key/value initialization.
.sp
Closes #8125 (#8125 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8125>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBno\-name\-in\-module\fP false positive raised when a package defines a
variable with the
same name as one of its submodules.
.sp
Closes #8148 (#8148 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8148>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBnested\-min\-max\fP suggestion message to indicate it\(aqs possible to splat
iterable objects.
.sp
Closes #8168 (#8168 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8168>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash happening when a class attribute was negated in the start
argument of an enumerate.
.sp
Closes #8207 (#8207 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8207>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.16.1?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-02\-02
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash happening for python interpreter < 3.9 following a failed typing
update.
.sp
Closes #8161 (#8161 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8161>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.16.0?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-02\-01
.SS Changes requiring user actions
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBaccept\-no\-raise\-doc\fP option related to \fBmissing\-raises\-doc\fP will now
be correctly taken into account all the time.
.sp
Pylint will no longer raise missing\-raises\-doc / W9006 \%<#\:missing-raises-doc> (W9006) when no exceptions are
documented and accept\-no\-raise\-doc is true (issue #7208).
If you were expecting missing\-raises\-doc / W9006 \%<#\:missing-raises-doc> errors to be raised in that case,
you
will now have to add \fBaccept\-no\-raise\-doc=no\fP in your configuration to keep
the same behavior.
.sp
Closes #7208 (#7208 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7208>)
.UNINDENT
.SS New Features
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Added the \fBno\-header\fP output format. If enabled with
\fB\-\-output\-format=no\-header\fP, it will not include the module name in the
output.
.sp
Closes #5362 (#5362 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5362>)
.IP \(bu 2
Added configuration option \fBclear\-cache\-post\-run\fP to support server\-like
usage.
Use this flag if you expect the linted files to be altered between runs.
.sp
Refs #5401 (#5401 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5401>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fB\-\-allow\-reexport\-from\-package\fP option to configure the
\fBuseless\-import\-alias\fP check not to emit a warning if a name
is reexported from a package.
.sp
Closes #6006 (#6006 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6006>)
.IP \(bu 2
Update \fBpyreverse\fP to differentiate between aggregations and compositions.
\fBpyreverse\fP checks if it\(aqs an Instance or a Call of an object via method
parameters (via type hints)
to decide if it\(aqs a composition or an aggregation.
.sp
Refs #6543 (#6543 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6543>)
.UNINDENT
.SS New Checks
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Adds a \fBpointless\-exception\-statement\fP check that emits a warning when an
Exception is created and not assigned, raised or returned.
.sp
Refs #3110 (#3110 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3110>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add a \fBshadowed\-import\fP message for aliased imports.
.sp
Closes #4836 (#4836 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4836>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add new check called \fBunbalanced\-dict\-unpacking\fP to check for unbalanced
dict unpacking
in assignment and for loops.
.sp
Closes #5797 (#5797 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5797>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add new checker \fBpositional\-only\-arguments\-expected\fP to check for cases
when
positional\-only arguments have been passed as keyword arguments.
.sp
Closes #6489 (#6489 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6489>)
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBsingledispatch\-method\fP which informs that \fB@singledispatch\fP should
decorate functions and not class/instance methods.
Added \fBsingledispatchmethod\-function\fP which informs that
\fB@singledispatchmethod\fP should decorate class/instance methods and not
functions.
.sp
Closes #6917 (#6917 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6917>)
.IP \(bu 2
Rename \fBbroad\-except\fP to \fBbroad\-exception\-caught\fP and add new checker
\fBbroad\-exception\-raised\fP
which will warn if general exceptions \fBBaseException\fP or \fBException\fP are
raised.
.sp
Closes #7494 (#7494 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7494>)
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBnested\-min\-max\fP which flags \fBmin(1, min(2, 3))\fP to simplify to
\fBmin(1, 2, 3)\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7546 (#7546 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7546>)
.IP \(bu 2
Extended \fBuse\-dict\-literal\fP to also warn about call to \fBdict()\fP when
passing keyword arguments.
.sp
Closes #7690 (#7690 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7690>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBnamed\-expr\-without\-context\fP check to emit a warning if a named
expression is used outside a context like \fBif\fP, \fBfor\fP, \fBwhile\fP, or
a comprehension.
.sp
Refs #7760 (#7760 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7760>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBinvalid\-slice\-step\fP check to warn about a slice step value of \fB0\fP
for common builtin sequences.
.sp
Refs #7762 (#7762 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7762>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBconsider\-refactoring\-into\-while\-condition\fP check to recommend
refactoring when
a while loop is defined with a constant condition with an immediate \fBif\fP
statement to check for \fBbreak\fP condition as a first statement.
.sp
Closes #8015 (#8015 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8015>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Extensions
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add new extension checker \fBdict\-init\-mutate\fP that flags mutating a
dictionary immediately
after the dictionary was created.
.sp
Closes #2876 (#2876 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:2876>)
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBbad\-dunder\-name\fP extension check, which flags bad or misspelled
dunder methods.
You can use the \fBgood\-dunder\-names\fP option to allow specific dunder names.
.sp
Closes #3038 (#3038 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3038>)
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBconsider\-using\-augmented\-assign\fP check for \fBCodeStyle\fP extension
which flags \fBx = x + 1\fP to simplify to \fBx += 1\fP\&.
This check is disabled by default. To use it, load the code style extension
with \fBload\-plugins=pylint.extensions.code_style\fP and add
\fBconsider\-using\-augmented\-assign\fP in the \fBenable\fP option.
.sp
Closes #3391 (#3391 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3391>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBmagic\-number\fP plugin checker for comparison with constants instead of
named constants or enums.
You can use it with \fB\-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.magic_value\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7281 (#7281 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7281>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBredundant\-typehint\-argument\fP message for \fItyping\fP plugin for duplicate
assign typehints.
Enable the plugin to enable the message with:
\fB\-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.typing\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7636 (#7636 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7636>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBunused\-variable\fP and \fBunused\-import\fP when a name
is only used in a string literal type annotation.
.sp
Closes #3299 (#3299 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3299>)
.IP \(bu 2
Document a known false positive for \fBuseless\-suppression\fP when disabling
\fBline\-too\-long\fP in a module with only comments and no code.
.sp
Closes #3368 (#3368 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3368>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtrailing\-whitespaces\fP is no longer reported within strings.
.sp
Closes #3822 (#3822 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3822>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBglobal\-variable\-not\-assigned\fP when a global
variable is re\-assigned via an \fBImportFrom\fP node.
.sp
Closes #4809 (#4809 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4809>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBuse\-maxsplit\-arg\fP with custom split method.
.sp
Closes #4857 (#4857 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4857>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBlogging\-fstring\-interpolation\fP false positive raised when logging and
f\-string with \fB%s\fP formatting.
.sp
Closes #4984 (#4984 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4984>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP in pattern matching
with a guard.
.sp
Closes #5327 (#5327 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5327>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBuse\-sequence\-for\-iteration\fP when unpacking a set with \fB*\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #5788 (#5788 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5788>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBdeprecated\-method\fP false positive when alias for method is similar to
name of deprecated method.
.sp
Closes #5886 (#5886 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5886>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBassigning\-non\-slot\fP when a class attribute is
re\-assigned.
.sp
Closes #6001 (#6001 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6001>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBtoo\-many\-function\-args\fP when a function call is
assigned to a class attribute inside the class where the function is defined.
.sp
Closes #6592 (#6592 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6592>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes false positive \fBabstract\-method\fP on Protocol classes.
.sp
Closes #7209 (#7209 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7209>)
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint now understands the \fBkw_only\fP keyword argument for \fBdataclass\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7290, closes #6550, closes #5857 (#7290 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7290>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBundefined\-loop\-variable\fP in \fBfor\-else\fP loops that
use a function
having a return type annotation of \fBNoReturn\fP or \fBNever\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7311 (#7311 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7311>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP for functions/classes defined in type checking
guard.
.sp
Closes #7368 (#7368 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7368>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBunhashable\-member\fP when subclassing \fBdict\fP and
using the subclass as a dictionary key.
.sp
Closes #7501 (#7501 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7501>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix the message for \fBunnecessary\-dunder\-call\fP for \fB__aiter__\fP and
\fB__aneext__\fP\&. Also
only emit the warning when \fBpy\-version\fP >= 3.10.
.sp
Closes #7529 (#7529 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7529>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP false positive when else branch calls
\fBsys.exit\fP or similar terminating functions.
.sp
Closes #7563 (#7563 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7563>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP for imports guarded by
\fBtyping.TYPE_CHECKING\fP later used in variable annotations.
.sp
Closes #7609 (#7609 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7609>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBsimplify\-boolean\-expression\fP when multiple values
are inferred for a constant.
.sp
Closes #7626 (#7626 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7626>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBunnecessary\-list\-index\-lookup\fP will not be wrongly emitted if
\fBenumerate\fP is called with \fBstart\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7682 (#7682 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7682>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn about \fBstop\-iteration\-return\fP when using \fBnext()\fP over
\fBitertools.cycle\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7765 (#7765 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7765>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP false positive when the walrus operator
is used in a ternary operator.
.sp
Closes #7779 (#7779 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7779>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBmissing\-param\-doc\fP false positive when function parameter has an
escaped underscore.
.sp
Closes #7827 (#7827 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7827>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes \fBmethod\-cache\-max\-size\-none\fP false positive for methods inheriting
from \fBEnum\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7857 (#7857 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7857>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmultiple\-statements\fP no longer triggers for function stubs using inlined
\fB\&...\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7860 (#7860 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7860>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when a name guarded by
\fBif TYPE_CHECKING:\fP is used as a type annotation in a function body and
later re\-imported in the same scope.
.sp
Closes #7882 (#7882 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7882>)
.IP \(bu 2
Prevent \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when imports guarded by \fBif
TYPE_CHECKING\fP
are guarded again when used.
.sp
Closes #7979 (#7979 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7979>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes false positive for \fBtry\-except\-raise\fP with multiple exceptions in one
except statement if exception are in different namespace.
.sp
Closes #8051 (#8051 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8051>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBinvalid\-name\fP errors for \fBtyping_extension.TypeVar\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #8089 (#8089 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8089>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBno\-kwoa\fP false positive for context managers.
.sp
Closes #8100 (#8100 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8100>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBredefined\-variable\-type\fP when \fBasync\fP methods
are present.
.sp
Closes #8120 (#8120 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8120>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Negatives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Code following a call to  \fBquit\fP,  \fBexit\fP, \fBsys.exit\fP or \fBos._exit\fP
will be marked as \fIunreachable\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #519 (#519 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:519>)
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when function arguments are redefined inside
an inner function and accessed there before assignment.
.sp
Closes #2374 (#2374 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:2374>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false negative for \fBunused\-import\fP when one module used an import in
a type annotation that was also used in another module.
.sp
Closes #4150 (#4150 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4150>)
.IP \(bu 2
Flag \fBsuperfluous\-parens\fP if parentheses are used during string
concatenation.
.sp
Closes #4792 (#4792 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4792>)
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when relying on names only defined under
conditions always testing false.
.sp
Closes #4913 (#4913 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4913>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-using\-join\fP can now be emitted for non\-empty string separators.
.sp
Closes #6639 (#6639 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6639>)
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP for further imports guarded by
\fBTYPE_CHECKING\fP
.sp
Previously, this message was only emitted for imports guarded directly under
\fBTYPE_CHECKING\fP, not guarded two if\-branches deep, nor when
\fBTYPE_CHECKING\fP
was imported from \fBtyping\fP under an alias.
.sp
Closes #7539 (#7539 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7539>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false negative for \fBunused\-import\fP when a constant inside
\fBtyping.Annotated\fP was treated as a reference to an import.
.sp
Closes #7547 (#7547 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7547>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-using\-any\-or\-all\fP message will now be raised in cases when
boolean is initialized, reassigned during loop, and immediately returned.
.sp
Closes #7699 (#7699 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7699>)
.IP \(bu 2
Extend \fBinvalid\-slice\-index\fP to emit an warning for invalid slice indices
used with string and byte sequences, and range objects.
.sp
Refs #7762 (#7762 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7762>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes \fBunnecessary\-list\-index\-lookup\fP false negative when \fBenumerate\fP is
called with \fBiterable\fP as a kwarg.
.sp
Closes #7770 (#7770 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7770>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBno\-else\-return\fP or \fBno\-else\-raise\fP will be emitted if \fBexcept\fP block
always returns or raises.
.sp
Closes #7788 (#7788 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7788>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBdangerous\-default\-value\fP false negative when \fB*\fP is used.
.sp
Closes #7818 (#7818 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7818>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-using\-with\fP now triggers for \fBpathlib.Path.open\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7964 (#7964 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7964>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix bug in detecting \fBunused\-variable\fP when iterating on variable.
.sp
Closes #3044 (#3044 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3044>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix bug in scanning of names inside arguments to \fBtyping.Literal\fP\&.
See \%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0586/#\:literals-enums-and-forward-references>
for details.
.sp
Refs #3299 (#3299 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3299>)
.IP \(bu 2
Update \fBdisallowed\-name\fP check to flag module\-level variables.
.sp
Closes #3701 (#3701 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3701>)
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint will no longer deadlock if a parallel job is killed but fail
immediately instead.
.sp
Closes #3899 (#3899 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3899>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix ignored files being linted when passed on stdin.
.sp
Closes #4354 (#4354 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4354>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBno\-member\fP false negative when augmented assign is done manually,
without \fB+=\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #4562 (#4562 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4562>)
.IP \(bu 2
Any assertion on a populated tuple will now receive a \fBassert\-on\-tuple\fP
warning.
.sp
Closes #4655 (#4655 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4655>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmissing\-return\-doc\fP, \fBmissing\-raises\-doc\fP and \fBmissing\-yields\-doc\fP now
respect
the \fBno\-docstring\-rgx\fP option.
.sp
Closes #4743 (#4743 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4743>)
.IP \(bu 2
Update \fBreimported\fP help message for clarity.
.sp
Closes #4836 (#4836 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4836>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-iterating\-dictionary\fP will no longer be raised if bitwise
operations are used.
.sp
Closes #5478 (#5478 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5478>)
.IP \(bu 2
Using custom braces in \fBmsg\-template\fP will now work properly.
.sp
Closes #5636 (#5636 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5636>)
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint will now filter duplicates given to it before linting. The output
should
be the same whether a file is given/discovered multiple times or not.
.sp
Closes #6242, #4053 (#6242 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6242>)
.IP \(bu 2
Remove \fB__index__\fP dunder method call from \fBunnecessary\-dunder\-call\fP
check.
.sp
Closes #6795 (#6795 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6795>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed handling of \fB\-\-\fP as separator between positional arguments and flags.
This was not actually fixed in 2.14.5.
.sp
Closes #7003, Refs #7096 (#7003 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7003>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt crash on \fBOSError\fP in config file discovery.
.sp
Closes #7169 (#7169 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7169>)
.IP \(bu 2
Messages sent to reporter are now copied so a reporter cannot modify the
message sent to other reporters.
.sp
Closes #7214 (#7214 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7214>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a case where custom plugins specified by command line could silently
fail.
.sp
Specifically, if a plugin relies on the \fBinit\-hook\fP option changing
\fBsys.path\fP before
it can be imported, this will now emit a \fBbad\-plugin\-value\fP message. Before
this
change, it would silently fail to register the plugin for use, but would load
any configuration, which could have unintended effects.
.sp
Fixes part of #7264. (#7264 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7264>)
.IP \(bu 2
Update \fBmodified_iterating\fP checker to fix a crash with \fBfor\fP loops on
empty list.
.sp
Closes #7380 (#7380 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7380>)
.IP \(bu 2
Update wording for \fBarguments\-differ\fP and \fBarguments\-renamed\fP to clarify
overriding object.
.sp
Closes #7390 (#7390 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7390>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdisable\-next\fP is now correctly scoped to only the succeeding line.
.sp
Closes #7401 (#7401 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7401>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash in the \fBunhashable\-member\fP checker when using a \fBlambda\fP as
a dict key.
.sp
Closes #7453 (#7453 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7453>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBmailcap\fP to deprecated modules list.
.sp
Closes #7457 (#7457 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7457>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the \fBmodified\-iterating\-dict\fP checker involving instance
attributes.
.sp
Closes #7461 (#7461 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7461>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-class\-object\fP does not crash anymore when \fB__class__\fP is
assigned alongside another variable.
.sp
Closes #7467 (#7467 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7467>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-help\-msg\fP now accepts a comma\-separated list of message IDs again.
.sp
Closes #7471 (#7471 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7471>)
.IP \(bu 2
Allow specifying non\-builtin exceptions in the \fBovergeneral\-exception\fP
option
using an exception\(aqs qualified name.
.sp
Closes #7495 (#7495 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7495>)
.IP \(bu 2
Report \fBno\-self\-argument\fP rather than \fBno\-method\-argument\fP for methods
with variadic arguments.
.sp
Closes #7507 (#7507 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7507>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed an issue where \fBsyntax\-error\fP couldn\(aqt be raised on files with
invalid encodings.
.sp
Closes #7522 (#7522 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7522>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBredefined\-outer\-name\fP when aliasing \fBtyping\fP
e.g. as \fBt\fP and guarding imports under \fBt.TYPE_CHECKING\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7524 (#7524 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7524>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash of the \fBmodified_iterating\fP checker when iterating on a set
defined as a class attribute.
.sp
Closes #7528 (#7528 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7528>)
.IP \(bu 2
Use \fBpy\-version\fP to determine if a message should be emitted for messages
defined with \fBmax\-version\fP or \fBmin\-version\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7569 (#7569 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7569>)
.IP \(bu 2
Improve \fBbad\-thread\-instantiation\fP check to warn if \fBtarget\fP is not
passed in as a keyword argument
or as a second argument.
.sp
Closes #7570 (#7570 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7570>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes edge case of custom method named \fBnext\fP raised an astroid error.
.sp
Closes #7610 (#7610 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7610>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a multi\-processing crash that prevents using any more than 1 thread on
MacOS.
.sp
The returned module objects and errors that were cached by the linter plugin
loader
cannot be reliably pickled. This means that \fBdill\fP would throw an error
when
attempting to serialise the linter object for multi\-processing use.
.sp
Closes #7635. (#7635 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7635>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash that happened when parsing files with unexpected encoding starting
with \(aqutf\(aq like \fButf13\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7661 (#7661 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7661>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash when a child class with an \fB__init__\fP method inherits from a
parent class with an \fB__init__\fP class attribute.
.sp
Closes #7742 (#7742 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7742>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBvalid\-metaclass\-classmethod\-first\-arg\fP default config value from \(dqcls\(dq
to \(dqmcs\(dq
which would cause both a false\-positive and false\-negative.
.sp
Closes #7782 (#7782 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7782>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes a crash in the \fBunnecessary_list_index_lookup\fP check when using
\fBenumerate\fP with \fBstart\fP and a class attribute.
.sp
Closes #7821 (#7821 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7821>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes a crash in \fBstop\-iteration\-return\fP when the \fBnext\fP builtin is
called without arguments.
.sp
Closes #7828 (#7828 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7828>)
.IP \(bu 2
When pylint exit due to bad arguments being provided the exit code will now
be the expected \fB32\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #7931 (#7931 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7931>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes a \fBModuleNotFound\fP exception when running pylint on a Django project
with the \fBpylint_django\fP plugin enabled.
.sp
Closes #7938 (#7938 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7938>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash when inferring a value and using its qname on a slice that was
being incorrectly called.
.sp
Closes #8067 (#8067 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8067>)
.IP \(bu 2
Use better regex to check for private attributes.
.sp
Refs #8081 (#8081 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8081>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix issue with new typing Union syntax in runtime context for Python 3.10+.
.sp
Closes #8119 (#8119 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:8119>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint now provides basic support for Python 3.11.
.sp
Closes #5920 (#5920 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5920>)
.IP \(bu 2
Update message for \fBabstract\-method\fP to include child class name.
.sp
Closes #7124 (#7124 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7124>)
.IP \(bu 2
Update Pyreverse\(aqs dot and plantuml printers to detect when class methods are
abstract and show them with italic font.
For the dot printer update the label to use html\-like syntax.
.sp
Closes #7346 (#7346 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7346>)
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBdocparams\fP extension now considers typing in Numpy style docstrings
as \(dqdocumentation\(dq for the \fBmissing\-param\-doc\fP message.
.sp
Refs #7398 (#7398 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7398>)
.IP \(bu 2
Relevant \fBDeprecationWarnings\fP are now raised with \fBstacklevel=2\fP, so
they have the callsite attached in the message.
.sp
Closes #7463 (#7463 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7463>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add a \fBminimal\fP option to \fBpylint\-config\fP and its toml generator.
.sp
Closes #7485 (#7485 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7485>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add method name to the error messages of \fBno\-method\-argument\fP and
\fBno\-self\-argument\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7507 (#7507 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7507>)
.IP \(bu 2
Prevent leaving the pip install cache in the Docker image.
.sp
Refs #7544 (#7544 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7544>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add a keyword\-only \fBcompare_constants\fP argument to \fBsafe_infer\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #7626 (#7626 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7626>)
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBdefault_enabled\fP option to optional message dict. Provides an option
to disable a checker message by default.
To use a disabled message, the user must enable it explicitly by adding the
message to the \fBenable\fP option.
.sp
Refs #7629 (#7629 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7629>)
.IP \(bu 2
Sort \fB\-\-generated\-rcfile\fP output.
.sp
Refs #7655 (#7655 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7655>)
.IP \(bu 2
epylint is now deprecated and will be removed in pylint 3.0.0. All emacs and
flymake related
files were removed and their support will now happen in an external
repository :
\%<https://\:github\:.com/\:emacsorphanage/\:pylint>\&.
.sp
Closes #7737 (#7737 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7737>)
.IP \(bu 2
Adds test for existing preferred\-modules configuration functionality.
.sp
Refs #7957 (#7957 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7957>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Internal Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add and fix regression tests for plugin loading.
.sp
This shores up the tests that cover the loading of custom plugins as affected
by any changes made to the \fBsys.path\fP during execution of an \fBinit\-hook\fP\&.
Given the existing contract of allowing plugins to be loaded by fiddling with
the path in this way, this is now the last bit of work needed to close Github
issue #7264.
.sp
Closes #7264 (#7264 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7264>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.15
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B Release
2.15
.TP
.B Date
2022\-08\-26
.UNINDENT
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.sp
In pylint 2.15.0, we added a new check \fBmissing\-timeout\fP to warn of
default timeout values that could cause a program to be hanging indefinitely.
.sp
We improved \fBpylint\fP\(aqs handling of namespace packages. More packages should
be linted without resorting to using the \fB\-\-recursive=y\fP option.
.sp
We still welcome any community effort to help review, integrate, and add good/bad examples to the doc for
<\%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5953>>\(ga_. This should be doable without any \fBpylint\fP or \fBastroid\fP
knowledge, so this is the perfect entrypoint if you want to contribute to \fBpylint\fP or open source without
any experience with our code!
.sp
Internally, we changed the way we generate the release notes, thanks to DudeNr33.
There will be no more conflict resolution to do in the changelog, and every contributor rejoice.
.sp
Marc Byrne became a maintainer, welcome to the team !
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.15.10?
.sp
Release date: 2023\-01\-09
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBuse\-sequence\-for\-iteration\fP when unpacking a set with \fB*\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #5788 (#5788 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5788>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBassigning\-non\-slot\fP when a class attribute is
re\-assigned.
.sp
Closes #6001 (#6001 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6001>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP false positive when the walrus operator
is used in a ternary operator.
.sp
Closes #7779 (#7779 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7779>)
.IP \(bu 2
Prevent \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when imports guarded by \fBif
TYPE_CHECKING\fP
are guarded again when used.
.sp
Closes #7979 (#7979 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7979>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Using custom braces in \fBmsg\-template\fP will now work properly.
.sp
Closes #5636 (#5636 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5636>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.15.9?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-12\-17
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP in pattern matching
with a guard.
.sp
Closes #5327 (#5327 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5327>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint will no longer deadlock if a parallel job is killed but fail
immediately instead.
.sp
Closes #3899 (#3899 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3899>)
.IP \(bu 2
When pylint exit due to bad arguments being provided the exit code will now
be the expected \fB32\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #7931 (#7931 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7931>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes a \fBModuleNotFound\fP exception when running pylint on a Django project
with the \fBpylint_django\fP plugin enabled.
.sp
Closes #7938 (#7938 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7938>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.15.8?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-12\-05
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Document a known false positive for \fBuseless\-suppression\fP when disabling
\fBline\-too\-long\fP in a module with only comments and no code.
.sp
Closes #3368 (#3368 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3368>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBlogging\-fstring\-interpolation\fP false positive raised when logging and
f\-string with \fB%s\fP formatting.
.sp
Closes #4984 (#4984 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4984>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes false positive \fBabstract\-method\fP on Protocol classes.
.sp
Closes #7209 (#7209 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7209>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBmissing\-param\-doc\fP false positive when function parameter has an
escaped underscore.
.sp
Closes #7827 (#7827 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7827>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmultiple\-statements\fP no longer triggers for function stubs using inlined
\fB\&...\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7860 (#7860 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7860>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.15.7?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-11\-27
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBdeprecated\-method\fP false positive when alias for method is similar to
name of deprecated method.
.sp
Closes #5886 (#5886 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5886>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP for imports guarded by
\fBtyping.TYPE_CHECKING\fP later used in variable annotations.
.sp
Closes #7609 (#7609 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7609>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint will now filter duplicates given to it before linting. The output
should
be the same whether a file is given/discovered multiple times or not.
.sp
Closes #6242, #4053 (#6242 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6242>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes a crash in \fBstop\-iteration\-return\fP when the \fBnext\fP builtin is
called without arguments.
.sp
Closes #7828 (#7828 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7828>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.15.6?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-11\-19
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBunhashable\-member\fP when subclassing \fBdict\fP and
using the subclass as a dictionary key.
.sp
Closes #7501 (#7501 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7501>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBunnecessary\-list\-index\-lookup\fP will not be wrongly emitted if
\fBenumerate\fP is called with \fBstart\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7682 (#7682 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7682>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn about \fBstop\-iteration\-return\fP when using \fBnext()\fP over
\fBitertools.cycle\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7765 (#7765 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7765>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Messages sent to reporter are now copied so a reporter cannot modify the
message sent to other reporters.
.sp
Closes #7214 (#7214 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7214>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes edge case of custom method named \fBnext\fP raised an astroid error.
.sp
Closes #7610 (#7610 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7610>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash that happened when parsing files with unexpected encoding starting
with \(aqutf\(aq like \fButf13\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7661 (#7661 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7661>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash when a child class with an \fB__init__\fP method inherits from a
parent class with an \fB__init__\fP class attribute.
.sp
Closes #7742 (#7742 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7742>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.15.5?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-10\-21
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBsimplify\-boolean\-expression\fP when multiple values
are inferred for a constant.
.sp
Closes #7626 (#7626 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7626>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Remove \fB__index__\fP dunder method call from \fBunnecessary\-dunder\-call\fP
check.
.sp
Closes #6795 (#6795 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6795>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a multi\-processing crash that prevents using any more than 1 thread on
MacOS.
.sp
The returned module objects and errors that were cached by the linter plugin
loader
cannot be reliably pickled. This means that \fBdill\fP would throw an error
when
attempting to serialise the linter object for multi\-processing use.
.sp
Closes #7635. (#7635 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7635>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add a keyword\-only \fBcompare_constants\fP argument to \fBsafe_infer\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #7626 (#7626 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7626>)
.IP \(bu 2
Sort \fB\-\-generated\-rcfile\fP output.
.sp
Refs #7655 (#7655 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7655>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.15.4?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-10\-10
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix the message for \fBunnecessary\-dunder\-call\fP for \fB__aiter__\fP and
\fB__anext__\fP\&. Also
only emit the warning when \fBpy\-version\fP >= 3.10.
.sp
Closes #7529 (#7529 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7529>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix bug in detecting \fBunused\-variable\fP when iterating on variable.
.sp
Closes #3044 (#3044 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3044>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed handling of \fB\-\-\fP as separator between positional arguments and flags.
This was not actually fixed in 2.14.5.
.sp
Closes #7003, Refs #7096 (#7003 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7003>)
.IP \(bu 2
Report \fBno\-self\-argument\fP rather than \fBno\-method\-argument\fP for methods
with variadic arguments.
.sp
Closes #7507 (#7507 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7507>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed an issue where \fBsyntax\-error\fP couldn\(aqt be raised on files with
invalid encodings.
.sp
Closes #7522 (#7522 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7522>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBredefined\-outer\-name\fP when aliasing \fBtyping\fP
e.g. as \fBt\fP and guarding imports under \fBt.TYPE_CHECKING\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7524 (#7524 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7524>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash of the \fBmodified_iterating\fP checker when iterating on a set
defined as a class attribute.
.sp
Closes #7528 (#7528 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7528>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix bug in scanning of names inside arguments to \fBtyping.Literal\fP\&.
See \%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0586/#\:literals-enums-and-forward-references>
for details.
.sp
Refs #3299 (#3299 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3299>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add method name to the error messages of \fBno\-method\-argument\fP and
\fBno\-self\-argument\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7507 (#7507 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7507>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.15.3?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-09\-19
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash in the \fBunhashable\-member\fP checker when using a \fBlambda\fP as a dict key.
.sp
Closes #7453 (#7453 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7453>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the \fBmodified\-iterating\-dict\fP checker involving instance attributes.
.sp
Closes #7461 (#7461 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7461>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-class\-object\fP does not crash anymore when \fB__class__\fP is assigned alongside another variable.
.sp
Closes #7467 (#7467 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7467>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBglobal\-variable\-not\-assigned\fP when a global variable is re\-assigned via an \fBImportFrom\fP node.
.sp
Closes #4809 (#4809 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4809>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBundefined\-loop\-variable\fP in \fBfor\-else\fP loops that use a function
having a return type annotation of \fBNoReturn\fP or \fBNever\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7311 (#7311 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7311>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-help\-msg\fP now accepts a comma\-separated list of message IDs again.
.sp
Closes #7471 (#7471 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7471>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.15.2?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-09\-07
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a case where custom plugins specified by command line could silently fail.
.sp
Specifically, if a plugin relies on the \fBinit\-hook\fP option changing \fBsys.path\fP before
it can be imported, this will now emit a \fBbad\-plugin\-value\fP message. Before this
change, it would silently fail to register the plugin for use, but would load
any configuration, which could have unintended effects.
.sp
Fixes part of #7264. (#7264 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7264>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP for functions/classes defined in type checking guard.
.sp
Closes #7368 (#7368 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7368>)
.IP \(bu 2
Update \fBmodified_iterating\fP checker to fix a crash with \fBfor\fP loops on empty list.
.sp
Closes #7380 (#7380 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7380>)
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBdocparams\fP extension now considers typing in Numpy style docstrings
as \(dqdocumentation\(dq for the \fBmissing\-param\-doc\fP message.
.sp
Refs #7398 (#7398 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7398>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBunused\-variable\fP and \fBunused\-import\fP when a name is only used in a string literal type annotation.
.sp
Closes #3299 (#3299 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3299>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fBtoo\-many\-function\-args\fP when a function call is assigned to a class attribute inside the class where the function is defined.
.sp
Closes #6592 (#6592 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6592>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix ignored files being linted when passed on stdin.
.sp
Closes #4354 (#4354 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4354>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmissing\-return\-doc\fP, \fBmissing\-raises\-doc\fP and \fBmissing\-yields\-doc\fP now respect
the \fBno\-docstring\-rgx\fP option.
.sp
Closes #4743 (#4743 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4743>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt crash on \fBOSError\fP in config file discovery.
.sp
Closes #7169 (#7169 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7169>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdisable\-next\fP is now correctly scoped to only the succeeding line.
.sp
Closes #7401 (#7401 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7401>)
.IP \(bu 2
Update \fBmodified_iterating\fP checker to fix a crash with \fBfor\fP loops on empty list.
.sp
Closes #7380 (#7380 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7380>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.15.1?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-09\-06
.sp
This is a \(dqgithub only release\(dq, it was mistakenly released as \fB2.16.0\-dev\fP on pypi. Replaced by \fB2.15.2\fP\&.
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 2.15.0?
.SS New Checks
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Added new checker \fBmissing\-timeout\fP to warn of default timeout values that could cause
a program to be hanging indefinitely.
.sp
Refs #6780 (#6780 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6780>)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Positives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt report \fBsuper\-init\-not\-called\fP for abstract \fB__init__\fP methods.
.sp
Closes #3975 (#3975 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3975>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt report \fBunsupported\-binary\-operation\fP on Python <= 3.9 when using the \fB|\fP operator
with types, if one has a metaclass that overloads \fB__or__\fP or \fB__ror__\fP as appropriate.
.sp
Closes #4951 (#4951 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4951>)
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt report \fBno\-value\-for\-parameter\fP for dataclasses fields annotated with \fBKW_ONLY\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #5767 (#5767 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5767>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed inference of \fBEnums\fP when they are imported under an alias.
.sp
Closes #5776 (#5776 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5776>)
.IP \(bu 2
Prevent false positives when accessing \fBPurePath.parents\fP by index (not slice) on Python 3.10+.
.sp
Closes #5832 (#5832 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5832>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBunnecessary\-list\-index\-lookup\fP is now more conservative to avoid potential false positives.
.sp
Closes #6896 (#6896 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6896>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix double emitting \fBtrailing\-whitespace\fP for multi\-line docstrings.
.sp
Closes #6936 (#6936 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6936>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBimport\-error\fP now correctly checks for \fBcontextlib.suppress\fP guards on import statements.
.sp
Closes #7270 (#7270 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7270>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive for \fIno\-self\-argument\fP/\fIno\-method\-argument\fP when a staticmethod is applied to a function but uses a different name.
.sp
Closes #7300 (#7300 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7300>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fIundefined\-loop\-variable\fP with \fIbreak\fP and \fIcontinue\fP statements in \fIelse\fP blocks.
.sp
Refs #7311 (#7311 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7311>)
.IP \(bu 2
Improve default TypeVar name regex. Disallow names prefixed with \fBT\fP\&.
E.g. use \fBAnyStrT\fP instead of \fBTAnyStr\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #7322 (\fI#7322 <https://github.com/pylint\-dev/pylint/issues/7322>\(ga_\fP)
.UNINDENT
.SS False Negatives Fixed
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when relying on a name that is reimported later in a function.
.sp
Closes #4624 (#4624 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:4624>)
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP for self\-referencing named expressions (\fB:=\fP) lacking
prior assignments.
.sp
Closes #5653 (#5653 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5653>)
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP for self\-referencing assignments under if conditions.
.sp
Closes #6643 (#6643 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6643>)
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBmodified\-iterating\-list\fP and analogous messages for dicts and sets when iterating
literals, or when using the \fBdel\fP keyword.
.sp
Closes #6648 (#6648 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6648>)
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when calling nested functions before assignment.
.sp
Closes #6812 (#6812 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6812>)
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBnonlocal\-without\-binding\fP when a nonlocal name has been assigned at a later point in the same scope.
.sp
Closes #6883 (#6883 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6883>)
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBusing\-constant\-test\fP when testing the truth value of a variable or call result
holding a generator.
.sp
Closes #6909 (#6909 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6909>)
.IP \(bu 2
Rename \fBunhashable\-dict\-key\fP to \fBunhashable\-member\fP and emit when creating sets and dicts,
not just when accessing dicts.
.sp
Closes #7034, Closes #7055 (#7034 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7034>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Bug Fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a failure to lint packages with \fB__init__.py\fP contained in directories lacking \fB__init__.py\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #1667 (#1667 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:1667>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a syntax\-error / E0001 \%<#\:syntax-error> crash that was not handled properly when the declared encoding of a file
was \fButf\-9\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #3860 (#3860 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3860>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the \fBnot\-callable\fP check when there is ambiguity whether an instance is being incorrectly provided to \fB__new__()\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7109 (#7109 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7109>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash when regex option raises a \fIre.error\fP exception.
.sp
Closes #7202 (#7202 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7202>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fIundefined\-loop\-variable\fP from walrus in comprehension test.
.sp
Closes #7222 (#7222 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7222>)
.IP \(bu 2
Check for \fI<cwd>\fP before removing first item from \fIsys.path\fP in \fImodify_sys_path\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #7231 (#7231 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7231>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix sys.path pollution in parallel mode.
.sp
Closes #7246 (#7246 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7246>)
.IP \(bu 2
Prevent \fIuseless\-parent\-delegation\fP for delegating to a builtin
written in C (e.g. \fIException.__init__\fP) with non\-self arguments.
.sp
Closes #7319 (#7319 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7319>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbad\-exception\-context\fP has been renamed to \fBbad\-exception\-cause\fP as it is about the cause and not the context.
.sp
Closes #3694 (#3694 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:3694>)
.IP \(bu 2
The message for \fBliteral\-comparison\fP is now more explicit about the problem and the
solution.
.sp
Closes #5237 (#5237 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5237>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBuseless\-super\-delegation\fP has been renamed to \fBuseless\-parent\-delegation\fP in order to be more generic.
.sp
Closes #6953 (#6953 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6953>)
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint now uses \fBtowncrier\fP for changelog generation.
.sp
Refs #6974 (#6974 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6974>)
.IP \(bu 2
Update \fBastroid\fP to 2.12.
.sp
Refs #7153 (#7153 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7153>)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash when a type\-annotated \fI__slots__\fP with no value is declared.
.sp
Closes #7280 (#7280 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7280>)
.UNINDENT
.SS Internal Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed an issue where it was impossible to update functional tests output when the existing
output was impossible to parse. Instead of raising an error we raise a warning message and
let the functional test fail with a default value.
.sp
Refs #6891 (#6891 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6891>)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint.testutils.primer\fP is now a private API.
.sp
Refs #6905 (#6905 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6905>)
.IP \(bu 2
We changed the way we handle the changelog internally by using towncrier.
If you\(aqre a contributor you won\(aqt have to fix merge conflicts in the
changelog anymore.
.sp
Closes #6974 (#6974 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:6974>)
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint is now using Scorecards to implement security recommendations from the
OpenSSF \%<https://\:openssf\:.org>\&. This is done in order to secure our supply chains using a combination
of automated tooling and best practices, most of which were already implemented before.
.sp
Refs #7267 (#7267 \%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:7267>)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.14
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.sp
With 2.14 \fBpylint\fP only supports Python version 3.7.2 and above.
.sp
We introduced several new checks among which \fBduplicate\-value\fP for sets,
\fBcomparison\-of\-constants\fP, and checks related to lambdas. We removed \fBno\-init\fP and
made \fBno\-self\-use\fP optional as they were too opinionated. We also added an option
to generate a toml configuration: \fB\-\-generate\-toml\-config\fP\&.
.sp
We migrated to \fBargparse\fP from \fBoptparse\fP and refactored the configuration handling
thanks to Daniël van Noord. On the user side it should change the output of the
\fB\-\-help\fP command, and some inconsistencies and bugs should disappear. The behavior
between options set in a config file versus on the command line will be more consistent. For us,
it will permit to maintain this part of the code easily in the future.
.sp
As a result of the refactor there are a lot of internal deprecations. If you\(aqre a library
maintainer that depends on pylint, please verify that you\(aqre ready for pylint 3.0
by activating deprecation warnings.
.sp
We continued the integration of \fBpylint\-error\fP and are now at 33%!. We still welcome any community effort
to help review, integrate, and add good/bad examples <\%<https://\:github\:.com/\:pylint-dev/\:pylint/\:issues/\:5953>>\(ga_. This should be doable
without any \fBpylint\fP or \fBastroid\fP knowledge, so this is the perfect entrypoint if you want
to contribute to \fBpylint\fP or open source without any experience with our code!
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Added new checker \fBcomparison\-of\-constants\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #6076
.IP \(bu 2
Added new checker \fBtypevar\-name\-mismatch\fP: TypeVar must be assigned to a variable with the same name as its name argument.
.sp
Closes #5224
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-enum\-extension\fP: Used when a class tries to extend an inherited Enum class.
.sp
Closes #5501
.IP \(bu 2
Added new checker \fBtypevar\-double\-variance\fP: The \(dqcovariant\(dq and \(dqcontravariant\(dq keyword arguments
cannot both be set to \(dqTrue\(dq in a TypeVar.
.sp
Closes #5895
.IP \(bu 2
Add new check \fBunnecessary\-dunder\-call\fP for unnecessary dunder method calls.
.sp
Closes #5936
.IP \(bu 2
\fBunnecessary\-lambda\-assignment\fP: Lambda expression assigned to a variable.
Define a function using the \(dqdef\(dq keyword instead.
\fBunnecessary\-direct\-lambda\-call\fP: Lambda expression called directly.
Execute the expression inline instead.
.sp
Closes #5976
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpotential\-index\-error\fP: Emitted when the index of a list or tuple exceeds its length.
This checker is currently quite conservative to avoid false positives. We welcome
suggestions for improvements.
.sp
Closes #578
.IP \(bu 2
Added new checker \fBunnecessary\-list\-index\-lookup\fP for indexing into a list while
iterating over \fBenumerate()\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #4525
.IP \(bu 2
Added new message called \fBduplicate\-value\fP which identifies duplicate values inside sets.
.sp
Closes #5880
.IP \(bu 2
Added the \fBsuper\-without\-brackets\fP checker, raised when a super call is missing its brackets.
.sp
Closes #4008
.UNINDENT
.SS Removed checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBno\-init\fP (W0232) warning has been removed. It\(aqs ok to not have an \fB__init__\fP in a class.
.sp
Closes #2409
.IP \(bu 2
Removed the \fBassign\-to\-new\-keyword\fP message as there are no new keywords in the supported Python
versions any longer.
.sp
Closes #4683
.IP \(bu 2
Moved \fBno\-self\-use\fP check to optional extension.
You now need to explicitly enable this check using
\fBload\-plugins=pylint.extensions.no_self_use\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #5502
.UNINDENT
.SS Extensions
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBRedefinedLoopNameChecker\fP
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Added optional extension \fBredefined\-loop\-name\fP to emit messages when a loop variable
is redefined in the loop body.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Closes #5072
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
\fBDocStringStyleChecker\fP
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Re\-enable checker \fBbad\-docstring\-quotes\fP for Python <= 3.7.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Closes #6087
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
\fBNoSelfUseChecker\fP
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBno\-self\-use\fP check, previously enabled by default.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Closes #5502
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Started ignoring underscore as a local variable for \fBtoo\-many\-locals\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #6488
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint can now be installed with an extra\-require called \fBspelling\fP (\fBpip install pylint[spelling]\fP).
This will add \fBpyenchant\fP to pylint\(aqs dependencies. You will still need to install the
requirements for \fBpyenchant\fP (the \fBenchant\fP library and any dictionaries) yourself. You will also
need to set the \fBspelling\-dict\fP option.
.sp
Refs #6462
.IP \(bu 2
Improved wording of the message of \fBdeprecated\-module\fP
.sp
Closes #6169
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPylint\fP now requires Python 3.7.2 or newer to run.
.sp
Closes #4301
.IP \(bu 2
We made a greater effort to reraise failures stemming from the \fBastroid\fP
library as \fBAstroidError\fP, with the effect that pylint emits \fBastroid\-error\fP
rather than merely \fBfatal\fP\&. Regardless, please report any such issues you encounter!
.IP \(bu 2
We have improved our recognition of inline disable and enable comments. It is
now possible to disable \fBbad\-option\-value\fP inline (as long as you disable it before
the bad option value is raised, i.e. \fBdisable=bad\-option\-value,bad\-message\fP not \fBdisable=bad\-message,bad\-option\-value\fP ) as well as certain other
previously unsupported messages.
.sp
Closes #3312
.IP \(bu 2
The main checker name is now \fBmain\fP instead of \fBmaster\fP\&. The configuration does not need to be updated as sections\(aq name are optional.
.sp
Closes #5467
.IP \(bu 2
Update \fBinvalid\-slots\-object\fP message to show bad object rather than its inferred value.
.sp
Closes #6101
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash in the \fBnot\-an\-iterable\fP checker involving multiple starred expressions
inside a call.
.sp
Closes #6372
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash in the \fBunused\-private\-member\fP checker involving chained private attributes.
.sp
Closes #6709
.IP \(bu 2
Disable spellchecking of mypy rule names in ignore directives.
.sp
Closes #5929
.IP \(bu 2
\fBimplicit\-str\-concat\fP will now be raised on calls like \fBopen(\(dqmyfile.txt\(dq \(dqa+b\(dq)\fP too.
.sp
Closes #6441
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a failure to respect inline disables for \fBfixme\fP occurring on the last line
of a module when pylint is launched with \fB\-\-enable=fixme\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Removed the broken \fBgenerate\-man\fP option.
.sp
Closes #5283
Closes #1887
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed failure to enable \fBdeprecated\-module\fP after a \fBdisable=all\fP
by making \fBImportsChecker\fP solely responsible for emitting \fBdeprecated\-module\fP instead
of sharing responsibility with \fBStdlibChecker\fP\&. (This could have led to double messages.)
.IP \(bu 2
Added the \fBgenerate\-toml\-config\fP option.
.sp
Refs #5462
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbad\-option\-value\fP will be emitted whenever a configuration value or command line invocation
includes an unknown message.
.sp
Closes #4324
.IP \(bu 2
Added the \fBunrecognized\-option\fP message. Raised if we encounter any unrecognized options.
.sp
Closes #5259
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negative for \fBbad\-string\-format\-type\fP if the value to be formatted is passed in
as a variable holding a constant.
.IP \(bu 2
The concept of checker priority has been removed.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBcache\-max\-size\-none\fP checker has been renamed to \fBmethod\-cache\-max\-size\-none\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #5670
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBmethod\-cache\-max\-size\-none\fP checker will now also check \fBfunctools.cache\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #5670
.IP \(bu 2
\fBBaseChecker\fP classes now require the \fBlinter\fP argument to be passed.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBset_config_directly\fP decorator has been removed.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt report \fBuseless\-super\-delegation\fP for the \fB__hash__\fP method in classes that also override the \fB__eq__\fP method.
.sp
Closes #3934
.IP \(bu 2
Fix falsely issuing \fBuseless\-suppression\fP on the \fBwrong\-import\-position\fP checker.
.sp
Closes #5219
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positive \fBno\-member\fP for Enums with self\-defined members.
.sp
Closes #5138
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false negative for \fBno\-member\fP when attempting to assign an instance
attribute to itself without any prior assignment.
.sp
Closes #1555
.IP \(bu 2
Changed message type from \fBredefined\-outer\-name\fP to \fBredefined\-loop\-name\fP
(optional extension) for redefinitions of outer loop variables by inner loops.
.sp
Closes #5608
.IP \(bu 2
By default the similarity checker will now ignore imports and ignore function signatures when computing
duplication. If you want to keep the previous behaviour set \fBignore\-imports\fP and \fBignore\-signatures\fP to \fBFalse\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint now expands the user path (i.e. \fB~\fP to \fBhome/yusef/\fP) and expands environment variables (i.e. \fBhome/$USER/$project\fP
to \fBhome/yusef/pylint\fP for \fBUSER=yusef\fP and \fBproject=pylint\fP) for pyreverse\(aqs \fBoutput\-directory\fP,
\fBimport\-graph\fP, \fBext\-import\-graph\fP,  \fBint\-import\-graph\fP options, and the spell checker\(aqs \fBspelling\-private\-dict\-file\fP
option.
.sp
Refs #6493
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit \fBunsubscriptable\-object\fP for string annotations.
Pylint doesn\(aqt check if class is only generic in type stubs only.
.sp
Closes #4369 and #6523
.IP \(bu 2
Fix pyreverse crash \fBRuntimeError: dictionary changed size during iteration\fP
.sp
Refs #6612
.IP \(bu 2
Fix syntax for return type annotations in MermaidJS diagrams produced with \fBpyreverse\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #6467
.IP \(bu 2
Fix type annotations of class and instance attributes using the alternative union syntax in \fBpyreverse\fP diagrams.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix bug where it writes a plain text error message to stdout, invalidating output formats.
.sp
Closes #6597
.IP \(bu 2
The refactoring checker now also raises \(aqconsider\-using\-a\-generator\(aq messages for
\fBmax()\fP, \fBmin()\fP and \fBsum()\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #6595
.IP \(bu 2
Update ranges for \fBusing\-constant\-test\fP and \fBmissing\-parentheses\-for\-call\-in\-test\fP
error messages.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit \fBno\-member\fP inside type annotations with
\fBfrom __future__ import annotations\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #6594
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBunexpected\-special\-method\-signature\fP false positive for \fB__init_subclass__\fP methods with one or more arguments.
.sp
Closes #6644
.UNINDENT
.SS Deprecations
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBignore\-mixin\-members\fP option has been deprecated. You should now use the new
\fBignored\-checks\-for\-mixins\fP option.
.sp
Closes #5205
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinterfaces.implements\fP has been deprecated and will be removed in 3.0. Please use standard inheritance
patterns instead of \fB__implements__\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #2287
.IP \(bu 2
All \fBInterface\fP classes in \fBpylint.interfaces\fP have been deprecated. You can subclass
the respective normal classes to get the same behaviour. The \fB__implements__\fP functionality
was based on a rejected PEP from 2001:
\%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0245>
.sp
Closes #2287
.IP \(bu 2
\fBMapReduceMixin\fP has been deprecated. \fBBaseChecker\fP now implements \fBget_map_data\fP and
\fBreduce_map_data\fP\&. If a checker actually needs to reduce data it should define \fBget_map_data\fP
as returning something different than \fBNone\fP and let its \fBreduce_map_data\fP handle a list
of the types returned by \fBget_map_data\fP\&.
An example can be seen by looking at \fBpylint/checkers/similar.py\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBconfig\fP attribute of \fBBaseChecker\fP has been deprecated. You can use \fBchecker.linter.config\fP
to access the global configuration object instead of a checker\-specific object.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBlevel\fP attribute of \fBBaseChecker\fP has been deprecated: everything is now
displayed in \fB\-\-help\fP, all the time.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBset_option\fP method of \fBBaseChecker\fP has been deprecated. You can use \fBchecker.linter.set_option\fP
to set an option on the global configuration object instead of a checker\-specific object.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBoptions_providers\fP attribute of \fBArgumentsManager\fP has been deprecated.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
Fix saving of persistent data files in environments where the user\(aqs cache
directory and the linted file are on a different drive.
.sp
Closes #6394
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBmethod\-cache\-max\-size\-none\fP checker will now also check \fBfunctools.cache\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBconfig\fP attribute of \fBPyLinter\fP is now of the \fBargparse.Namespace\fP type instead of
\fBoptparse.Values\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUnsupportedAction\fP has been deprecated.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOptionsManagerMixIn\fP has been deprecated.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOptionParser\fP has been deprecated.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOption\fP has been deprecated.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOptionsProviderMixIn\fP has been deprecated.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
\fBConfigurationMixIn\fP has been deprecated.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBoption_groups\fP attribute of \fBPyLinter\fP has been deprecated.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
\fBget_global_config\fP has been deprecated. You can now access all global options from
\fBchecker.linter.config\fP\&.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOptionsManagerMixIn\fP has been replaced with \fBArgumentsManager\fP\&. \fBArgumentsManager\fP is considered
private API and most methods that were public on \fBOptionsManagerMixIn\fP have now been deprecated and will
be removed in a future release.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
\fBOptionsProviderMixIn\fP has been replaced with \fBArgumentsProvider\fP\&. \fBArgumentsProvider\fP is considered
private API and most methods that were public on \fBOptionsProviderMixIn\fP have now been deprecated and will
be removed in a future release.
.sp
Refs #5392
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint.pyreverse.ASTWalker\fP has been removed, as it was only used internally by a single child class.
.sp
Refs #6712
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpyreverse\fP: Resolving and displaying implemented interfaces that are defined by the \fB__implements__\fP
attribute has been deprecated and will be removed in 3.0.
.sp
Refs #6713
.IP \(bu 2
\fBis_class_subscriptable_pep585_with_postponed_evaluation_enabled\fP has been deprecated.
Use \fBis_postponed_evaluation_enabled(node) and is_node_in_type_annotation_context(node)\fP
instead.
.sp
Refs #6536
.UNINDENT
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.14.5?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-07\-17
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash in the \fBundefined\-loop\-variable\fP check when \fBenumerate()\fP is used
in a ternary expression.
.sp
Closes #7131
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed handling of \fB\-\-\fP as separator between positional arguments and flags.
.sp
Closes #7003
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed the disabling of \fBfixme\fP and its interaction with \fBuseless\-suppression\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Allow lists of default values in parameter documentation for \fBNumpy\fP style.
.sp
Closes #4035
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.14.4?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-06\-29
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBdiffering\-param\-doc\fP check was triggered by positional only arguments.
.sp
Closes #6950
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed an issue where scanning \fI\&.\fP directory recursively with \fB\-\-ignore\-path=^path/to/dir\fP is not
ignoring the \fIpath/to/dir\fP directory.
.sp
Closes #6964
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed regression that didn\(aqt allow quoted \fBinit\-hooks\fP in option files.
.sp
Closes #7006
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a false positive for \fBmodified\-iterating\-dict\fP when updating an existing key.
.sp
Closes #6179
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed an issue where many\-core Windows machines (>~60 logical processors) would hang when
using the default jobs count.
.sp
Closes #6965
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed an issue with the recognition of \fBsetup.cfg\fP files.
Only \fB\&.cfg\fP files that are exactly named \fBsetup.cfg\fP require section names that
start with \fBpylint.\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #3630
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt report \fBimport\-private\-name\fP for relative imports.
.sp
Closes #7078
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.14.3?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-06\-18
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed two false positives for \fBbad\-super\-call\fP for calls that refer to a non\-direct parent.
.sp
Closes #4922, Closes #2903
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a false positive for \fBuseless\-super\-delegation\fP for subclasses that specify the number of
of parameters against a parent that uses a variadic argument.
.sp
Closes #2270
.IP \(bu 2
Allow suppressing \fBundefined\-loop\-variable\fP and \fBundefined\-variable\fP without raising \fBuseless\-suppression\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positive for \fBundefined\-variable\fP for \fB__class__\fP in inner methods.
.sp
Closes #4032
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.14.2?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-06\-15
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a false positive for \fBunused\-variable\fP when a function returns an
\fBargparse.Namespace\fP object.
.sp
Closes #6895
.IP \(bu 2
Avoided raising an identical \fBundefined\-loop\-variable\fP message twice on the same line.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt crash if \fBlint.run._query_cpu()\fP is run within a Kubernetes Pod, that has only
a fraction of a cpu core assigned. Just go with one process then.
.sp
Closes #6902
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a false positive in \fBconsider\-using\-f\-string\fP if the left side of a \fB%\fP is not a string.
.sp
Closes #6689
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a false positive in \fBunnecessary\-list\-index\-lookup\fP and \fBunnecessary\-dict\-index\-lookup\fP
when the subscript is updated in the body of a nested loop.
.sp
Closes #6818
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed an issue with multi\-line \fBinit\-hook\fP options which did not record the line endings.
.sp
Closes #6888
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a false positive for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP when a try block returns
but an except handler defines a name via type annotation.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-errors\-only\fP no longer enables previously disabled messages. It was acting as
\(dqemit \fIall\fP and only error messages\(dq without being clearly documented that way.
.sp
Closes #6811
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.14.1?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-06\-06
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Avoid reporting \fBunnecessary\-dict\-index\-lookup\fP or \fBunnecessary\-list\-index\-lookup\fP
when the index lookup is part of a destructuring assignment.
.sp
Closes #6788
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed parsing of unrelated options in \fBtox.ini\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #6800
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash when linting \fB__new__()\fP methods that return a call expression.
.sp
Closes #6805
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt crash if we can\(aqt find the user\(aqs home directory.
.sp
Closes #6802
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positives for \fBunused\-import\fP when aliasing \fBtyping\fP e.g. as \fBt\fP
and guarding imports under \fBt.TYPE_CHECKING\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #3846
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a false positive regression in 2.13 for \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP where it is safe to rely
on a name defined only in an \fBexcept\fP block because the \fBelse\fP block returned.
.sp
Closes #6790
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed the use of abbreviations for some special options on the command line.
.sp
Closes #6810
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in the optional \fBpylint.extensions.private_import\fP extension.
.sp
Closes #6624
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbad\-option\-value\fP (E0012) is now a warning \fBunknown\-option\-value\fP (W0012). Deleted messages that do not exist
anymore in pylint now raise \fBuseless\-option\-value\fP (R0022) instead of \fBbad\-option\-value\fP\&. This allows to
distinguish between genuine typos and configuration that could be cleaned up.  Existing message disables for
\fBbad\-option\-value\fP will still work on both new messages.
.sp
Refs #6794
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.14.0?
.sp
Release date: 2022\-06\-01
