.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 2.9
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.sp
Pylint is now compatible with python 3.10.
.sp
A lot of new checks have been added, some non\-opinionated performance warnings
like \fBuse\-maxsplit\-arg\fP, some consensual style warnings like
\fBunnecessary\-dict\-index\-lookup\fP or new deprecation checks.
.sp
We\(aqre aiming to reduce pylint noise for first time users and making some
new checks optional is a step in that direction. In order to do that we
created an optional code style checker that can be loaded using
\fBpylint.extensions.code_style\fP with the \fBload\-plugins\fP options.
More than ever, if as a veteran you want the most checks you can possibly get,
you should check the list of pylint extensions. \%<https://\:pylint\:.readthedocs\:.io/\:en/\:latest/\:user_guide/\:checkers/\:extensions\:.html#\:optional-checkers>\&.
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdeprecated\-decorator\fP: Emitted when deprecated decorator is used.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-using\-dict\-items\fP: Emitted when iterating over dictionary keys and then
indexing the same dictionary with the key within loop body.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBuse\-maxsplit\-arg\fP: Emitted either when accessing only the first or last
element of \fBstr.split()\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
An \fBignore_signatures\fP option has been added to the similarity checker. It will permits  to reduce false positives when multiple functions have the same parameters.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBunnecessary\-dict\-index\-lookup\fP: Emitted when iterating over dictionary items
(key\-value pairs) and accessing the value by index lookup.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-using\-from\-import\fP: Emitted when a submodule/member of a package is imported and aliased with the same name.
.IP \(bu 2
New checker \fBunused\-private\-member\fP: Emitted when a private member (i.e., starts with \fB__\fP) of a class is defined but not used.
.IP \(bu 2
New checker \fBinvalid\-class\-object\fP: Emitted when a non\-class is assigned to a \fB__class__\fP attribute.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-all\-format\fP: Emitted when \fB__all__\fP has an invalid format,
i.e. isn\(aqt a \fBtuple\fP or \fBlist\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
New checker \fBawait\-outside\-async\fP: Emitted when await is used outside an async function.
.IP \(bu 2
Add new extension \fBCodeStyleChecker\fP\&. It includes checkers that can improve code
consistency. As such they don\(aqt necessarily provide a performance benefit
and are often times opinionated.
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-using\-tuple\fP: Emitted when an in\-place defined list or set can be replaced by a tuple.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-using\-namedtuple\-or\-dataclass\fP: Emitted when dictionary values
can be replaced by namedtuples or dataclass instances.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive \fBconsider\-using\-with\fP (R1732) if a ternary conditional is used together with \fBwith\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive \fBconsider\-using\-with\fP (R1732) if \fBcontextlib.ExitStack\fP takes care of calling the \fB__exit__\fP method
.IP \(bu 2
Add type annotations to pyreverse dot files
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint\(aqs tags are now the standard form \fBvX.Y.Z\fP and not \fBpylint\-X.Y.Z\fP anymore.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive \fBtoo\-many\-ancestors\fP when inheriting from builtin classes,
especially from the \fBcollections.abc\fP module
.IP \(bu 2
The output messages for \fBarguments\-differ\fP error message have been customized based on the different error cases.
.IP \(bu 2
New option \fB\-\-fail\-on=<msg ids>\fP to return non\-zero exit codes regardless of \fBfail\-under\fP value.
.IP \(bu 2
A new error called \fBarguments\-renamed\fP has been created, which identifies any changes at the parameter names
of overridden functions. It aims to separate the functionality of \fBarguments\-differ\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix incompatibility with Python 3.6.0 caused by \fBtyping.Counter\fP and \fBtyping.NoReturn\fP usage
.IP \(bu 2
Allow comma\-separated list in \fBoutput\-format\fP and separate output files for
each specified format.  Each output file can be defined after a semicolon for example : \fB\-\-output\-format=json:myfile.json,colorized\fP
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBusing\-constant\-test\fP checker now detects constant tests consisting of list literals
like \fB[]\fP and \fB[1, 2, 3]\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBignore\-paths\fP configuration directive has been added. Defined regex patterns are matched against file path.
.IP \(bu 2
Added handling of floating point values when parsing configuration from pyproject.toml
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBuseless\-type\-doc\fP on ignored argument using \fBpylint.extensions.docparams\fP when a function
was typed using pep484 but not inside the docstring.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix missing support for detecting deprecated aliases to existing functions/methods.
functions/methods.
.IP \(bu 2
Added various deprecated functions/methods for python 3.10, 3.7, 3.6 and 3.3
.IP \(bu 2
No longer emit \fBconsider\-using\-with\fP for \fBThreadPoolExecutor\fP and \fBProcessPoolExecutor\fP
as they have legitimate use cases without a \fBwith\fP block.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash if a callable returning a context manager was assigned to a list or dict item
.UNINDENT
