.IP \(bu 2
New check: \fBconsider\-using\-generator\fP
.sp
This check warns when a comprehension is used inside an \fBany\fP or \fBall\fP function,
since it is unnecessary and should be replaced by a generator instead.
Using a generator would be less code and way faster.
.sp
Closes #3165
.IP \(bu 2
Add Github Actions to replace Travis and AppVeyor in the future
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 2.6
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbad\-continuation\fP and \fBbad\-whitespace\fP have been removed. \fBblack\fP or another formatter can help you with this better than Pylint
.IP \(bu 2
Added support for isort 5
.UNINDENT
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBsuper\-with\-arguments\fP check for flagging instances of Python 2 style super calls.
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBraise\-missing\-from\fP check for exceptions that should have a cause.
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbad\-continuation\fP and \fBbad\-whitespace\fP have been removed. \fBblack\fP or another formatter can help you with this better than Pylint
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBno\-space\-check\fP option has been removed, it\(aqs no longer possible to consider empty line like a \fBtrailing\-whitespace\fP by using clever options.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmixed\-indentation\fP has been removed, it is no longer useful since TabError is included directly in python3
.IP \(bu 2
Fix superfluous\-parens / C0325 \%<#\:superfluous-parens> false\-positive for the walrus operator
.IP \(bu 2
Add support for both isort 4 and isort 5. If you have pinned isort 4 in your project requirements, nothing changes. If you use isort 5, though, note that the \fBknown\-standard\-library\fP option is not interpreted the same in isort 4 and isort 5 (see \fIthe migration guide in isort documentation\fP (no longer available) for further details). For compatibility\(aqs sake for most pylint users, the \fBknown\-standard\-library\fP option in pylint now maps to \fBextra\-standard\-library\fP in isort 5. If you really want what \fBknown\-standard\-library\fP now means in isort 5, you must disable the \fBwrong\-import\-order\fP check in pylint and run isort manually with a proper isort configuration file.
.UNINDENT
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.6.1?
.sp
Release date: 2021\-02\-16
