Closes #3383
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBfail\-under\fP not accepting floats
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a bug with \fBignore\-docstrings\fP ignoring all lines in a module
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBpre\-commit\fP config that could lead to undetected duplicate lines of code
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in parallel mode when the module\(aqs filepath is not set
.sp
Closes #3564
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBraise\-missing\-from\fP check for exceptions that should have a cause.
.IP \(bu 2
Support both isort 4 and isort 5. If you have pinned isort 4 in your project requirements, nothing changes. If you use isort 5, though, note that the \fBknown\-standard\-library\fP option is not interpreted the same in isort 4 and isort 5 (see the migration guide in isort documentation for further details). For compatibility\(aqs sake for most pylint users, the \fBknown\-standard\-library\fP option in pylint now maps to \fBextra\-standard\-library\fP in isort 5. If you really want what \fBknown\-standard\-library\fP now means in isort 5, you must disable the \fBwrong\-import\-order\fP check in pylint and run isort manually with a proper isort configuration file.
.sp
Closes #3722
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash caused by not guarding against \fBInferenceError\fP when calling \fBinfer_call_result\fP
.sp
Closes #3690
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash in parallel mode when the module\(aqs filepath is not set
.sp
Closes #3564
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 2.5
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A new check \fBisinstance\-second\-argument\-not\-valid\-type\fP was added.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
This check is emitted whenever \fBpylint\fP finds a call to the \fBisinstance\fP
function with a second argument that is not a type. Such code is likely
unintended as it will cause a TypeError to be thrown at runtime error.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check \fBassert\-on\-string\-literal\fP was added.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
This check is emitted whenever \fBpylint\fP finds an assert statement
with a string literal as its first argument. Such assert statements
are probably unintended as they will always pass.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check \fBf\-string\-without\-interpolation\fP was added.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
This check is emitted whenever \fBpylint\fP detects the use of an
f\-string without having any interpolated values in it, which means
that the f\-string can be a normal string.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Multiple checks for invalid return types of protocol functions were added:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-bool\-returned\fP: \fB__bool__\fP did not return a bool
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-index\-returned\fP: \fB__index__\fP did not return an integer
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-repr\-returned)\fP: \fB__repr__\fP did not return a string
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-str\-returned)\fP: \fB__str__\fP did not return a string
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-bytes\-returned)\fP: \fB__bytes__\fP did not return a string
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-hash\-returned)\fP: \fB__hash__\fP did not return an integer
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-length\-hint\-returned)\fP: \fB__length_hint__\fP did not return a non\-negative integer
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-format\-returned)\fP: \fB__format__\fP did not return a string
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-getnewargs\-returned)\fP: \fB__getnewargs__\fP did not return a tuple
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-getnewargs\-ex\-returned)\fP: \fB__getnewargs_ex__\fP did not return a tuple of the form (tuple, dict)
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check \fBinconsistent\-quotes\fP was added.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
This check is emitted when quotes delimiters (\fB\(dq\fP and \fB\(aq\fP) are not used
consistently throughout a module.  It allows avoiding unnecessary escaping,
allowing, for example, \fB\(dqDon\(aqt error\(dq\fP in a module in which single\-quotes
otherwise delimit strings so that the single quote in \fBDon\(aqt\fP doesn\(aqt need to be escaped.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check \fBnon\-str\-assignment\-to\-dunder\-name\fP was added to ensure that only strings are assigned to \fB__name__\fP attributes.
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Configuration can be read from a setup.cfg or pyproject.toml file in the current directory.
A setup.cfg must prepend pylintrc section names with \fBpylint.\fP, for example \fB[pylint.MESSAGES CONTROL]\fP\&.
A pyproject.toml file must prepend section names with \fBtool.pylint.\fP, for example \fB[tool.pylint.\(aqMESSAGES CONTROL\(aq]\fP\&.
These files can also be passed in on the command line.
.IP \(bu 2
Add new \fBgood\-names\-rgx\fP and \fBbad\-names\-rgx\fP to enable permitting or disallowing of names via regular expressions
.sp
To enable better handling of permitted/disallowed names, we added two new config options: good\-names\-rgxs: a comma\-
separated list of regexes, that if a name matches will be exempt from naming\-checking. bad\-names\-rgxs: a comma\-
separated list of regexes, that if a name matches will be always marked as a disallowed name.
.IP \(bu 2
Mutable \fBcollections.*\fP are now flagged as dangerous defaults.
.IP \(bu 2
Add new \fB\-\-fail\-under\fP flag for setting the threshold for the score to fail overall tests. If the score is over the fail\-under threshold, pylint will complete SystemExit with value 0 to indicate no errors.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new option \fBnotes\-rgx\fP to make fixme warnings more flexible. Now either \fBnotes\fP or \fBnotes\-rgx\fP option can be used to detect fixme warnings.
.IP \(bu 2
Non\-ASCII characters are now allowed by \fBinvalid\-name\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP no longer emits \fBinvalid\-name\fP for non\-constants found at module level.
.sp
Pylint was considering all module level variables as constants, which is not what PEP 8 is actually mandating.
.IP \(bu 2
A new check \fBnon\-ascii\-name\fP was added to detect identifiers with non\-ASCII characters.
.IP \(bu 2
Overloaded typing functions no longer trigger \fBno\-self\-use\fP, \fBunused\-argument\fP, \fBmissing\-docstring\fP and similar checks
that assumed that overloaded functions are normal functions.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpython \-m pylint\fP can no longer be made to import files from the local directory.
.IP \(bu 2
A new command \fB\-\-list\-extensions\fP was added.
.sp
This command lists all extensions present in \fBpylint.extensions\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Various false positives have been fixed which you can read more about in the Changelog files.
.IP \(bu 2
Multiple types of string formatting are allowed in logging functions.
.UNINDENT
.sp
The \fBlogging\-fstring\-interpolation\fP message has been brought back to allow
multiple types of string formatting to be used.
The type of formatting to use is chosen through enabling and disabling messages
rather than through the logging\-format\-style option.
The fstr value of the logging\-format\-style option is not valid.
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.5.3?
.sp
Release date: 2020\-06\-8
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a regression where disable comments that have checker names with numbers in them are not parsed correctly
.sp
