.sp
Closes #3373
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive of \fBself\-assigning\-variable\fP on tuple unpacking.
.sp
Closes #3433
.IP \(bu 2
\fBno\-self\-use\fP is no longer emitted for typing stubs.
.sp
Closes #3439
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for \fBundefined\-variable\fP when \fB__class__\fP is used
.sp
Closes #3090
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBinvalid\-name\fP for variables defined in loops at module level.
.sp
Closes #2695
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check for cases where the second argument to \fBisinstance\fP is not a type.
.sp
Closes #3308
.IP \(bu 2
Add \(aqnotes\-rgx\(aq option, to be used for fixme check.
.sp
Closes #2874
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfunction\-redefined\fP exempts function redefined on a condition.
.sp
Closes #2410
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtyping.overload\fP functions are exempted from docstring checks
.sp
Closes #3350
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBinvalid\-overridden\-method\fP for improper async def overrides.
.sp
Closes #3355
.IP \(bu 2
Do not allow \fBpython \-m pylint ...\fP to import user code
.sp
\fBpython \-m pylint ...\fP adds the current working directory as the first element
of \fBsys.path\fP\&. This opens up a potential security hole where \fBpylint\fP will import
user level code as long as that code resides in modules having the same name as stdlib
or pylint\(aqs own modules.
.sp
Closes #3386
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBdummy\-variables\-rgx\fP option for \fB_redeclared\-assigned\-name\fP check.
.sp
Closes #3341
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed graph creation for relative paths
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check for asserts on string literals.
.sp
Closes #3284
.IP \(bu 2
\fBnot in\fP is considered iterating context for some of the Python 3 porting checkers.
.IP \(bu 2
A new check \fBinconsistent\-quotes\fP was added.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check for non string assignment to __name__ attribute.
.sp
Closes #583
.IP \(bu 2
\fB__pow__\fP, \fB__imatmul__\fP, \fB__trunc__\fP, \fB__floor__\fP, and \fB__ceil__\fP are recognized as special method names.
.sp
Closes #3281
.IP \(bu 2
Added errors for protocol functions when invalid return types are detected.
E0304 (invalid\-bool\-returned / E0304 \%<#\:invalid-bool-returned>): __bool__ did not return a bool
E0305 (invalid\-index\-returned / E0305 \%<#\:invalid-index-returned>): __index__ did not return an integer
E0306 (invalid\-repr\-returned / E0306 \%<#\:invalid-repr-returned>): __repr__ did not return a string
E0307 (invalid\-str\-returned / E0307 \%<#\:invalid-str-returned>): __str__ did not return a string
E0308 (invalid\-bytes\-returned / E0308 \%<#\:invalid-bytes-returned>): __bytes__ did not return a string
E0309 (invalid\-hash\-returned / E0309 \%<#\:invalid-hash-returned>): __hash__ did not return an integer
E0310 (invalid\-length\-hint\-returned / E0310 \%<#\:invalid-length-hint-returned>): __length_hint__ did not return a non\-negative integer
E0311 (invalid\-format\-returned / E0311 \%<#\:invalid-format-returned>): __format__ did not return a string
E0312 (invalid\-getnewargs\-returned / E0312 \%<#\:invalid-getnewargs-returned>): __getnewargs__ did not return a tuple
E0313 (invalid\-getnewargs\-ex\-returned / E0313 \%<#\:invalid-getnewargs-ex-returned>): __getnewargs_ex__ did not return a tuple of the form (tuple, dict)
.sp
Closes #560
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmissing\-*\-docstring\fP can look for \fB__doc__\fP assignments.
.sp
Closes #3301
.IP \(bu 2
\fBundefined\-variable\fP can now find undefined loop iterables
.sp
Closes #498
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsafe_infer\fP can infer a value as long as all the paths share the same type.
.sp
Closes #2503
.IP \(bu 2
Add a \-\-fail\-under <score> flag, also configurable in a .pylintrc file. If the final score is more than the specified score, it\(aqs considered a success and pylint exits with exitcode 0. Otherwise, it\(aqs considered a failure and pylint exits with its current exitcode based on the messages issued.
.sp
Closes #2242
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit \fBline\-too\-long\fP for multilines when \fBdisable=line\-too\-long\fP comment stands at their end
.sp
Closes #2957
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed an \fBAttributeError\fP caused by improper handling of \fBdataclasses\fP inference in \fBpyreverse\fP
.sp
Closes #3256
.IP \(bu 2
Do not exempt bare except from \fBundefined\-variable\fP and similar checks
.sp
If a node was wrapped in a \fBTryExcept\fP, \fBpylint\fP was taking a hint
from the except handler when deciding to emit or not a message.
We were treating bare except as a fully fledged ignore but only
the corresponding exceptions should be handled that way (e.g. \fBNameError\fP or \fBImportError\fP)
.sp
Closes #3235
.IP \(bu 2
No longer emit \fBassignment\-from\-no\-return\fP when a function only raises an exception
.sp
Closes #3218
.IP \(bu 2
Allow import aliases to exempt \fBimport\-error\fP when used in type annotations.
.sp
Closes #3178
.IP \(bu 2
\fBEllipsis\(ga is exempted from \(ga\(gamultiple\-statements\fP for function overloads.
.sp
Closes #3224
.IP \(bu 2
No longer emit \fBinvalid\-name\fP for non\-constants found at module level.
.sp
Pylint was taking the following statement from PEP\-8 too far, considering
all module level variables as constants, which is not what the statement is saying:
.sp
\fIConstants are usually defined on a module level and written in
all capital letters with underscores separating words.\fP
.sp
Closes #3111
Closes #3132
.IP \(bu 2
Allow \fBimplicit\-str\-concat\-in\-sequence\fP to be emitted for string juxtaposition
.sp
Closes #3030
.IP \(bu 2
\fBimplicit\-str\-concat\-in\-sequence\fP was renamed \fBimplicit\-str\-concat\fP
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBjson\fP reporter no longer bypasses \fBredirect_stdout\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #3227
.IP \(bu 2
Move \fBNoFileError\fP, \fBOutputLine\fP, \fBFunctionalTestReporter\fP,
\fBFunctionalTestFile\fP, \fBLintModuleTest\fP and related methods from
\fBtest_functional.py\fP to \fBpylint.testutils\fP to help testing for 3rd
party pylint plugins.
.IP \(bu 2
Can read config from a setup.cfg or pyproject.toml file.
.sp
Closes #617
.IP \(bu 2
Fix exception\-escape false positive with generators
.sp
Closes #3128
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinspect.getargvalues\fP is no longer marked as deprecated.
.IP \(bu 2
A new check \fBf\-string\-without\-interpolation\fP was added
.sp
Closes #3190
.IP \(bu 2
Flag mutable \fBcollections.*\fP utilities as dangerous defaults
.sp
Closes #3183
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdocparams\fP extension supports multiple types in raises sections.
.sp
Multiple types can also be separated by commas in all valid sections.
.sp
Closes #2729
.IP \(bu 2
Allow parallel linting when run under Prospector
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positives of \fBmethod\-hidden\fP when a subclass defines the method that is being hidden.
.sp
Closes #414
.IP \(bu 2
Python 3 porting mode is 30\-50% faster on most codebases
.IP \(bu 2
Python 3 porting mode no longer swallows syntax errors
.sp
Closes #2956
.IP \(bu 2
Pass the actual PyLinter object to sub processes to allow using custom
PyLinter classes.
.sp
PyLinter object (and all its members except reporter) needs to support
pickling so the PyLinter object can be passed to worker processes.
.IP \(bu 2
Clean up setup.py
.sp
Make pytest\-runner a requirement only if running tests, similar to McCabe.
.sp
Clean up the setup.py file, resolving a number of warnings around it.
.IP \(bu 2
Handle SyntaxError in files passed via \fB\-\-from\-stdin\fP option
.sp
Pylint no longer outputs a traceback, if a file, read from stdin,
contains a syntaxerror.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix uppercase style to disallow 3+ uppercase followed by lowercase.
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed \fBundefined\-variable\fP and \fBunused\-import\fP false positives
when using a metaclass via an attribute.
.sp
Closes #1603
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBunused\-argument\fP for functions that partially uses their argument list before raising an exception.
.sp
Closes #3246
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed \fBbroad_try_clause\fP extension to check try/finally statements and to
check for nested statements (e.g., inside of an \fBif\fP statement).
.IP \(bu 2
Recognize classes explicitly inheriting from \fBabc.ABC\fP or having an
\fBabc.ABCMeta\fP metaclass as abstract. This makes them not trigger W0223.
.sp
Closes #3098
.IP \(bu 2
Fix overzealous \fBarguments\-differ\fP when overridden function uses variadics
.sp
No message is emitted if the overriding function provides positional or
keyword variadics in its signature that can feasibly accept and pass on
all parameters given by the overridden function.
.sp
Closes #1482
Closes #1553
.IP \(bu 2
Multiple types of string formatting are allowed in logging functions.
.sp
The \fBlogging\-fstring\-interpolation\fP message has been brought back to allow
multiple types of string formatting to be used.
.sp
Closes #3361
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 2.4
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBimport\-outside\-toplevel\fP
.sp
This check warns when modules are imported from places other than a
module toplevel, e.g. inside a function or a class.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBconsider\-using\-sys\-exit\fP
.sp
This check is emitted when we detect that a quit() or exit() is invoked
instead of sys.exit(), which is the preferred way of exiting in program.
.sp
Closes #2925
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBarguments\-out\-of\-order\fP
.sp
This check warns if you have arguments with names that match those in
a function\(aqs signature but you are passing them in to the function
in a different order.
.sp
Closes #2975
.IP \(bu 2
Added new checks, \fBno\-else\-break\fP and \fBno\-else\-continue\fP
.sp
These checks highlight unnecessary \fBelse\fP and \fBelif\fP blocks after
\fBbreak\fP and \fBcontinue\fP statements.
.sp
Closes #2327
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBunnecessary\-comprehension\fP that detects unnecessary comprehensions.
.sp
This check is emitted when \fBpylint\fP finds list\-, set\- or dict\-comprehensions,
that are unnecessary and can be rewritten with the list\-, set\- or dict\-constructors.
.sp
Closes #2905
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBinvalid\-overridden\-method\fP
.sp
This check is emitted when we detect that a method is overridden
as a property or a property is overridden as a method. This can indicate
a bug in the application code that will trigger a runtime error.
.sp
Closes #2670
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBredeclared\-assigned\-name\fP
.sp
This check is emitted when \fBpylint\fP detects that a name was assigned one or multiple times in the same assignment,
which indicate a potential bug.
.sp
Closes #2898
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBself\-assigning\-variable\fP
.sp
This check is emitted when we detect that a variable is assigned
to itself, which might indicate a potential bug in the code application.
.sp
For example, the following would raise this warning:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def new_a(attr, attr2):
  a_inst = Aclass()
  a_inst.attr2 = attr2
  # should be: a_inst.attr = attr, but have a typo
  attr = attr
  return a_inst
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Closes #2930
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check \fBproperty\-with\-parameters\fP which detects when a property
has more than a single argument.
.sp
Closes #3006
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBsubprocess\-run\-check\fP to handle subprocess.run without explicitly set \fBcheck\fP keyword.
.sp
Closes #2848
.IP \(bu 2
We added a new check message \fBdict\-iter\-missing\-items\fP\&.
This is emitted when trying to iterate through a dict in a for loop without calling its .items() method.
.sp
Closes #2761
.IP \(bu 2
We added a new check message \fBmissing\-parentheses\-for\-call\-in\-test\fP\&.
This is emitted in case a call to a function is made inside a test but
it misses parentheses.
.IP \(bu 2
A new check \fBclass\-variable\-slots\-conflict\fP was added.
.sp
This check is emitted when \fBpylint\fP finds a class variable that conflicts with a slot
name, which would raise a \fBValueError\fP at runtime.
.sp
For example, the following would raise an error:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class A:
    __slots__ = (\(aqfirst\(aq, \(aqsecond\(aq)
    first = 1
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check \fBpreferred\-module\fP was added.
.sp
This check is emitted when \fBpylint\fP finds an imported module that has a
preferred replacement listed in \fBpreferred\-modules\fP\&.
.sp
For example, you can set the preferred modules as \fBxml:defusedxml,json:ujson\fP
to make \fBpylint\fP suggest using \fBdefusedxml\fP instead of \fBxml\fP
and \fBujson\fP rather than \fBjson\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
A new extension \fBbroad_try_clause\fP was added.
.sp
This extension enforces a configurable maximum number of statements inside
of a try clause. This facilitates enforcing PEP 8\(aqs guidelines about try / except
statements and the amount of code in the try clause.
.sp
You can enable this extension using \fB\-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.broad_try_clause\fP
and you can configure the amount of statements in a try statement using
\fB\-\-max\-try\-statements\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit \fBprotected\-access\fP when a single underscore prefixed attribute is used
inside a special method
.sp
Closes #1802
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlen\-as\-condition\fP now only fires when a \fBlen(x)\fP call is made without an explicit comparison.
.sp
The message and description accompanying this checker has been changed
reflect this new behavior, by explicitly asking to either rely on the
fact that empty sequence are false or to compare the length with a scalar.
.sp
OK:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if len(x) == 0:
  pass

while not len(x) == 0:
  pass

assert len(x) > 5, message
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
KO:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if not len(x):
  pass

while len(x) and other_cond:
  pass

assert len(x), message
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A file is now read from stdin if the \fB\-\-from\-stdin\fP flag is used on the
command line. In addition to the \fB\-\-from\-stdin\fP flag a (single) file
name needs to be specified on the command line, which is needed for the
report.
.IP \(bu 2
The checker for ungrouped imports is now more permissive.
.UNINDENT
.sp
The import can now be sorted alphabetically by import style.
This makes pylint compatible with isort.
.sp
The following imports do not trigger an \fBungrouped\-imports\fP anymore
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import unittest
import zipfile
from unittest import TestCase
from unittest.mock import MagicMock
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The checker for missing return documentation is now more flexible.
.UNINDENT
.sp
The following does not trigger a \fBmissing\-return\-doc\fP anymore
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def my_func(self):
    \(dq\(dq\(dqThis is a docstring.

    Returns
    \-\-\-\-\-\-\-
    :obj:\(galist\(ga of :obj:\(gastr\(ga
        List of strings
    \(dq\(dq\(dq
    return [\(dqhi\(dq, \(dqbye\(dq] #@
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsignature\-mutators\fP CLI and config option was added.
.UNINDENT
.sp
With this option, users can choose to ignore \fBtoo\-many\-function\-args\fP, \fBunexpected\-keyword\-arg\fP,
and \fBno\-value\-for\-parameter\fP for functions decorated with decorators that change
the signature of a decorated function.
.sp
For example a test may want to make use of hypothesis.
Adding \fBhypothesis.extra.numpy.arrays\fP to \fBsignature_mutators\fP
would mean that \fBno\-value\-for\-parameter\fP would not be raised for:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
@given(img=arrays(dtype=np.float32, shape=(3, 3, 3, 3)))
def test_image(img):
    ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Allow the option of f\-strings as a valid logging string formatting method.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBlogging\-fstring\-\-interpolation\fP has been merged into
\fBlogging\-format\-interpolation\fP to allow the \fBlogging\-format\-style\fP option
to control which logging string format style is valid.
To allow this, a new \fBfstr\fP value is valid for the \fBlogging\-format\-style\fP
option.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-list\-msgs\-enabled\fP command was added.
.UNINDENT
.sp
When enabling/disabling several messages and groups in a config file,
it can be unclear which messages are actually enabled and which are disabled.
This new command produces the final resolved lists of enabled/disabled messages,
sorted by symbol but with the ID provided for use with \fB\-\-help\-msg\fP\&.
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.4.4?
.sp
Release date: 2019\-11\-13
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Exempt all the names found in type annotations from \fBunused\-import\fP
.sp
The previous code was assuming that only \fBtyping\fP names need to be
exempted, but we need to do that for the rest of the type comment
names as well.
.sp
Closes #3112
.IP \(bu 2
Relax type import detection for names that do not come from the \fBtyping\fP module
.sp
Closes #3191
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.4.3?
.sp
Release date: 2019\-10\-18
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix an issue with \fBunnecessary\-comprehension\fP in comprehensions with additional repacking of elements.
.sp
Closes #3148
.IP \(bu 2
\fBimport\-outside\-toplevel\fP is emitted for \fBImportFrom\fP nodes as well.
.sp
Closes #3175
.IP \(bu 2
Do not emit \fBno\-method\-argument\fP for functions using positional only args.
.sp
Closes #3161
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-using\-sys\-exit\fP is no longer emitted when \fBexit\fP is imported in the local scope.
.sp
Closes #3147
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-overridden\-method\fP takes \fBabc.abstractproperty\fP in account
.sp
Closes #3150
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed \fBmissing\-yield\-type\-doc\fP getting incorrectly raised when
a generator does not document a yield type but has a type annotation.
.sp
Closes #3185
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtyping.overload\fP functions are exempted from \fBtoo\-many\-function\-args\fP
.sp
Closes #3170
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.4.2?
.sp
Release date: 2019\-09\-30
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBignored\-modules\fP can skip submodules.
.sp
Closes #3135
.IP \(bu 2
\fBself\-assigning\-variable\fP skips class level assignments.
.sp
Closes #2930
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-using\-sys\-exit\fP is exempted when \fBexit()\fP is imported from \fBsys\fP
.sp
Closes #3145
.IP \(bu 2
Exempt annotated assignments without variable from \fBclass\-variable\-slots\-conflict\fP
.sp
Closes #3141
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fButils.is_error\fP to account for functions returning early.
.sp
This fixes a false negative with \fBunused\-variable\fP which was no longer triggered
when a function raised an exception as the last instruction, but the body of the function
still had unused variables.
.sp
Closes #3028
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.4.1?
.sp
Release date: 2019\-09\-25
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Exempt type checking definitions defined in both clauses of a type checking guard
.sp
Closes #3127
.IP \(bu 2
Exempt type checking definitions inside the type check guard
.sp
In a7f236528bb3758886b97285a56f3f9ce5b13a99 we added basic support
for emitting \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP if a variable was only defined
inside a type checking guard (using \fBTYPE_CHECKING\fP variable from \fItyping\fP)
Unfortunately that missed the case of using those type checking imports
inside the guard itself, which triggered spurious used\-before\-assignment / E0601 \%<#\:used-before-assignment> errors.
.sp
Closes #3119
.IP \(bu 2
Require astroid >= 2.3 to avoid any compatibility issues.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.4.0?
.sp
Release date: 2019\-09\-24
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
New check: \fBimport\-outside\-toplevel\fP
.sp
This check warns when modules are imported from places other than a
module toplevel, e.g. inside a function or a class.
.IP \(bu 2
Handle inference ambiguity for \fBinvalid\-format\-index\fP
.sp
Closes #2752
.IP \(bu 2
Removed Python 2 specific checks such as \fBrelative\-import\fP,
\fBinvalid\-encoded\-data\fP, \fBmissing\-super\-argument\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Support forward references for \fBfunction\-redefined\fP check.
.sp
Closes #2540
.IP \(bu 2
Handle redefinitions in case of type checking imports.
.sp
Closes #2834
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBconsider\-using\-sys\-exit\fP
.sp
This check is emitted when we detect that a quit() or exit() is invoked
instead of sys.exit(), which is the preferred way of exiting in program.
.sp
Closes #2925
.IP \(bu 2
\fBuseless\-suppression\fP check now ignores \fBcyclic\-import\fP suppressions,
which could lead to false positives due to incomplete context at the time
of the check.
.sp
Closes #3064
.IP \(bu 2
Added new checks, \fBno\-else\-break\fP and \fBno\-else\-continue\fP
.sp
These checks highlight unnecessary \fBelse\fP and \fBelif\fP blocks after
\fBbreak\fP and \fBcontinue\fP statements.
.sp
Closes #2327
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit \fBprotected\-access\fP when a single underscore prefixed attribute
is used inside a special method
.sp
Closes #1802
.IP \(bu 2
Fix the \(dqstatement\(dq values in the PyLinter\(aqs stats reports by module.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBinvalid\-overridden\-method\fP
.sp
This check is emitted when we detect that a method is overridden
as a property or a property is overridden as a method. This can indicate
a bug in the application code that will trigger a runtime error.
.sp
Closes #2670
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBarguments\-out\-of\-order\fP
.sp
This check warns if you have arguments with names that match those in
a function\(aqs signature but you are passing them in to the function
in a different order.
.sp
Closes #2975
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBredeclared\-assigned\-name\fP
.sp
This check is emitted when \fBpylint\fP detects that a name
was assigned one or multiple times in the same assignment,
which indicate a potential bug.
.sp
Closes #2898
.IP \(bu 2
Ignore lambda calls with variadic arguments without a context.
.sp
Inferring variadic positional arguments and keyword arguments
will result into empty Tuples and Dicts, which can lead in
some cases to false positives with regard to no\-value\-for\-parameter / E1120 \%<#\:no-value-for-parameter>\&.
In order to avoid this, until we\(aqll have support for call context
propagation, we\(aqre ignoring such cases if detected.
We already did that for function calls, but the previous fix
was not taking in consideration \fBlambdas\fP
.sp
Closes #2918
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBself\-assigning\-variable\fP\&. This check is emitted
when we detect that a variable is assigned to itself, which might
indicate a potential bug in the code application.
.sp
Closes #2930
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBproperty\-with\-parameters\fP\&.
.sp
This check is emitted when we detect that a defined property also
has parameters, which are useless.
.sp
Closes #3006
.IP \(bu 2
Excluded protocol classes from a couple of checks.
.sp
Closes #3002.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check \fBunnecessary\-comprehension\fP that detects unnecessary comprehensions.
.sp
This check is emitted when \fBpylint\fP finds list\-, set\- or dict\-comprehensions,
that are unnecessary and can be rewritten with the list\-, set\- or dict\-constructors.
.sp
Closes #2905
.IP \(bu 2
Excluded PEP 526 instance and class variables from \fBno\-member\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #2945
.IP \(bu 2
Excluded \fBattrs\fP from \fBtoo\-few\-public\-methods\fP check.
.sp
Closes #2988.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBunused\-import\fP emitted for the right import names in function scopes.
.sp
Closes #2928
.IP \(bu 2
Dropped support for Python 3.4.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBassignment\-from\-no\-return\fP not triggered for async methods.
.sp
Closes #2902
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit \fBattribute\-defined\-outside\-init\fP for variables defined in setters.
.sp
Closes #409
.IP \(bu 2
Syntax errors report the column number.
.sp
Closes #2914
.IP \(bu 2
Support fully qualified typing imports for type annotations.
.sp
Closes #2915
.IP \(bu 2
Exclude \fB__dict__\fP from \fBattribute\-defined\-outside\-init\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Fix pointer on spelling check when the error are more than one time in the same line.
.sp
Closes #2895
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash happening when parent of called object cannot be determined
.IP \(bu 2
Allow of in \fBGoogleDocstring.re_multiple_type\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBsubprocess\-run\-check\fP to handle subrocess.run without explicitly set \fBcheck\fP keyword.
.sp
Closes #2848
.IP \(bu 2
When we can\(aqt infer bare except handlers, skip \fBtry\-except\-raise\fP
.sp
Closes #2853
.IP \(bu 2
Handle more \fBunnecessary\-lambda\fP cases when dealing with additional kwargs in wrapped calls
.sp
Closes #2845
.IP \(bu 2
Better postponed evaluation of annotations handling
.sp
Closes #2847
.IP \(bu 2
Support postponed evaluation of annotations for variable annotations.
.sp
Closes #2838
.IP \(bu 2
\fBepylint.py_run\fP defaults to \fBpython\fP in case the current executable is not a Python one.
.sp
Closes #2837
.IP \(bu 2
Ignore raw docstrings when running Similarities checker with \fBignore\-docstrings=yes\fP option
.IP \(bu 2
Fix crash when calling \fBinherit_from_std_ex\fP on a class which is its own ancestor
.sp
Closes #2680
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check that warns the user if a function call is used inside a test but parentheses are missing.
.sp
Closes #2658
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlen\-as\-condition\fP now only fires when a \fBlen(x)\fP call is made without an explicit comparison
.sp
The message and description accompanying this checker has been changed
reflect this new behavior, by explicitly asking to either rely on the
fact that empty sequence are false or to compare the length with a scalar.
.sp
Closes #2684
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBpreferred\-module\fP checker that notify if an import has a replacement module that should be used.
.sp
This check is emitted when \fBpylint\fP finds an imported module that has a
preferred replacement listed in \fBpreferred\-modules\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBassigning\-non\-slot\fP not emitted for classes with unknown base classes.
.sp
Closes #2807
.IP \(bu 2
\fBold\-division\fP is not emitted for non\-Const nodes.
.sp
Closes #2808
.IP \(bu 2
Added method arguments to the dot writer for pyreverse.
.sp
Closes #2139
.IP \(bu 2
Support for linting file from stdin.
.sp
IDEs may benefit from the support for linting from an in\-memory file.
.sp
Closes #1187
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check \fBclass\-variable\-slots\-conflict\fP
.sp
This check is emitted when \fBpylint\fP finds a class variable that conflicts with a slot
name, which would raise a \fBValueError\fP at runtime.
.IP \(bu 2
Added new check: dict\-iter\-missing\-items / E1141 \%<#\:dict-iter-missing-items> (E1141)
.sp
Closes #2761
.IP \(bu 2
Fix issue with pylint name in output of python \-m pylint \-\-version
.sp
Closes #2764
.IP \(bu 2
Relicense logo material under the CC BY\-SA 4.0 license.
.IP \(bu 2
Skip \fBif\fP expressions from f\-strings for the \fBcheck_elif\fP checker
.sp
Closes #2816
.IP \(bu 2
C0412 (ungrouped\-import) is now compatible with isort.
.sp
Closes #2806
.IP \(bu 2
Added new extension to detect too much code in a try clause
.sp
Closes #2877
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsignature\-mutators\fP option was added.
With this option, users can choose to ignore \fBtoo\-many\-function\-args\fP, \fBunexpected\-keyword\-arg\fP,
and \fBno\-value\-for\-parameter\fP for functions decorated with decorators that change
the signature of a decorated function.
.sp
Closes #259
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a pragma comment on its own physical line being ignored when part
of a logical line with the previous physical line.
.sp
Closes #199
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false \fBundefined\-loop\-variable\fP for a function defined in the loop,
that uses the variable defined in that loop.
.sp
Closes #202
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed \fBunused\-argument\fP and \fBfunction\-redefined\fP getting raised for
functions decorated with \fBtyping.overload\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #1581
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a false positive with \fBconsider\-using\-dict\-comprehension\fP for constructions that can\(aqt be converted to a comprehension
.sp
Closes #2963
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fB__post_init__\fP to \fBdefining\-attr\-methods\fP in order to avoid \fBattribute\-defined\-outside\-init\fP in dataclasses.
.sp
Closes #2581
.IP \(bu 2
Changed description of W0199 to use the term 2\-item\-tuple instead of 2\-uple.
.IP \(bu 2
Allow a \fB\&.\fP as a prefix for Sphinx name resolution.
.IP \(bu 2
Checkers must now keep a 1 to 1 relationship between \(dqmsgid\(dq (ie: C1234) and \(dqsymbol\(dq (i.e. : human\-readable\-symbol)
.IP \(bu 2
In checkers, an old_names can now be used for multiple new messages and pylint is now a little faster
.sp
It means if you do a partial old_names for a message definition an exception will tell you that you
must rename the associated identification.
.IP \(bu 2
Allow the choice of f\-strings as a valid way of formatting logging strings.
.sp
Closes #2395
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fB\-\-list\-msgs\-enabled\fP command to list all enabled and disabled messages given the current RC file and command line arguments.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 2.3
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
This release improves the performance of the 2.X series after it was affected by a performance regression a couple of releases ago.
.UNINDENT
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
We added a new check message \fBwrong\-exception\-operation\fP\&.
This is emitted when an operation is done against an exception, but the operation
is not valid for the exception in question. Usually emitted when having
binary operations between exceptions in except handlers.
.sp
Closes #2494
.IP \(bu 2
We added a new \fBno\-else\-raise\fP warning similar to \fBno\-else\-return\fP
.sp
Closes #2558
.IP \(bu 2
We added a new option \fBcheck\-str\-concat\-over\-line\-jumps\fP to check
\fBimplicit\-str\-concat\-in\-sequence\fP over multiple lines.
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.sp
Quite a lot of bug fixes and improvements went into this release, here\(aqs a handful of them.
For the full changes, check the full changelog.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
We no longer emit \fB*\-not\-iterating\fP checks for builtins consumed by \fBitertools\fP
.IP \(bu 2
We fixed some false positives for \fBno\-self\-argument\fP and \fBunsubscriptable\-object\fP
when using \fB__class_getitem__\fP (new in Python 3.7)
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP now supports \fBEllipsis\fP as a synonym for \fBpass\fP statements.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfixme\fP gets triggered only on comments.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP exempts starred unpacking from \fB*\-not\-iterating\fP Python 3 checks.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcompare\-to\-zero\fP is now less zealous by checking against equality and identity.
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fI\(ga\(gayield from\(ga\(ga is exempted from \(ga\(ga\fP\-not\-iterating\(ga\(ga Python 3 checks.
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A false positive with \fBnot\-async\-context\-manager\fP caused by not understanding
\fBcontextlib.asynccontextmanager\fP was fixed.
.IP \(bu 2
We refactored \fBbad\-reversed\-sequence\fP to account for more objects that can define \fB__reversed__\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBno\-member\fP is now emitted for enums when they lack a member.
.IP \(bu 2
Plugins can now use the \fBload_configuration()\fP hook.
This hook is executed after configuration is loaded to prevent overwriting plugin
specific configuration via user\-based configuration.
.IP \(bu 2
There\(aqs a new command line option \fBlist\-groups\fP for listing all the check groups
\fBpylint\fP knows about. This is useful to know what groups you can disable or enable
individually.
.UNINDENT
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.3.0?
.sp
Release date: 2019\-02\-27
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Protect against \fBNonDeducibleTypeHierarchy\fP when calling semi\-private \fBis_subtype\fP
.sp
\fBastroid.helpers.is_subtype\fP raises \fBNonDeducibleTypeHierarchy\fP when it cannot infer
the base classes of the given types, but that makes sense in its context given that
the method is mostly used to inform the inference process about the hierarchy of classes.
Doesn\(aqt make that much sense for \fBpylint\fP itself, which is why we\(aqre handling the
exception here, rather than in \fBastroid\fP
.sp
Closes pylint\-dev/astroid#644
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new command line option \fBlist\-groups\fP for listing all the check groups \fBpylint\fP knows about.
.IP \(bu 2
Allow \fBBaseException\fP for emitting \fBbroad\-except\fP, just like \fBException\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #2741
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash that occurred for \fBbad\-str\-strip\-call\fP when \fBstrip()\fP received \fBNone\fP
.sp
Closes #2743
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit \fB*\-not\-iterating\fP checks for builtins consumed by \fBitertools\fP
.sp
Closes #2731
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash caused by iterating over \fBUninferable\fP in a string formatting check.
.sp
Closes #2727
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positives for \fBno\-self\-argument\fP and \fBunsubscriptable\-object\fP when using \fB__class_getitem__\fP (new in Python 3.7)
.sp
Closes #2416
.IP \(bu 2
Support \fBEllipsis\fP as a synonym for \fBpass\fP statements.
.sp
Closes #2718
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfixme\fP gets triggered only on comments.
.sp
Closes #2321
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a false positive for \fBunused\-variable\fP and \fBnonlocal\fP assignments
.sp
Closes #2671
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBload_configuration()\fP hook for plugins
.sp
New optional hook for plugins is added: \fBload_configuration()\fP\&.
This hook is executed after configuration is loaded to prevent
overwriting plugin specific configuration via user\-based
configuration.
.sp
Closes #2635
.IP \(bu 2
Fix missing\-raises\-doc / W9006 \%<#\:missing-raises-doc> false positive (W9006)
.sp
Closes #1502
.IP \(bu 2
Exempt starred unpacking from \fB*\-not\-iterating\fP Python 3 checks
.sp
Closes #2651
.IP \(bu 2
Make \fBcompare\-to\-zero\fP less zealous by checking against equality and identity
.sp
Closes #2645
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBno\-else\-raise\fP warning (R1720)
.sp
Closes #2558
.IP \(bu 2
Exempt \fByield from\fP from \fB*\-not\-iterating\fP Python 3 checks.
.sp
Closes #2643
.IP \(bu 2
Fix incorrect generation of \fBno\-else\-return\fP warnings (R1705)
.sp
Fixed issue where \fBif\fP statements with nested \fBif\fP statements
were incorrectly being flagged as \fBno\-else\-return\fP in some cases and
not being flagged as \fBno\-else\-return\fP in other cases.  Added tests
for verification and updated pylint source files to eliminate newly
exposed warnings.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive with \fBnot\-async\-context\-manager\fP caused by not understanding \fBcontextlib.asynccontextmanager\fP
.sp
Closes #2440
.IP \(bu 2
Refactor \fBbad\-reversed\-sequence\fP to account for more objects that can define \fB__reversed__\fP
.sp
One such object would be an enum class, for which \fB__reversed__\fP yields each individual enum.
As such, the check for \fBbad\-reversed\-sequence\fP needs to not differentiate between classes
and instances when it comes for checking of \fB__reversed__\fP presence.
.sp
Closes #2598
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBwrong\-exception\-operation\fP
.sp
Used when an operation is done against an exception, but the operation
is not valid for the exception in question. Usually emitted when having
binary operations between exceptions in except handlers.
.sp
Closes #2494
.IP \(bu 2
\fBno\-member\fP is emitted for enums when they lack a member
.sp
Previously we weren\(aqt doing this because we detected a
\fB__getattr__\fP implementation on the \fBEnum\fP class
(and this check is skipped for classes with \fB__getattr__\fP),
but that is fine for Enums, given that they are inferred in a customised
way in astroid.
.sp
Closes #2565
.IP \(bu 2
Generalize \fBchained\-comparison\fP
.sp
Previous version incorrectly detects \fIa < b < c and b < d\fP and fails to
detect \fIa < b < c and c < d\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Avoid popping __main__ when using multiple jobs
.sp
Closes #2689
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new option \(aqcheck\-str\-concat\-over\-line\-jumps\(aq to check implicit\-str\-concat\-in\-sequence / W1403 \%<#\:implicit-str-concat-in-sequence>\(aq
.IP \(bu 2
Fixes for the new style logging format linter.
.sp
The number of arguments was not handled properly, leading to an always
successful check.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBnot\-callable\fP for uninferable properties.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBuseless\-else\-on\-loop\fP if the break is deep in the else
of an inner loop.
.IP \(bu 2
Minor improvements to the help text for a few options.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 2.2
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
String checker now reports format string type mismatches.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBduplicate\-string\-formatting\-argument\fP was added for detecting duplicate string
formatting arguments that should be passed instead as named arguments.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlogging\-format\-style\fP is a new option for the logging checker for usage of
str.format() style format strings in calls to loggers.
.sp
It accepts two options: \fB\-\-logging\-format\-style=old\fP for using \fI%\fP style formatting,
which is the assumed default, and \fB\-\-logging\-format\-style=new\fP for using \fI{}\fP style formatting.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBimplicit\-str\-concat\-in\-sequence\fP detects string concatenation inside lists, sets & tuples.
.sp
Example of code that would generate such warning:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
woops = (\(aqa\(aq, \(aqb\(aq \(aqc\(aq)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtry\-except\-raise\fP checker now handles multilevel inheritance hirerachy for exceptions correctly.
.sp
Closes #2484
.IP \(bu 2
Ignore import x.y.z as z cases for checker \fBuseless\-import\-alias\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBunnecessary\-pass\fP is now also emitted when a function or class contains only docstring and pass statement,
in which case, docstring is enough for empty definition.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBundefined\-variable\fP and \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP with nonlocal keyword usage.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix exceptions being raised when one of the params is not a ClassDef for \fBcheckers.utils.is_subclass_of\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP now picks the latest value from the inferred values of the exception that gets
raised, when looking for \fBraising\-non\-exception\fP\&. This helps when reusing a variable name
for multiple types, since \fBpylint\fP was picking just the first inferred value, leading
to spurious false positives.
.sp
Closes #2431
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP used to emit a \fBnot\-an\-iterable\fP error when looking at coroutines built
with \fBasyncio.coroutine\fP\&. This is no longer the case as we handle coroutines explicitly.
.sp
Closes #996
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP used to emit an \fBunused\-variable\fP error if unused import was found in the function. Now instead of
\fBunused\-variable\fP, \fBunused\-import\fP is emitted.
.sp
Closes #2421
.UNINDENT
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.2.2?
.sp
Release date: 2018\-11\-28
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Change the \fBlogging\-format\-style\fP to use name identifier instead of their
corresponding Python identifiers
.sp
This is to prevent users having to think about escaping the default value for
\fBlogging\-format\-style\fP in the generated config file. Also our config parsing
utilities don\(aqt quite support escaped values when it comes to \fBchoices\fP detection,
so this would have needed various hacks around that.
.sp
Closes #2614
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.2.1?
.sp
Release date: 2018\-11\-27
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash caused by \fBimplicit\-str\-concat\-in\-sequence\fP and multi\-bytes characters.
.sp
Closes #2610
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.2?
.sp
Release date: 2018\-11\-25
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Consider \fBrange()\fP objects for \fBundefined\-loop\-variable\fP leaking from iteration.
.sp
Closes #2533
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdeprecated\-method\fP can use the attribute name for identifying a deprecated method
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Previously we were using the fully qualified name, which we still do, but the fully
qualified name for some \fBunittest\fP deprecated aliases leads to a generic
deprecation function. Instead on relying on that, we now also rely on the attribute
name, which should solve some false positives.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Closes #1653
Closes #1946
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix compatibility with changes to stdlib tokenizer.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP is less eager to consume the whole line for pragmas
.sp
Closes #2485
.IP \(bu 2
Obtain the correct number of CPUs for virtualized or containerized environments.
.sp
Closes #2519
.IP \(bu 2
Change \fBunbalanced\-tuple\-unpacking\fP back to a warning.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
It used to be a warning until a couple of years ago, after it was promoted to
an error. But the check might be suggesting the wrong thing in some cases,
for instance when checking against \fBsys.argv\fP which cannot be known at static
analysis time. Given it might rely on potential unknown data, it\(aqs best to
have it as a warning.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Closes #2522
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Remove \fBenumerate\fP usage suggestion when defining \fB__iter__\fP (C0200)
.sp
Closes #2477
.IP \(bu 2
Emit \fBtoo\-many\-starred\-assignment\fP only when the number of Starred nodes is per assignment elements
.sp
Closes #2513
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtry\-except\-raise\fP checker now handles multilevel inheritance hirerachy for exceptions correctly.
.sp
Closes #2484
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new check, \fBsimplifiable\-if\-expression\fP for expressions like \fBTrue if cond else False\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #2487
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtoo\-few\-public\-methods\fP is not reported for \fBtyping.NamedTuple\fP
.sp
Closes #2459
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\(gatoo\-few\-public\-methods\fP is not reported for dataclasses created with options.
.sp
Closes #2488
.IP \(bu 2
Remove wrong modules from \(aqbad\-python3\-import\(aq.
.sp
Closes #2453
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBjson\fP reporter prints an empty list when no messages are emitted
.sp
Closes #2446
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new check, \fBduplicate\-string\-formatting\-argument\fP
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This new check is emitted whenever a duplicate string formatting argument
is found.
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Closes #497
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBassignment\-from\-no\-return\fP is not emitted for coroutines.
.sp
Closes #1715
.IP \(bu 2
Report format string type mismatches.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBconsider\-using\-ternary\fP and \fBsimplified\-boolean\-expression\fP no longer emit for sequence based checks
.sp
Closes #2473
.IP \(bu 2
Handle \fBAstroidSyntaxError\fP when trying to import a module.
.sp
Closes #2313
.IP \(bu 2
Allow \fB__module__\fP to be redefined at a class level.
.sp
Closes #2451
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP used to emit an \fBunused\-variable\fP error if unused import was found in the function. Now instead of
\fBunused\-variable\fP, \fBunused\-import\fP is emitted.
.sp
Closes #2421
.IP \(bu 2
Handle asyncio.coroutine when looking for \fBnot\-an\-iterable\fP check.
.sp
Closes #996
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBlocally\-enabled\fP check is gone.
.sp
Closes #2442
.IP \(bu 2
Infer decorated methods when looking for method\-hidden
.sp
Closes #2369
.IP \(bu 2
Pick the latest value from the inferred values when looking for \fBraising\-non\-exception\fP
.sp
Closes #2431
.IP \(bu 2
Extend the TYPE_CHECKING guard to TYPE_CHECKING name as well, not just the attribute
.sp
Closes #2411
.IP \(bu 2
Ignore import x.y.z as z cases for checker \fBuseless\-import\-alias\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #2309
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBundefined\-variable\fP and \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP with nonlocal keyword usage.
.sp
Closes #2049
.IP \(bu 2
Stop \fBprotected\-access\fP exception for missing class attributes
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit \fBassignment\-from\-no\-return\fP for decorated function nodes
.sp
Closes #2385
.IP \(bu 2
\fBunnecessary\-pass\fP is now also emitted when a function or class contains only docstring and pass statement.
.sp
In Python, stubbed functions often have a body that contains just a single \fBpass\fP statement,
indicating that the function doesn\(aqt do anything. However, a stubbed function can also have just a
docstring, and function with a docstring and no body also does nothing.
.sp
Closes #2208
.IP \(bu 2
\fBduplicate\-argument\-name\fP is emitted for more than one duplicate argument per function
.sp
Closes #1712
.IP \(bu 2
Allow double indentation levels for more distinguishable indentations
.sp
Closes #741
.IP \(bu 2
Consider tuples in exception handler for \fBtry\-except\-raise\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #2389
.IP \(bu 2
Fix astroid.ClassDef check in checkers.utils.is_subclass_of
.IP \(bu 2
Fix wildcard imports being ignored by the import checker
.IP \(bu 2
Fix external/internal distinction being broken in the import graph
.IP \(bu 2
Fix wildcard import check not skipping \fB__init__.py\fP
.sp
Closes #2430
.IP \(bu 2
Add new option to logging checker, \fBlogging_format_style\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \-\-ignore\-imports to understand multi\-line imports
.sp
Closes #1422
Closes #2019
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new check \(aqimplicit\-str\-concat\-in\-sequence\(aq to spot string concatenation inside lists, sets & tuples.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBliteral\-comparison\fP is now emitted for 0 and 1 literals.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 2.1
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
This release mostly includes fixes for bugs found after the launch of 2.0.
.UNINDENT
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBmisplaced\-format\-function\fP\&.
.sp
This message is emitted when pylint detects that a format function is called on non str object.
This can occur due to wrong placement of closing bracket, e.g
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
print(\(aqvalue: {}\(aq).format(123) # bad

print(\(aqvalue: {}\(aq.format(123)) # good
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtry\-except\-raise\fP check was demoted from an error to a warning, as part of issue #2323.
.IP \(bu 2
Correctly handle the new name of the Python implementation of the \fBabc\fP module.
.sp
In Python 3.7, the \fBabc\fP module has both a C implementation as well as a Python one,
but the Python implementation has a different file name that what \fBpylint\fP was expecting,
resulting in some checks getting confused.
.IP \(bu 2
Modules with \fB__getattr__\fP are exempted by default from \fBno\-member\fP
.sp
There\(aqs no easy way to figure out if a module has a particular member when
the said module uses \fB__getattr__\fP, which is a new addition to Python 3.7.
Instead we assume the safe thing to do, in the same way we do for classes,
and skip those modules from checking.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid name\fP is no longer triggered for function and attribute names longer
than 30 characters. The upper limit was removed completely.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive \fBundefined\-variable\fP for self referential class name in lamdbas
.IP \(bu 2
\fBno\-else\-return\fP also specifies the type of the branch that is causing the error.
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed inconsistent behaviour for bad\-continuation on first line of file.
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a bug where \fBpylint\fP was not able to disable certain messages on the last line through
the global disable option.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP no longer emits \fBuseless\-return\fP when it finds a single statement that is the \fBreturn\fP itself
.sp
We still want to be explicit when a function is supposed to return
an optional value; even though \fBpass\fP could still work, it\(aqs not explicit
enough and the function might look like it\(aqs missing an implementation.
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a bug where \fBpylint\fP was crashing when being unable to infer the value of an argument to \fBnext()\fP
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP no longer emit \fBnot\-an\-iterable\fP when dealing with async iterators.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\fP gained the ability to specify a default docstring type for when the check cannot guess the type
.sp
For this we added a \fB\-\-default\-docstring\-type\fP command line option.
.UNINDENT
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.1.1?
.sp
Release date: 2018\-08\-07
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
fix pylint crash due to \fBmisplaced\-format\-function\fP not correctly handling class attribute.
.sp
Closes #2384
.IP \(bu 2
Do not emit *\-builtin for Python 3 builtin checks when the builtin is used inside a try\-except
.sp
Closes #2228
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsimplifiable\-if\-statement\fP not emitted when dealing with subscripts
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.1?
.sp
Release date: 2018\-08\-01
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtrailing\-comma\-tuple\fP gets emitted for \fByield\fP statements as well.
.sp
Closes #2363
.IP \(bu 2
Get only the arguments of the scope function for \fBredefined\-argument\-from\-local\fP
.sp
Closes #2364
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check \fBmisplaced\-format\-function\fP which is emitted if format function is used on
non str object.
.sp
Closes #2200
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchain.from_iterable\fP no longer emits \fIdict\-{}\-not\-iterating\fP when dealing with dict values and keys
.IP \(bu 2
Demote the \fBtry\-except\-raise\fP message from an error to a warning (E0705 \-> W0706)
.sp
Closes #2323
.IP \(bu 2
Correctly handle the new name of the Python implementation of the \fBabc\fP module.
.sp
Closes pylint\-dev/astroid#2288
.IP \(bu 2
Modules with \fB__getattr__\fP are exempted by default from \fBno\-member\fP
.sp
There\(aqs no easy way to figure out if a module has a particular member when
the said module uses \fB__getattr__\fP, which is a new addition to Python 3.7.
Instead we assume the safe thing to do, in the same way we do for classes,
and skip those modules from checking.
.sp
Closes #2331
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive \fBinvalid name\fP message when method or attribute name is longer then 30 characters.
.sp
Closes #2047
.IP \(bu 2
Include the type of the next branch in \fBno\-else\-return\fP
.sp
Closes #2295
.IP \(bu 2
Fix inconsistent behaviour for bad\-continuation on first line of file
.sp
Closes #2281
