.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 2.0
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Dropped support for Python 2. This release will work only on Python 3.4+.
.sp
If you need to use \fBpylint\fP with Python 2, you can use Pylint 1.9+. We\(aqll continue
to do bug releases until 2020, when Python 2 goes officially EOL.
\fBpylint\fP will gain the ability to analyze Python 2 files, but some checks might not work
as they will assume that their running environment is Python 2.
.IP \(bu 2
Given the dropping of Python 2, the Python 3 porting mode (enabled via \fB\-\-py3k\fP) can now
also run with Python 3.
.sp
The porting mode used to be a no\-op on Python 3, but most of the messages can now be emitted
when the running interpreter is Python 3. The only messages that won\(aqt be emitted are those that
rely on a particular syntax specific to Python 2, for instance \fBprint\fP as a statement.
.UNINDENT
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBuseless\-object\-inheritance\fP\&.
.sp
This refactoring message is emitted when pylint detects that a class inherits from object,
which is redundant as in Python 3, every class implicitly inherits from object.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class A(object):
    pass

class A:    # better
    pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBcomparison\-with\-callable\fP\&.
.sp
This refactoring message is emitted when pylint detects that a comparison with a callable was
made, which might suggest that some parenthesis were omitted, resulting in potential unwanted
behaviour.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def foo():
    return None

def goo():
    return None

if foo == 786:  # bad
    pass

if foo() == 786:    # good
    pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBchained\-comparison\fP\&.
.sp
This refactoring message is emitted if a boolean operation can be simplified by chaining some
of its operations. check below example:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if a < b and b < c:
    pass

if a < b < c:   # better
    pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBuseless\-import\-alias\fP\&.
.sp
This refactoring message is emitted when an import alias does not rename the original package.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import numpy as numpy # bad
import numpy as np # good
from collection import OrderedDict as OrderedDict # bad
from collection import OrderedDict as ordered_dict # good
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBcomparison\-with\-itself\fP\&.
.sp
This refactoring message is emitted when a variable is compared against itself.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if variable == variable:  # bad
    pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBconsider\-using\-in\fP\&.
.sp
This refactoring message is emitted when a variable is compared against multiple
values concatenated by ors instead of using the faster, more idiomatic \(dqin\(dq check.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if variable == 1 or variable == 2 or variable == 3:  # bad
    pass

if variable in (1, 2, 3):  # good
    pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBconsider\-using\-get\fP\&.
.sp
This refactoring message is emitted when manually checking if a key is in a dictionary
and getting its value if it is (and optionally a default if not)
instead of the more idiomatic dict.get.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if \(aqkey\(aq in dictionary:  # bad
    variable = dictionary[\(aqkey\(aq]
else:
    variable = \(aqdefault\(aq

variable = dictionary.get(\(aqkey\(aq, \(aqdefault\(aq)  # good
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBconsider\-using\-join\fP\&.
.sp
This refactoring message is emitted when using a for loop over an iterable to join strings
instead of the faster, less memory consuming and more idiomatic str.join(sequence).
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
result = \(aq\(aq  # bad
for number in [\(aq1\(aq, \(aq2\(aq, \(aq3\(aq]:
    result += number

result = \(aq\(aq.join([\(aq1\(aq, \(aq2\(aq, \(aq3\(aq])  # good
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
New \fBuseless\-return\fP message when function or method ends with a \(dqreturn\(dq or
\(dqreturn None\(dq statement and this is the only return statement in the body.
.IP \(bu 2
New \fBuse\-symbolic\-message\-instead\fP message when a message is activated or
deactivated by id instead of symbol.
The use of symbol is more explicit and easier to remind.
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBconsider\-swap\-variables\fP\&.
.sp
This refactoring message is emitted when using a temporary variable in order
to swap the values of two variables instead of the shorter, more idiomatic
approach with tuple\-unpacking.
.sp
Instead of a temporary variable, the one\-line syntax with commas should be used.
.sp
See this style guide \%<https://\:docs\:.python-guide\:.org/\:writing/\:style> document or the Pycon 2007 \fIswap values presentation\fP for details.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
temp = a  # the wrong way
a = b
b = temp

a, b = b, a  # the right way
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Two new checks, \fBinvalid\-envvar\-value\fP and \fBinvalid\-envvar\-default\fP, were added.
.sp
The former is trigger whenever pylint detects that environment variable manipulation
functions uses a different type than strings, while the latter is emitted whenever
the said functions are using a default variable of different type than expected.
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBsubprocess\-popen\-preexec\-fn\fP,
.sp
This refactoring message is emitted when using the keyword argument preexec_fn
when creating subprocess.Popen instances which may be unsafe when used in
the presence of threads.
.sp
See subprocess.Popen \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:subprocess\:.html#\:popen-constructor>
for full warning details.
.IP \(bu 2
New \fBtry\-except\-raise\fP message when an except handler block has a bare
\fBraise\fP statement as its first operator or the exception type being raised
is the same as the one being handled.
.IP \(bu 2
New \fBpossibly\-unused\-variable\fP check added.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
This is similar to \fBunused\-variable\fP, the only difference is that it is
emitted when we detect a locals() call in the scope of the unused variable.
The \fBlocals()\fP call could potentially use the said variable, by consuming
all values that are present up to the point of the call. This new check
allows to disable this error when the user intentionally uses \fBlocals()\fP
to consume everything.
.sp
For instance, the following code will now trigger this new error:
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def func():
    some_value = some_call()
    return locals()
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
New \fBunhashable\-dict\-key\fP check added to detect dict lookups using
unhashable keys such as lists or dicts.
.IP \(bu 2
New \fBself\-cls\-assignment\fP warning check added.
.sp
This is warning if the first argument of an instance/ class method gets
assigned
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Foo(object):
    def foo(self, bar):
        self = bar
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
New verbose mode option \fB\-\-verbose\fP to display of extra non\-checker\-related output. Disabled by default.
.IP \(bu 2
Two new checks were added for recommending dict and set comprehensions where possible.
.sp
These two checks are going to flag the following examples:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
dict([(k, v) for (k, v) in ...]) # better as {k: v for k, v in ...}
set([k for k in ...]) # better as {k for k in ...}
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A couple of performance improvements brought to \fBastroid\fP should make
\fBpylint\fP should be a bit faster as well.
.sp
We added a new flag, \fBmax_inferable_values\fP on \fBastroid.MANAGER\fP for
limiting the maximum amount of values that \fBastroid\fP can infer when inferring
values. This change should improve the performance when dealing with large frameworks
such as \fBdjango\fP\&.
You can also control this behaviour with \fBpylint \-\-limit\-inference\-results\fP
.sp
We also rewrote how \fBnodes_of_class\fP and \fBget_children\fP methods operate which
should result in a performance boost for a couple of checks.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP message when exception is raised inside
an else statement.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn for \fBmissing\-type\-doc\fP and/or \fBmissing\-return\-type\-doc\fP, if type annotations
exist on the function signature for a parameter and/or return type.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP message when if
statement is inside try/except.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP message when
\fBwhile\fP loop are used.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix emission of false positive \fBno\-member\fP message for class with
\(dqprivate\(dq attributes whose name is mangled.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBunused\-argument\fP false positives with overshadowed variable in dictionary comprehension.
.IP \(bu 2
Fixing false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP when
never returning functions are used (i.e such as sys.exit).
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP message when a
function is defined under an if statement.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP message by
avoiding useless exception inference if the exception is not handled.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBundefined\-variable\fP for lambda argument in class definitions
.IP \(bu 2
Suppress false\-positive \fBnot\-callable\fP messages from certain staticmethod descriptors
.IP \(bu 2
Expand \fBignored\-argument\-names\fP include starred arguments and keyword arguments
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsingleton\-comparison\fP will suggest better boolean conditions for negative conditions.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBundefined\-loop\-variable\fP takes in consideration non\-empty iterred objects before emitting.
.sp
For instance, if the loop iterable is not empty, this check will no longer be emitted.
.IP \(bu 2
Enum classes no longer trigger \fBtoo\-few\-methods\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Special methods now count towards \fBtoo\-few\-methods\fP,
and are considered part of the public API.
They are still not counted towards the number of methods for
\fBtoo\-many\-methods\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdocparams\fP extension allows abstract methods to document returns
documentation even if the default implementation does not return something.
They also no longer need to document raising a \fBNotImplementedError.\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Skip wildcard import check for \fB__init__.py\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn useless\-super\-delegation / W0235 \%<#\:useless-super-delegation>\(aq if the subclass method has different type annotations.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn that a global variable is unused if it is defined by an import
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def func():
    global sys
    import sys
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Added basic support for postponed evaluation of function annotations.
.sp
If \fBpylint\fP detects the corresponding \fBfrom __future__ import annotations\fP import,
it will not emit \fBused\-before\-assignment\fP and \fBundefined\-variable\fP in the cases
triggered by the annotations.
.sp
More details on the postponed evaluation of annotations can be read in
PEP 563 \%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0563>\&.
.IP \(bu 2
A new command line option was added, \fB\-\-exit\-zero\fP, for the use of continuous integration
scripts which abort if a command returns a non\-zero status code.  If the
option is specified, and Pylint runs successfully, it will exit with 0
regardless of the number of lint issues detected.
.sp
Configuration errors, parse errors, and calling Pylint with invalid
command\-line options all still return a non\-zero error code, even if
\fB\-\-exit\-zero\fP is specified.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit \fBunused\-import\fP anymore for typing imports used in type comments. For instance,
in the following example pylint used to complain that \fBAny\fP and \fBList\fP are not used,
while they should be considered used by a type checker.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from typing import Any, List
a = 1 # type: List[Any]
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBline\-too\-long\fP for commented lines at the end of module
.IP \(bu 2
Fix emitting \fBuseless\-super\-delegation\fP when changing the default value of keyword arguments.
.IP \(bu 2
Support \fBtyping.TYPE_CHECKING\fP for \fI:ref:\(gaunused\-import\(ga\fP errors
.sp
When modules are imported under \fBtyping.TYPE_CHECKING\fP guard, \fBpylint\fP
will no longer emit \fI:ref:\(gaunused\-import\(ga\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBunused\-variable\fP in lambda default arguments
.IP \(bu 2
\fBassignment\-from\-no\-return\fP considers methods as well as functions.
.sp
If you have a method that doesn\(aqt return a value, but later on you assign
a value to a function call to that method (so basically it will be \fBNone\fP),
then \fBpylint\fP is going to emit an \fBassignment\-from\-no\-return\fP error.
.IP \(bu 2
A new flag was added, \fB\-\-ignore\-none\fP which controls the \fBno\-member\fP
behaviour with respect to \fBNone\fP values.
.sp
Previously \fBpylint\fP was not emitting \fBno\-member\fP if it inferred that
the owner of an attribute access is a \fBNone\fP value. In some cases,
this might actually cause bugs, so if you want to check for \fBNone\fP values
as well, pass \fB\-\-ignore\-none=n\fP to pylint.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive \fBbad\-continuation\fP for with statements
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive \fBbad\-whitespace\fP message for typing annoatations
with ellipses in them
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive \fBundefined\-variable\fP for nested lambdas
.UNINDENT
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 2.0?
.sp
Release date: 2018\-07\-15
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtry\-except\-raise\fP should not be emitted if there are any parent exception class handlers.
.sp
Closes #2284
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtrailing\-comma\-tuple\fP can be emitted for \fBreturn\fP statements as well.
.sp
Closes #2269
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP message when exception is raised
inside an else statement.
.sp
Closes #1782
.IP \(bu 2
\fBImportFrom\fP nodes correctly use the full name for the import sorting checks.
.sp
Closes #2181
.IP \(bu 2
[].extend and similar builtin operations don\(aqt emit \fIdict\-*\-not\-iterating\fP with the Python 3 porting checker
.sp
Closes #2187
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check \fBconsider\-using\-dict\-comprehension\fP which is emitted if for dict initialization
the old style with list comprehensions is used.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check \fBconsider\-using\-set\-comprehension\fP which is emitted if for set initialization
the old style with list comprehensions is used.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlogging\-not\-lazy\fP is emitted whenever pylint infers that a string is built with addition
.sp
Closes #2193
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check \fBchained\-comparison\fP which is emitted if a boolean operation can be simplified
by chaining some of its operations.
e.g \(dqa < b and b < c\(dq, can be simplified as \(dqa < b < c\(dq.
.sp
Closes #2032
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check \fBconsider\-using\-in\fP for comparisons of a variable against
multiple values with \(dq==\(dq and \(dqor\(dqs instead of checking if the variable
is contained \(dqin\(dq a tuple of those values.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBin\fP is considered iterating context for some of the Python 3 porting checkers
.sp
Closes #2186
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fB\-\-ignore\-none\fP flag to control if pylint should warn about \fBno\-member\fP where the owner is None
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive related to \fBtoo\-many\-arguments\fP and bounded \fB__get__\fP methods
.sp
Closes #2172
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmcs\fP as the first parameter of metaclass\(aqs \fB__new__\fP method was replaced by \fBcls\fP
.sp
Closes #2028
.IP \(bu 2
\fBassignment\-from\-no\-return\fP considers methods as well.
.sp
Closes #2081
.IP \(bu 2
Support typing.TYPE_CHECKING for \fI:ref:\(gaunused\-import\(ga\fP errors
.sp
Closes #1948
.IP \(bu 2
Inferred classes at a function level no longer emit \fBinvalid\-name\fP
when they don\(aqt respect the variable regular expression
.sp
Closes #1049
.IP \(bu 2
Added basic support for postponed evaluation of function annotations.
.sp
Closes #2069
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a bug with \fBmissing\-kwoa\fP and variadics parameters
.sp
Closes #1111
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsimplifiable\-if\-statement\fP takes in account only when assigning to same targets
.sp
Closes #1984
.IP \(bu 2
Make \fBlen\-as\-condition\fP test more cases, such as \fBlen() < 1\fP or \fBlen <= 0\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive \fBline\-too\-long\fP message emission for
commented line at the end of a module
.sp
Closes #1950
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive \fBbad\-continuation\fP for with statements
.sp
Closes #461
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn about \fBstop\-iteration\-return\fP when using \fBnext()\fP over \fBitertools.count\fP
.sp
Closes #2158
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check \fBconsider\-using\-get\fP for unidiomatic usage of value/default\-retrieval
for a key from a dictionary
.sp
Closes #2076
.IP \(bu 2
invalid\-slice\-index / E1127 \%<#\:invalid-slice-index> is not emitted when the slice is used as index for a complex object.
.sp
We only use a handful of known objects (list, set and friends) to figure out if
we should emit invalid\-slice\-index / E1127 \%<#\:invalid-slice-index> when the slice is used to subscript an object.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit \fBunused\-import\fP anymore for typing imports used in type comments.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new check useless\-import\-alias / C0414 \%<#\:useless-import-alias>\(aq.
.sp
Closes #2052
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBcomparison\-with\-callable\fP to warn for comparison with bare callable, without calling it.
.sp
Closes #2082
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn for \fBmissing\-type\-doc\fP and/or \fBmissing\-return\-type\-doc\fP, if type
annotations exist on the function signature for a parameter and/or return type.
.sp
Closes #2083
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fB\-\-exit\-zero\fP option for continuous integration scripts to more
easily call Pylint in environments that abort when a program returns a
non\-zero (error) status code.
.sp
Closes #2042
.IP \(bu 2
Warn if the first argument of an instance/ class method gets assigned
.sp
Closes #977
.IP \(bu 2
New check \fBcomparison\-with\-itself\fP to check comparison between same value.
.sp
Closes #2051
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, logging\-fstring\-interpolation / W1203 \%<#\:logging-fstring-interpolation>\(aq, emitted when f\-string
is used within logging function calls.
.sp
Closes #1998
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt show useless\-super\-delegation / W0235 \%<#\:useless-super-delegation>\(aq if the subclass method has different type annotations.
.sp
Closes #1923
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBunhashable\-dict\-key\fP check.
.sp
Closes #586
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn that a global variable is unused if it is defined by an import
.sp
Closes #1453
.IP \(bu 2
Skip wildcard import check for \fB__init__.py\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #2026
.IP \(bu 2
The Python 3 porting mode can now run with Python 3 as well.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtoo\-few\-public\-methods\fP is not emitted for dataclasses.
.sp
Closes #1793
.IP \(bu 2
New verbose mode option, enabled with \fB\-\-verbose\fP command line flag, to
display of extra non\-checker\-related output. It is disabled by default.
.sp
Closes #1863
.IP \(bu 2
\fBundefined\-loop\-variable\fP takes in consideration non\-empty iterred objects before emitting
.sp
Closes #2039
.IP \(bu 2
Add support for numpydoc optional return value names.
.sp
Closes #2030
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsingleton\-comparison\fP accounts for negative checks
.sp
Closes #2037
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check \fBconsider\-using\-in\fP for comparisons of a variable against
multiple values with \(dq==\(dq and \(dqor\(dqs instead of checking if the variable
is contained \(dqin\(dq a tuple of those values.
.sp
Closes #1977
.IP \(bu 2
defaultdict and subclasses of dict are now handled for dict\-iter\-* checks
.sp
Closes #2005
.IP \(bu 2
\fBlogging\-format\-interpolation\fP also emits when f\-strings are used instead of % syntax.
.sp
Closes #1788
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt trigger misplaced\-bare\-raise / E0704 \%<#\:misplaced-bare-raise> when the raise is in a finally clause
.sp
Closes #1924
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new check, \fBpossibly\-unused\-variable\fP\&.
.sp
This is similar to \fBunused\-variable\fP, the only difference is that it is
emitted when we detect a locals() call in the scope of the unused variable.
The \fBlocals()\fP call could potentially use the said variable, by consuming
all values that are present up to the point of the call. This new check
allows to disable this error when the user intentionally uses \fBlocals()\fP
to consume everything.
.sp
Closes #1909.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBno\-else\-return\fP accounts for multiple cases
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
The check was a bit overrestrictive because we were checking for
return nodes in the .orelse node. At that point though the if statement
can be refactored to not have the orelse. This improves the detection of
other cases, for instance it now detects TryExcept nodes that are part of
the .else branch.
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Closes #1852
.IP \(bu 2
Added two new checks, \fBinvalid\-envvar\-value\fP and \fBinvalid\-envvar\-default\fP\&.
.sp
The former is trigger whenever pylint detects that environment variable manipulation
functions uses a different type than strings, while the latter is emitted whenever
the said functions are using a default variable of different type than expected.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check \fBconsider\-using\-join\fP for concatenation of strings using str.join(sequence)
.sp
Closes #1952
.IP \(bu 2
Add a check \fBconsider\-swap\-variables\fP for swapping variables with tuple unpacking
.sp
Closes #1922
.IP \(bu 2
Add new checker \fBtry\-except\-raise\fP that warns the user if an except handler block
has a \fBraise\fP statement as its first operator. The warning is shown when there is
a bare raise statement, effectively re\-raising the exception that was caught or the
type of the exception being raised is the same as the one being handled.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt crash on invalid strings when checking for \fBlogging\-format\-interpolation\fP
.sp
Closes #1944
.IP \(bu 2
Exempt \fB__doc__\fP from triggering a \fBredefined\-builtin\fP
.sp
\fB__doc__\fP can be used to specify a docstring for a module without
passing it as a first\-statement string.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive bad\-whitespace from function arguments with default
values and annotations
.sp
Closes #1831
.IP \(bu 2
Fix stop\-iteration\-return / R1708 \%<#\:stop-iteration-return> false positive when next builtin has a
default value in a generator
.sp
Closes #1830
.IP \(bu 2
Fix emission of false positive \fBno\-member\fP message for class with  \(dqprivate\(dq attributes whose name is mangled.
.sp
Closes #1643
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a crash which occurred when \fBUninferable\fP wasn\(aqt properly handled in \fBstop\-iteration\-return\fP
.sp
Closes #1779
.IP \(bu 2
Use the proper node to get the name for redefined functions (#1792)
.sp
Closes #1774
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt crash when encountering bare raises while checking inconsistent returns
.sp
Closes #1773
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP message when if statement is inside try/except.
.sp
Closes #1770
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP message when while loop are used.
.sp
Closes #1772
.IP \(bu 2
Correct column number for whitespace conventions.
.sp
Previously the column was stuck at 0
.sp
Closes #1649
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBunused\-argument\fP false positives with overshadowed variable in
dictionary comprehension.
.sp
Closes #1731
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP message when never
returning functions are used (i.e sys.exit for example).
.sp
Closes #1771
.IP \(bu 2
Fix error when checking if function is exception, as in \fBbad\-exception\-context\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP message when a
function is defined under an if statement.
.sp
Closes #1794
.IP \(bu 2
New \fBuseless\-return\fP message when function or method ends with a \(dqreturn\(dq or
\(dqreturn None\(dq statement and this is the only return statement in the body.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP message by
avoiding useless exception inference if the exception is not handled.
.sp
Closes #1794 (second part)
.IP \(bu 2
Fix bad thread instantiation check when target function is provided in args.
.sp
Closes #1840
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed false positive when a numpy Attributes section follows a Parameters
section
.sp
Closes #1867
.IP \(bu 2
Fix incorrect file path when file absolute path contains multiple \fBpath_strip_prefix\fP strings.
.sp
Closes #1120
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive undefined\-variable / E0602 \%<#\:undefined-variable> for lambda argument in class definitions
.sp
Closes #1824
.IP \(bu 2
Add of a new checker that warns the user if some messages are enabled or disabled
by id instead of symbol.
.sp
Closes #1599
.IP \(bu 2
Suppress false\-positive \fBnot\-callable\fP messages from certain
staticmethod descriptors
.sp
Closes #1699
.IP \(bu 2
Fix indentation handling with tabs
.sp
Closes #1148
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive \fBbad\-continuation\fP error
.sp
Closes #638
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positive unused\-variable / W0612 \%<#\:unused-variable> in lambda default arguments
.sp
Closes #1921
Closes #1552
Closes #1099
Closes #210
.IP \(bu 2
Updated the default report format to include paths that can be clicked on in some terminals (e.g. iTerm).
.IP \(bu 2
Fix inline def behavior with \fBtoo\-many\-statements\fP checker
.sp
Closes #1978
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBKeyError\fP raised when using docparams and NotImplementedError is documented.
.sp
Closes #2102
.IP \(bu 2
Fix method\-hidden / E0202 \%<#\:method-hidden>\(aq raised when assigning to a property or data descriptor.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix emitting \fBuseless\-super\-delegation\fP when changing the default value of keyword arguments.
.sp
Closes #2022
.IP \(bu 2
Expand ignored\-argument\-names include starred arguments and keyword arguments
.sp
Closes #2214
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive undefined\-variable / E0602 \%<#\:undefined-variable> in nested lambda
.sp
Closes #760
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false\-positive \fBbad\-whitespace\fP message for typing annoatations
with ellipses in them
.sp
Close 1992
.IP \(bu 2
Broke down \(dqmissing\-docstrings\(dq between \(dqmodule\(dq, \(dqclass\(dq and \(dqfunction\(dq
.sp
For this to work we had to make multiple messages with the same old name
possible.
.sp
Closes #1164
.UNINDENT
.SS 1.x
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 1.9
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
None so far
.UNINDENT
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 checker was added to warn about the removed \fBoperator.div\fP function.
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 checker was added to warn about accessing functions that have been
moved from the urllib module in corresponding subpackages, such as \fBurllib.request\fP\&.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from urllib import urlencode
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead the previous code should use \fBurllib.parse\fP or \fBsix.moves\fP to import a
module in a Python 2 and 3 compatible fashion:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from six.moves.urllib.parse import urlencode
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
To have this working on Python 3 as well, please use the \fBsix\fP library:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
six.reraise(Exception, \(dqvalue\(dq, tb)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added to warn about using unicode raw string literals. This is
a syntax error in Python 3:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
a = ur\(aq...\(aq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new \fBdeprecated\-sys\-function\fP check, emitted when accessing removed \fBsys\fP members.
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBxreadlines\-attribute\fP check, emitted when the \fBxreadlines()\fP attribute is accessed
on a file object.
.IP \(bu 2
Added two new Python 3 porting checks, \fBexception\-escape\fP and \fBcomprehension\-escape\fP
.sp
These two are emitted whenever pylint detects that a variable defined in the
said blocks is used outside of the given block. On Python 3 these values are deleted.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
try:
  1/0
except ZeroDivisionError as exc:
   ...
print(exc) # This will raise a NameError on Python 3

[i for i in some_iterator if some_condition(i)]
print(i) # This will raise a NameError on Python 3
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdefaultdict\fP and subclasses of \fBdict\fP are now handled for \fIdict\-iter\-*\fP checks. That
means that the following code will now emit warnings for when \fBiteritems\fP and friends
are accessed:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
some_dict = defaultdict(list)
\&...
some_dict.iterkeys()
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Enum classes no longer trigger \fBtoo\-few\-methods\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Special methods now count towards \fBtoo\-few\-methods\fP,
and are considered part of the public API.
They are still not counted towards the number of methods for
\fBtoo\-many\-methods\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
docparams allows abstract methods to document returns documentation even
if the default implementation does not return something.
They also no longer need to document raising a NotImplementedError.
.UNINDENT
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.9?
.sp
Release date: 2018\-05\-15
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Added two new Python 3 porting checks, \fBexception\-escape\fP and \fBcomprehension\-escape\fP
.sp
These two are emitted whenever pylint detects that a variable defined in the
said blocks is used outside of the given block. On Python 3 these values are deleted.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new \fBdeprecated\-sys\-function\fP, emitted when accessing removed sys members.
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBxreadlines\-attribute\fP, emitted when the \fBxreadlines()\fP attribute is accessed.
.IP \(bu 2
The Python 3 porting mode can now run with Python 3 as well.
.IP \(bu 2
docparams extension allows abstract methods to document what overriding
implementations should return, and to raise NotImplementedError without
documenting it.
.sp
Closes #2044
.IP \(bu 2
Special methods do not count towards \fBtoo\-few\-methods\fP,
and are considered part of the public API.
.IP \(bu 2
Enum classes do not trigger \fBtoo\-few\-methods\fP
.sp
Closes #605
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 2/3 check for accessing \fBoperator.div\fP, which is removed in Python 3
.sp
Closes #1936
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 2/3 check for accessing removed urllib functions
.sp
Closes #1997
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 1.8
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
None so far
.UNINDENT
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBshallow\-copy\-environ\fP\&.
.sp
This warning message is emitted when shallow copy of os.environ is created.
Shallow copy of os.environ doesn\(aqt work as people may expect. os.environ
is not a dict object but rather a proxy object, so any changes made
on copy may have unexpected effects on os.environ
.sp
Instead of copy.copy(os.environ) method os.environ.copy() should be used.
.sp
See \%<https://\:bugs\:.python\:.org/\:issue15373> for details.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import copy
import os
wrong_env_copy = copy.copy(os.environ)  # will emit pylint warning
wrong_env_copy[\(aqENV_VAR\(aq] = \(aqnew_value\(aq  # changes os.environ
assert os.environ[\(aqENV_VAR\(aq] == \(aqnew_value\(aq

good_env_copy = dict(os.environ)  # the right way
good_env_copy[\(aqENV_VAR\(aq] = \(aqdifferent_value\(aq  # doesn\(aqt change os.environ
assert os.environ[\(aqENV_VAR\(aq] == \(aqnew_value\(aq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBkeyword\-arg\-before\-vararg\fP\&.
.sp
This warning message is emitted when a function is defined with a keyword
argument appearing before variable\-length positional arguments (*args).
This may lead to args list getting modified if keyword argument\(aqs value is
not provided in the function call assuming it will take default value provided
in the definition.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def foo(a, b=3, *args):
    print(a, b, args)

# Case1: a=0, b=2, args=(4,5)
foo(0,2,4,5) # 0 2 (4,5) ==> Observed values are same as expected values

# Case2: a=0, b=<default_value>, args=(4,5)
foo(0,4,5) # 0 4 (5,) ==> args list got modified as well as the observed value of b

# Case3: Syntax Error if tried as follows
foo(0,b=2,4,5) # syntax error
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBsimplify\-boolean\-expression\fP\&.
.sp
This message is emitted when \fBconsider\-using\-ternary\fP check would emit
not equivalent code, due to truthy element being falsy in boolean context.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
value = condition and False or other_value
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This flawed construct may be simplified to:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
value = other_value
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBbad\-thread\-instantiation\fP\&.
.sp
This message is emitted when the threading.Thread class does not
receive the target argument, but receives just one argument, which
is by default the group parameter.
.sp
In the following example, the instantiation will fail, which is definitely
not desired:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import threading
threading.Thread(lambda: print(1)) # Oups, this is the group parameter
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 checker was added to warn about accessing functions that have been
removed from the itertools module \fBizip\fP, \fBimap\fP, \fBiflter\fP, \fBizip_longest\fP, and \fBifilterfalse\fP\&.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from itertools import izip
print(list(izip([1, 2], [3])))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead use \fBsix.moves\fP to import a Python 2 and Python 3 compatible function:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from six.moves import zip
print(list(zip([1, 2], [3])))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 checker was added to warn about accessing deprecated fields from
the types module like \fBListType\fP or \fBIntType\fP
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from types import ListType
print(isinstance([], ListType))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead use the declarations in the builtin namespace:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
print(isinstance([], list))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 checker was added to warn about declaring a \fBnext\fP method that
would have implemented the \fBIterator\fP protocol in Python 2 but is now a normal
method in Python 3.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Foo(object):
    def next(self):
        return 42
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead implement a \fB__next__\fP method and use \fBsix.Iterator\fP as a base class
or alias \fBnext\fP to \fB__next__\fP:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Foo(object):
    def __next__(self):
        return 42
    next = __next__
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Three new Python 3 checkers were added to warn about using dictionary methods
in non\-iterating contexts.
.sp
For example, the following are returning iterators in Python 3:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
\&.. code\-block:: python
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
d = {}
d.keys()[0]
d.items()[0]
d.values() + d.keys()
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 porting check was added, \fBnon\-ascii\-bytes\-literals\fP
.sp
This message is emitted whenever we detect that a bytes string contain
non\-ASCII characters, which results in a SyntaxError on Python 3.
.IP \(bu 2
A new warning, \fBraising\-format\-tuple\fP, will catch situations where the
intent was likely raising an exception with a formatted message string,
but the actual code did omit the formatting and instead passes template
string and value parameters as separate arguments to the exception
constructor.  So it detects things like
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
raise SomeError(\(aqmessage about %s\(aq, foo)
raise SomeError(\(aqmessage about {}\(aq, foo)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
which likely were meant instead as
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
raise SomeError(\(aqmessage about %s\(aq % foo)
raise SomeError(\(aqmessage about {}\(aq.format(foo))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This warning can be ignored on projects which deliberately use lazy
formatting of messages in all user\-facing exception handlers.
.IP \(bu 2
Following the recommendations of PEP479 \%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0479> ,a new Python 3.0 checker was added to warn about raising a \fBStopIteration\fP inside
a generator. Raising a \fBStopIteration\fP inside a generator may be due a direct call
to \fBraise StopIteration\fP:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def gen_stopiter():
    yield 1
    yield 2
    yield 3
    raise StopIteration
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead use a simple \fBreturn\fP statement
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def gen_stopiter():
    yield 1
    yield 2
    yield 3
    return
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Raising a \fBStopIteration\fP may also be due to the call to \fBnext\fP function with a generator
as argument:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def gen_next_raises_stopiter():
    g = gen_ok()
    while True:
        yield next(g)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
In this case, surround the call to \fBnext\fP with a try/except block:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def gen_next_raises_stopiter():
    g = gen_ok()
    while True:
        try:
            yield next(g)
        except StopIteration:
            return
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
The check about raising a StopIteration inside a generator is also valid if the exception
raised inherit from StopIteration.
.sp
Closes #1385
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python checker was added to warn about using a \fB+\fP operator inside call of logging methods
when one of the operands is a literal string:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import logging
var = \(dq123\(dq
logging.log(logging.INFO, \(dqVar: \(dq + var)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead use formatted string and positional arguments :
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import logging
var = \(dq123\(dq
logging.log(logging.INFO, \(dqVar: %s\(dq, var)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python checker was added to warn about \fBinconsistent\-return\-statements\fP\&. A function or a method
has inconsistent return statements if it returns both explicit and implicit values :
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def mix_implicit_explicit_returns(arg):
    if arg < 10:
        return True
    elif arg < 20:
        return
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
According to PEP8 \%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0008>, if any return statement returns an expression,
any return statements where no value is returned should explicitly state this as return None,
and an explicit return statement should be present at the end of the function (if reachable).
Thus, the previous function should be written:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def mix_implicit_explicit_returns(arg):
    if arg < 10:
        return True
    elif arg < 20:
        return None
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Closes #1267
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixing u\(aq\(aq string in superfluous\-parens / C0325 \%<#\:superfluous-parens> message.
.IP \(bu 2
Configuration options of invalid name checker are significantly redesigned.
Predefined rules for common naming styles were introduced. For typical
setups, user friendly options like \fB\-\-function\-naming\-style=camelCase\fP may
be used in place of hand\-written regular expressions. Default linter config
enforce PEP8\-compatible naming style. See documentation for details.
.IP \(bu 2
Raise meaningful exception in case of invalid reporter class (output format)
being selected.
.IP \(bu 2
The docparams extension now allows a property docstring to document both
the property and the setter. Therefore setters can also have no docstring.
.IP \(bu 2
The docparams extension now understands property type syntax.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Foo(object):
    @property
    def foo(self):
        \(dq\(dq\(dqMy Sphinx style docstring description.

        :type: int
        \(dq\(dq\(dq
        return 10
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Foo(object):
    @property
    def foo(self):
        \(dq\(dq\(dqint: My Numpy and Google docstring style description.\(dq\(dq\(dq
        return 10
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
In case of \fB\-\-output\-format=json\fP, the dictionary returned holds a new key\-value pair.
The key is \fBmessage\-id\fP and the value the message id.
.IP \(bu 2
Spelling checker has a new configuration parameter \fBmax\-spelling\-suggestions\fP, which
affects maximum count of suggestions included in emitted message.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fB:ref:\(gainvalid\-name\(ga\fP check contains the name of the template that caused the failure.
.sp
For the given code, \fBpylint\fP used to emit \fBinvalid\-name\fP in the form \fBInvalid constant name var\fP,
without offering any context why \fBvar\fP is not such a good name.
.sp
With this change, it is now more clear what should be improved for a name to be accepted according to
its corresponding template.
.IP \(bu 2
New configuration flag, \fBsuggestion\-mode\fP was introduced. When enabled, pylint would
attempt to emit user\-friendly suggestions instead of spurious errors for some known
false\-positive scenarios. Flag is enabled by default.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsuperfluous\-parens\fP is no longer wrongly emitted for logical statements involving \fBin\fP operator
(see example below for what used to be false\-positive).
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
foo = None
if \(aqbar\(aq in (foo or {}):
  pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Redefinition of dummy function is now possible. \fBfunction\-redefined\fP message won\(aqt be emitted anymore when
dummy functions are redefined.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBmissing\-param\-doc\fP and \fBmissing\-type\-doc\fP are no longer emitted when
\fBArgs\fP and \fBKeyword Args\fP are mixed in Google docstring.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix of false positive \fBuseless\-super\-delegation\fP message when
parameters default values are different from those used in the base class.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix of false positive \fBuseless\-else\-on\-loop\fP message when break statements
are deeply nested inside loop.
.IP \(bu 2
The Python 3 porting checker no longer emits multiple \fBno\-absolute\-import\fP per file.
.IP \(bu 2
The Python 3 porting checker respects disabled checkers found in the config file.
.IP \(bu 2
Modules, classes, or methods consist of compound statements that exceed the \fBdocstring\-min\-length\fP
are now correctly emitting \fBmissing\-docstring\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Fix no \fBwrong\-import\-order\fP message emitted on ordering of first and third party libraries.
With this fix, pylint distinguishes first and third party modules when checking
import order.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix the ignored \fBpylint disable=fixme\fP directives for comments following
the last statement in a file.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBline\-too\-long\fP message deactivated by wrong disable directive.
The directive \fBdisable=fixme\fP doesn\(aqt deactivate anymore the emission
of \fBline\-too\-long\fP message for long commented lines.
.IP \(bu 2
If the rcfile specified on the command line doesn\(aqt exist, then an
IOError exception is raised.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix the wrong scope of \fBdisable=\fP directive after a commented line.
For example when a \fBdisable=line\-too\-long\fP directive is at the end of a
long commented line, it no longer disables the emission of \fBline\-too\-long\fP
message for lines that follow.
.UNINDENT
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.8.1?
.sp
Release date: 2017\-12\-15
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Wrong version number in __pkginfo__.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.8?
.sp
Release date: 2017\-12\-15
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Respect disable=... in config file when running with \-\-py3k.
.IP \(bu 2
New warning \fBshallow\-copy\-environ\fP added
.sp
Shallow copy of os.environ doesn\(aqt work as people may expect. os.environ
is not a dict object but rather a proxy object, so any changes made
on copy may have unexpected effects on os.environ
.sp
Instead of copy.copy(os.environ) method os.environ.copy() should be
used.
.sp
See \%<https://\:bugs\:.python\:.org/\:issue15373> for details.
.sp
Closes #1301
.IP \(bu 2
Do not display no\-absolute\-import warning multiple times per file.
.IP \(bu 2
.INDENT 2.0
.TP
.B \fBtrailing\-comma\-tuple\fP refactor check now extends to assignment with
more than one element (such as lists)
.UNINDENT
.sp
Closes #1713
.IP \(bu 2
Fixing u\(aq\(aq string in superfluous\-parens / C0325 \%<#\:superfluous-parens> message
.sp
Closes #1420
.IP \(bu 2
\fBabstract\-class\-instantiated\fP is now emitted for all inference paths.
.sp
Closes #1673
.IP \(bu 2
Add set of predefined naming style to ease configuration of checking
naming conventions.
.sp
Closes #1013
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check, \fBkeyword\-arg\-before\-vararg\fP
.sp
This is emitted for function definitions
in which keyword arguments are placed before variable
positional arguments (*args).
.sp
This may lead to args list getting modified if keyword argument\(aqs value
is not provided in the function call assuming it will take default value
provided in the definition.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBinvalid\-name\fP check contains the name of the template that caused the failure
.sp
Closes #1176
.IP \(bu 2
Using the \-j flag won\(aqt start more child linters than needed.
.sp
Closes #1614
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive with bad\-python3\-import on relative imports
.sp
Closes #1608
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 3 check, \fBnon\-ascii\-bytes\-literals\fP
.sp
Closes #1545
.IP \(bu 2
Added a couple of new Python 3 checks for accessing dict methods in non\-iterable context
.IP \(bu 2
Protocol checks (not\-a\-mapping / E1134 \%<#\:not-a-mapping>, not\-an\-iterable / E1133 \%<#\:not-an-iterable> and co.) aren\(aqt emitted on classes with dynamic getattr
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning, bad\-thread\-instantiation / W1506 \%<#\:bad-thread-instantiation>\(aq
.sp
This message is emitted when the threading.Thread class does not
receive the target argument, but receives just one argument, which
is by default the group parameter.
.sp
Closes #1327
.IP \(bu 2
In non\-quiet mode, absolute path of used config file is logged to
standard error.
.sp
Closes #1519
.IP \(bu 2
Raise meaningful exception for invalid reporter class being selected
.sp
When unknown reporter class will be selected as Pylint reporter,
meaningful error message would be raised instead of bare \fBImportError\fP
or \fBAttributeError\fP related to module or reporter class being not found.
.sp
Closes #1388
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 3 check for accessing removed functions from itertools
like \fBizip\fP or \fBifilterfalse\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 3 check for accessing removed fields from the types
module like \fBUnicodeType\fP or \fBXRangeType\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 3 check for declaring a method \fBnext\fP that would have
been treated as an iterator in Python 2 but a normal function in Python 3.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new key\-value pair in json output. The key is \fBmessage\-id\fP
and the value is the message id.
.sp
Closes #1512
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 3.0 check for raising a StopIteration inside a generator.
The check about raising a StopIteration inside a generator is also valid if the exception
raised inherit from StopIteration.
.sp
Closes #1385
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning, \fBraising\-format\-tuple\fP, to detect multi\-argument
exception construction instead of message string formatting.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new check for method of logging module that concatenate string via + operator
.sp
Closes #1479
.IP \(bu 2
Added parameter for limiting number of suggestions in spellchecking checkers
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a corner\-case in \fBconsider\-using\-ternary\fP checker.
.sp
When object \fBA\fP used in  \fBX and A or B\fP was falsy in boolean context,
Pylint incorrectly emitted non\-equivalent ternary\-based suggestion.
After a change message is correctly not emitted for this case.
.sp
Closes #1559
.IP \(bu 2
Added \fBsuggestion\-mode\fP configuration flag. When flag is enabled, informational
message is emitted instead of cryptic error message for attributes accessed on
c\-extensions.
.sp
Closes #1466
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive \fBuseless\-super\-delegation\fP message when
parameters default values are different from those used in the base class.
.sp
Closes #1085
.IP \(bu 2
Disabling wrong\-import\-order / C0411 \%<#\:wrong-import-order>\(aq, wrong\-import\-position / C0413 \%<#\:wrong-import-position>\(aq, or
ungrouped\-imports / C0412 \%<#\:ungrouped-imports>\(aq for a single line now prevents that line from
triggering violations on subsequent lines.
.sp
Closes #1336
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python check for inconsistent return statements inside method or function.
.sp
Closes #1267
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBsuperfluous\-parens\fP false positive related to handling logical statements
involving \fBin\fP operator.
.sp
Closes #574
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfunction\-redefined\fP message is no longer emitted for functions and
methods which names matches dummy variable name regular expression.
.sp
Closes #1369
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBmissing\-param\-doc\fP and \fBmissing\-type\-doc\fP false positives when
mixing \fBArgs\fP and \fBKeyword Args\fP in Google docstring.
.sp
Closes #1409
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBmissing\-docstring\fP false negatives when modules, classes, or methods
consist of compound statements that exceed the \fBdocstring\-min\-length\fP
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBuseless\-else\-on\-loop\fP false positives when break statements are
deeply nested inside loop.
.sp
Closes #1661
.IP \(bu 2
Fix no \fBwrong\-import\-order\fP message emitted on ordering of first and third party
libraries. With this fix, pylint distinguishes third and first party
modules when checking import order.
.sp
Closes #1702
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBpylint disable=fixme\fP directives ignored for comments following the
last statement in a file.
.sp
Closes #1681
.IP \(bu 2
Fix \fBline\-too\-long\fP message deactivated by wrong disable directive.
The directive \fBdisable=fixme\fP doesn\(aqt deactivate anymore the emission
of \fBline\-too\-long\fP message for long commented lines.
.sp
Closes #1741
.IP \(bu 2
If the rcfile specified on the command line doesn\(aqt exist, then an
IOError exception is raised.
.sp
Closes #1747
.IP \(bu 2
Fix the wrong scope of the \fBdisable=\fP directive after a commented line.
For example when a \fBdisable=line\-too\-long\fP directive is at the end of
a long commented line, it no longer disables the emission of \fBline\-too\-long\fP
message for lines that follow.
.sp
Closes #1742
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 1.7
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsingle\-string\-used\-for\-slots\fP check was added, which is used
whenever a class is using a single string as a slot value. While this
is technically not a problem per se, it might trip users when manipulating
the slots value as an iterable, which would in turn iterate over characters
of the slot value. In order to be more straight\-forward, always try to use
a container such as a list or a tuple for defining slot values.
.IP \(bu 2
We added a new check, \fBliteral\-comparison\fP, which is used
whenever \fBpylint\fP can detect a comparison to a literal. This is usually
not what we want and, potentially, error prone. For instance, in the given example,
the first string comparison returns true, since smaller strings are interned
by the interpreter, while for larger ones, it will return False:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
mystring = \(dqok\(dq
if mystring is \(dqok\(dq: # Returns true
   ...

mystring = \(dqa\(dq * 1000
if mystring is (\(dqa\(dq * 1000): # This will return False
   ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead of using the \fBis\fP operator, you should use the \fB==\fP operator for
this use case.
.IP \(bu 2
We added a new refactoring message, \fBconsider\-merging\-isinstance\fP, which is
emitted whenever we can detect that consecutive \fIisinstance\fP calls can be merged
together.
For instance, in this example, we can merge the first two \fIisinstance\fP calls:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# $ cat a.py
if isinstance(x, int) or isinstance(x, float):
    pass
if isinstance(x, (int, float)) or isinstance(x, str):
    pass
# $ pylint a.py
# R:  1, 0: Consider merging these isinstance calls to isinstance(x, (float, int)) (consider\-merging\-isinstance)
# R:  3, 0: Consider merging these isinstance calls to isinstance(x, (int, float, str)) (consider\-merging\-isinstance)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new error check was added, \fBinvalid\-metaclass\fP, which is used whenever \fIpylint\fP
can detect that a given class is using a metaclass which is invalid for the purpose
of the class. This usually might indicate a problem in the code, rather than
something done on purpose.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# Needs to inherit from *type* in order to be valid
class SomeClass(object):
    ...

class MyClass(metaclass=SomeClass):
    pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new warning was added, \fBuseless\-super\-delegation\fP, which is used whenever
we can detect that an overridden method is useless, relying on \fIsuper()\fP delegation
to do the same thing as another method from the MRO.
.sp
For instance, in this example, the first two methods are useless, since they
do the exact same thing as the methods from the base classes, while the next
two methods are not, since they do some extra operations with the passed
arguments.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Impl(Base):

    def __init__(self, param1, param2):
        super(Impl, self).__init__(param1, param2)

    def useless(self, first, second):
        return super(Impl, self).useless(first, second)

    def not_useless(self, first, **kwargs):
        debug = kwargs.pop(\(aqdebug\(aq, False)
        if debug:
            ...
        return super(Impl, self).not_useless(first, **kwargs)

    def not_useless_1(self, first, *args):
        return super(Impl, self).not_useless_1(first + some_value, *args)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new warning was added, \fBlen\-as\-condition\fP, which is used whenever
we detect that a condition uses \fBlen(SEQUENCE)\fP incorrectly. Instead
one could use \fBif SEQUENCE\fP or \fBif not SEQUENCE\fP\&.
.sp
For instance, all of the examples below:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if len(S):
  pass

if not len(S):
  pass

if len(S) > 0:
  pass

if len(S) != 0:
  pass

if len(S) == 0:
  pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
can be written in a more natural way:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if S:
  pass

if not S:
  pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
See \%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0008/#\:programming-recommendations>
for more information.
.IP \(bu 2
A new extension was added, \fBemptystring.py\fP which detects whenever
we detect comparisons to empty string constants. This extension is disabled
by default. For instance, the examples below:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if S != \(dq\(dq:
  pass

if S == \(aq\(aq:
  pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
can be written in a more natural way:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if S:
  pass

if not S:
  pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
An exception to this is when empty string is an allowed value whose meaning
is treated differently than \fBNone\fP\&. For example the meaning could be
user selected no additional options vs. user has not made their selection yet!
.sp
You can activate this checker by adding the line:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.emptystring
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
to the \fBMAIN\fP section of your \fB\&.pylintrc\fP or using the command:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ pylint a.py \-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.emptystring
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new extension was added, \fBcomparetozero.py\fP which detects whenever
we compare integers to zero. This extension is disabled by default.
For instance, the examples below:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if X != 0:
  pass

if X == 0:
  pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
can be written in a more natural way:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if X:
  pass

if not X:
  pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
An exception to this is when zero is an allowed value whose meaning
is treated differently than \fBNone\fP\&. For example the meaning could be
\fBNone\fP means no limit, while \fB0\fP means the limit it zero!
.sp
You can activate this checker by adding the line:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.comparetozero
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
to the \fBMAIN\fP section of your \fB\&.pylintrc\fP or using the command:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ pylint a.py \-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.comparetozero
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
We\(aqve added new error conditions for \fBbad\-super\-call\fP which now detect
the usage of \fBsuper(type(self), self)\fP and \fBsuper(self.__class__, self)\fP
patterns. These can lead to recursion loop in derived classes. The problem
is visible only if you override a class that uses these incorrect invocations
of \fBsuper()\fP\&.
.sp
For instance, \fBDerived.__init__()\fP will correctly call \fBBase.__init__\fP\&.
At this point \fBtype(self)\fP will be equal to \fBDerived\fP and the call again
goes to \fBBase.__init__\fP and we enter a recursion loop.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Base(object):
    def __init__(self, param1, param2):
        super(type(self), self).__init__(param1, param2)

class Derived(Base):
    def __init__(self, param1, param2):
        super(Derived, self).__init__(param1, param2)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
The warnings \fBmissing\-returns\-doc\fP and \fBmissing\-yields\-doc\fP have each
been replaced with two new warnings \- \fBmissing\-[return|yield]\-doc\fP and
\fBmissing\-[return|yield]\-type\-doc\fP\&. Having these as separate warnings
allows the user to choose whether their documentation style requires
text descriptions of function return/yield, specification of return/yield
types, or both.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# This will raise missing\-return\-type\-doc but not missing\-return\-doc
def my_sphinx_style_func(self):
    \(dq\(dq\(dqThis is a Sphinx\-style docstring.

    :returns: Always False
    \(dq\(dq\(dq
    return False

# This will raise missing\-return\-doc but not missing\-return\-type\-doc
def my_google_style_func(self):
    \(dq\(dq\(dqThis is a Google\-style docstring.

    Returns:
        bool:
    \(dq\(dq\(dq
    return False
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new refactoring check was added, \fBredefined\-argument\-from\-local\fP, which is
emitted when \fBpylint\fP can detect than a function argument is redefined locally
in some potential error prone cases. For instance, in the following piece of code,
we have a bug, since the check will never return \fBTrue\fP, given the fact that we
are comparing the same object to its attributes.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def test(resource):
    for resource in resources:
        # The \(ga\(gafor\(ga\(ga is reusing \(ga\(garesource\(ga\(ga, which means that the following
        # \(ga\(garesource\(ga\(ga is not what we wanted to check against.
        if resource.resource_type == resource:
           call_resource(resource)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Other places where this check looks are \fIwith\fP statement name bindings and
except handler\(aqs name binding.
.IP \(bu 2
A new refactoring check was added, \fBno\-else\-return\fP, which is
emitted when pylint encounters an else following a chain of ifs,
all of them containing a return statement.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def foo1(x, y, z):
    if x:
        return y
    else:  # This is unnecessary here.
        return z
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
We could fix it deleting the \fBelse\fP statement.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def foo1(x, y, z):
    if x:
        return y
    return z
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 check was added, \fBeq\-without\-hash\fP, which enforces classes that implement
\fB__eq__\fP \fIalso\fP implement \fB__hash__\fP\&.  The behavior around classes which implement \fB__eq__\fP
but not \fB__hash__\fP changed in Python 3; in Python 2 such classes would get \fBobject.__hash__\fP
as their default implementation.  In Python 3, aforementioned classes get \fBNone\fP as their
implementation thus making them unhashable.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class JustEq(object):
   def __init__(self, x):
     self.x = x

   def __eq__(self, other):
     return self.x == other.x

class Neither(object):
  def __init__(self, x):
    self.x = x

class HashAndEq(object):
   def __init__(self, x):
     self.x = x

   def __eq__(self, other):
     return self.x == other.x

   def __hash__(self):
     return hash(self.x)

{Neither(1), Neither(2)}  # OK in Python 2 and Python 3
{HashAndEq(1), HashAndEq(2)}  # OK in Python 2 and Python 3
{JustEq(1), JustEq(2)}  # Works in Python 2, throws in Python 3
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
In general, this is a poor practice which motivated the behavior change.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
as_set = {JustEq(1), JustEq(2)}
print(JustEq(1) in as_set)  # prints False
print(JustEq(1) in list(as_set))  # prints True
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
In order to fix this error and avoid behavior differences between Python 2 and Python 3, classes
should either explicitly set \fB__hash__\fP to \fBNone\fP or implement a hashing function.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class JustEq(object):
   def __init__(self, x):
     self.x = x

   def __eq__(self, other):
     return self.x == other.x

   __hash__ = None

{JustEq(1), JustEq(2)}  # Now throws an exception in both Python 2 and Python 3.
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
3 new Python 3 checkers were added, \fBdiv\-method\fP, \fBidiv\-method\fP and \fBrdiv\-method\fP\&.
The magic methods \fB__div__\fP and \fB__idiv__\fP have been phased out in Python 3 in favor
of \fB__truediv__\fP\&.  Classes implementing \fB__div__\fP that still need to be used from Python
2 code not using \fBfrom __future__ import division\fP should implement \fB__truediv__\fP and
alias \fB__div__\fP to that implementation.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from __future__ import division

class DivisibleThing(object):
   def __init__(self, x):
     self.x = x

   def __truediv__(self, other):
     return DivisibleThing(self.x / other.x)

   __div__ = __truediv__
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 checker was added to warn about accessing the \fBmessage\fP attribute on
Exceptions.  The message attribute was deprecated in Python 2.7 and was removed in Python 3.
See \%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0352/#\:retracted-ideas> for more information.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
try:
  raise Exception(\(dqOh No!!\(dq)
except Exception as e:
  print(e.message)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead of relying on the \fBmessage\fP attribute, you should explicitly cast the exception to a
string:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
try:
  raise Exception(\(dqOh No!!\(dq)
except Exception as e:
  print(str(e))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 checker was added to warn about using \fBencode\fP or \fBdecode\fP on strings
with non\-text codecs.  This check also checks calls to \fBopen\fP with the keyword argument
\fBencoding\fP\&.  See \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:whatsnew/\:3\:.4\:.html#\:improvements-to-codec-handling>
for more information.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
\(aqhello world\(aq.encode(\(aqhex\(aq)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead of using the \fBencode\fP method for non\-text codecs use the \fBcodecs\fP module.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import codecs
codecs.encode(\(aqhello world\(aq, \(aqhex\(aq)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new warning was added, \fBoverlapping\-except\fP, which is emitted
when an except handler treats two exceptions which are \fIoverlapping\fP\&.
This means that one exception is an ancestor of the other one or it is
just an alias.
.sp
For example, in Python 3.3+, IOError is an alias for OSError. In addition, socket.error is
an alias for OSError. The intention is to find cases like the following:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import socket
try:
    pass
except (ConnectionError, IOError, OSError, socket.error):
    pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 checker was added to warn about accessing \fBsys.maxint\fP\&.  This attribute was
removed in Python 3 in favor of \fBsys.maxsize\fP\&.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import sys
print(sys.maxint)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead of using \fBsys.maxint\fP, use \fBsys.maxsize\fP
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import sys
print(sys.maxsize)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 checker was added to warn about importing modules that have either moved or been
removed from the standard library.
.sp
One of the major undertakings with Python 3 was a reorganization of the standard library to
remove old or supplanted modules and reorganize some of the existing modules.  As a result,
roughly 100 modules that exist in Python 2 no longer exist in Python 3.  See
\%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-3108> and \%<https://\:peps\:.python\:.org/\:pep-0004> for more
information.  There were suggestions on how to handle this, at
pythonhosted.org/six/#module\-six.moves (dead link) or python3porting.com/stdlib.html (dead link).
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from cStringIO import StringIO
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead of directly importing the deprecated module, either use \fBsix.moves\fP or a conditional
import.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from six.moves import cStringIO as StringIO

if sys.version_info[0] >= 3:
    from io import StringIO
else:
    from cStringIO import StringIO
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This checker will assume any imports that happen within a conditional or a \fBtry/except\fP block
are valid.
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 checker was added to warn about accessing deprecated functions on the string
module.  Python 3 removed functions that were duplicated from the builtin \fBstr\fP class.  See
\%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:2/\:library/\:string\:.html#\:deprecated-string-functions> for more information.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import string
print(string.upper(\(aqhello world!\(aq))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Instead of using \fBstring.upper\fP, call the \fBupper\fP method directly on the string object.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
\(dqhello world!\(dq.upper()
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new Python 3 checker was added to warn about calling \fBstr.translate\fP with the removed
\fBdeletechars\fP parameter.  \fBstr.translate\fP is frequently used as a way to remove characters
from a string.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
\(aqhello world\(aq.translate(None, \(aqlow\(aq)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Unfortunately, there is not an idiomatic way of writing this call in a 2and3 compatible way.  If
this code is not in the critical path for your application and the use of \fBtranslate\fP was a
premature optimization, consider using \fBre.sub\fP instead:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
import re
chars_to_remove = re.compile(\(aq[low]\(aq)
chars_to_remove.sub(\(aq\(aq, \(aqhello world\(aq)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
If this code is in your critical path and must be as fast as possible, consider declaring a
helper method that varies based upon Python version.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
if six.PY3:
    def _remove_characters(text, deletechars):
        return text.translate({ord(x): None for x in deletechars})
else:
    def _remove_characters(text, deletechars):
        return text.translate(None, deletechars)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new refactoring check was added, \fBconsider\-using\-ternary\fP, which is
emitted when pylint encounters constructs which were used to emulate
ternary statement before it was introduced in Python 2.5.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
value = condition and truth_value or false_value
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Warning can be fixed by using standard ternary construct:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
value = truth_value if condition else false_value
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new refactoring check was added, \fBtrailing\-comma\-tuple\fP, which is emitted
when pylint finds an one\-element tuple, created by a stray comma. This can
suggest a potential problem in the code and it is recommended to use parentheses
in order to emphasise the creation of a tuple, rather than relying on the comma
itself.
.sp
The warning is emitted for such a construct:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
a = 1,
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The warning can be fixed by adding parentheses:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
a = (1, )
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Two new check were added for detecting an unsupported operation
over an instance, \fBunsupported\-assignment\-operation\fP and \fBunsupported\-delete\-operation\fP\&.
The first one is emitted whenever an object does not support item assignment, while
the second is emitted when an object does not support item deletion:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class A:
    pass
instance = A()
instance[4] = 4 # unsupported\-assignment\-operation
del instance[4] # unsupported\-delete\-operation
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBrelative\-beyond\-top\-level\fP, which is emitted
when a relative import tries to access too many levels in the current package.
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBtrailing\-newlines\fP, which is emitted when a file
has trailing new lines.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-length\-returned\fP check was added, which is emitted when a \fB__len__\fP
implementation does not return a non\-negative integer.
.IP \(bu 2
There is a new extension, \fBpylint.extensions.mccabe\fP, which can be used for
computing the McCabe complexity of classes and functions.
.sp
You can enable this extension through \fB\-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.mccabe\fP
.IP \(bu 2
A new check was added, \fBused\-prior\-global\-declaration\fP\&. This is emitted when
a name is used prior a global declaration, resulting in a SyntaxError in Python 3.6.
.IP \(bu 2
A new message was added, \fBassign\-to\-new\-keyword\fP\&. This is emitted when used name
is known to become a keyword in future Python release. Assignments to keywords
would result in \fBSyntaxError\fP after switching to newer interpreter version.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
# While it\(aqs correct in Python 2.x, it raises a SyntaxError in Python 3.x
True = 1
False = 0

# Same as above, but it\(aqll be a SyntaxError starting from Python 3.7
async = \(dqasync\(dq
await = \(dqawait\(dq
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
We don\(aqt emit by default \fBno\-member\fP if we have opaque inference objects in the inference results
.sp
This is controlled through the new flag \fB\-\-ignore\-on\-opaque\-inference\fP, which is by
default True. The inference can return  multiple potential results while
evaluating a Python object, but some branches might not be evaluated, which
results in partial inference. In that case, it might be useful to still emit
no\-member / E1101 \%<#\:no-member> and other checks for the rest of the inferred objects.
.IP \(bu 2
Namespace packages are now supported by pylint. This includes both explicit namespace
packages and implicit namespace packages, supported in Python 3 through PEP 420.
.IP \(bu 2
A new option was added, \fB\-\-analyse\-fallback\-block\fP\&.
.sp
This can be used to support both Python 2 and 3 compatible import block code,
which means that the import block might have code that exists only in one or another
interpreter, leading to false positives when analysed. By default, this is false, you
can enable the analysis for both branches using this flag.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBignored\-argument\-names\fP option is now used for ignoring arguments
for unused\-variable / W0612 \%<#\:unused-variable> check.
.sp
This option was used for ignoring arguments when computing the correct number of arguments
a function should have, but for handling the arguments with regard
to unused\-variable / W0612 \%<#\:unused-variable> check, dummy\-variables\-rgx was used instead. Now, ignored\-argument\-names
is used for its original purpose and also for ignoring the matched arguments for
the unused\-variable / W0612 \%<#\:unused-variable> check. This offers a better control of what should be ignored
and how.
Also, the same option was moved from the design checker to the variables checker,
which means that the option now appears under the \fB[VARIABLES]\fP section inside
the configuration file.
.IP \(bu 2
A new option was added, \fBredefining\-builtins\-modules\fP, for controlling the modules
which can redefine builtins, such as six.moves and future.builtins.
.IP \(bu 2
A new option was added, \fBignore\-patterns\fP, which is used for building a
ignore list of directories and files matching the regex patterns, similar to the
\fBignore\fP option.
.IP \(bu 2
The reports are now disabled by default, as well as the information category
warnings.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBarguments\-differ\fP check was rewritten to take in consideration
keyword only parameters and variadics.
.sp
Now it also complains about losing or adding capabilities to a method,
by introducing positional or keyword variadics. For instance, \fIpylint\fP
now complains about these cases:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Parent(object):

    def foo(self, first, second):
        ...

    def bar(self, **kwargs):
        ...

    def baz(self, *, first):
        ...

class Child(Parent):

    # Why subclassing in the first place?
    def foo(self, *args, **kwargs):
        # mutate args or kwargs.
        super(Child, self).foo(*args, **kwargs)

    def bar(self, first=None, second=None, **kwargs):
        ...
        # The overridden method adds two new parameters,
        # which can also be passed as positional arguments,
        # breaking the contract of the parent\(aqs method.

    def baz(self, first):
        ...
        # Not keyword\-only
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
\fBredefined\-outer\-name\fP is now also emitted when a
nested loop\(aqs target variable is the same as an outer loop.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
for i, j in [(1, 2), (3, 4)]:
    for j in range(i):
        print(j)
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
relax character limit for method and function names that starts with \fB_\fP\&.
This will let people to use longer descriptive names for methods and
functions with a shorter scope (considered as private). The same idea
applies to variable names, only with an inverse rule: you want long
descriptive names for variables with bigger scope, like globals.
.IP \(bu 2
Add \fBInvalidMessageError\fP exception class and replace \fBassert\fP in
pylint.utils with \fBraise InvalidMessageError\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBUnknownMessageError\fP (formerly \fBUnknownMessage\fP) and
\fBEmptyReportError\fP (formerly \fBEmptyReport\fP) are now provided by the new
\fBpylint.exceptions\fP submodule instead of \fBpylint.utils\fP as before.
.IP \(bu 2
We now support inline comments for comma separated values in the configurations
.sp
For instance, you can now use the \fB#\fP sign for having comments inside
comma separated values, as seen below:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
disable=no\-member, # Don\(aqt care about it for now
        bad\-indentation, # No need for this
        import\-error
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Of course, interweaving comments with values is also working:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
disable=no\-member,
        # Don\(aqt care about it for now
        bad\-indentation # No need for this
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
This works by setting the inline comment prefixes \%<https://\:docs\:.python\:.org/\:3/\:library/\:configparser\:.html#\:customizing-parser-behaviour> accordingly.
.IP \(bu 2
Added epytext docstring support to the docparams extension.
.IP \(bu 2
We added support for providing hints when not finding a missing member.
.sp
For example, given the following code, it should be obvious that
the programmer intended to use the \fBmail\fP attribute, rather than
\fBemail\fP\&.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Contribution:
    def __init__(self, name, email, date):
        self.name = name
        self.mail = mail
        self.date = date

for c in contributions:
    print(c.email) # Oups
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
\fBpylint\fP will now warn that there is a chance of having a typo,
suggesting new names that could be used instead.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ pylint a.py
E: 8,10: Instance of \(aqContribution\(aq has no \(aqemail\(aq member; maybe \(aqmail\(aq?
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The behaviour is controlled through the \fB\-\-missing\-member\-hint\fP option.
Other options that come with this change are \fB\-\-missing\-member\-max\-choices\fP
for choosing the total number of choices that should be picked in this
situation and \fB\-\-missing\-member\-hint\-distance\fP, which specifies a metric
for computing the distance between the names (this is based on Levenshtein
distance, which means the lower the number, the more pickier the algorithm
will be).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPyLinter.should_analyze_file\fP has a new parameter, \fBis_argument\fP,
which specifies if the given path is a \fBpylint\fP argument or not.
.sp
\fBshould_analyze_file\fP is called whenever \fBpylint\fP tries to determine
if a file should be analyzed, defaulting to files with the \fB\&.py\fP
extension, but this function gets called only in the case where the said
file is not passed as a command line argument to \fBpylint\fP\&. This usually
means that pylint will analyze a file, even if that file has a different
extension, as long as the file was explicitly passed at command line.
Since \fBshould_analyze_file\fP cannot be overridden to handle all the cases,
the check for the provenience of files was moved into \fBshould_analyze_file\fP\&.
This means we now can write something similar with this example, for ignoring
every file respecting the desired property, disregarding the provenience of the
file, being it a file passed as CLI argument or part of a package.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from pylint.lint import Run, PyLinter

class CustomPyLinter(PyLinter):

     def should_analyze_file(self, modname, path, is_argument=False):
         if respect_condition(path):
             return False
         return super().should_analyze_file(modname, path, is_argument=is_argument)


class CustomRun(Run):
     LinterClass = CustomPyLinter

CustomRun(sys.argv[1:])
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Imports aliased with underscore are skipped when checking for unused imports.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbad\-builtin\fP and \fBredefined\-variable\-type\fP are now extensions,
being disabled by default. They can be enabled through:
\fB\-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.redefined_variable_type,pylint.extensions.bad_builtin\fP
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
Imports checker supports new switch \fBallow\-wildcard\-with\-all\fP which disables
warning on wildcard import when imported module defines \fB__all__\fP variable.
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdiffering\-param\-doc\fP is now used for the differing part of the old \fBmissing\-param\-doc\fP,
and \fBdiffering\-type\-doc\fP for the differing part of the old \fBmissing\-type\-doc\fP\&.
.UNINDENT
.SS Bug fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive of \fBredundant\-returns\-doc\fP, occurred when the documented
function was using \fIyield\fP instead of \fIreturn\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive of \fBmissing\-param\-doc\fP and \fBmissing\-type\-doc\fP,
occurred when a class docstring uses the \fBFor the parameters, see\fP
magic string but the class \fB__init__\fP docstring does not, or vice versa.
.IP \(bu 2
Added proper exception type inference for \fBmissing\-raises\-doc\fP\&. Now:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
def my_func():
    \(dq\(dq\(dq\(dqMy function.\(dq\(dq\(dq
    ex = ValueError(\(aqfoo\(aq)
    raise ex
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
will properly be flagged for missing documentation of
\fB:raises ValueError:\fP instead of \fB:raises ex:\fP, among other scenarios.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positives of \fBmissing\-[raises|params|type]\-doc\fP due to not
recognizing valid keyword synonyms supported by Sphinx.
.IP \(bu 2
More thorough validation in \fBMessagesStore.register_messages()\fP to detect
conflicts between a new message and any existing message id, symbol,
or \fBold_names\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
We now support having plugins that shares the same name and with each one
providing options.
.sp
A plugin can be logically split into multiple classes, each class providing
certain capabilities, all of them being tied under the same name. But when
two or more such classes are also adding options, then \fBpylint\fP crashed,
since it already added the first encountered section. Now, these should
work as expected.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from pylint.checkers import BaseChecker


class DummyPlugin1(BaseChecker):
    name = \(aqdummy_plugin\(aq
    msgs = {\(aqI9061\(aq: (\(aqDummy short desc 01\(aq, \(aqdummy\-message\-01\(aq, \(aqDummy long desc\(aq)}
    options = (
        (\(aqdummy_option_1\(aq, {
            \(aqtype\(aq: \(aqstring\(aq,
            \(aqmetavar\(aq: \(aq<string>\(aq,
            \(aqhelp\(aq: \(aqDummy option 1\(aq,
        }),
    )


class DummyPlugin2(BaseChecker):
    name = \(aqdummy_plugin\(aq
    msgs = {\(aqI9060\(aq: (\(aqDummy short desc 02\(aq, \(aqdummy\-message\-02\(aq, \(aqDummy long desc\(aq)}
    options = (
        (\(aqdummy_option_2\(aq, {
            \(aqtype\(aq: \(aqstring\(aq,
            \(aqmetavar\(aq: \(aq<string>\(aq,
            \(aqhelp\(aq: \(aqDummy option 2\(aq,
        }),
    )


def register(linter):
    linter.register_checker(DummyPlugin1(linter))
    linter.register_checker(DummyPlugin2(linter))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
We do not yield \fBunused\-argument\fP for singledispatch implementations and
do not warn about \fBfunction\-redefined\fP for multiple implementations with same name.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from functools import singledispatch

@singledispatch
def f(x):
    return 2*x

@f.register(str)
def _(x):
    return \-1

@f.register(int)
@f.register(float)
def _(x):
    return \-x
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
\fBunused\-variable\fP checker has new functionality of warning about unused
variables in global module namespace. Since globals in module namespace
may be a part of exposed API, this check is disabled by default. For
enabling it, set \fBallow\-global\-unused\-variables\fP option to false.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false\-positive \fBlogging\-format\-interpolation\fP message, when format
specifications are used in formatted string. In general, these operations
are not always convertible to old\-style formatting used by logging module.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new switch \fBsingle\-line\-class\-stmt\fP to allow single\-line declaration
of empty class bodies (as seen in the example below). Pylint won\(aqt emit a
\fBmultiple\-statements\fP message when this option is enabled.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class MyError(Exception): pass
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 2.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtoo\-many\-format\-args\fP and \fBtoo\-few\-format\-args\fP are emitted correctly
(or not emitted at all, when exact count of elements in RHS cannot be
inferred) when starred expressions are used in RHS tuple. For example,
code block as shown below detects correctly that the used tuple has in
fact three elements, not two.
.UNINDENT
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
meat = [\(aqspam\(aq, \(aqham\(aq]
print(\(aq%s%s%s\(aq % (\(aqeggs\(aq, *meat))
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcyclic\-import\fP checker supports local disable clauses. When one
of cycle imports was done in scope where disable clause was active,
cycle is not reported as violation.
.UNINDENT
.SS Removed Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBpylint\-gui\fP was removed, because it was deemed unfit for being included
in \fIpylint\fP\&. It had a couple of bugs and misfeatures, its usability was subpar
and since its development was neglected, we decided it is best to move on without it.
.IP \(bu 2
The HTML reporter was removed, including the \fB\-\-output\-format=html\fP option.
It was lately a second class citizen in Pylint, being mostly neglected.
Since we now have the JSON reporter, it can be used as a basis for building
more prettier HTML reports than what Pylint can currently generate. This is
part of the effort of removing cruft from Pylint, by removing less used
features.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fB\-\-files\-output\fP option was removed. While the same functionality cannot
be easily replicated, the JSON reporter, for instance, can be used as a basis
for generating the messages per each file.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-required\-attributes\fP option was removed.
.IP \(bu 2
\fB\-\-ignore\-iface\-methods\fP option was removed.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fB\-\-optimize\-ast\fP flag was removed.
.sp
The option was initially added for handling pathological cases,
such as joining too many strings using the addition operator, which
was leading pylint to have a recursion error when trying to figure
out what the string was. Unfortunately, we decided to ignore the
issue, since the pathological case would have happen when the
code was parsed by Python as well, without actually reaching the
runtime step and as such, we decided to remove the error altogether.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBepylint.py_run\fP\(aqs \fIscript\fP parameter was removed.
.sp
Now \fBepylint.py_run\fP is always using the underlying \fBepylint.lint\fP
method from the current interpreter. This avoids some issues when multiple
instances of \fBpylint\fP are installed, which means that \fBepylint.py_run\fP
might have ran a different \fBepylint\fP script than what was intended.
.UNINDENT
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.7.1?
.sp
Release date: 2017\-04\-17
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive which occurred when an exception was reraised
.sp
Closes #1419
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive of \fBdisallow\-trailing\-tuple\fP
.sp
The check was improved by verifying for non\-terminating newlines, which
should exempt function calls and function definitions from the check
.sp
Closes #1424
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.7?
.sp
Release date: 2017\-04\-13
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit missing\-final\-newline / C0304 \%<#\:missing-final-newline> or trailing\-whitespace / C0303 \%<#\:trailing-whitespace> for formfeeds (page breaks).
.sp
Closes #1218 and #1219
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit by default no\-member / E1101 \%<#\:no-member> if we have opaque inference objects in the inference results
.sp
This is controlled through the new flag ignore\-on\-opaque\-inference, which is by
default True. The inference can return  multiple potential results while
evaluating a Python object, but some branches might not be evaluated, which
results in partial inference. In that case, it might be useful to still emit
no\-member / E1101 \%<#\:no-member> and other checks for the rest of the inferred objects.
.IP \(bu 2
Added new message \fBassign\-to\-new\-keyword\fP to warn about assigning to names which
will become a keyword in future Python releases.
.sp
Closes #1351
.IP \(bu 2
Split the \(aqmissing or differing\(aq in parameter documentation in different error.
differing\-param\-doc / W9017 \%<#\:differing-param-doc> covers the differing part of the old missing\-param\-doc / W9015 \%<#\:missing-param-doc>\(aq,
and differing\-type\-doc / W9018 \%<#\:differing-type-doc>\(aq covers the differing part of the old missing\-type\-doc / W9016 \%<#\:missing-type-doc>\(aq
.sp
Closes #1342
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new error, used\-prior\-global\-declaration / E0118 \%<#\:used-prior-global-declaration>\(aq, which is emitted when a name
is used prior a global declaration in a function. This causes a SyntaxError in
Python 3.6
.sp
Closes #1257
.IP \(bu 2
The protocol checks are emitting their messages when a special method is set to None.
.sp
Closes #1263
.IP \(bu 2
Properly detect if imported name is assigned to same name in different
scope.
.sp
Closes #636, #848, #851, and #900
.IP \(bu 2
Require one space for annotations with type hints, as per PEP 8.
.IP \(bu 2
trailing\-comma\-tuple / R1707 \%<#\:trailing-comma-tuple>\(aq check was added
.sp
This message is emitted when pylint finds an one\-element tuple,
created by a stray comma. This can suggest a potential problem in the
code and it is recommended to use parentheses in order to emphasise the
creation of a tuple, rather than relying on the comma itself.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit not\-callable / E1102 \%<#\:not-callable> for instances with unknown bases.
.sp
Closes #1213
.IP \(bu 2
Treat keyword only arguments the same as positional arguments with regard to unused\-argument / W0613 \%<#\:unused-argument> check
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt try to access variables defined in a separate scope when checking for \fBprotected\-access\fP
.IP \(bu 2
Added new check to detect incorrect usage of len(SEQUENCE) inside
test conditions.
.IP \(bu 2
Added new extension to detect comparisons against empty string constants
.IP \(bu 2
Added new extension to detect comparisons of integers against zero
.IP \(bu 2
Added new error conditions for bad\-super\-call / E1003 \%<#\:bad-super-call>\(aq
.sp
Now detects \fBsuper(type(self), self)\fP and \fBsuper(self.__class__, self)\fP
which can lead to recursion loop in derived classes.
.IP \(bu 2
PyLinter.should_analyze_file has a new optional parameter, called \fBis_argument\fP
.sp
Closes #1079
.IP \(bu 2
Add attribute hints for missing members
.sp
Closes #1035
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, redefined\-argument\-from\-local / R1704 \%<#\:redefined-argument-from-local>\(aq
.sp
Closes #649
.IP \(bu 2
Support inline comments for comma separated values in the config file
.sp
Closes #1024
.IP \(bu 2
epylint.py_run\(aqs \fIscript\fP parameter was removed.
.IP \(bu 2
epylint.py_run now uses \fBshell=False\fP for running the underlying process.
.sp
Closes #441
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning, useless\-super\-delegation / W0235 \%<#\:useless-super-delegation>\(aq
.sp
Close 839.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new error, invalid\-metaclass / E1139 \%<#\:invalid-metaclass>\(aq, raised when
we can detect that a class is using an improper metaclass.
.sp
Closes #579
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new refactoring message, literal\-comparison / R0123 \%<#\:literal-comparison>\(aq.
.sp
Closes #786
.IP \(bu 2
arguments\-differ / W0221 \%<#\:arguments-differ> takes in consideration kwonlyargs and variadics
.sp
Closes #983
.IP \(bu 2
Removed \-\-optimized\-ast
.sp
Fixes part of #975
.IP \(bu 2
Removed \-\-files\-output option
.sp
Fixes part of #975
.IP \(bu 2
Removed pylint\-gui from the package.
.IP \(bu 2
Removed the HTML reporter
.sp
Fixes part of #975
.IP \(bu 2
ignored\-argument\-names is now used for ignoring arguments for unused\-variable / W0612 \%<#\:unused-variable> check.
.sp
This option was used for ignoring arguments when computing the correct number of arguments
a function should have, but for handling the arguments with regard
to unused\-variable / W0612 \%<#\:unused-variable> check, dummy\-variables\-rgx was used instead. Now, ignored\-argument\-names
is used for its original purpose and also for ignoring the matched arguments for
the unused\-variable / W0612 \%<#\:unused-variable> check. This offers a better control of what should be ignored
and how.
Also, the same option was moved from the design checker to the variables checker,
which means that the option now appears under the \fB[VARIABLES]\fP section inside
the configuration file.
.sp
Closes #862.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for keyword variadics with regard to keyword only arguments.
.sp
If a keyword only argument was necessary for a function, but that function was called
with keyword variadics (**kwargs), then we were emitting a missing\-kwoa / E1125 \%<#\:missing-kwoa> false positive,
which is now fixed.
.sp
Closes #934.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix some false positives with unknown sized variadics.
.sp
Closes #878
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new extension, check_docstring, for checking PEP 257 conventions.
.sp
Closes #868.
.IP \(bu 2
config files with BOM markers can now be read.
.sp
Closes #864.
.IP \(bu 2
epylint.py_run does not crash on big files, using .communicate() instead of .wait()
.sp
Closes #599
.IP \(bu 2
Disable reports by default and show the evaluation score by default
.sp
The reports were disabled by default in order to simplify the interaction
between the tool and the users. The score is still shown by default, as
a way of closely measuring when it increases or decreases due to changes
brought to the code.
.sp
Refs #746
.IP \(bu 2
Disable the information category messages by default. This is a step towards
making pylint more sane.
.sp
Refs #746.
.IP \(bu 2
Catch more cases as not proper iterables for __slots__ with
regard to invalid\-slots / E0238 \%<#\:invalid-slots> pattern.
.sp
Closes #775
.IP \(bu 2
empty indent strings are rejected.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new error, relative\-beyond\-top\-level / E0402 \%<#\:relative-beyond-top-level>\(aq, which is emitted
when a relative import was attempted beyond the top level package.
.sp
Closes #588
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning, unsupported\-assignment\-operation / E1137 \%<#\:unsupported-assignment-operation>\(aq, which is
emitted when item assignment is tried on an object which doesn\(aqt
have this ability.
.sp
Closes #591
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning, unsupported\-delete\-operation / E1138 \%<#\:unsupported-delete-operation>\(aq, which is
emitted when item deletion is tried on an object which doesn\(aqt
have this ability.
.sp
Closes #592
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive of redundant\-returns\-doc / W9008 \%<#\:redundant-returns-doc>\(aq, occurred when the documented
function was using \fIyield\fP instead of \fIreturn\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #984.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix false positives of \(aqmissing\-[raises|params|type]\-doc\(aq due to not
recognizing keyword synonyms supported by Sphinx.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new refactoring message, consider\-merging\-isinstance / R1701 \%<#\:consider-merging-isinstance>\(aq, which is
emitted whenever we can detect that consecutive isinstance calls can be
merged together.
.sp
Closes #968
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive of missing\-param\-doc / W9015 \%<#\:missing-param-doc>\(aq and missing\-type\-doc / W9016 \%<#\:missing-type-doc>\(aq,
occurred when a class docstring uses the \(aqFor the parameters, see\(aq
magic string but the class __init__ docstring does not, or vice versa.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBredefined\-outer\-name\fP is now also emitted when a nested loop\(aqs target
variable is the same as a target variable in an outer loop.
.sp
Closes #911.
.IP \(bu 2
Added proper exception type inference for missing\-raises\-doc / W9006 \%<#\:missing-raises-doc>\(aq.
.IP \(bu 2
Added InvalidMessageError exception class to replace asserts in
pylint.utils.
.IP \(bu 2
More thorough validation in MessagesStore.register_messages() to avoid
one message accidentally overwriting another.
.IP \(bu 2
InvalidMessageError, UnknownMessage, and EmptyReport exceptions are
moved to the new pylint.exceptions submodule.
.IP \(bu 2
UnknownMessage and EmptyReport are renamed to UnknownMessageError and
EmptyReportError.
.IP \(bu 2
Warnings \(aqmissing\-returns\-type\-doc\(aq and \(aqmissing\-yields\-type\-doc\(aq
have each been split into two warnings \- \(aqmissing\-[return|yield]\-doc\(aq
and \(aqmissing\-[return|yield]\-type\-doc\(aq.
.IP \(bu 2
Added epytext support to docparams extension.
.sp
Closes #1029
.IP \(bu 2
Support having plugins with the same name and with options defined
.sp
Closes #1018
.IP \(bu 2
Sort configuration options in a section
.sp
Closes #1087
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 3 warning around implementing \(aq__div__\(aq, \(aq__idiv__\(aq, or
\(aq__rdiv__\(aq as those methods are phased out in Python 3.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning, overlapping\-except / W0714 \%<#\:overlapping-except>\(aq, which is
emitted when two exceptions in the same except\-clause are aliases
for each other or one exceptions is an ancestor of another.
.IP \(bu 2
Avoid crashing on ill\-formatted strings when checking for string formatting errors.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 3 warning for calling \(aqstr.encode\(aq or \(aqstr.decode\(aq with a non\-text
encoding.
.IP \(bu 2
Added new coding convention message, single\-string\-used\-for\-slots / C0205 \%<#\:single-string-used-for-slots>\(aq.
.sp
Closes #1166
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 3 check for accessing \(aqsys.maxint\(aq which was removed in Python 3 in favor
of \(aqsys.maxsize\(aq
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 3 check for bad imports.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new Python 3 check for accessing deprecated string functions.
.IP \(bu 2
Do not warn about unused arguments or function being redefined in singledispatch
registered implementations.
.sp
Closes #1032 and #1034
.IP \(bu 2
Added refactoring message no\-else\-return / R1705 \%<#\:no-else-return>\(aq.
.IP \(bu 2
Improve unused\-variable / W0612 \%<#\:unused-variable> checker to warn about unused variables in module scope.
.sp
Closes #919
.IP \(bu 2
Ignore modules import as _ when checking for unused imports.
.sp
Closes #1190
.IP \(bu 2
Improve handing of Python 3 classes with metaclasses declared in nested scopes.
.sp
Closes #1177
.IP \(bu 2
Added refactoring message consider\-using\-ternary / R1706 \%<#\:consider-using-ternary>\(aq.
.sp
Closes #1204
.IP \(bu 2
Bug\-fix for false\-positive logging\-format\-interpolation\(ga when format specifications
are used in formatted string.
.sp
Closes #572
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new switch \fBsingle\-line\-class\-stmt\fP to allow single\-line declaration
of empty class bodies.
.sp
Closes #738
.IP \(bu 2
Protected access in form \fBtype(self)._attribute\fP are now allowed.
.sp
Closes #1031
.IP \(bu 2
Let the user modify msg\-template when Pylint is called from a Python script
.sp
Closes #1269
.IP \(bu 2
Imports checker supports new switch \fBallow\-wildcard\-with\-all\fP which disables
warning on wildcard import when imported module defines \fB__all__\fP variable.
.sp
Closes #831
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtoo\-many\-format\-args\fP and \fBtoo\-few\-format\-args\fP are emitted correctly when
starred expression are used in RHS tuple.
.sp
Closes #957
.IP \(bu 2
\fBcyclic\-import\fP checker supports local disable clauses. When one
of cycle imports was done in scope where disable clause was active,
cycle is not reported as violation.
.sp
Closes #59
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 1.6
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
From pylint 1.6.0 to 2.14.0, on top of the full changelog there was also a summary
of (mostly user facing) changes.
.sp
Ticket numbers can be internal to logilab or come from bitbucket.
.SS Summary \-\- Release highlights
.sp
Nothing major.
.SS New checkers
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
We added a new recommendation check, \fBconsider\-iterating\-dictionary\fP,
which is emitted when a dictionary is iterated by using \fB\&.keys()\fP\&.
.sp
For instance, the following code would trigger this warning, since
the dictionary\(aqs keys can be iterated without calling the method explicitly.
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
for key in dictionary.keys():
    ...

# Can be refactored to:
for key in dictionary:
    ...
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtrailing\-newlines\fP check was added, which is emitted when a file has trailing newlines.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBinvalid\-length\-returned\fP check was added, which is emitted when the \fB__len__\fP
special method returns something else than a non\-negative number. For instance, this
example is triggering it:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
class Container(object):
    def __len__(self):
        return self._items # Oups, forgot to call len() over it.
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new check to the \fIcheck_docs\fP extension for looking for duplicate
constructor parameters in a class constructor docstring or in a class docstring.
.sp
The check \fBmultiple\-constructor\-doc\fP is emitted when the parameter is documented
in both places.
.IP \(bu 2
We added a new extension plugin, \fBpylint.extensions.mccabe\fP, which can be used
for warning about the complexity in the code.
.sp
You can enable it as in:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ pylint module_or_project \-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.mccabe
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
See more at Design checker \%<#\:pylint-extensions-mccabe>
.UNINDENT
.SS New features
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgenerated\-members\fP now supports qualified names through regular expressions.
.sp
For instance, for ignoring all the errors generated by \fBnumpy.core\fP\(aqs attributes, we can
now use:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ pylint a.py \-\-generated\-members=numpy.*
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
Add the ability to ignore files based on regex matching, with the new \fB\-\-ignore\-patterns\fP option.
.sp
Rather than clobber the existing \fBignore\fP option, we decided to have a separate
option for it. For instance, for ignoring all the test files, we can now use:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ pylint myproject \-\-ignore\-patterns=test.*?py
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
We added a new option, \fBredefining\-builtins\-modules\fP, which is used for
defining the modules which can redefine builtins.
\fIpylint\fP will emit an error when a builtin is redefined, such as defining
a variable called \fBnext\fP\&. But in some cases, the builtins can be
redefined in the case they are imported from other places, different
than the \fBbuiltins\fP module, such is the case for \fBsix.moves\fP, which
contains more forward\-looking functions:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ cat a.py
# Oups, now pylint emits a redefined\-builtin message.
from six.moves import open
$ pylint a.py \-\-redefining\-builtins\-modules=six.moves
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
Default values: \fBsix.moves,future.builtins\fP
.UNINDENT
.SS Bug fixes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a bug where the top name of a qualified import was detected as an unused variable.
.IP \(bu 2
We don\(aqt warn about \fBinvalid\-sequence\-index\fP if the indexed object has unknown
base classes, that Pylint cannot deduce.
.UNINDENT
.SS Other Changes
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBbad\-builtin\fP check was moved into an extension.
.sp
The check was complaining about used builtin functions which
were supposed to not be used. For instance, \fBmap\fP and \fBfilter\fP
were falling into this category, since better alternatives can
be used, such as list comprehensions. But the check was annoying,
since using \fBmap\fP or \fBfilter\fP can have its use cases and as
such, we decided to move it to an extension check instead.
It can now be enabled through \fB\-\-load\-plugins=pylint.extensions.bad_builtin\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
We use the \fBconfigparser\fP backport internally, for Python 2.
.sp
This allows having comments inside list values, in the configuration,
such as:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
disable=no\-member,
        # Don\(aqt like this check
        bad\-indentation
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
We now use the isort \%<https://\:pypi\:.org/\:project/\:isort> package internally.
.sp
This improves the \fB\(gawrong\-import\-order\fP check, so now
we should have less false positives regarding the import order.
.IP \(bu 2
We do not emit \fBimport\-error\fP or \fBno\-name\-in\-module\fP for fallback import blocks by default.
.sp
A fallback import block can be considered a TryExcept block, which contains imports in both
branches, such as:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
try:
    import urllib.request as request
except ImportError:
    import urllib2 as request
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
In the case where \fBpylint\fP can not find one import from the \fBexcept\fP branch, then
it will emit an \fBimport\-error\fP, but this gets cumbersome when trying to write
compatible code for both Python versions. As such, we don\(aqt check these blocks by default,
but the analysis can be enforced by using the new \fB\-\-analyse\-fallback\-block\fP flag.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBreimported\fP is emitted when the same name is imported from different module, as in:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
from collections import deque, OrderedDict, deque
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SS Deprecated features
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The HTML support was deprecated and will be eventually removed
in Pylint 1.7.0.
.sp
This feature was lately a second class citizen in Pylint, being
often neglected and having a couple of bugs. Since we now have
the JSON reporter, this can be used as a basis for more prettier
HTML outputs than what Pylint can currently offer.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fB\-\-files\-output\fP option was deprecated and will be eventually
removed in Pylint 1.7.0.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fB\-\-optimize\-ast\fP option was deprecated and will be eventually
removed in Pylint 1.7.0.
.sp
The option was initially added for handling pathological cases,
such as joining too many strings using the addition operator, which
was leading pylint to have a recursion error when trying to figure
out what the string was. Unfortunately, we decided to ignore the
issue, since the pathological case would have happen when the
code was parsed by Python as well, without actually reaching the
runtime step and as such, we will remove the option in the future.
.IP \(bu 2
The \fBcheck_docs\fP extension is now deprecated. The extension is still available
under the \fBdocparams\fP name, so this should work:
.INDENT 2.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
$ pylint module_or_package \-\-load\-extensions=pylint.extensions.docparams
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.sp
The old name is still kept for backward compatibility, but it will be
eventually removed.
.UNINDENT
.SS Removed features
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
None yet
.UNINDENT
.SS Full changelog
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 1.6.3?
.sp
Release date: 2016\-07\-18
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Do not crash when inferring uninferable exception types for docparams extension
.sp
Closes #998
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 1.6.2?
.sp
Release date: 2016\-07\-15
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Do not crash when printing the help of options with default regular expressions
.sp
Closes #990
.IP \(bu 2
More granular versions for deprecated modules.
.sp
Closes #991
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs new in Pylint 1.6.1?
.sp
Release date: 2016\-07\-07
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Use environment markers for supporting conditional dependencies.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.6.0?
.sp
Release date: 2016\-07\-03
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new extension, \fBpylint.extensions.mccabe\fP, for warning
about complexity in code.
.IP \(bu 2
Deprecate support for \-\-optimize\-ast
.sp
Fixes part of #975
.IP \(bu 2
Deprecate support for the HTML output
.sp
Fixes part of #975
.IP \(bu 2
Deprecate support for \-\-output\-files
.sp
Fixes part of #975
.IP \(bu 2
Fixed a documentation error for the check_docs extension.
.sp
Closes #735
.IP \(bu 2
Made the list of property\-defining decorators configurable.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a bug where the top name of a qualified import was detected as unused variable.
.sp
Closes #923
.IP \(bu 2
bad\-builtin / W0141 \%<#\:bad-builtin> is now an extension check.
.IP \(bu 2
generated\-members support qualified name through regular expressions.
.sp
For instance, one can specify a regular expression as \-\-generated\-members=astroid.node_classes.*
for ignoring every no\-member / E1101 \%<#\:no-member> error that is accessed as in \fBastroid.node_classes.missing.object\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Add the ability to ignore files based on regex matching, with the new \fB\-\-ignore\-patterns\fP
option. Allow for multiple ignore patterns to be specified. Rather than clobber the existing
ignore option, we introduced a new one called ignore\-patterns.
.sp
Closes #156
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new error, trailing\-newlines / C0305 \%<#\:trailing-newlines>, which is emitted when a file
has trailing new lines.
.sp
Closes #682
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new option, \(aqredefining\-builtins\-modules\(aq, for controlling the modules
which can redefine builtins, such as six.moves and future.builtins.
.sp
Closes #464
.IP \(bu 2
\(aqreimported\(aq is emitted when the same name is imported from different module.
.sp
Closes #162
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new recommendation checker, consider\-iterating\-dictionary / C0201 \%<#\:consider-iterating-dictionary>, which is emitted
which is emitted when a dictionary is iterated through .keys().
.sp
Closes #699
.IP \(bu 2
Use the configparser backport for Python 2
.sp
This fixes a problem we were having with comments inside values, which is fixed
in Python 3\(aqs configparser.
.sp
Closes #828
.IP \(bu 2
A new error was added, invalid\-length\-returned / E0303 \%<#\:invalid-length-returned>, when the \fB__len__\fP
special method returned something else than a non\-negative number.
.sp
Closes #557
.IP \(bu 2
Switch to using isort internally for wrong\-import\-order / C0411 \%<#\:wrong-import-order>\&.
.sp
Closes #879
.IP \(bu 2
check_docs extension can find constructor parameters in __init__.
.sp
Closes #887
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn about invalid\-sequence\-index / E1126 \%<#\:invalid-sequence-index> if the indexed object has unknown base
classes.
.sp
Closes #867
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt crash when checking, for super\-init\-not\-called / W0231 \%<#\:super-init-not-called>, a method defined in an if block.
.IP \(bu 2
Do not emit import\-error / E0401 \%<#\:import-error> or no\-name\-in\-module / E0611 \%<#\:no-name-in-module> for fallback import blocks by default.
.sp
Until now, we warned with these errors when a fallback import block (a TryExcept block
that contained imports for Python 2 and 3) was found, but this gets cumbersome when
trying to write compatible code. As such, we don\(aqt check these blocks by default,
but the analysis can be enforced by using the new \fB\-\-analyse\-fallback\-block\fP flag.
.sp
Closes #769.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Ticket numbers are almost can be internal to Logilab, or from bitbucket. In latest
version it\(aqs also github issues.
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 1.5
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.5.5?
.sp
Release date: 2016\-03\-21
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Let visit_importfrom from Python 3 porting checker be called when everything is disabled
.sp
Because the visit method was filtering the patterns it was expecting to be activated,
it didn\(aqt run when everything but one pattern was disabled, leading to spurious false
positives
.sp
Closes #852
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit unsubscriptable\-value for classes with unknown
base classes.
.sp
Closes #776.
.IP \(bu 2
Use an OrderedDict for storing the configuration elements
.sp
This fixes an issue related to impredictible order of the disable / enable
elements from a config file. In certain cases, the disable was coming before
the enable which resulted in classes of errors to be enabled, even though the intention
was to disable them. The best example for this was in the context of running multiple
processes, each one of it having different enables / disables that affected the output.
.sp
Closes #815
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt consider bare and broad except handlers as ignoring NameError,
AttributeError and similar exceptions, in the context of checkers for
these issues.
.sp
Closes #826
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.5.4?
.sp
Release date: 2016\-01\-15
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Merge StringMethodChecker with StringFormatChecker. This fixes a
bug where disabling all the messages and enabling only a handful of
messages from the StringFormatChecker would have resulted in no
messages at all.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt apply unneeded\-not / C0113 \%<#\:unneeded-not> over sets.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.5.3?
.sp
Release date: 2016\-01\-11
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Handle the import fallback idiom with regard to wrong\-import\-order / C0411 \%<#\:wrong-import-order>\&.
.sp
Closes #750
.IP \(bu 2
Decouple the displaying of reports from the displaying of messages
.sp
Some reporters are aggregating the messages instead of displaying
them when they are available. The actual displaying was conflatted
in the generate_reports. Unfortunately this behaviour was flaky
and in the case of the JSON reporter, the messages weren\(aqt shown
at all if a file had syntax errors or if it was missing.
In order to fix this, the aggregated messages can now be
displayed with Reporter.display_message, while the reports are
displayed with display_reports.
.sp
Closes #766
Closes #765
.IP \(bu 2
Ignore function calls with variadic arguments without a context.
.sp
Inferring variadic positional arguments and keyword arguments
will result into empty Tuples and Dicts, which can lead in
some cases to false positives with regard to no\-value\-for\-parameter / E1120 \%<#\:no-value-for-parameter>\&.
In order to avoid this, until we\(aqll have support for call context
propagation, we\(aqre ignoring such cases if detected.
.sp
Closes #722
.IP \(bu 2
Treat AsyncFunctionDef just like FunctionDef nodes,
by implementing visit_asyncfunctiondef in terms of
visit_functiondef.
.sp
Closes #767
.IP \(bu 2
Take in account kwonlyargs when verifying that arguments
are defined with the check_docs extension.
.sp
Closes #745
.IP \(bu 2
Suppress reporting unneeded\-not / C0113 \%<#\:unneeded-not> inside \fB__ne__\fP methods
.sp
Closes #749
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.5.2?
.sp
Release date: 2015\-12\-21
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt crash if graphviz is not installed, instead emit a
warning letting the user to know.
.sp
Closes #168
.IP \(bu 2
Accept only functions and methods for the deprecated\-method / W4902 \%<#\:deprecated-method> checker.
.sp
This prevents a crash which can occur when an object doesn\(aqt have
\&.qname() method after the inference.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit super\-on\-old\-class on classes with unknown bases.
.sp
Closes #721
.IP \(bu 2
Allow statements in \fBif\fP or \fBtry\fP blocks containing imports.
.sp
Closes #714
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.5.1?
.sp
Release date: 2015\-12\-02
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash which occurred when old visit methods are encountered
in plugin modules.
.sp
Closes #711
.IP \(bu 2
Add wrong\-import\-position / C0413 \%<#\:wrong-import-position> to check_messages\(aqs decorator arguments
for ImportChecker.leave_module
This fixes an esoteric bug which occurs when ungrouped\-imports / C0412 \%<#\:ungrouped-imports> and
wrong\-import\-order / C0411 \%<#\:wrong-import-order> are disabled and pylint is executed on multiple files.
What happens is that without wrong\-import\-position / C0413 \%<#\:wrong-import-position> in check_messages,
leave_module will never be called, which means that the first non\-import node
from other files might leak into the current file,
leading to wrong\-import\-position / C0413 \%<#\:wrong-import-position> being emitted by pylint.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash which occurred when old visit methods are encountered
in plugin modules.
.sp
Closes #711
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit import\-self / W0406 \%<#\:import-self> and cyclic\-import / R0401 \%<#\:cyclic-import> for relative imports
of modules with the same name as the package itself.
.sp
Closes #708
Closes #706.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.5.0?
.sp
Release date: 2015\-11\-29
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Added multiple warnings related to imports. wrong\-import\-order / C0411 \%<#\:wrong-import-order>
is emitted when PEP 8 recommendations regarding imports are not
respected (that is, standard imports should be followed by third\-party
imports and then by local imports). ungrouped\-imports / C0412 \%<#\:ungrouped-imports> is emitted
when imports from the same package or module are not placed
together, but scattered around in the code. wrong\-import\-position / C0413 \%<#\:wrong-import-position>
is emitted when code is mixed with imports, being recommended for the
latter to be at the top of the file, in order to figure out easier by
a human reader what dependencies a module has.
.sp
Closes #692
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new refactoring warning, unneeded\-not / C0113 \%<#\:unneeded-not>, emitted
when an expression with the not operator could be simplified.
.sp
Closes #670
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new refactoring warning, simplifiable\-if\-statement / R1703 \%<#\:simplifiable-if-statement>,
used when an if statement could be reduced to a boolean evaluation
of its test.
.sp
Closes #698
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new refactoring warning, too\-many\-boolean\-expressions / R0916 \%<#\:too-many-boolean-expressions>,
used when an if statement contains too many boolean expressions,
which makes the code less maintainable and harder to understand.
.sp
Closes #677
.IP \(bu 2
Property methods are shown as attributes instead of functions in
pyreverse class diagrams.
.sp
Closes #284
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new refactoring error, too\-many\-nested\-blocks / R1702 \%<#\:too-many-nested-blocks>, which is emitted
when a function or a method has too many nested blocks, which makes the
code less readable and harder to understand.
.sp
Closes #668
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, unsubscriptable\-object / E1136 \%<#\:unsubscriptable-object>, that is emitted when
value used in subscription expression doesn\(aqt support subscription
(i.e. doesn\(aqt define __getitem__ method).
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn about abstract classes instantiated in their own body.
.sp
Closes #627
.IP \(bu 2
Obsolete options are not present by default in the generated
configuration file.
.sp
Closes #632
.IP \(bu 2
non\-iterator\-returned / E0301 \%<#\:non-iterator-returned> can detect classes with iterator\-metaclasses.
.sp
Closes #679
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, unsupported\-membership\-test / E1135 \%<#\:unsupported-membership-test>, emitted when value
to the right of the \(aqin\(aq operator doesn\(aqt support membership test
protocol (i.e. doesn\(aqt define __contains__/__iter__/__getitem__)
.IP \(bu 2
Add new errors, not\-an\-iterable / E1133 \%<#\:not-an-iterable>, emitted when non\-iterable value
is used in an iterating context (starargs, for\-statement,
comprehensions, etc), and not\-a\-mapping / E1134 \%<#\:not-a-mapping>, emitted when non\-mapping
value is used in a mapping context.
.sp
Closes #563
.IP \(bu 2
Make no\-self\-use / R6301 \%<#\:no-self-use> checker not emit a warning if there is a \(aqsuper()\(aq
call inside the method.
.sp
Closes #667
.IP \(bu 2
Add checker to identify multiple imports on one line.
.sp
Closes #598
.IP \(bu 2
Fix unused\-argument / W0613 \%<#\:unused-argument> false positive when the \(dq+=\(dq operator is used.
.sp
Closes #518
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit import\-error / E0401 \%<#\:import-error> for ignored modules. PyLint will not emit import
errors for any import which is, or is a subpackage of, a module in
the ignored\-modules list.
.sp
Closes #223
.IP \(bu 2
Fix unused\-import / W0611 \%<#\:unused-import> false positive when the import is used in a
class assignment.
.sp
Closes #475
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, not\-context\-manager / E1129 \%<#\:not-context-manager>, emitted when something
that doesn\(aqt implement __enter__ and __exit__ is used in a with
statement.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, confusing\-with\-statement / W0124 \%<#\:confusing-with-statement>, emitted by the
base checker, when an ambiguous looking with statement is used.
For example \fIwith open() as first, second\fP which looks like a
tuple assignment but is actually 2 context managers.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, duplicate\-except / W0705 \%<#\:duplicate-except>, emitted when there is an
exception handler which handles an exception type that was handled
before.
.sp
Closes #485
.IP \(bu 2
A couple of warnings got promoted to errors, since they could uncover
potential bugs in the code. These warnings are: assignment\-from\-none / E1128 \%<#\:assignment-from-none>,
unbalanced\-tuple\-unpacking / W0632 \%<#\:unbalanced-tuple-unpacking>, unpacking\-non\-sequence / E0633 \%<#\:unpacking-non-sequence>, non\-iterator\-returned / E0301 \%<#\:non-iterator-returned>\&.
.sp
Closes #388
.IP \(bu 2
Allow ending a pragma control with a semicolon. In this way, users
can continue a pragma control with a reason for why it is used,
as in \fI# pylint: disable=old\-style\-class;reason=...\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #449
.IP \(bu 2
\-\-jobs can be used with \-\-load\-plugins now.
.sp
Closes #456
.IP \(bu 2
Improve the performance of \-\-jobs when dealing only with a package name.
.sp
Closes #479
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit an unused\-wildcard\-import / W0614 \%<#\:unused-wildcard-import> when the imported name comes
from another module and it is in fact a __future__ name.
.IP \(bu 2
The colorized reporter now works on Windows.
.sp
Closes #96.
.IP \(bu 2
Remove pointless\-except warning. It was previously disabled by
default and it wasn\(aqt very useful.
.sp
Closes #506.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash on Python 3 related to the string checker, which
crashed when it encountered a bytes string with a .format
method called.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn about no\-self\-use / R6301 \%<#\:no-self-use> for builtin properties.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive for bad\-reversed\-sequence / E0111 \%<#\:bad-reversed-sequence>, when a subclass
of a \fBdict\fP provides a __reversed__ method.
.IP \(bu 2
Change the default no\-docstring\-rgx so missing\-docstring / C0111 \%<#\:missing-docstring> isn\(aqt
emitted for private functions.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit redefined\-outer\-name / W0621 \%<#\:redefined-outer-name> for __future__ directives.
.sp
Closes #520.
.IP \(bu 2
Provide some hints for the bad\-builtin / W0141 \%<#\:bad-builtin> message.
.sp
Closes #522.
.IP \(bu 2
When checking for invalid arguments to a callable, in typecheck.py,
look up for the __init__ in case the found __new__ comes from builtins.
.sp
Since the __new__ comes from builtins, it will not have attached any
information regarding what parameters it expects, so the check
will be useless. Retrieving __init__ in that case will at least
detect a couple of false negatives.
.sp
Closes #429.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit no\-member / E1101 \%<#\:no-member> for classes with unknown bases.
.sp
Since we don\(aqt know what those bases might add, we simply ignore
the error in this case.
.IP \(bu 2
Lookup in the implicit metaclass when checking for no\-member / E1101 \%<#\:no-member>,
if the class in question has an implicit metaclass, which is
True for new style classes.
.sp
Closes #438.
.IP \(bu 2
Add two new warnings, duplicate\-bases / E0241 \%<#\:duplicate-bases> and inconsistent\-mro / E0240 \%<#\:inconsistent-mro>\&.
.sp
duplicate\-bases / E0241 \%<#\:duplicate-bases> is emitted when a class has the same bases
listed more than once in its bases definition, while inconsistent\-mro / E0240 \%<#\:inconsistent-mro>
is emitted when no sane mro hierarchy can be determined.
.sp
Closes #526.
.IP \(bu 2
Remove interface\-not\-implemented warning.
.sp
Closes #532.
.IP \(bu 2
Remove the rest of interface checks: interface\-is\-not\-class,
missing\-interface\-method, unresolved\-interface. The reason is that
it\(aqs better to start recommending ABCs instead of the old Zope era
of interfaces. One side effect of this change is that ignore\-iface\-methods
becomes a noop, it\(aqs deprecated and it will be removed at some time.
.IP \(bu 2
Emit a proper deprecation warning for reporters.BaseReporter.add_message.
.sp
The alternative way is to use handle_message. add_message will be removed in
Pylint 1.6.
.IP \(bu 2
Added new module \(aqextensions\(aq for optional checkers with the test
directory \(aqtest/extensions\(aq and documentation file \(aqdoc/extensions.rst\(aq.
.IP \(bu 2
Added new checker \(aqextensions.check_docs\(aq that verifies parameter
documentation in Sphinx, Google, and Numpy style.
.IP \(bu 2
Detect undefined variable cases, where the \(dqdefinition\(dq of an undefined
variable was in del statement. Instead of emitting used\-before\-assignment / E0601 \%<#\:used-before-assignment>,
which is totally misleading, it now emits undefined\-variable / E0602 \%<#\:undefined-variable>\&.
.sp
Closes #528.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit attribute\-defined\-outside\-init / W0201 \%<#\:attribute-defined-outside-init> and access\-member\-before\-definition / E0203 \%<#\:access-member-before-definition>
for mixin classes. Actual errors can occur in mixin classes, but this is
controlled by the ignore\-mixin\-members option.
.sp
Closes #412.
.IP \(bu 2
Improve the detection of undefined variables and variables used before
assignment for variables used as default arguments to function,
where the variable was first defined in the class scope.
.sp
Closes #342 and issue #404.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, unexpected\-special\-method\-signature / E0302 \%<#\:unexpected-special-method-signature>, which is emitted
when a special method (dunder method) doesn\(aqt have the expected signature,
which can lead to actual errors in the application code.
.sp
Closes #253.
.IP \(bu 2
Remove bad\-context\-manager / E0235 \%<#\:bad-context-manager> due to the inclusion of unexpected\-special\-method\-signature / E0302 \%<#\:unexpected-special-method-signature>\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit no\-name\-in\-module / E0611 \%<#\:no-name-in-module> if the import is guarded by an ImportError, Exception or
a bare except clause.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit no\-member / E1101 \%<#\:no-member> if the attribute access node is protected by an
except handler, which handles AttributeError, Exception or it is a
bare except.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit import\-error / E0401 \%<#\:import-error> if the import is guarded by an ImportError, Exception or a
bare except clause.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit undefined\-variable / E0602 \%<#\:undefined-variable> if the node is guarded by a NameError, Exception
or bare except clause.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, using\-constant\-test / W0125 \%<#\:using-constant-test>, which is emitted when a conditional
statement (If, IfExp) uses a test which is always constant, such as numbers,
classes, functions etc. This is most likely an error from the user\(aqs part.
.sp
Closes #524.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit raising\-non\-exception / E0710 \%<#\:raising-non-exception> when the exception has unknown
bases. We don\(aqt know what those bases actually are and it\(aqs better
to assume that the user knows what he is doing rather than emitting
a message which can be considered a false positive.
.IP \(bu 2
Look for a .pylintrc configuration file in the current folder,
if pylintrc is not found. Dotted pylintrc files will not be searched
in the parents of the current folder, as it is done for pylintrc.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, \(aqinvalid\-unary\-type\-operand\(aq, emitted when
an unary operand is used on something which doesn\(aqt support that
operation (for instance, using the unary bitwise inversion operator
on an instance which doesn\(aqt implement __invert__).
.IP \(bu 2
Take in consideration differences between arguments of various
type of functions (classmethods, staticmethods, properties)
when checking for \fBarguments\-differ\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #548.
.IP \(bu 2
astroid.inspector was moved to pylint.pyreverse, since it belongs
there and it doesn\(aqt need to be in astroid.
.IP \(bu 2
astroid.utils.LocalsVisitor was moved to pylint.pyreverse.LocalsVisitor.
.IP \(bu 2
pylint.checkers.utils.excepts_import_error was removed.
Use pylint.checkers.utils.error_of_type instead.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit undefined\-all\-variables for nodes which can\(aqt be
inferred (YES nodes).
.IP \(bu 2
yield\-outside\-func is also emitted for \fByield from\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, too\-many\-star\-expressions / E0112 \%<#\:too-many-star-expressions>, emitted when
there are more than one starred expression (\fI*x\fP) in an assignment.
The warning is emitted only on Python 3.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, invalid\-star\-assignment\-target / E0113 \%<#\:invalid-star-assignment-target>, emitted when
a starred expression (\fI*x\fP) is used as the lhs side of an assignment,
as in \fI*x = [1, 2]\fP\&. This is not a SyntaxError on Python 3 though.
.IP \(bu 2
Detect a couple of objects which can\(aqt be base classes (bool,
slice, range and memoryview, which weren\(aqt detected until now).
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error for the Python 3 porting checker, \fBimport\-star\-module\-level\fP,
which is used when a star import is detected in another scope than the
module level, which is an error on Python 3. Using this will emit a
SyntaxWarning on Python 2.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, star\-needs\-assignment\-target / E0114 \%<#\:star-needs-assignment-target>, emitted on Python 3 when
a Starred expression (\fI*x\fP) is not used in an assignment target. This is not
caught when parsing the AST on Python 3, so it needs to be a separate check.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, unsupported\-binary\-operation / E1131 \%<#\:unsupported-binary-operation>, emitted when
two a binary arithmetic operation is executed between two objects
which don\(aqt support it (a number plus a string for instance).
This is currently disabled, since the it exhibits way too many false
positives, but it will be re\-enabled as soon as possible.
.IP \(bu 2
New imported features from astroid into pyreverse: pyreverse.inspector.Project,
pyreverse.inspector.project_from_files and pyreverse.inspector.interfaces.
.sp
These were moved since they didn\(aqt belong in astroid.
.IP \(bu 2
Enable misplaced\-future / W0410 \%<#\:misplaced-future> for Python 3.
.sp
Closes #580.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, nonlocal\-and\-global / E0115 \%<#\:nonlocal-and-global>, which is emitted when a
name is found to be both nonlocal and global in the same scope.
.sp
Closes #581.
.IP \(bu 2
ignored\-classes option can work with qualified names (ignored\-classes=optparse.Values)
.sp
Closes #297
.IP \(bu 2
ignored\-modules can work with qualified names as well as with Unix pattern
matching for recursive ignoring.
.sp
Closes #244
.IP \(bu 2
Improve detection of relative imports in non\-packages, as well as importing
missing modules with a relative import from a package.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit no\-init if not all the bases from a class are known.
.sp
Closes #604.
.IP \(bu 2
\-\-no\-space\-check option accepts \fBempty\-line\fP as a possible option.
.sp
Closes #541.
.IP \(bu 2
\-\-generate\-rcfile generates by default human readable symbols
for the \-\-disable option.
.sp
Closes #608.
.IP \(bu 2
Improved the not\-in\-loop / E0103 \%<#\:not-in-loop> checker to properly detect more cases.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, continue\-in\-finally / W0136 \%<#\:continue-in-finally>, which is emitted when
the \fBcontinue\fP keyword is found inside a \fBfinally\fP clause, which
is a SyntaxError.
.IP \(bu 2
The \-\-zope flag is deprecated and it is slated for removal
in Pylint 1.6.
.sp
The reason behind this removal is the fact that it\(aqs a specialized
flag and there are solutions for the original problem:
use \-\-generated\-members with the members that causes problems
when using Zope or add AST transforms tailored to the zope
project.
.sp
At the same time, \-\-include\-ids and \-\-symbols will also be removed
in Pylint 1.6.
.sp
Closes #570.
.IP \(bu 2
missing\-module\-attribute was removed and the corresponding
CLI option, required\-attributes, which is slated for removal
in Pylint 1.6.
.IP \(bu 2
missing\-reversed\-argument was removed.
.sp
The reason behind this is that this kind of errors should be
detected by the type checker for \fIall\fP the builtins and not
as a special case for the reversed builtin. This will happen
shortly in the future.
.IP \(bu 2
\-\-comment flag is obsolete and it will be removed in Pylint 1.6.
.IP \(bu 2
\-\-profile flag is obsolete and it will be removed in Pylint 1.6.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, misplaced\-bare\-raise / E0704 \%<#\:misplaced-bare-raise>\&.
.sp
The error is used when a bare raise is not used inside an except clause.
This can generate a RuntimeError in Python, if there are no active exceptions
to be reraised. While it works in Python 2 due to the fact that the exception
leaks outside of the except block, it\(aqs nevertheless a behaviour that
a user shouldn\(aqt depend upon, since it\(aqs not obvious to the reader of the code
what exception will be raised and it will not be compatible with Python 3 anyhow.
.sp
Closes #633.
.IP \(bu 2
Bring logilab\-common\(aqs ureports into pylint.reporters.
.sp
With this change, we moved away from depending on logilab\-common,
having in Pylint all the components that were used from logilab\-common.
The API should be considered an implementation detail and can change at
some point in the future.
.sp
Closes #621.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBreimported\fP is emitted for reimported objects on the same line.
.sp
Closes #639.
.IP \(bu 2
Abbreviations of command line options are not supported anymore.
.sp
Using abbreviations for CLI options was never considered to be
a feature of pylint, this fact being only a side effect of using optparse.
As this was the case, using \-\-load\-plugin or other abbreviation
for \-\-load\-plugins never actually worked, while it also didn\(aqt raise
an error.
.sp
Closes #424.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, nonlocal\-without\-binding / E0117 \%<#\:nonlocal-without-binding>
.sp
The error is emitted on Python 3 when a nonlocal name is not bound
to any variable in the parents scopes.
.sp
Closes #582.
.IP \(bu 2
.INDENT 2.0
.TP
.B deprecated\-module / W4901 \%<#\:deprecated-module> can be shown for modules which aren\(aqt
available.
.UNINDENT
.sp
Closes #362.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt consider a class abstract if its members can\(aqt
be properly inferred.
.sp
This fixes a false positive related to abstract\-class\-instantiated / E0110 \%<#\:abstract-class-instantiated>\&.
.sp
Closes #648.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new checker for the async features added by PEP 492.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, yield\-inside\-async\-function / E1700 \%<#\:yield-inside-async-function>, emitted on
Python 3.5 and upwards when the \fByield\fP statement is found inside
a new coroutine function (PEP 492).
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, not\-async\-context\-manager / E1701 \%<#\:not-async-context-manager>, emitted when
an async context manager block is used with an object which doesn\(aqt
support this protocol (PEP 492).
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new convention warning, singleton\-comparison / C0121 \%<#\:singleton-comparison>, emitted when
comparison to True, False or None is found.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit assigning\-non\-slot / E0237 \%<#\:assigning-non-slot> for descriptors.
.sp
Closes #652.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new error, repeated\-keyword / E1132 \%<#\:repeated-keyword>, when a keyword argument is passed
multiple times into a function call.
.sp
This is similar with redundant\-keyword\-arg / E1124 \%<#\:redundant-keyword-arg>, but it\(aqs mildly different
that it needs to be a separate error.
.IP \(bu 2
\-\-enable=all can now be used.
.sp
Closes #142.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new convention message, misplaced\-comparison\-constant / C2201 \%<#\:misplaced-comparison-constant>,
emitted when a constant is placed in the left hand side of a comparison,
as in \(aq5 == func()\(aq. This is also called Yoda condition, since the
flow of code reminds of the Star Wars green character, conditions usually
encountered in languages with variabile assignments in conditional
statements.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new convention message, consider\-using\-enumerate / C0200 \%<#\:consider-using-enumerate>, which is
emitted when code that uses \fBrange\fP and \fBlen\fP for iterating is encountered.
.sp
Closes #684.
.IP \(bu 2
Added two new refactoring messages, no\-classmethod\-decorator / R0202 \%<#\:no-classmethod-decorator> and
no\-staticmethod\-decorator / R0203 \%<#\:no-staticmethod-decorator>, which are emitted when a static method or a class
method is declared without using decorators syntax.
.sp
Closes #675.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 1.4
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.4.3?
.sp
Release date: 2015\-03\-14
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Remove three warnings: star\-args, abstract\-class\-little\-used,
abstract\-class\-not\-used. These warnings don\(aqt add any real value
and they don\(aqt imply errors or problems in the code.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new option for controlling the peephole optimizer in astroid.
The option \fB\-\-optimize\-ast\fP will control the peephole optimizer,
which is used to optimize a couple of AST subtrees. The current problem
solved by the peephole optimizer is when multiple joined strings,
with the addition operator, are encountered. If the numbers of such
strings is high enough, Pylint will then fail with a maximum recursion
depth exceeded error, due to its visitor architecture. The peephole
just transforms such calls, if it can, into the final resulting string
and this exhibit a problem, because the visit_binop method stops being
called (in the optimized AST it will be a Const node).
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.4.2?
.sp
Release date: 2015\-03\-11
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt require a docstring for empty modules.
.sp
Closes #261
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive with \fBtoo\-few\-format\-args\fP string warning,
emitted when the string format contained a normal positional
argument (\(aq{0}\(aq), mixed with a positional argument which did
an attribute access (\(aq{0.__class__}\(aq).
.sp
Closes #463
.IP \(bu 2
Take in account all the methods from the ancestors
when checking for too\-few\-public\-methods / R0903 \%<#\:too-few-public-methods>\&.
.sp
Closes #471
.IP \(bu 2
Catch enchant errors and emit invalid\-characters\-in\-docstring / C0403 \%<#\:invalid-characters-in-docstring>
when checking for spelling errors.
.sp
Closes #469
.IP \(bu 2
Use all the inferred statements for the super\-init\-not\-called / W0231 \%<#\:super-init-not-called>
check.
.sp
Closes #389
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, \(aqunichr\-builtin\(aq, emitted by the Python 3
porting checker, when the unichr builtin is found.
.sp
Closes #472
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, \(aqintern\-builtin\(aq, emitted by the Python 3
porting checker, when the intern builtin is found.
.sp
Closes #473
.IP \(bu 2
Add support for editable installations.
.IP \(bu 2
The HTML output accepts the \fB\-\-msg\-template\fP option. Patch by
Dan Goldsmith.
.IP \(bu 2
Add \(aqmap\-builtin\-not\-iterating\(aq (replacing \(aqimplicit\-map\-evaluation\(aq),
\(aqzip\-builtin\-not\-iterating\(aq, \(aqrange\-builtin\-not\-iterating\(aq, and
\(aqfilter\-builtin\-not\-iterating\(aq which are emitted by \fB\-\-py3k\fP when the
appropriate built\-in is not used in an iterating context (semantics
taken from 2to3).
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, unidiomatic\-typecheck / C0123 \%<#\:unidiomatic-typecheck>, emitted when an explicit
typecheck uses type() instead of isinstance(). For example,
\fItype(x) == Y\fP instead of \fIisinstance(x, Y)\fP\&. Patch by Chris Rebert.
.sp
Closes #299
.IP \(bu 2
Add support for combining the Python 3 checker mode with the \-\-jobs
flag (\-\-py3k and \-\-jobs).
.sp
Closes #467
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning for the Python 3 porting checker, \(aqusing\-cmp\-argument\(aq,
emitted when the \fBcmp\fP argument for the \fBlist.sort\fP or \fBsorted builtin\fP
is encountered.
.IP \(bu 2
Make the \-\-py3k flag commutative with the \-E flag. Also, this patch
fixes the leaks of error messages from the Python 3 checker when
the errors mode was activated.
.sp
Closes #437
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.4.1?
.sp
Release date: 2015\-01\-16
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Look only in the current function\(aqs scope for bad\-super\-call / E1003 \%<#\:bad-super-call>\&.
.sp
Closes #403
.IP \(bu 2
Check the return of properties when checking for not\-callable / E1102 \%<#\:not-callable>\&.
.sp
Closes #406
.IP \(bu 2
Warn about using the input() or round() built\-ins for Python 3.
.sp
Closes #411
.IP \(bu 2
Proper abstract method lookup while checking for abstract\-class\-instantiated / E0110 \%<#\:abstract-class-instantiated>\&.
.sp
Closes #401
.IP \(bu 2
Use a mro traversal for finding abstract methods.
.sp
Closes #415
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive with catching\-non\-exception / E0712 \%<#\:catching-non-exception> and tuples of exceptions.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false negative with raising\-non\-exception / E0710 \%<#\:raising-non-exception>, when the raise used
an uninferrable exception context.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive on Python 2 for raising\-bad\-type / E0702 \%<#\:raising-bad-type>, when
raising tuples in the form \(aqraise (ZeroDivisionError, None)\(aq.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive with invalid\-slots\-objects, where the slot entry
was a unicode string on Python 2.
.sp
Closes #421
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, redundant\-unittest\-assert / W1503 \%<#\:redundant-unittest-assert>, emitted when using
unittest\(aqs methods assertTrue and assertFalse with constant value
as argument. Patch by Vlad Temian.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new JSON reporter, usable through \-f flag.
.IP \(bu 2
Add the method names for the signature\-differs / W0222 \%<#\:signature-differs> and \(aqargument\-differs\(aq
warnings.
.sp
Closes #433
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt compile test files when installing.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash which occurred when using multiple jobs and the files
given as argument didn\(aqt exist at all.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.4.0?
.sp
Release date: 2014\-11\-23
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Added new options for controlling the loading of C extensions.
By default, only C extensions from the stdlib will be loaded
into the active Python interpreter for inspection, because they
can run arbitrary code on import. The option
\fB\-\-extension\-pkg\-whitelist\fP can be used to specify modules
or packages that are safe to load.
.IP \(bu 2
Change default max\-line\-length to 100 rather than 80
.IP \(bu 2
Drop BaseRawChecker class which were only there for backward
compatibility for a while now
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt try to analyze string formatting with objects coming from
function arguments.
.sp
Closes #373
.IP \(bu 2
Port source code to be Python 2/3 compatible. This drops the
need for 2to3, but does drop support for Python 2.5.
.IP \(bu 2
Each message now comes with a confidence level attached, and
can be filtered base on this level. This allows to filter out
all messages that were emitted even though an inference failure
happened during checking.
.IP \(bu 2
Improved presenting unused\-import / W0611 \%<#\:unused-import> message.
.sp
Closes #293
.IP \(bu 2
Add new checker for finding spelling errors. New messages:
wrong\-spelling\-in\-comment / C0401 \%<#\:wrong-spelling-in-comment>, wrong\-spelling\-in\-docstring / C0402 \%<#\:wrong-spelling-in-docstring>\&.
New options: spelling\-dict, spelling\-ignore\-words.
.IP \(bu 2
Add new \(aq\-j\(aq option for running checks in sub\-processes.
.IP \(bu 2
Added new checks for line endings if they are mixed (LF vs CRLF)
or if they are not as expected. New messages: mixed\-line\-endings / C0327 \%<#\:mixed-line-endings>,
unexpected\-line\-ending\-format / C0328 \%<#\:unexpected-line-ending-format>\&. New option: expected\-line\-ending\-format.
.IP \(bu 2
dangerous\-default\-value / W0102 \%<#\:dangerous-default-value> no longer evaluates the value of the arguments,
which could result in long error messages or sensitive data being leaked.
.sp
Closes #282
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive with string formatting checker, when
encountering a string which uses only position\-based arguments.
.sp
Closes #285
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive with string formatting checker, when using
keyword argument packing.
.sp
Closes #288
.IP \(bu 2
Proper handle class level scope for lambdas.
.IP \(bu 2
Handle too\-few\-format\-args / E1306 \%<#\:too-few-format-args> or too\-many\-format\-args / E1305 \%<#\:too-many-format-args> for format
strings with both named and positional fields.
.sp
Closes #286
.IP \(bu 2
Analyze only strings by the string format checker.
.sp
Closes #287
.IP \(bu 2
Properly handle nested format string fields.
.sp
Closes #294
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit attribute\-defined\-outside\-init / W0201 \%<#\:attribute-defined-outside-init> if the attribute
was set by a function call in a defining method.
.sp
Closes #192
.IP \(bu 2
Properly handle unicode format strings for Python 2.
.sp
Closes #296
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit import\-error / E0401 \%<#\:import-error> if an import was protected by a try\-except,
which excepted ImportError.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix an unused\-import / W0611 \%<#\:unused-import> false positive, when the error was emitted
for all the members imported with \(aqfrom import\(aq form.
.sp
Closes #304
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit invalid\-name / C0103 \%<#\:invalid-name> when assigning a name in an
ImportError handler.
.sp
Closes #302
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt count branches from nested functions.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive with too\-few\-format\-args / E1306 \%<#\:too-few-format-args>, when the format
strings contains duplicate manual position arguments.
.sp
Closes #310
.IP \(bu 2
fixme regex handles comments without spaces after the hash.
.sp
Closes #311
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit unused\-import / W0611 \%<#\:unused-import> when a special object is imported
(__all__, __doc__ etc.).
.sp
Closes #309
.IP \(bu 2
Look in the metaclass, if defined, for members not found in the current
class.
.sp
Closes #306
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit protected\-access / W0212 \%<#\:protected-access> if the attribute is accessed using
a property defined at the class level.
.IP \(bu 2
Detect calls of the parent\(aqs __init__, through a binded super() call.
.IP \(bu 2
Check that a class has an explicitly defined metaclass before
emitting \(aqold\-style\-class\(aq for Python 2.
.IP \(bu 2
Emit catching\-non\-exception / E0712 \%<#\:catching-non-exception> for non\-class nodes.
.sp
Closes #303
.IP \(bu 2
Order of reporting is consistent.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, boolean\-datetime / W1502 \%<#\:boolean-datetime>, emitted when an instance
of \(aqdatetime.time\(aq is used in a boolean context.
.sp
Closes #239
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a crash which occurred while checking for method\-hidden / E0202 \%<#\:method-hidden>,
when the parent frame was something different than a function.
.IP \(bu 2
Generate html output for missing files.
.sp
Closes #320
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive with too\-many\-format\-args / E1305 \%<#\:too-many-format-args>, when the format
string contains mixed attribute access arguments and manual
fields.
.sp
Closes #322
.IP \(bu 2
Extend the cases where undefined\-variable / E0602 \%<#\:undefined-variable> and used\-before\-assignment / E0601 \%<#\:used-before-assignment>
can be detected.
.sp
Closes #291
.IP \(bu 2
Add support for customising callback identifiers, by adding a new
\(aq\-\-callbacks\(aq command line option.
.sp
Closes #326
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, logging\-format\-interpolation / W1202 \%<#\:logging-format-interpolation>, emitted when .format()
string interpolation is used within logging function calls.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit unbalanced\-tuple\-unpacking / W0632 \%<#\:unbalanced-tuple-unpacking> when the rhs of the assignment
is a variable length argument.
.sp
Closes #329
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning, inherit\-non\-class / E0239 \%<#\:inherit-non-class>, emitted when a class inherits
from something which is not a class.
.sp
Closes #331
.IP \(bu 2
Fix another false positives with undefined\-variable / E0602 \%<#\:undefined-variable>, where the variable
can be found as a class assignment and used in a function annotation.
.sp
Closes #342
.IP \(bu 2
Handle assignment of the string format method to a variable.
.sp
Closes #351
.IP \(bu 2
Support wheel packaging format for PyPi.
.sp
Closes #334
.IP \(bu 2
Check that various built\-ins that do not exist in Python 3 are not
used: apply, basestring, buffer, cmp, coerce, execfile, file, long
raw_input, reduce, StandardError, unicode, reload and xrange.
.IP \(bu 2
Warn for magic methods which are not used in any way in Python 3:
__coerce__, __delslice__, __getslice__, __setslice__, __cmp__,
__oct__, __nonzero__ and __hex__.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit assigning\-non\-slot / E0237 \%<#\:assigning-non-slot> when the assignment is for a property.
.sp
Closes #359
.IP \(bu 2
Fix for regression: \(aq{path}\(aq was no longer accepted in \(aq\-\-msg\-template\(aq.
.IP \(bu 2
Report the percentage of all messages, not just for errors and warnings.
.sp
Closes #319
.IP \(bu 2
too\-many\-public\-methods / R0904 \%<#\:too-many-public-methods> is reported only for methods defined in a class,
not in its ancestors.
.sp
Closes #248
.IP \(bu 2
too\-many\-lines / C0302 \%<#\:too-many-lines> disable pragma can be located on any line, not only the
first.
.sp
Closes #321
.IP \(bu 2
Warn in Python 2 when an import statement is found without a
corresponding \fBfrom __future__ import absolute_import\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Warn in Python 2 when a non\-floor division operation is found without
a corresponding \fBfrom __future__ import division\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new option, \(aqexclude\-protected\(aq, for excluding members
from the protected\-access / W0212 \%<#\:protected-access> warning.
.sp
Closes #48
.IP \(bu 2
Warn in Python 2 when using dict.iter*(), dict.view*(); none of these
methods are available in Python 3.
.IP \(bu 2
Warn in Python 2 when calling an object\(aqs next() method; Python 3 uses
__next__() instead.
.IP \(bu 2
Warn when assigning to __metaclass__ at a class scope; in Python 3 a
metaclass is specified as an argument to the \(aqclass\(aq statement.
.IP \(bu 2
Warn when performing parameter tuple unpacking; it is not supported in
Python 3.
.IP \(bu 2
abstract\-class\-instantiated / E0110 \%<#\:abstract-class-instantiated> is also emitted for Python 2.
It was previously disabled.
.IP \(bu 2
Add \(aqlong\-suffix\(aq error, emitted when encountering the long suffix
on numbers.
.IP \(bu 2
Add support for disabling a checker, by specifying an \(aqenabled\(aq
attribute on the checker class.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new CLI option, \-\-py3k, for enabling Python 3 porting mode. This
mode will disable all other checkers and will emit warnings and
errors for constructs which are invalid or removed in Python 3.
.IP \(bu 2
Add \(aqold\-octal\-literal\(aq to Python 3 porting checker, emitted when
encountering octals with the old syntax.
.IP \(bu 2
Add \(aqimplicit\-map\-evaluation\(aq to Python 3 porting checker, emitted
when encountering the use of map builtin, without explicit evaluation.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 1.3
.sp
Release date: 2014\-07\-26
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Allow hanging continued indentation for implicitly concatenated
strings.
.sp
Closes #232.
.IP \(bu 2
Pylint works under Python 2.5 again, and its test suite passes.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix some false positives for the cellvar\-from\-loop warnings.
.sp
Closes #233.
.IP \(bu 2
Return new astroid class nodes when the inferencer can detect that
that result of a function invocation on a type (like \fBtype\fP or
\fIabc.ABCMeta\fP) is requested.
.sp
Closes #205.
.IP \(bu 2
Emit undefined\-variable / E0602 \%<#\:undefined-variable> for undefined names when using the
Python 3 \fBmetaclass=\fP argument.
.IP \(bu 2
Checkers respect priority now.
.sp
Closes #229
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive regarding W0511.
.sp
Closes #149.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix unused\-import / W0611 \%<#\:unused-import> false positive with Python 3 metaclasses
.sp
Closes #143
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt warn with bad\-format\-character / E1300 \%<#\:bad-format-character> when encountering
the \(aqa\(aq format on Python 3.
.IP \(bu 2
Add multiple checks for PEP 3101 advanced string formatting:
bad\-format\-string / W1302 \%<#\:bad-format-string>, missing\-format\-argument\-key / W1303 \%<#\:missing-format-argument-key>,
unused\-format\-string\-argument / W1304 \%<#\:unused-format-string-argument>, format\-combined\-specification / W1305 \%<#\:format-combined-specification>,
missing\-format\-attribute / W1306 \%<#\:missing-format-attribute> and invalid\-format\-index / W1307 \%<#\:invalid-format-index>\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Issue broad\-except / W0703 \%<#\:broad-except> and bare\-except / W0702 \%<#\:bare-except> even if the number
of except handlers is different than 1.
.sp
Closes #113
.IP \(bu 2
Issue attribute\-defined\-outside\-init / W0201 \%<#\:attribute-defined-outside-init> for all cases, not just
for the last assignment.
.sp
Closes #262
.IP \(bu 2
Emit not\-callable / E1102 \%<#\:not-callable> when calling properties.
.sp
Closes #268.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false positive with unbalanced iterable unpacking,
when encountering starred nodes.
.sp
Closes #273.
.IP \(bu 2
Add new checks, invalid\-slice\-index / E1127 \%<#\:invalid-slice-index> and invalid\-sequence\-index / E1126 \%<#\:invalid-sequence-index>
for invalid sequence and slice indices.
.IP \(bu 2
Add assigning\-non\-slot / E0237 \%<#\:assigning-non-slot> warning, which detects assignments to
attributes not defined in slots.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit no\-name\-in\-module / E0611 \%<#\:no-name-in-module> for ignored modules.
.sp
Closes #223.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix an unused\-variable / W0612 \%<#\:unused-variable> false positive, where the variable is
assigned through an import.
.sp
Closes #196.
.IP \(bu 2
Definition order is considered for classes, function arguments
and annotations.
.sp
Closes #257.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit unused\-variable / W0612 \%<#\:unused-variable> when assigning to a nonlocal.
.sp
Closes #275.
.IP \(bu 2
Do not let ImportError propagate from the import checker, leading to crash
in some namespace package related cases.
.sp
Closes #203.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit pointless\-string\-statement / W0105 \%<#\:pointless-string-statement> for attribute docstrings.
.sp
Closes #193.
.IP \(bu 2
Use the proper mode for pickle when opening and writing the stats file.
.sp
Closes #148.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit hidden\-method message when the attribute has been
monkey\-patched, you\(aqre on your own when you do that.
.IP \(bu 2
Only emit attribute\-defined\-outside\-init / W0201 \%<#\:attribute-defined-outside-init> for definition within the same
module as the offended class, avoiding to mangle the output in some cases.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit unnecessary\-lambda / W0108 \%<#\:unnecessary-lambda> if the body of the lambda call contains
call chaining.
.sp
Closes #243.
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt emit missing\-docstring / C0111 \%<#\:missing-docstring> when the actual docstring uses \fB\&.format\fP\&.
.sp
Closes #281.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 1.2
.sp
Release date: 2014\-04\-30
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Restore the ability to specify the init\-hook option via the
configuration file, which was accidentally broken in 1.2.0.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning [bad\-continuation] for badly indented continued
lines.
.IP \(bu 2
Emit assignment\-from\-none / E1128 \%<#\:assignment-from-none> when the function contains bare returns.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #191
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning for closing over variables that are
defined in loops.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #176
.IP \(bu 2
Do not warn about u escapes in string literals when Unicode literals
are used for Python 2.*.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #151
.IP \(bu 2
Extend the checking for unbalanced\-tuple\-unpacking / W0632 \%<#\:unbalanced-tuple-unpacking> and
unpacking\-non\-sequence / E0633 \%<#\:unpacking-non-sequence> to instance attribute unpacking as well.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix explicit checking of python script (1.2 regression)
.sp
Closes #219
.IP \(bu 2
Restore \-\-init\-hook, renamed accidentally into \-\-init\-hooks in 1.2.0
.sp
Closes #211
.IP \(bu 2
Add \(aqindexing\-exception\(aq warning, which detects that indexing
an exception occurs in Python 2 (behaviour removed in Python 3).
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 1.2.0?
.sp
Release date: 2014\-04\-18
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Pass the current python paths to pylint process when invoked via
epylint.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #133.
.IP \(bu 2
Add \-i / \-\-include\-ids and \-s / \-\-symbols back as completely ignored
options.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #180.
.IP \(bu 2
Extend the number of cases in which logging calls are detected.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #182.
.IP \(bu 2
Improve pragma handling to not detect pylint:* strings in non\-comments.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #79.
.IP \(bu 2
Do not crash with UnknownMessage if an unknown message ID/name appears
in disable or enable in the configuration. Patch by Cole Robinson.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #170
.IP \(bu 2
Add new warning eval\-used / W0123 \%<#\:eval-used>, checking that the builtin function \fBeval\fP was used.
.IP \(bu 2
Make it possible to show a naming hint for invalid name by setting
include\-naming\-hint. Also make the naming hints configurable.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #138
.IP \(bu 2
Added support for enforcing multiple, but consistent name styles for
different name types inside a single module; based on a patch written
by \%<morbo@\:google\:.com>\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Also warn about empty docstrings on overridden methods; contributed
by \%<sebastianu@\:google\:.com>\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Also inspect arguments to constructor calls, and emit relevant
warnings; contributed by \%<sebastianu@\:google\:.com>\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new configuration option logging\-modules to make the list
of module names that can be checked for logging\-not\-lazy / W1201 \%<#\:logging-not-lazy> et. al.
configurable; contributed by \%<morbo@\:google\:.com>\&.
.IP \(bu 2
ensure init\-hooks is evaluated before other options, notably load\-plugins
.sp
Closes #166
.IP \(bu 2
Python 2.5 support restored: fixed small issues preventing pylint to run
on python 2.5.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #50
Closes BitBucket #62
.IP \(bu 2
pylint doesn\(aqt crash when looking for used\-before\-assignment / E0601 \%<#\:used-before-assignment> in context manager assignments.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #128
.IP \(bu 2
Add new warning, bad\-reversed\-sequence / E0111 \%<#\:bad-reversed-sequence>, for checking that the
reversed() builtin receive a sequence (implements \fB__getitem__\fP and \fB__len__\fP,
without being a dict or a dict subclass) or an instance which implements
\fB__reversed__\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Mark \fBfile\fP as a bad function when using python2
.sp
Closes #8
.IP \(bu 2
Add new warning bad\-exception\-context / E0703 \%<#\:bad-exception-context>, checking
that \fBraise ... from ...\fP uses a proper exception context
(None or an exception).
.IP \(bu 2
Enhance the check for used\-before\-assignment / E0601 \%<#\:used-before-assignment> to look
for \(aqnonlocal\(aq uses.
.IP \(bu 2
Emit undefined\-all\-variable / E0603 \%<#\:undefined-all-variable> if a package\(aqs __all__
variable contains a missing submodule.
.sp
Closes #126
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning abstract\-class\-instantiated / E0110 \%<#\:abstract-class-instantiated> for checking
that abstract classes created with \fBabc\fP module and
with abstract methods are instantiated.
.IP \(bu 2
Do not warn about return\-arg\-in\-generator / E0106 \%<#\:return-arg-in-generator> in Python 3.3+.
.IP \(bu 2
Do not warn about abstract\-method / W0223 \%<#\:abstract-method> when the abstract method
is implemented through assignment
.sp
Closes #155
.IP \(bu 2
Improve cyclic import detection in the case of packages, patch by Buck Golemon
.IP \(bu 2
Add new warnings for checking proper class __slots__:
\fBinvalid\-slots\-object\fP and \fBinvalid\-slots\fP\&.
.IP \(bu 2
Search for rc file in \fI~/.config/pylintrc\fP if \fI~/.pylintrc\fP
doesn\(aqt exists
.sp
Closes #121
.IP \(bu 2
Don\(aqt register the new style checker w/ python >= 3
.IP \(bu 2
Fix unused\-import / W0611 \%<#\:unused-import> false positive w/ augment assignment
.sp
Closes #78
.IP \(bu 2
Fix access\-member\-before\-definition / E0203 \%<#\:access-member-before-definition> false negative wrt aug assign
.sp
Closes #164
.IP \(bu 2
Do not attempt to analyze non python file, e.g. .so file
.sp
Closes #122
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 1.1
.sp
Release date: 2013\-12\-22
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add new check for use of deprecated\-pragma / I0022 \%<#\:deprecated-pragma> directives \(dqpylint:disable\-msg\(dq
or \(dqpylint:enable\-msg\(dq which was previously emitted as a regular warn().
.IP \(bu 2
Avoid false used\-before\-assignment / E0601 \%<#\:used-before-assignment> for except handler defined
identifier used on the same line.
.sp
Closes #111
.IP \(bu 2
Combine \(aqno\-space\-after\-operator\(aq, \(aqno\-space\-after\-comma\(aq and
\(aqno\-space\-before\-operator\(aq into a new warning \(aqbad\-whitespace\(aq.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new warning superfluous\-parens / C0325 \%<#\:superfluous-parens> for unnecessary
parentheses after certain keywords.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a potential crash in the redefine\-in\-handler warning
if the redefined name is a nested getattr node.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a new option for the multi\-statement warning to
allow single\-line if statements.
.IP \(bu 2
Add bad\-context\-manager / E0235 \%<#\:bad-context-manager> error, checking that \(aq__exit__\(aq
special method accepts the right number of arguments.
.IP \(bu 2
Run pylint as a python module \(aqpython \-m pylint\(aq (Anatoly Techtonik).
.IP \(bu 2
Check for non\-exception classes inside an except clause.
.IP \(bu 2
epylint support options to give to pylint after the file to analyze and
have basic input validation, patches provided by
felipeochoa and Brian Lane.
.sp
Closes BitBucket #53
Closes BitBucket #54
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning, non\-iterator\-returned / E0301 \%<#\:non-iterator-returned>, for non\-iterators
returned by \(aq__iter__\(aq.
.IP \(bu 2
Add new checks for unpacking non\-sequences in assignments
(unpacking\-non\-sequence / E0633 \%<#\:unpacking-non-sequence>) as well as unbalanced tuple unpacking
(unbalanced\-tuple\-unpacking / W0632 \%<#\:unbalanced-tuple-unpacking>).
.IP \(bu 2
useless\-else\-on\-loop / W0120 \%<#\:useless-else-on-loop> not emitted if there is a break in the
else clause of inner loop.
.sp
Closes #117
.IP \(bu 2
don\(aqt mark \fBinput\fP as a bad function when using python3.
.sp
Closes #110
.IP \(bu 2
badly\-implemented\-container caused several problems in its
current implementation. Deactivate it until we have something
better.
.sp
Refs #112
.IP \(bu 2
Use attribute regexp for properties in python3, as in python2
.IP \(bu 2
Create the \fBPYLINTHOME\fP directory when needed, it might fail and lead to
spurious warnings on import of pylint.config.
.IP \(bu 2
Fix setup.py so that pylint properly install on Windows when using python3
.IP \(bu 2
Various documentation fixes and enhancements
.IP \(bu 2
Fix a false\-positive trailing\-whitespace / C0303 \%<#\:trailing-whitespace> on Windows
.sp
Closes #55
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New In Pylint 1.0
.sp
Release date: 2013\-08\-06
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
Add check for the use of \(aqexec\(aq function
.IP \(bu 2
New \-\-msg\-template option to control output, deprecating \(dqmsvc\(dq and
\(dqparseable\(dq output formats as well as killing \fB\-\-include\-ids\fP and \fB\-\-symbols\fP
options
.IP \(bu 2
Do not emit [fixme] for every line if the config value \(aqnotes\(aq
is empty, but [fixme] is enabled.
.IP \(bu 2
Emit warnings about lines exceeding the column limit when
those lines are inside multiline docstrings.
.IP \(bu 2
Do not double\-check parameter names with the regex for parameters and
inline variables.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning missing\-final\-newline / C0304 \%<#\:missing-final-newline> for files missing
the final newline.
.IP \(bu 2
Methods that are decorated as properties are now treated as attributes
for the purposes of name checking.
.IP \(bu 2
Names of derived instance class member are not checked any more.
.IP \(bu 2
Names in global statements are now checked against the regular
expression for constants.
.IP \(bu 2
For toplevel name assignment, the class name regex will be used if
pylint can detect that value on the right\-hand side is a class
(like collections.namedtuple()).
.IP \(bu 2
Simplified invalid\-name / C0103 \%<#\:invalid-name> message
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning invalid\-encoded\-data (W0512) for files that
contain data that cannot be decoded with the specified or
default encoding.
.IP \(bu 2
New warning bad\-open\-mode / W1501 \%<#\:bad-open-mode> for calls to open (or file) that
specify invalid open modes (Original implementation by Sasha Issayev).
.IP \(bu 2
New warning old\-style\-class (C1001) for classes that do not have any
base class.
.IP \(bu 2
Add new name type \(aqclass_attribute\(aq for attributes defined
in class scope. By default, allow both const and variable names.
.IP \(bu 2
New warning trailing\-whitespace / C0303 \%<#\:trailing-whitespace> that warns about
trailing whitespace.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning unpacking\-in\-except (W0712) about unpacking
exceptions in handlers, which is unsupported in Python 3.
.IP \(bu 2
Add a configuration option for missing\-docstring / C0111 \%<#\:missing-docstring> to
optionally exempt short functions/methods/classes from
the check.
.IP \(bu 2
Add the type of the offending node to missing\-docstring / C0111 \%<#\:missing-docstring>
and empty\-docstring / C0112 \%<#\:empty-docstring>\&.
.IP \(bu 2
New utility classes for per\-checker unittests in testutils.py
.IP \(bu 2
Do not warn about redefinitions of variables that match the
dummy regex.
.IP \(bu 2
Do not treat all variables starting with _ as dummy variables,
only _ itself.
.IP \(bu 2
Make the line\-too\-long / C0301 \%<#\:line-too-long> warning configurable by adding a regex for lines
for with the length limit should not be enforced
.IP \(bu 2
Do not warn about a long line if a pylint disable
option brings it above the length limit
.IP \(bu 2
Do not flag names in nested with statements as undefined.
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new warning \(aqold\-raise\-syntax\(aq for the deprecated syntax
raise Exception, args
.IP \(bu 2
Support for PEP 3102 and new missing\-kwoa / E1125 \%<#\:missing-kwoa> message for missing
mandatory keyword argument
.sp
Closes Logilab #107788
.IP \(bu 2
Fix spelling of max\-branchs option, now max\-branches
.IP \(bu 2
Added a new base class and interface for checkers that work on the
tokens rather than the syntax, and only tokenize the input file
once.
.IP \(bu 2
Follow astng renaming to astroid
.IP \(bu 2
Check for unbalanced unpacking in assignments
.sp
Closes BitBucket #37
.IP \(bu 2
Fix incomplete\-protocol false positive for read\-only containers like tuple
.sp
Closes BitBucket #25
.IP \(bu 2
Fix False positive E1003 on Python 3 for argument\-less super()
.sp
Closes BitBucket #16
.IP \(bu 2
Put back documentation in source distribution
.sp
Closes BitBucket #6
.IP \(bu 2
epylint shouldn\(aqt hang anymore when there is a large output on pylint\(aqstderr
.sp
Closes BitBucket #15
.IP \(bu 2
Fix epylint w/ python3
.sp
Closes BitBucket #7
.IP \(bu 2
Remove string module from the default list of deprecated modules
.sp
Closes BitBucket #3
.UNINDENT
.SS 0.x
.sp
From pylint\(aqs beginning to pylint 2.14.0 included, we had a changelog that contained \fIall\fP
nontrivial changes to Pylint, including changes that were
not user facing, i.e. change that might interest you only if you\(aqre a developer
working on pylint or pylint plugins or an open\-source historian.
.sp
Ticket numbers are almost always internal to Logilab, some come from bitbucket.
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.28.0?
.sp
Release date: 2013\-04\-25
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
bitbucket #1: fix \(dqdictionary changed size during iteration\(dq crash
.IP \(bu 2
#74013: new E1310[bad\-str\-strip\-call] message warning when a call to a
{l,r,}strip method contains duplicate characters (patch by Torsten Marek)
.IP \(bu 2
#123233: new E0108[duplicate\-argument\-name] message reporting duplicate
argument names
.IP \(bu 2
#81378: emit W0120[useless\-else\-on\-loop] for loops without break
.IP \(bu 2
#124660: internal dependencies should not appear in external dependencies
report
.IP \(bu 2
#124662: fix name error causing crash when symbols are included in output
messages
.IP \(bu 2
#123285: apply pragmas for warnings attached to lines to physical source
code lines
.IP \(bu 2
#123259: do not emit E0105 for yield expressions inside lambdas
.IP \(bu 2
#123892: don\(aqt crash when attempting to show source code line that can\(aqt
be encoded with the current locale settings
.IP \(bu 2
Simplify checks for dangerous default values by unifying tests for all
different mutable compound literals.
.IP \(bu 2
Improve the description for redundant\-keyword\-arg / E1124 \%<#\:redundant-keyword-arg>
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.27.0?
.sp
Release date: 2013\-02\-26
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
#20693: replace pylint.el by Ian Eure version (patch by J.Kotta)
.IP \(bu 2
#105327: add support for \-\-disable=all option and deprecate the
\(aqdisable\-all\(aq inline directive in favour of \(aqskip\-file\(aq (patch by
A.Fayolle)
.IP \(bu 2
#110840: add messages I0020 and I0021 for reporting of suppressed
messages and useless suppression pragmas. (patch by Torsten Marek)
.IP \(bu 2
#112728: add warning E0604 for non\-string objects in __all__
(patch by Torsten Marek)
.IP \(bu 2
#120657: add warning W0110/deprecated\-lambda when a map/filter
of a lambda could be a comprehension (patch by Martin Pool)
.IP \(bu 2
#113231: logging checker now looks at instances of Logger classes
in addition to the base logging module. (patch by Mike Bryant)
.IP \(bu 2
#111799: don\(aqt warn about octal escape sequence, but warn about o
which is not octal in Python (patch by Martin Pool)
.IP \(bu 2
#110839: bind <F5> to Run button in pylint\-gui
.IP \(bu 2
#115580: fix erroneous W0212 (access to protected member) on super call
(patch by Martin Pool)
.IP \(bu 2
#110853: fix a crash when an __init__ method in a base class has been
created by assignment rather than direct function definition (patch by
Torsten Marek)
.IP \(bu 2
#110838: fix pylint\-gui crash when include\-ids is activated (patch by
Omega Weapon)
.IP \(bu 2
#112667: fix emission of reimport warnings for mixed imports and extend
the testcase (patch by Torsten Marek)
.IP \(bu 2
#112698: fix crash related to non\-inferable __all__ attributes and
invalid __all__ contents (patch by Torsten Marek)
.IP \(bu 2
Python 3 related fixes:
.IP \(bu 2
.INDENT 2.0
.TP
.B #110213: fix import of checkers broken with python 3.3, causing
\(dqNo such message id W0704\(dq breakage
.UNINDENT
.IP \(bu 2
#120635: redefine cmp function used in pylint.reporters
.IP \(bu 2
Include full warning id for I0020 and I0021 and make sure to flush
warnings after each module, not at the end of the pylint run.
(patch by Torsten Marek)
.IP \(bu 2
Changed the regular expression for inline options so that it must be
preceded by a # (patch by Torsten Marek)
.IP \(bu 2
Make dot output for import graph predictable and not depend
on ordering of strings in hashes. (patch by Torsten Marek)
.IP \(bu 2
Add hooks for import path setup and move pylint\(aqs sys.path
modifications into them. (patch by Torsten Marek)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.26.0?
.sp
Release date: 2012\-10\-05
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
#106534: add \-\-ignore\-imports option to code similarity checking
and \(aqsymilar\(aq command line tool (patch by Ry4an Brase)
.IP \(bu 2
#104571: check for anomalous backslash escape, introducing new
W1401 and W1402 messages (patch by Martin Pool)
.IP \(bu 2
#100707: check for boolop being used as exception class, introducing
new W0711 message (patch by Tim Hatch)
.IP \(bu 2
#4014: improve checking of metaclass methods first args, introducing
new C0204 message (patch by \%<lothiraldan@\:gmail\:.com> finalized by sthenault)
.IP \(bu 2
#4685: check for consistency of a module\(aqs __all__ variable,
introducing new E0603 message
.IP \(bu 2
#105337: allow custom reporter in output\-format (patch by Kevin Jing Qiu)
.IP \(bu 2
#104420: check for protocol completeness and avoid false R0903
(patch by Peter Hammond)
.IP \(bu 2
#100654: fix grammatical error for W0332 message (using \(aql\(aq as
long int identifier)
.IP \(bu 2
#103656: fix W0231 false positive for missing call to object.__init__
(patch by \%<lothiraldan@\:gmail\:.com>)
.IP \(bu 2
#63424: fix similarity report disabling by properly renaming it to RP0801
.IP \(bu 2
#103949: create a console_scripts entry point to be used by
easy_install, buildout and pip
.IP \(bu 2
fix cross\-interpreter issue (non compatible access to __builtins__)
.IP \(bu 2
stop including tests files in distribution, they causes crash when
installed with python3 (#72022, #82417, #76910)
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.25.2?
.sp
Release date: 2012\-07\-17
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
#93591: Correctly emit warnings about clobbered variable names when an
except handler contains a tuple of names instead of a single name.
(patch by \%<tmarek@\:google\:.com>)
.IP \(bu 2
#7394: W0212 (access to protected member) not emitted on assignments
(patch by \%<lothiraldan@\:gmail\:.com>)
.IP \(bu 2
#18772; no prototype consistency check for mangled methods (patch by
\%<lothiraldan@\:gmail\:.com>)
.IP \(bu 2
#92911: emit W0102 when sets are used as default arguments in functions
(patch by \%<tmarek@\:google\:.com>)
.IP \(bu 2
#77982: do not emit E0602 for loop variables of comprehensions
used as argument values inside a decorator (patch by \%<tmarek@\:google\:.com>)
.IP \(bu 2
#89092: don\(aqt emit E0202 (attribute hiding a method) on @property methods
.IP \(bu 2
#92584: fix pylint\-gui crash due to internal API change
.IP \(bu 2
#87192: fix crash when decorators are accessed through more than one dot
(for instance @a.b is fine, @a.b.c crash)
.IP \(bu 2
#88914: fix parsing of \-\-generated\-members options, leading to crash
when using a regexp value set
.IP \(bu 2
fix potential crashes with utils.safe_infer raising InferenceError
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.25.1?
.sp
Release date: 2011\-12\-08
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
#81078: Warn if names in  exception handlers clobber overwrite
existing names (patch by \%<tmarek@\:google\:.com>)
.IP \(bu 2
#81113: Fix W0702 messages appearing with the wrong line number.
(patch by \%<tmarek@\:google\:.com>)
.IP \(bu 2
#50461, #52020, #51222: Do not issue warnings when using 2.6\(aqs
property.setter/deleter functionality (patch by \%<dneil@\:google\:.com>)
.IP \(bu 2
#9188, #4024: Do not trigger W0631 if a loop variable is assigned
in the else branch of a for loop.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.25.0?
.sp
Release date: 2011\-10\-7
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
#74742: make allowed name for first argument of class method configurable
(patch by Google)
.IP \(bu 2
#74087: handle case where inference of a module return YES; this avoid
some cases of \(dqTypeError: \(aq_Yes\(aq object does not support indexing\(dq (patch
by Google)
.IP \(bu 2
#74745: make \(dqtoo general\(dq exception names configurable (patch by Google)
.IP \(bu 2
#74747: crash occurs when lookup up a special attribute in class scope
(patch by google)
.IP \(bu 2
#76920: crash if on e.g. \(dqpylint \-\-rcfile\(dq (patch by Torsten Marek)
.IP \(bu 2
#77237: warning for E0202 may be very misleading
.IP \(bu 2
#73941: HTML report messages table is badly rendered
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.24.0?
.sp
Release date: 2011\-07\-18
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
#69738: add regular expressions support for \(dqgenerated\-members\(dq
.IP \(bu 2
ids of logging and string_format checkers have been changed:
logging: 65 \-> 12, string_format: 99 \-> 13
Also add documentation to say that ids of range 1\-50 shall be reserved
to pylint internal checkers
.IP \(bu 2
#69993: Additional string format checks for logging module:
check for missing arguments, too many arguments, or invalid string
formats in the logging checker module. Contributed by Daniel Arena
.IP \(bu 2
#69220: add column offset to the reports. If you\(aqve a custom reporter,
this change may break it has now location gain a new item giving the
column offset.
.IP \(bu 2
#60828: Fix false positive in reimport check
.IP \(bu 2
#70495: absolute imports fail depending on module path (patch by Jacek Konieczny)
.IP \(bu 2
#22273: Fix \-\-ignore option documentation to match reality
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.23.0?
.sp
Release date: 2011\-01\-11
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
documentation update, add manpages
.IP \(bu 2
several performance improvements
.IP \(bu 2
finalize python3 support
.IP \(bu 2
new W0106 warning \(aqExpression \(dq%s\(dq is assigned to nothing\(aq
.IP \(bu 2
drop E0501 and E0502 messages about wrong source encoding: not anymore
interesting since it\(aqs a syntax error for python >= 2.5 and we now only
support this python version and above.
.IP \(bu 2
don\(aqt emit W0221 or W0222 when methods as variable arguments (e.g. *arg
and/or **args). Patch submitted by Charles Duffy.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.22.0?
.sp
Release date: 2010\-11\-15
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
python versions: minimal python3.x support; drop python < 2.5 support
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.21.4?
.sp
Release date: 2010\-10\-27
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
fix #48066: pylint crashes when redirecting output containing non\-ascii characters
.IP \(bu 2
fix #19799: \(dqpylint \-blah\(dq exit with status 2
.IP \(bu 2
update documentation
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.21.3?
.sp
Release date: 2010\-09\-28
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
restored python 2.3 compatibility. Along with logilab\-astng
0.21.3 and logilab\-common 0.52, this will much probably be the
latest release supporting python < 2.5.
.UNINDENT
.SS What\(aqs New in Pylint 0.21.2?
.sp
Release date: 2010\-08\-26
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
fix #36193: import checker raise exception on cyclic import
.IP \(bu 2
fix #28796: regression in \-\-generated\-members introduced pylint 0.20
.IP \(bu 2
some documentation cleanups
